{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play","id":216621,"title":"Old gods of Jakarta (Mummy Actual Play)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-02T02:42:45-07:00","id":216621,"title":"Old gods of Jakarta (Mummy Actual Play)","content":"It's been a while since I tried doing recaps of my game sessions, but I figured that at the very least this would be a good way of keeping track of what's happened in the game so far. We just finished our first session of Mummy: The Curse, and it was an absolute blast. Events didn't exactly pan out as I had anticipated, which serves me right for actually trying to plan the first few sessions instead of attempting my usual sandbox approach.<br /> <br /> The campaign is set in Jakarta in 2012. Of the group, two members (myself and one player) have actually spent some time in South-East Asia, although not a lot in Jakarta specifically so even our knowledge is a bit scarce. The other two have never been there. If anyone reading actually lives in Jakarta... I'll be honest, I'm sure I'm going to portray something woefully wrong at some point. Using a mix of Block by Bloody Block and Damnation City, I've split Jakarta into various zones so I can track moods and cult influence in various areas separately. This is critical to the management of the Cult, because I decided early on that I wouldn't have the players spend experience on something that fluctuates so readily. Instead, they start the game sharing a Reach 1, Grasp 1 Tribal Cult. Anytime their influence in an area grows to the point that they supplant the current group in power I present them with a choice that will get them a point of Reach or Grasp, or possibly allow them to change the nature of the Cult to Enterprise or Conspiracy or to add one of the additional merits.<br /> <br /> I then proceeded to give all the players 35 experience and told them to make more or less whatever characters they wanted, and we ended up with the following:<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra, the Unbending Spine - A Guildmaster of the Tef-Aabhi and a member of the Ka Decree. He is a native of Irem, a big, heavily built man from a lifetime of masonry and heavy lifting, and every bit as strong in will as he is in body. He loathes compromise, getting his title from a combination of his work in building Irem's Pillars and his utter refusal to bend his knee for any but the gods and Shan'iatu. His tomb is enormous, taking up the top five stories of a skyscraper in the inner city (it has both the Famous and Obscure attributes as well). It is built around his relic, a three story tall obelisk that causes those to see him as automatically perceiving him as Status 5 in their own organisation/s so long as he is in the seat of his power, the skyscraper that holds his tomb.<br /> He remembers struggling in his previous descent, five years earlier, to manipulate and coerce a variety of officials in order to get a project off the ground and build a bypass. He faced perpetual opposition from a criminal motorbike gang, an extremely powerful and ancient ghost at the site of construction, and a lawyer representing unknown corporate interests. He ended his descent having completed the task for which he was summoned, retrieve a recently located relic, but with construction of the bypass having ground to a complete halt.<br /> He also remembers that he was involved in the construction of the Empire State Building once, and his Sadikh is an Italian American who was born in the 1920s. He can't recall the circumstances of the move to Indonesia, as he takes advantage of his relic to ensure that he is almost as constantly active as he can afford. It's left him with many, many descents between then, leaving the memories quite deeply buried.<br /> If I remember right, his Affinities are Model Lifeweb, Dominating Might, and Builder's Wisdom. His Utterances are Blessed is the God-King (although he can only use Tier 1 at present) and Chthonic Dominion (Tiers 1 and 2).<br /> <br /> Aquila Ashex, the Sphinx of Rome - A Guildmaster of the Mesen-Nebu and a member of the Ab decree. She is a beautiful woman with long dark hair, olive skin, and green eyes. She usually wears garments provided by the Dust Beneath Feet Utterance. At some point, her own conception of Dedwen became the concept that improving humans on a moral level should have more value than anything else, and she strives to make that dream a reality. She sides with the oppressed, the dispossessed, seeking an end to the era of modern slavery and trying to reform Jakarta's slums. Her position as Guildmaster is somewhat tenuous as a result, as the majority of the Guild doesn't exactly share her point of view. Luckily, Jakarta has a small Arisen population and she has thus far escaped scrutiny. Her tomb lies in one of the city's slums, not far from the resting place of a rival Mesen-Nebu.<br /> She was last raised in the mid-90s to help the hierophant's wife through childbirth. When both wife and child died, she brought them both back from the dead.<br /> Her Affinities are Divine Flesh, Miraculous Benefactor, Glorious Mein, Divine Countenance. Her Utterances are Gift of the Golden Ankh (Tiers 1 and 3) and Dust Beneath Feet (only Tier 1 available).<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet, or Bast for short, She Who Is Power And Devours - A journeyman (Status 4) of the Su-Menent, and a member of the Sheut decree. She has dark brown skin, her ancestors coming from conquered territories to the south and west of Irem, and her hair has been shaved save for a single strip along the top of her head that falls down to her shoulders in braids. She is a thoroughly brutal Arisen, bears a lack of respect that borders on disgust towards almost all mortals, and believes that her Purpose is above all. She begins the game with the Pale Brood as her relic.<br /> She was last active in the late 1970s. She was backing Pol Pot's regime in Cambodia at the time, and fled to Indonesia when his grip on power began to fail. She is disgusted at her failure there, especially at the fact that all the forced labour camps at her disposal were unable to uncover a single lost relic for her. She made a pact with Sesu Ra, one that she recalls but that he no longer remembers, and he accepted what was left of her cult into his own.<br /> Her Affinities are Fated Soul, Fearsome Soul, Grip of Death, and Withering Judgement. Her Utterances are Ancestry of Forgotten Stars and Secrets Ripped From Skies. As the game begins she has access to Tier 1 and 2 for both.<br /> <br /> Each of the players has been asked to write a character journal. Thus far they've each done one describing their previous descents from their perspectives. I'll post them up at some point in the near future, I hope.<br /> <br /> The final &quot;character&quot; at play is the player cult. They call themselves the Families of the West, and are split roughly into three bloodlines. The Lehn family came from Cambodia in the 70s along with Sekhet Bastet. Their younger members are now mostly of mixed Cambodian-Indonesian descent, the eldest still remember what they were ordered to do by Bast under the regime. The Mayehi family take Sesu Ra as their patron, and have largely dominated the cult's leadership for the past few decades. The final family has no family name. They are headed by an ancient matriarch named Phatri, and hold Aquila as their master and deliverer. The cult is based on an islet out in the Thousand Islands, a small village of about two dozen houses. Some among the Cult travel to and live in Jakarta for work and to keep an eye on their masters' tombs. When the game begins, the Cult has been led by the hierophant Richard Mayehi for almost 20 years.<br /> <br /> So that's where we were when the game began.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T04:03:29-07:00","id":216641,"title":"","content":"We began our first game with Aquila rising for her Sothic Turn. She woke on a stone slab underground, and felt immediately that she was not in her tomb. Two other mummified bodies were laid out on slabs on either side of her, and a ladder was in a corner of the room. I kept the descriptions here deliberately basic, following the advice at the back of the book, on account of her being Memory 0 for this first scene.<br /> <br /> The top of the ladder was opened, an alarm went up, and four mortals dropped down to fight her. Aquila sunk beneath the ground and began trying to strike at the humans without exposing herself overly. A terrified mortal hit a dramatic failure, tripped over her arm, and knocked one of the bodies from the table. Sekhet Bastet rose in fury, struck the man down and turned on the others. One mortal fled, somehow leaping from the base of the ladder to the top in a single bound, while the remaining two stood their ground. Aquila swum after the fleeing man, leaving bast to face two men armed with machetes. It hardly proved an obstacle, as she seized one man and mummified him on the spot (Withering Judgement was a pure joy to describe to the other players, who had no idea what kind of things the Su-Menent could do), then knocked the other man unconscious in short order. She then grabbed up the machete and decapitated all three for disturbing her repose.<br /> <br /> Outside, in what turned out to be a farm somewhere in the middle of nowhere, Aquila found her quarry clambering into a jeep. She emerged to stop him but he'd already alerted more men standing outside, and she barely avoided death by Molotov. Whoever they were facing was quite well prepared for fighting Arisen, as it turned out. The jeeps took off, but Aquila grabbed hold of one (Strength 10) and allowed herself to be carried. The vehicles withdrew to a safe distance, save for one which continued to flee the scene.<br /> <br /> Bast climbed the ladder and found two men, one tied to a chair and clearly having been tortured recently, the other suspended from the ceiling by his hands and gagged. She was all set to ignore them until the one on the chair addressed her in the old tongue, and she almost seemed about to help him. That would have been too generous though, so instead she stuck the machete in the floor about a foot from where he was tied and told him that, if he was worthy, he would find his own way out. She then walked outside and a fight between her and two jeeps full of mortals ended quite quickly as she called down meteors to smash the jeeps and burn their occupants to death. Aquila was still holding onto one, and ended up suffering some aggravated damage when the vehicle she was clinging to suddenly became a burning wreck. Meanwhile, the occupants of a couch in the real world are all staring at Sekhet Bastet's player thinking something along the lines of &quot;flipping heck&quot;.<br /> <br /> Aquila felt the fog on her mind begin to recede, stirring her conscience, and she risked the flames to drag the driver of the jeep free from the wreckage. Alas, she was too late. He died quickly, and after a moment's dilemma she unleashed the full power of Gift of the Golden Ankh to raise him to life. Our first character hit Sekhem 9. Bast seemed... somewhat annoyed about this. Her memories were coming back as well, and some part of her was telling her that the man's life was hers to take, not for Aquila to give back. An argument promptly started over the subject.<br /> <br /> After a while they felt Sekhem flare. One of the men in the house behind her had won free, grabbed the other, and descended the ladder. It seemed he was Sesu Ra's Sadikh, and he lifted the Black Caul to raise his master with the command &quot;Protect your people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet used Secrets Ripped From Skies to determine that they were only a few miles from Jakarta. The Sadikh, going by the name Luca Tomasino in this life, explained that he had been ordered to look after Sesu Ra's finances while his master rested. He and his taxi driver (I believe the exact words he used were Iremite for &quot;palanquin bearer&quot;, as Sesu Ra is the only one of the Mummies to speak a modern language) were captured and dragged to this location, then tortured. He didn't know much more than that. The Arisen sent him back to gather clothing and equipment for them. Although Sesu Ra and Aquila acknowledged the necessity of covering up until their Sekhem dropped further, Sekhet Bastet refused to debase herself just to provide the mortals with a sense of security. Aquila garbed herself by using Dust Beneath Feet to provide herself with something approximating a burka, and Sesu Ra used a mix of clothing scavenged from the dead and covered his head in the linen bandages he had woken wearing. Bast dropped to Sekhem 9. I decided not to count this scene towards Sesu Ra's descent, he'd only been active a few minutes and hadn't even picked up the dice yet.<br /> <br /> With all forms of transportation wrecked and still burning in the background, the Arisen and their servant continued on foot to the outskirts of Jakarta. Aquila carried the man she'd resurrected, who was yet to regain consciousness. There was a very brief encounter with the driver of a tuk tuk, who fled after Sesu Ra tapped him on the shoulder to get his attention and then removed his face wrappings. The Arisen piled in, although Sekhet Bastet did express her disgust at the ignoble method of transportation.<br /> <br /> They went first to Bast's Tomb. Sesu Ra's is Famous, and Aquila's is both Haunted and Under Surveillance, so it seemed like the best option at the time. There was no sign of the cultist who was meant to be on guard, and the door was open when they arrived. The tomb was built on the edge of an unofficial graveyard in a riverside slum, far underground. When they entered they discovered that the sarcophagus was open, but that the rest of her possessions, including the Pale Brood, were undisturbed and still sealed within their stone chests. Bast and Sesu Ra both meditated, but Aquila's captive regained consciousness at this point and started screaming so Aquila and Luca moved him outside for a... discussion.<br /> <br /> After an hour of futile attempts to win the man's trust, not helped by the fact that Aquila had to use Luca as a translator and Luca might... not really have been the most comforting of translators, the others emerged with a few extra pillar points. Despite the language barrier, Bast broke the man's will in short order. They then found out a few things.<br /> <br /> First, the men that attacked them were called &quot;the Faithful&quot;. The man they had captured was just an initiate. It was meant to be their first feast. They didn't know the name of the man who had recruited them. All they really knew was that they had been asked to go to this place in the countryside. They were chosen when this strange man, the leader, approached them and showed them a human skull. He asked them what they felt. They replied &quot;Hungry&quot;, and he told them they had been selected to worship the gods and partake in divinity. Finally, they learned their captive's name was Petro.<br /> <br /> Bast promptly went for Kepher, as they were pretty sure they had just heard the description of an Uter relic. She rolled an exceptional success on, I think, six dice. So... they now knew through visions that a houseboat in the bay was where the relic, the leader of these &quot;Faithful&quot;, and, presumably, the rest of this cult were all located.<br /> <br /> Aquila demanded they visit the cultists first, as the absence of a guard was worrying her. It was an interesting choice, as it would prompt descent checks for her and Sekhet Bastet. They set off, but Petro made a break for it, Luca chased him, and the Arisen were approached some minutes later by a European man saying his master requested their presence. Bast had sort of neglected to mention that her home was made neighbouring the territory of Mot-Tan of the Rising Teeth, a Maa-Kep who was somewhat infamous for his unfriendly and flat out territorial disposition.<br /> <br /> They followed the European man, who called himself Haig, and found themselves at a large slum dwelling right on the river. Mot-Tan spoke to them from behind a semi-transparent curtain, while his cult stood guard around the group. The players mostly just exchanged pleasantries, and Sesu Ra chose to reveal pretty much everything they knew except the existence of the skull-relic. Mot-Tan dismissed his Cultists, preferring them not to know about the blasphemies being perpetrated by these &quot;Faithful&quot;, and drew back the curtain. He turned out to be a masked Arisen at the far lower end of his Descent, the opposite of the three creatures facing him who were still all so powerful they still appeared as desiccated corpses. He wore a ring, a relic, in the place of a wedding ring, and gestured behind him to a young woman or girl of maybe 16 years old, who he introduced as his wife and hierophant. He was quite perturbed by what they described, said they should take their prisoner Petro before the head of the Sesha-Hebsu for judgement, and that the cult of the Mistress of Bones, the Su-Menent Guildmaster, should be informed so that they could wake their mistress to destroy this blasphemy. He then let them go, Petro and Luca in tow, without any further trouble, but warned them all that he would be preparing his cult to defend his territory against a possible attack from the Faithful and that they shouldn't trespass again without seeking his permission.<br /> <br /> The group obtained a new tuk tuk, the old one had disappeared, in the same manner as they had the first. Sesu Ra dropped to Sekhem 9. They then drove to the bay, found a wharf with fishing boats tied up, and scared some fishermen until they had a wooden dinghy which they drove out to the Thousand Islands. There was a brief exchange, with them handing over Petro to the cultists and Sesu Ra attempting to gather warriors for an attack on the Faithful's boat. Rom Mayehi, brother of the hierophant, volunteered his services and supplied Luca with a shotgun. They did learn that Richard Mayehi, the current hierophant, had gone missing three days earlier during his regular trip into Jakarta. No one had heard from him since, but his wife (the one who was resurrected by Aquila in her previous descent) expressed her utmost faith that they would find him safe and sound.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Sekhet Bastet fell to Sekhem 8, their bodies filling themselves in and becoming human in appearance. Sesu Ra was still in the good old undead horror stage.<br /> <br /> So they attacked the houseboat, Bast's Kepher triggering automatically to guide her through the nest of anchored boats to the right one. They sent Rom and Luca aboard using stealth, as none of the Arisen were too good at sneaking, and they took up positions on the overhead hatches. Then the Mummies thundered aboard, Sesu Ra smashed the door down, and Aquila's player realised she was completely out of Pillars just in time for the showdown. That was entertaining.<br /> <br /> Sneak attacks from Rom and Luca almost dropped two of the four men inside the boat. One, the leader, snatched up the skull relic from the table and held it over his head. It let out a painful screaming sound that caused the supernatural creatures, all three Arisen and Luca, to take a point of Aggravated damage each. The Faithful tried to keep the Arisen penned in at the doorway, giving the relic more time to harm them. Sesu Ra ordered Luca to fire on the man with the relic, and Luca rolled an incredible number of successes. Unfortunately, he caught the relic in the blast as well, and rolled really well for damage on that as well. The relic was blasted apart, and two chimeras emerged (seriously, the dice were hot as all heck at this point, for everybody, and I decided to roll to see if Amkhata emerged and landed an exceptional success). They went straight for the nearest source of Sekhem, Sesu Ra, who was grappling with one of the Faithful. A snake-bodied, jackal-headed creature with falcon wings wrapped itself around his left arm and started draining his pillars, while the lion-headed bull just bit him in the leg.<br /> <br /> Unable to get past the door, Sekhet Bastet clambered up on deck, tore open her forehead with a deck hook, and phased through the deck as she unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars to become a scaled, eight-limbed demon-thing with three eyes. A terrified Faithful shot her, but bullets did nothing to her in her semi-incorporeal form. The snake-creature on Sesu Ra's arm drained him dry of pillars, so the lion-headed bull turned and attacked Bast from behind. She struggled with it, as Aquila slipped past the fighters and managed to knock one of the other Faithful out. On the roof Rom was able to pick off and kill two of the Faithful, one after the other, but Luca was picked up and thrown over the side of the boat by a telekinetic ability wielded by the man who had once held the relic. As the lion-headed bull drained the last of Bast's pillars and it and the snake-thing dematerialised, the Faithful leader decided all was lost and detonated a bomb somewhere in bowels of the boat.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'll ever forget the next sequence of events. It went like thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;Everyone, make a Wits + Athletics roll to find and get behind some cover.&quot;<br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah. So, Sesu Ra, the Unbending Spine, considered it beneath him to huddle and hide before a mere explosion. As everyone else aboard threw themselves clear, leapt behind tables or furniture or tried to make it to the cockpit, he just stood and faced down the flame. When the fire and smoke cleared he was still standing there, and he chose not to abandon ship as the boat started sinking. He went down, making sure that there was nothing aboard of any import besides the burnt bodies of the dead Faithful. Eventually he swam back up to the surface, got aboard the player's boat, and the group went ashore.<br /> <br /> We were pretty much out of time at this point, so I had a ghostly messenger inform them that the Mistress of Bones had called all Arisen active in the city to the city's Temple for a meeting, and we ended it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T04:26:03-07:00","id":216648,"title":"","content":"Something I feel I should mention:<br /> <br /> This story arc was originally meant to last four sessions. Sekhet Bastet's player leaves us in a month's time, so I thought a quick story about hunting tomb raiders would be a good start. The fact that she was awoken by someone damaging her remains was just perfect. However, I... honestly kinda underestimated Kepher, and definitely underestimated my players' ability to roll an exceptional success on six dice (Sekhem 9 minus 6 plus Willpower). That cut things quite, quite short, leading to the death of everyone the meret was hunting at a very early stage. It also means Sekhet Bastet has now completed her purpose, dropping her to Sekhem 7.<br /> <br /> I'm really just amused at how it played out. It almost perfectly fits some of the themes of Mummy. Yeah, they killed everyone they faced because they had terrifically high Sekhem and, well, Bast and Sesu Ra anyway, were loaded to the gills with Pillar-buffed Strength and Stamina and Utterances. But they don't have any real context for what they just did. They don't know who the men they just killed were, who or what the Faithful are as an organisation, how they were stolen from their tombs, or any of the surrounding circumstances. At least one of the players has been pondering whether Aquila's Sothic Turn happening in the time between their bodies being stolen and their bodies being eaten was a coincidence or if something more is going on. I feel it captured the main dilemma of Mummy perfectly. The players have power, but no context. By the time they have their context, they'll no longer have the power to act on it as effectively. Can't wait to see how the game goes from here. The characters are all fantastic and we're all loving how Mummies play as these near-godlike beings at high Sekhem, and Sesu Ra's player is having a quiet freakout over the hybrid abominations he just unleashed on the world given that he has no idea what they are or what they're capable of.<br /> <br /> If people are interested, I'll try to have the players' descriptions of their previous descent up tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T00:22:40-07:00","id":217252,"title":"","content":"I'm interested!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T02:43:55-07:00","id":217267,"title":"","content":"Fantastic. For their last descents, I provided the characters with a list of a few individuals they would likely have met at that time. About half of these were NPCs I planned on having in the game, the rest were ones I made up so that the players could decide their fates.<br /> <br /> The first I have is Sesu Ra's. His character keeps notes in something that is more scrapbook than diary, so he used a lot of little details to convey that (changing fonts, differently coloured paper, that sort of thing). One that gave us all a good chuckle was that he made an effort to make sure that the dates and spellings were in the American style, reflecting where his character had learned English. Without further ado:<br /> <br /> <i>The leather bound book lay open on the desk with numerous scraps of paper added to its already bloated volume. Flicking through the book reveals highlighted or otherwise attention drawing passages. They read as the following</i><br /> 02/21/2007<br /> My purpose for this descent (as issued to me by my cult) is to locate and retrieve an important relic that has been known to have entered the city. With little more than a description hopefully this directive will give me ample time to complete some of my projects in the city. My Sadikh has not revealed himself to me yet, perhaps he has adopted a lazy persona this time.<br /> 02/25/2007<br /> I have sent out feelers to gather information on the standing of the city and it is apparent that Jakata is continuing to grow uncontrollably, despite my efforts thus far. I have organised to meet with Rekhenaten, Master of the Pit to discuss potential solutions. I will have to postpone the trivial search for the relic for the time being while I look to tame Jakata (I will keep this to myself, however).<br /> 03/01/2007<br /> My Sadikh\u2019s appearance has been fortuitously timed as I feel like I am being forced into being in multiple places at once. I have organised some key locations with Rekhenaten to try and put to flow of heka through this city into some kind of manageable state and have sent my Sadikh (with a considerable budget) to make sure that goes off without a hitch.<br /> I have started a multitude of small, but important projects all over the city to keep control of the heka on a city wide scale. One of these projects is a major bypass in Patra Kunnigan that will help link the projects I have started with Rekhenaten together. To get such a major piece of infrastructure off the ground I simply bribed a few government officials. In this process I dealt with a man by the name of Ramad who was slower than most to accept the deal, I will keep tabs on him for the time being.<br /> I have encountered the guildmaster of the Su-Menent, Kotira, Mistress of Bones, for what I am sure is not the first time. With my current situation in mind I have decided to gather her support by helping her obtain an area where her temple can remain undisturbed<br /> I have also heard of the guildmaster of the Sesha-Hebsu (Yama-Het of the Bloody Pen) having issues with the Premen in West Jakata. This provides a good opportunity to gather her support but I am beginning to be stretched thin as it is, so I will simply observe the situation for now.<br /> <br /> 05/08/2007<br /> <br /> My plans are encountering unforseen problems, some are requiring more resources than expected (these greedy politicians will require the cane over the carrot should they push me any further, I am not known as The Unbending Spine for nothing!). Other projects are having their workers attacked by what appears to be a mortal gang called the Pelamat. I can see no logical motive for this behaviour and have therefore concluded that they are merely a pawn being used by a real player. I would investigate , but I am barely holding everything together and cannot spare the resources, hopefully these attacks will cease on their own accord.<br /> My aiding of the Mistress of Bones has turned a stone on the location of the relic I was risen to find, but this comes as a mixed blessing since completing my task will reduce my time here.<br /> <br /> 06/19/2007<br /> <br /> More set backs are being experienced as a lawyer named Syifa has begun to threaten legal action against me for some of my more \u201cillegal\u201d activities. I find the particularly amusing since I believe she is behind bribery to prevent some of my projects from completing.<br /> A man by the name of Jack Hale has also peaked my interest by importing stange objects including animals, archaeological discoveries and even medical products. Naturally I suspect him to have something to do with relics but I lack the time and conviction to investigate the matter.<br /> <br /> 07/13/2007<br /> <br /> I have been personally warned by Andre (a worker of the bypass through Patra kunnigan) of the existence of \u201csupernatural forces\u201d present in the construction site. From what I have heard I assume this to be a simple ghost, hopefully the spirit will prove to be benign since I don\u2019t have the time for any delays if I hope to finish this project before I return to Duat. I believe this to be Andre\u2019s first supernatural experience (besides me of course) and have convinced him to stay quiet.<br /> I have been unable to delay investigating the lead given to me by the Mistress of Bones and have personally obtained the relic while my Sadikh maintains my projects.<br /> <br /> 08/20/2007<br /> <br /> Tragedy has struck, the ghost has killed a dozen workers and Syifa has seized the opportunity to shut down the project (I\u2019m certain that a bribe to Ramad was involved). This mortal lawyer has proved to be too much of a problem and I have hired some local Premen to threaten her to back down.<br /> The ghost under the bypass appears to be very strong and with my current weakened state, I fear I will not be able to solve the problem this descent, thus putting the project on hold. From the attack I have been able to determine that the ghosts name is apparently \u201cBuk\u201d and has at least two anchors, a skeleton and a small piece of blue pottery that is currently in safe keeping. Andre has been crippled by another Pelamat attack and has begun to blackmail me so he can support his family without a job. I will pay him for now, but only because I lack the time to confront him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T03:37:21-07:00","id":217316,"title":"","content":"And it seems we've temporarily mislaid Aquila's log of the last descent. A bit annoying. If it turns up I'll be sure to post it. In the meantime, here's Sekhet Bastet's:<br /> <br /> I have awoken again.<br /> <br /> The country that I currently reside in is in turmoil. These tiny humans each try and gain another\u2019s trust by offering things they can\u2019t promise and promises they can\u2019t keep. All for pathetic political gain and the ability to order the peasants around like the insects they are.<br /> <br /> I do not like them, but they do have their uses.<br /> <br /> Pama Len, my faithful soldier and mediator to his own kind, has told me I guided the young leader Saloth Sar to power. Now that he holds this land by the throat it is time for me to reap the rewards. My power is much and I am sure that this human will still remember me and the fear I induced last time. This time he will not be so lucky.<br /> <br /> I have come back to search for the relics. I know they are here and my faithful servants, Irem\u2019s faithful servants, tell me we are close to finding them. Tomorrow I will meet with Saloth Sar once again and he will know who gave him his power and ultimately who still controls it. The humans of this country are terrified, the fear of their imminent deaths is intoxicating. There is a war being fought just over the borders and I gather from what I have been told that it will perhaps spread into this seat of power. I must find the relics before this happens. I will not get caught up in the mortal\u2019s petty war. The only thing I am concerned with is Irem\u2019s memory and the relics of power.<br /> <br /> Glory to the Su-Menent.<br /> <br /> Glory to Irem. <br /> <br /> July 1978<br /> <br /> Salroth Sar still remembers me. Or he remembers my Pale Brood. One tiny rattle of the white linen bag and he was ready to kneel to me. And kneel he did. His terror was intoxicating. Funny how these humans fear their deaths. I do not understand it, for death is Glory. And inevitable.<br /> <br /> Though perhaps not for me.<br /> <br /> It is good that he has unknowingly continued the work I started. The people of this land have spent years of forced labour on \u2018building projects\u2019, digging for the lost relics that must be here. My followers assure me. I have wondered why they have not found anything in the intervening years since I last Awoke. Salroth Sar assures me that those years were spent planning and changing the people and the land to better suit his own ideals, my own ideals.<br /> <br /> I spoke through Pama Len the entire meeting, for the human peasants are not worthy enough to speak directly to me. I left Pama Len to watch over Salroth Sar and ensure that my work is being carried out.<br /> <br /> I will leave the capitol on the morrow and tour the sights of where the relics could be.<br /> <br /> The air is tense in this place. The people are afraid and this war over the border is coming closer to devouring this country. I must finish my search before then. Salroth Sar must remain in power long enough for me to find what a seek. I will not be caught up in these petty human wars. I serve a greater cause.<br /> <br /> Glory to the Su-Menent.<br /> <br /> Glory to Irem. <br /> <br /> <br /> October 1978<br /> <br /> These last few months have tried my patience. I can see the countryside of this spit of land is being worked by thousands, they do not call it slavery of the people. I do not see why not, slavery is a fine institution that has been the foundation of many empires. This \u2018forced labour\u2019 leaves a bitter taste in my mouth, however, the people are terrorised and there is much death so I console myself to the reason I am here. Namely serving my Judge Her-Uru.<br /> <br /> The sites upon which these \u2018projects\u2019 are carried out are where we expect to find the lost relics. But so far it has been a failure. Nothing has been found and I am beginning to feel an inkling of doubt. I will crush this emotion, I cannot afford to feel doubt. I must serve my Judge. I will find these relics.<br /> <br /> The only time this trip has been of worth was when I visited the mass graves. The burials may not seem proper but these people are of little consequence to me. I did however, make sure the graves were as geometrical as possible. I will let these people serve Irem and the Su Menent even in death.<br /> <br /> I return to the city with Pama Len now. He is certainly a faithful servant and surprisingly useful for a mortal. I will await news in the capitol for any relics.<br /> <br /> Glory to the Su Menent<br /> <br /> Glory to Irem <br /> <br /> November 1978<br /> <br /> The leaders of this country are tense. The war is progressing with the neighbouring land and it does not favour them in the slightest. I gather that there will soon be and invasion and the capitol will fall. I must find the relics before this happens.<br /> <br /> Salroth Sar still says he serves me but I am sceptical. He no longer seems as fearful as he once was. Even as I faintly rattle the Pale Brood he does not seem as shaken as before. Perhaps it is time for a demonstration. <br /> <br /> December 1978<br /> <br /> The fighting has escalated. The country is in chaos and this small nation of people has still not found my relics! I have taken my wrath out on some of their \u2018minor\u2019 government members so they will not get any ideas that they can defy me. I will not tolerate failure. Her-Uru will not tolerate failure.<br /> <br /> Pama Len is getting increasingly nervous. His family, my faithful servants, are encouraging me to leave. Cowards. I will not leave until I have my hands on these relics.<br /> <br /> I do not want to think too much on this but I suspect there may be another one of the Arisen encroaching on my territory. Perhaps even influencing Salroth Sar. Well, I will not allow it. I will investigate and any who think it is within their right to cross me will feel the full force of my power.<br /> <br /> Even as it wanes.<br /> <br /> My fury is cold. I will succeed in this task. <br /> <br /> December 1978<br /> <br /> We are leaving.<br /> <br /> It galls me but I have failed. Salroth Sar has failed. This entire venture has failed.<br /> <br /> Now I am fleeing, like a deer before the hunter, I disgust even myself. I was correct in my assumption that perhaps there was another power in play here.<br /> <br /> I saw him. In the capitol, in the very seat of my own power he thought to flaunt his own. Well, I will see how well he fares when I speak the words of power and the heavens shall answer with a flaming meteorite. I did not find his name but this Arisen will pay dearly for the strife he has caused me. And to add salt into the wounds he found some relics. Relics that should be MINE!<br /> <br /> He will suffer for this. Though I fear that I am not strong enough to fight him. My power grows weak and this impending war is something I do not wish to be involved in.<br /> <br /> Perhaps my next awakening will allow me the vengeance I wish for. <br /> <br /> January 1979<br /> <br /> I have arrived in the city of Jakarta. My servants accompanied me through the jungles and over the seas so that I may arrive safely. My rage is still potent from my failure. At least the other Arisen got what was coming to him. Though I ran afterwards, there is always something inherently satisfying about dropping a meteor onto one who has defied me.<br /> <br /> My servants have left me to settle on an island with another Arisen\u2019s family. I met them briefly and they offered me succour from the war. I suppose I should be thankful if I wasn\u2019t so furious.<br /> <br /> No matter though. I will soon end this miserable failure and sleep once again.<br /> <br /> I settled my new tomb in a graveyard, just off the Ciliwung River. It was suitable for a time but in hindsight it should have been somewhere where there wasn\u2019t a Choir of The Drowning Dead. How am I even meant to meditate? <br /> <br /> January 1979<br /> <br /> There are many Arisen in this city. I will have to tread carefully.<br /> <br /> The other cult members are suitable of my needs. Vania in particular seems worthy of my attention and she can also speak ancient Irennian (??). She seems an outcast. Perhaps I will convert her, not befriend her, just accept her into my service. Yes. She could be useful.<br /> <br /> I have met with my fellow Se Menent Yarikh and he seems\u2026 unremarkable.<br /> <br /> It seems I came very close to testing the ire of the city\u2019s most territorial Arisen: Mot- Tan. My tomb comes dangerously close to his territory and he almost called me out on it. But the only time I met him I seemed to see scorn and not a little bit of contempt in his eyes. It seems stories of my failure have spread, I would challenge him for his insolence but my power is very scarce.<br /> <br /> I will finish my descent soon\u2026<br /> <br /> I promise the next time I am Awoken I will not fail in my endeavours. I will crush any opposition. I will have my revenge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:45:49-07:00","id":222561,"title":"","content":"Ok, so a quick run-down of the second session.<br /> <br /> Kotira, the Mistress of Bones and Guildmaster of the Su-Menent, dispatched messengers to the characters to gather them at the city's Temple. Sesu Ra remembered helping use his political connections during his previous descent to help &quot;seal&quot; the temple and protect it from prying eyes. The protection turned out to be masquerading the Temple, a half-subsided pyramid structure, behind scaffolding and other construction apparatus. The characters gathered there and entered, passing the Temple Guardian. There they encountered all the Arisen currently awake in Jakarta. For ease of reference:<br /> <br /> Yama-Het of the Bloody Pen, Guildmaster of the Sesha-Hebsu. She looks barely older than sixteen or seventeen, and Aquila remembers dealing with her last descent as they allied to break the hold of organised crime over an area in west Jakarta.<br /> <br /> Yarikh, Speaker to the Thrice-Dead, a member of the Su-Menent. A tall, thin, ascetic fellow from Irem's North-Western territories, prefers to keep to himself. Sekhet Bastet was not overly impressed with him.<br /> <br /> Mot-Tan of the Rising Teeth, the only Maa-Kep in the city. The characters met him last session. Not very good at being a Maa-Kep, apparently, as he was pretty belligerent and tried to have his mortal wife enter the Temple with him.<br /> <br /> Finally, Kotira Nahan, the Mistress of Bones, entered the chamber by a secret entrance. It was clear that she had been awoken only hours before, she still sported the withered flesh of a high-Sekhem Mummy.<br /> <br /> They also heard that there were only four other Arisen in the city, still asleep. So we have eight NPC Mummies and three PCs, for a nome of 11.<br /> <br /> The Arisen were gathered to discuss this troubling incident involving mortals attempting to devour Arisen flesh. Sekhet Bastet found a soul-mate in her Guildmaster, Kotira, over their shared distaste for mortals. Although the group felt sure that they had destroyed the Faithful with their attack on the ship, they confessed that they couldn't be sure. The Mistress of Bones declared it the will of the Judges that any Faithful in the city be hunted down and slaughtered immediately. Aquila looked uncomfortable at that, thinking of Petro back on the islands.<br /> <br /> When the meeting ended the meret spent a few moments catching up with Arisen they remembered from their last descent, and then they departed. Sesu Ra retired to his tomb to turn his relic into a Talisman, deciding he had best conserve his Sekhem for now (dropped him to Sekhem 7, but still functionally 8) and storing manifestations of his Blessed is the God King and Chthonic Dominion Utterances. Aquila joined the rest at Sekhem 7.<br /> <br /> Luca was dispatched to try and rustle up some word of Faithful operations, and the group decided to focus on the disappearance of their hierophant, Richard Mayehi. Aquila and Sekhet Bastet combed the docks for clues. At one point they visited a police station to see if they could find out if anything of interest had been reported. Standing in the queue, Aquila had a brief memory of another time and place, of standing in chains in a line of slaves.<br /> <br /> Aquila eventually located a witness in the dock area who, after being persuaded, informed them that she'd seen Richard be taken by a group of men and hauled into a van with a logo on the side. The logo in turn led them to a ransacked grocery store, where they discovered blood, a necklace that Aquila recalled Richard wearing in her last Descent, and finally Richard's ghost. The ghost couldn't believe that it was dead, and spent a while gently traumatising Aquila by begging her to heal him. When they were finally able to get it to talk, Richard said he had been tortured but he couldn't remember what it was that he had told his captors. The group figured that this was likely how the Faithful had learned the location of their tombs.<br /> <br /> Still with no clues as to the identity of the torturers though, the mummies located the owner of the store. After a lot of intimidation he confessed that he'd heard one called &quot;Ditri&quot;, and that they'd rolled up to his store on motorbikes and threatened he and his family unless they cleared out and didn't return for the next week. Luca managed to use that and a physical description of the man to tell them that a few drug dealers in the nightclub district bought their product from a man with the same name and description. It being early evening at this point, the Arisen decided it was time to hit the town.<br /> <br /> A series of interrogations ensued as the group worked their way through the criminal network, using Sekhet Bastet's Fearsome Soul Affinity to break people quickly and discover who was next in the chain. Eventually, it was revealed that Ditri belonged to the Pelamat, the motorbike gang that had plagued Sesu Ra in his previous descent. This threw everyone a little, they weren't sure how this connected to the Faithful. Still, the obvious course of action was to kick the door down and interrogate, then execute, Ditri for his crimes against his Cult.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet, her inner eye still exposed from the fight on the dock, unleashed her demonic form as they arrived at the final location. She then phased through the door and found herself facing eight gangsters, while Aquila and Sesu Ra battered the door down. Sybaris from Bast promptly put six of the eight men out of the fight, and the last two went down quickly. Aquila then healed the injuries on Ditri (one of the two fighters) enough for him to be interrogated. Again, Fearsome Soul broke him quickly. He divulged a few interesting pieces of information.<br /> <br /> -The Pelamat had been ordered to kidnap Richard, interrogate him, and sell the information to an unknown third party (the description matched the Faithful leader the players killed last session).<br /> -He didn't know why they were ordered to interfere with Sesu Ra's plans, the orders came from higher up.<br /> -He reported to a boss named Rangarni.<br /> -The Pelamat knew some facts about Arisen. Not their nature, just that there were monsters from foreign lands out there, and that some of them had infiltrated the city.<br /> -The Pelamat were led by a woman. Ditri was terrified of her, but couldn't say much more than popular rumours of what she did to those who failed her (all grisly).<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra ordered Luca to inform the authorities that there were scoundrels lying incapacitated in this building. Luca made a phone call, and the group was about to leave. Bast, however, wasn't quite finished. She grabbed Ditri's head and spun it around until his neck broke. They all left together, Bast's Memory dropping to 2.<br /> <br /> We ended it there, and everyone fell to Sekhem 6 (functionally still 7 in Sesu Ra's case though). Not quite as exciting a session as the previous one. There were a few fun scenes, like Sesu Ra using Dominating Might and a khopesh to sheer through a door in a single blow to get at a Pelamat drug dealer. And Sekhet Bastet phasing through a door in her demon form and putting six out of the eight gangsters out of commission just from the sight of her was hilarious. And the premise, three Arisen trying to figure out why they killed all those people last time, was great to see in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T18:43:08-07:00","id":227472,"title":"","content":"Session 3<br /> <br /> Aquila began the session travelling back to the island to break the news of Richard's death to Ami. She stayed there a while, talking to her cultists and using Gift of the Golden Ankh to heal Phatri and boost her resistance to disease. She spoke to Petro, their captive Faithful initiate, and convinced him to follow her and keep close so that she could protect him from other Arisen in the city.<br /> <br /> After this, she returned to the city and visited her tomb for the first time. It is buried beneath a slum in East Jakarta, and the poverty and illness she witnessed on the way there broke her heart. She descended to her tomb, barely more than a closet built beneath a squatter dwelling, and tried to clear her mind to meditate. She hadn't been at it long, however, when she was attacked. Ami and a young man descended to the tomb and stabbed her as she lay in wait. Broken, bleeding, and nearly dead, Aquila used Dust Beneath Feet to hide underground. When she emerged, the wounds she thought she had been suffering were gone, there was no sign of either of her attackers, and she realised that she was now completely out of Pillars.<br /> <br /> Haunted Tombs can be a pain, basically.<br /> <br /> The rest of the group spent all this just resting and meditating, having agreed to meet at Sesu Ra's tomb the next morning. When they did so they were contacted by a cultist of Kotira's, and asked to come to the Temple. A room had been set up in a neighbouring building with a television to show some captured security footage, retrieved by Kotira's Cultists. Yama-Het was already there, watching it. It showed a hotel restaurant, mostly empty, just before Kotira and a pack of Nenitu burst through the front door and attacked a group of the guests. One, a European man, was killed while the other two fled. Sesu Ra realised that one of those that fled was the badly burned leader of the Faithful they had killed in the first session, a man he had watched burn and then seen lying dead on the bottom of the ocean. Aquila went outside to talk to Yama-Het, trying to find out how the gentrification of Yama-Het's territory was going.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet, however, was distracted by the third man. He was a South-East Asian man wearing a cowboy hat, and the sight of him triggered a flashback. She was in the jungle, decades ago, leading an attack on a ruined temple. American soldiers were fighting with the locals, and the sound of conflict was everywhere. She stumbled upon a scene at the centre of the temple and found three mortals feasting on an Arisen's remains (but she couldn't recall the identity of the Arisen). One of the men teleported away, using an ability remarkably similar to By Steps Unseen. Before he vanished she recognised him as a younger version of the man in the video footage. She fought and killed the other two, and it quickly became apparent that they were each demonstrating different Affinity-like powers.<br /> <br /> Next door, in the Temple, the group met with Kotira. She was speaking with an animate corpse, a man with the skull exposed on the right side of his face, but she stopped as they approached. The corpse of the dead man from the video was laid out on the table. The group tried to find out how she had tracked down the Faithful, and it turned out to be Kotira using Words of Dead Glory. The dead man, Kotira called him &quot;Makhet&quot;, had been created to seek out the Faithful. Kotira left one of his Passions up to Fate, which led him (and in turn, her) to the Hotel Shangri-la. They found the Faithful there, and attacked them.<br /> <br /> Yarikh was then called in to make use of Flesh-Culled Secrets so they could interrogate the corpse. The &quot;yes or no&quot; question aspect gave the players fits, but they found out a few things.<br /> <br /> -There are more than 10 Faithful in the city.<br /> -The Faithful do not know the location of any sleeping Mummies.<br /> -They do not currently have any Arisen on hand to devour.<br /> -This dead man was staying at the hotel.<br /> -He will return to life within the next two days.<br /> <br /> The group split here. Sesu Ra was far more interested in the Pelamat, and Aquila wanted justice for Richard, so they decided to pursue the lead they got last session about a warehouse where Rangarni, a local Pelamat boss, might be hiding. Bast preferred to pursue the Faithful, and went to the hotel Kotira had attacked to search the dead man's room. It was an interesting choice, with the social and investigative characters going off to fight while the combat character tried to perform an investigation.<br /> <br /> So, Kotira and Bast, with the help of Kotira's highly influential cultists, gained access to the hotel. Thanks to the retrieval of the tape, the effects of Sybaris, and a combination of bribes and judicious use of Veil of Forgetting, Kotira had managed to ensure that the hotel was running as per normal. No police, no heightened security, the two Mummies just strode through the front door and got in the lift. They had the dead man's room key, so they went up to room 603 and scoured the place for clues. Despite not being very good at the whole Investigation thing, Bast found the man's suitcase, broke it open, and discovered two important documents (which she couldn't read on account of only speaking the Old Tongue, but Kotira informed her that they were a passport in the name Curt Bolsworth and a book on articles of the faith for the Faithful).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Aquila and Sesu Ra were checking out a seemingly abandoned warehouse. Luca was sent around the back to kill anyone who tried to run. Aquila used the few Pillars she had managed to regenerate since the fight in her tomb to give Dust Beneath Feet to herself and Sesu Ra, and they attacked from below. The two men on the ground floor went down quickly (Sesu Ra actually killed one of them with a rather obscene dice roll, but put his faith in his Judge and passed his degeneration roll). More tried to attack, but Aquila activated her Mesen-Nebu affinity to armour herself in gold and Sybaris downed one and added a hefty penalty to the other two's attack rolls. The fourth and final man just folded his arms and watched.<br /> <br /> Aquila dodged past her attackers and rushed up the stairs towards the unaffected man. She found herself meeting a cold, unfeeling stare, and the words, &quot;You don't know what you are getting yourself into. Retreat and learn,&quot; seared themselves into her brain. She was compelled to back down the stairs and sink beneath the floor, and the speaker walked past Sesu Ra as he battled the two Pelamat and out the back door. Where he was promptly shot by Luca. Only a single bullet was fired, however, and despite an exceptionally high dice roll the man didn't seemed too badly affected. He walked up and spoke quietly to Luca for a moment, and Luca put his weapon away. The man then clambered onto a motorbike and drove away.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra finished off the Pelamat and turned on his allies, demanding to know why they let the man (he assumed he'd been the leader called &quot;Rangarni&quot; that they'd heard about) get away. After a bit of discussion they agreed that it seemed remarkably like the Voice of Conscience Affinity, forcing Aquila to act with Prudence. Then Luca added that the man hadn't bled when he was shot. Some kind of undead, they assumed, but they weren't sure what.<br /> <br /> With the discovery that the building held a large number of weapons and a small supply of drugs, Luca was dispatched to gather cultists and secure the area. Aquila and Sesu Ra returned to the temple, met up with Sekhet Bastet, and shared their information. They returned to the warehouse to oversee the cultists and make sure the surviving Pelamat could be interrogated. Luca met them there, a group of cultists in tow, and tried to quietly inform Sesu Ra that there was a leadership dispute unfolding back on the island and his leadership could be used. Bast and Aquila overheard though, and after a short argument the whole lot of them left Luca behind to oversee the cultists securing the warehouse and the Arisen all went back to their cult's home.<br /> <br /> A long argument unfolded on the boat ride home, spoken in the language of Irem so that the cultist driving the boat couldn't understand. As the group saw it, there were three potential leaders. Rom Mayehi, the brother of Richard (the dead former hierophant) and the warrior who had fought so successfully alongside them in the attack on the Faithful's boat in the first session, was the first. Sesu Ra advocated supporting him, and a lot of Tef-Aabhi truisms started to come up. &quot;Forsake no proven tool, rely on no unproven one,&quot; he said, saying that the Mayehi's had worked well in leading the Cult so far. &quot;What is worthy lasts, what lasts is worthy,&quot; came up when Aquila tried to argue that they should hold off on this for a few days until Richard had been properly mourned. Richard didn't last, he wasn't worthy, why bother any further with him? Bast liked this one. After saying it, Sesu Ra realised he was still carrying the necklace that served as Richard's ghost's anchor, which led to a slightly awkward moment.<br /> <br /> The others, in turn, each backed candidates from their own patron families. Bast supported Pama Lehn, her obedient follower since the days in Cambodia. Aquila put forward Ligo, Phatri's grandson, who had apparently been groomed for leadership since birth. Funnily enough, Rom, Pama, and Ligo were the three I had decided would be the ones arguing over the leadership when they arrived.<br /> <br /> Arriving on the island, the meret found it in chaos. Groups of squabbling cultists were yelling at one another all over the beach. Sure enough, at the centre of it all were Rom, Pama, and Ligo. Aquila silenced them, and told them to wait a few hours while a ceremony was performed mourning Richard's death.<br /> <br /> Bast tracked down Vania, the chronicler of the Families of the West. She was a bit of a social outcast, but had come into the village for the funeral/leadership debate. She laid out a rough overview of what each of the candidates stood for. This is basically the first example of how I'm handling the Cult in this game. In-game actions, rather than experience points, are used to expand and change it. Each of the three leadership candidates stood for a different benefit the Cult would gain:<br /> <br /> -Rom Mayehi led the warriors under his brother, and argued that this should be the focus of the Cult. The Faithful had attacked them, and the Families must respond in kind. Under his leadership, the Cult would get better warriors thanks to the Wrathful perk.<br /> -Ligo had been raised in the traditions of the Cult. He believed that keeping to the old ways would see them through. He would give the Cult the Ritualistic perk, helping their masters meditate.<br /> -Pama Lehn, true to form as the servant of Sheut Mummy, believed that there was nothing of worth mortals could accomplish on their own. Fighting and prayer were as nothing next to the power of their masters. The only thing the Families could do would be to subsume themselves before the mastery of the Arisen. He would give the Cult the Obedient perk.<br /> <br /> There were a couple of other potential candidates the players could have spoken to that may have provided different options, but they didn't bother. They retired one of the houses and summoned each potential leader to make a speech in turn. At the end they debated, and eventually settled on Rom Mayehi as the new hierophant. The vote was ultimately unanimous, although Aquila was a bit reluctant and disliked the militant nature it would lend to the Families.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Arisen emerged from seclusion and announced their decision to the Cultists. Rom Mayehi would lead from now on. We closed the session on that pronouncement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T23:50:06-07:00","id":227638,"title":"","content":"It has been quite a while since I tried doing write-ups of my game sessions, so if people have any comments or criticisms, please do tell me. I'm contemplating starting each write-up with a rundown of all the relevant non-player characters for the coming session at the start of each write-up, as I know it can be a bit hard to keep track when you're not actually playing the game. If you think that would help, just tell me and I'll be sure to do it in future.<br /> <br /> On another note, to anyone who has read Mortal Remains (thankfully, none of my players have), I'm sure it's quite clear that the Faithful are the Faithful of Shulpae. Since their rules were built on Hunter mechanics rather than for use as antagonists in Mummy, I decided for my game to change them to the following:<br /> <br /> -All Faithful are Witnesses.<br /> -Faithful can gain Affinities by devouring Arisen or Shuankhsen, or the bodies of dead Faithful. Usually only one Affinity per &quot;Feast&quot;.<br /> -They can have one Affinity per level of Status in the organisation. Their Status is used as if it were the relevant Pillar for that Affinity. For example, Guardian Wrath requires Status 2 (in place of Ka 2), and when defending their Temple or other Faithful the bonus rises from +2 to +Status.<br /> -To continue with the example above, any reference to a tomb generally becomes the Faithful Temple that the character belongs to. Generally speaking, any reference to &quot;cultists&quot; becomes &quot;lower Status Faithful&quot;.<br /> -Beast Soul Fury, and any other Affinity that changes how a Mummy spends Pillars, allows the Faithful to spend Willpower like Pillars in that particular case (so Beast Soul Fury enables a Faithful to buff their Strength and Stamina using Willpower as if they were a Sekhem 10 Mummy using Pillars).<br /> -They can't gain Guild Affinities, only Soul and Bane.<br /> -Arisen they eat have the same chance of being corrupted, as if they'd been eaten by one of the Shuankhsen.<br /> -From Status 3+, Faithful return to life 24 hours after being killed so long as their bodies are largely intact. They return on full health, but it costs them a dot of Stamina each time.<br /> -At Status 5, Faithful gain access to other magical powers. These may include Utterances, merits from Second Sight, or really anything else I feel is cool.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of corner-case Affinities that are strange and just don't apply to the Faithful (Entombed Glory springs to mind), but other than that it seems to work quite smoothly. They are, obviously, designed as antagonists rather than player characters, so I haven't payed too much attention to smoothing over any weird glitches that might occur from this adaptation. They've worked pretty well so far though.<br /> <br /> Just thought that might interest anyone wondering about the Faithful in this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T04:20:49-07:00","id":239019,"title":"","content":"Session four<br /> <br /> After declaring Rom Mayehi the Cult's new hierophant, the group remained on the island to oversee a celebration both in honour of Rom's new appointment and Richard's funeral. Sekhet Bastet was approached during the celebration by a cultist, who introduced himself as Izman Lehn. He told her about his duties working at a resort on a nearby island, where he was tasked with keeping an eye on a smuggling operation using the resort as cover. This smuggling group had apparently driven the Families away from controlling businesses and illegal activities that they had traditionally run in the region.<br /> <br /> The group decided that they should secure their own territory before they continued with their hunts for the Faithful and Pelamat. The next day, Izman escorted them all to the resort. As a staff member, he had a pass that allowed them to get in through security without a problem. Once inside Aquila sent Izman to fetch the resort's owner, Sesu Ra mingled with the guests, and Sekhet Bastet snuck away to try and find any evidence of criminal activity. Aquila seduced the resort's owner quite easily, but made a series of social blunders afterwards that meant she didn't uncover much information and ended up being escorted from the premises.<br /> <br /> Luckily, Sesu Ra had more success. With help from Izman, he discovered that a staff member named Ike was always on the night shift whenever a transfer of goods needed to take place, that there existed a middleman named Gorijo who oversaw the transfer, and that one of the guests had been complaining about members of the staff trying to foist packages on her. A chat with the latter, a young American tourist named Erica, led to him persuading her that he was an investigator. A quick search of her luggage revealed that items, including a handgun, had been secreted away within the lining of her bag.<br /> <br /> Izman informed the group that he was already friends with Ike, and that he would try to persuade the man to take him along the next time a trade took place. He would contact them when that happened. The group left, Aquila still fuming about how she'd been treated, and they headed back to the mainland.<br /> <br /> Each player spent the time waiting to look after some personal interests. Sekhet Bastet asked Sesu Ra for permission to use his Tomb to turn the Pale Brood into a Talisman. After a bit of hesitation he agreed, in return for her help in a future endeavour. He spent the next few hours marshalling the resources at his disposal. With the power of his own Relic granting him Status 5 inside his skyscraper, he set certain businesses within to gathering information from locations around the city.<br /> <br /> Aquila, meanwhile, returned to her tomb and meditated. Nothing suspicious happened, to everyone's surprise. She regained a few Pillars and then left to explore the surrounding slum, trying to find out as much about the situation there as she could. She eventually discovered that a group called the Sons of Gold Dust held sway, mainly by having control of the nearby residential complexes. If you don't cooperate with them, you find yourself living in a squatter's shelter in short order.<br /> <br /> Aquila resolved to make this gang do work for her, hoping to bring out the good in them and have them achieve good works at the same time. She located and approached one of the group's lieutenants at his home in the largest of the rundown apartment buildings. Unfortunately, when they turned down her offer, her anger got the better of her and she inflicted Sybaris on the group. The lieutenant, a man named Isok, and one of his men were unaffected. The others in the room all suffered variations on the &quot;collapse screaming and begging for mercy&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> It was at this point that it became apparent that the Sons of Gold Dust were a Mummy's Cult. Thinking themselves under attack, they decided to wake their master. Aquila felt the Sekhem flare, and decided to sit back and see how things developed. A few minutes latter, a Sekhem 10 Mummy strode into the room and absolutely demolished her in a fight. She escaped thanks to Dust Beneath Feet, dropping through the concrete building and hiding far beneath the ground. A bad first impression, for everyone concerned.<br /> <br /> Aquila fled back to the island. The others joined her there, but she chose not to share what had happened. After two days of waiting, Izman returned to say that he and Ike were rostered on to the night shift and Ike had asked him to help with some &quot;heavy lifting&quot;. The meret headed out that evening and prepared their trap.<br /> <br /> Aquila used Dust Beneath Feet to position herself underneath the ground close to the docks' entrance, which is where the players assumed the smuggler's vessel would come ashore. When Izman and Ike passed her, she planned to pop up and seal any escape by land. The others walked underwater Pirates of the Caribbean style, ready to climb up and onto the boat when it arrived. Unfortunately, they were spotted by someone aboard when the smugglers came in to land.<br /> <br /> A quick fight ensued. Sesu Ra struck the docks from below, sending Izman and Ike toppling into the water. Sekhet Bastet unleashed her demon form and sprinted across the water's surface and onto the boat. She knocked one man unconscious, turned a second one into a mummified corpse with Withering Judgement, and Sesu Ra seized the third man when he tried to make a swim for it. The group bundled everybody aboard this vessel, although they let Izman return to the resort to maintain his cover, and headed back to their own island.<br /> <br /> Once home, they interrogated the middleman, Gorijo. Sekhet Bastet used Luca as a translator, and quickly discovered that there were two groups of smugglers using the resort to trade contraband. One, based in the islands alongside their Cult, was led by a man named Reza. They brought items of interest into the area and traded them to the second group, based in Jakarta. This second group was a man named Kudava Jav, and Gorijo seemed quite scared of him.<br /> <br /> The group decided to take care of the Thousand Islands' operation first. Gorijo gave them the location of Reza's island, and the party headed there immediately. They faced off against Reza, a mountain of a man, and a group of his friends. Luca took advantage of his position as Sesu Ra's Sadikh and unleashed the third tier of Blessed is the God King. The appearance of a bull-headed avatar quickly cowed (I am so, so sorry) the smugglers. Some conversation and a series of solid Intimidation rolls by Aquila persuaded the smugglers to merge with the players' Cult. The Cult gained a point of Grasp, and they secured control over their home territory.<br /> <br /> Later, Aquila returned to the Temple for some meditation. She was confronted there by Yama-Het, Kotira, and a new Mummy named Sem-Huf. It quickly became apparent that he had been raised to destroy her, and was keeping himself from doing so only due to the sacred ground of the Temple. Despite being a journeyman of the Mesen-Nebu, and thus technically subordinate to Aquila, he clearly felt that his duty to the Judges came first. Swearing to strike her down, he stormed out.<br /> <br /> Talking to Kotira afterwards, Aquila discovered that Kotira had been filling the newly woken Mummy in on the Faithful situation in the city. Apparently, Curt Bolsworth, the slain Faithful soldier from the hotel, had returned to life earlier that morning. Kotira's cultists had extracted all the important information that they could, including the fact that the two men he'd been meeting with were the highest ranking Faithful in the city. Kotira then had him burned to death.<br /> <br /> Aquila remained at the Temple after everyone left. She needed to replenish her Pillars again after the attack on the smugglers, and felt that returning to her Tomb was unwise given that it sat next door to Sem-Huf's. When she eventually left the Temple she was met by her cultist Ligo. He informed her, barely fighting back the tears, and they had discovered his uncle impaled on a stake in front of her Tomb. Aquila was certain that Sem-Huf was involved, so she located the other members of her meret and informed them that they had a new enemy waging war against their Cult.<br /> <br /> And we ended it there. Aquila's impulsiveness drew a fair amount of exasperation from the other players, both in-character and out-of-character. But hey, it was all entirely in keeping with an Ab Mummy's behaviour. We'll see how the face-off with a higher Sekhem Mummy plays out in the next session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T06:24:11-07:00","id":242208,"title":"","content":"I should mention at this point that we have begun to dip, ever so slightly, into spoilery territory here. If you're a Mummy player and don't want any of the setting's secret stuff revealed, I'd suggest not reading this particular recap.<br /> <br /> Session 5<br /> <br /> The issue with Sem-Huf was preying on everyone's minds. Sesu Ra and Sekhet Bastet decided to pay him a visit without Aquila. They made it clear that attacks on their cultists would raise their ire, but that until then it was between Aquila and him. He, in turn, handed down a message. If Aquila surrendered herself to his judgement before midnight, he would destroy her a single time and declare their feud ended. Otherwise, it would spend the rest of his Descent seeking her destruction.<br /> <br /> Bast and Sesu Ra went from here to continue the hunt for the Faithful. They went back to the hotel where they had last seen members of the group, and after a bit of digging turned up a description and license plate of the vehicle the escaping Faithful had been driving. A few corrupt cops and other such contacts later, and they were able to track the car to a residential home in the north side of the city. Naturally, it turned out to be a trap. The house was set alight, but the Mummies simply leapt from an upper store building. Luca used Blessed Is The God King, and quickly tore his opponent apart. Bast summoned a meteor and downed the other as he ran. They then stopped the man from dying at the last moment, and dragged him back to the island for interrogation.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet informed Aquila of Sem-Huf's offer. When Aquila made it clear that she had no intention of giving herself up, an argument between the pair unfolded. Finally, Bast pulled out her Pale Brood and whispered Petro's name into it. Shocked and appalled, Aquila ran to find her servant Faithful and found him, apparently unharmed, in his hut. Bast then left to tell Sem-Huf that Aquila had turned down his generous offer, and to reiterate that he should stay away from their joint cultists.<br /> <br /> Aquila resolved to stick by Petro's side every moment of the day to try and prevent the Pale Brood's curse from coming into effect. In the meantime, she healed the Faithful captive the players had just brought in and persuaded him to implicate Sem-Huf as being involved in supporting the Faithful. Unfortunately, when Bast returned and interrogated him a short time later, her Fearsome Soul Affinity ensured that he broke so thoroughly all thoughts of lying fled his mind. Bast then executed the man, after learning that only the Faithful's Grandmasters were left alive from the Faithful cell they had encountered. The masters were named Xan and Tset Lehn. The latter caused a bit of consternation, and Pama Lehn was summoned to be asked if a member of the Cult may have gone rogue. He claimed not to know the name, and the group focussed on their final lead. A nearby mangrove swamp was home to a secret temple. The masters had fled there.<br /> <br /> The meret resolved to prepare themselves and then strike at the masters. Aquila went ashore, accompanied by Petro. Sem-Huf, dressed in full Iremite regalia and accompanied by his cultists, confronted them there before they could reach the shore and a solid, earthen ground for Aquila to use as an escape route. Before anyone could speak, he unleashed the third tier of Power of Re. Every mortal around was blinded, Petro (fulfilling the curse of the Pale Brood) was immediately turned into a screaming pillar of salt and ash, and Aquila barely closed her eyes in time. She threw herself at Sem-Huf in her rage, but he was able to do an enormous amount of damage through a ludicrously good attack roll, driving his spear deep into her body. Panicking, Aquila decided to escape. She didn't manage it in time. Sesu Ra unleashed the Power of Re one more time. She saw a bright white light, and then entered a Death Cycle.<br /> <br /> In the in-between realm that separates Duat and the living world, Aquila's soul found itself lost. In the form of a half-woman, half-lioness, she wandered the twisting paths of Neter-Khertet. A funeral dirge led her to a crossroads, spiralling away in every direction. She was lost, and despite the Rite of Return riveting her to the living world, she had no idea how to make the final leg of the journey.<br /> <br /> And then a god appeared to her. Anpu, the Jackal-headed Ferryman, judged her with eyes that saw even her immortality as just a short moment in eternity. Without a word he handed her an iron lantern, and the path before her became clear. She continued on, knowing the way now, and Anpu disappeared.<br /> <br /> To reach the living world, Aquila had to pass through a long-buried memory. In 1940, she and a much-young Phatri were discussing the completion of a stone prison somewhere in the Thousand Islands. After a short while Aquila entered this buried prison (passing through the wall using Dust Beneath Feet). Inside, she found Sesu Ra and another Mummy. Sesu Ra had just arrived in Indonesia, fleeing from the United States. His Pillars were in ruins and his Memory absolutely shattered. As far as Aquila could tell, he had destroyed his own Memory and wanted to lose the last vestiges of it to rid himself of the knowledge of something he had encountered, but refused to speak of. The Unbending Spine had refused to bend, and so he had been broken instead. Aquila had decided to take him in, both out of compassion and because he was liable to commit an act of mass murder to burn away that last bit of Memory if he wasn't confined somewhere.<br /> <br /> As for the second Mummy, he was already at Memory 0, and had been sealed away until some humanity returned to him (this is going to be our new player, who will be introduced properly next session).<br /> <br /> Acceding to Sesu Ra's wishes, Aquila and Luca eventually tracked down something from Sesu Ra's mortal life. Something he could destroy, and thus rid himself of the last of his Memories. Luca quietly told Aquila that he had born witness to something that must never be revealed to his master. In fact, his master had compelled him to tell no soul of what had transpired. Aquila resolved that, next descent, she would try and nurse him back to a more stable position. She eventually used some contacts to obtain a stele that seemed to be some work of Sesu Ra's, and delivered it to him to be destroyed. He did so, ridding himself of whatever haunted him and rendering himself a Memory 0 Mummy.<br /> <br /> Aquila's final memories were of making sure that the information on Sesu Ra's stele were recorded before he destroyed the item. She handed the recording to Phatri for safe keeping, telling her to return the document only when Aquila asked for it.<br /> <br /> And then Aquila returned to life. She dropped to Sekhem 4 as a result of the Death Cycle. Her body had been destroyed by the Power of Re, so she reformed in her tomb around one of her organs. She stayed there and meditated on what she had learned, restoring a few pillars. There was a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Sekhet Bastet continued their pursuit of the Faithful. They teamed up with someone called Mr Black, a security contractor hired by an unknown third party (he was a pregenerated character I whipped up in a hurry for our new player to play until we figured out what his Mummy character would be like). Those three, alongside Luca, travelled deep into the mangrove swamp and located the temple. They were attacked there by the two Faithful masters. Bast suffered a lot of Aggravated damage when she was struck with a flaming torch by the man in the cowboy hat, who she now knew was Tset Lehn. Seeing the man face-to-face for the first time triggered a brief flashback, and she realised that decades ago he had been a hierophant of her Cambodian cult. He turned traitor, joined the Faithful, and then attacked her to destroy her tomb and any evidence of the Faithful's existence.<br /> <br /> The fight ended in short order after that, thanks to some lucky rolls on the players' part. Bast was able to mummify Tset Lehn and then dispatch him. The other master, the burned man from the ship who they only knew as Xan, fought Luca and Mr Black. Two solid pistol rounds to the chest, and a lot of very high dice rolls, put him in the ground. The players built a pyre and stayed to ensure that the corpses were charred properly.<br /> <br /> They then returned to the Temple, and asked for Kotira. When she arrived they announced the good news. The Faithful cell was destroyed, there were no more left and they wouldn't be coming back. Kotira congratulated them, and enquired as to where Aquila was. The two Arisen realised that they hadn't seen her in a while. Bast announced that it was time for her to withdraw in contemplation. Her mission in the living world was now complete.<br /> <br /> And with that, the session ended. The opening Faithful arc was tied up nicely, everyone with any serious power destroyed and burned to dust. Our first Death Cycle was immensely interesting, providing insight into a part of the meret's history that no one knew about. Unfortunately, Sekhet Bastet's player leaves us for six months at this point. I'm certainly hoping to still be running this game by the time she gets back, though, so hopefully this isn't the last of her. And at least we got the Faithful out of the way before she left.<br /> <br /> We have a new player joining us in her place, however. At some point in the next week we'll get around to hashing out his character. New Mummies are always so much fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T00:21:58-07:00","id":244613,"title":"","content":"Ok, our newest player has just finished character creation. Won't actually be playing our next game for a few days yet, but the new guy is as follows:<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, the Fog of Torment - A journeyman of the Su-Menent and a member of the Ren Decree, Akenakhi has long been disillusioned with the Judges. He has pursued heretical knowledge for as long as he can remember, in secret and without the knowledge of his guildmates. Even Sekhiru, his Judge, appears to be unaware of his intent. He appears to be a thin young man from modern day Syria, and is usually a quiet and reserved individual. His main skills lie in research and gathering lost information, but centuries of pursuing forbidden knowledge have given him quite a talent for lying.<br /> His last memories involve a Descent in France during the Great War, of his entire Cult being lost in the fighting, and a time spent wandering the Earth in despair. He can't recall how he ended up in Jakarta, but when our next game begins he will be waking for his Sothic Turn inside a stone prison built for him by Aquila some 70 years ago. He has a Haunted Tomb somewhere in the city, built beneath a well-to-do restaurant.<br /> His Affinities are Beast Companion, Blessed Panoply, and Fated Soul, and his Utterances are Obedient Clay, Palace Knows Its Pharaoh, and Revelations of Smoke and Flame. He has access to Tier 2 in all of them when the game begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T18:00:39-07:00","id":250255,"title":"","content":"Session 6<br /> <br /> Aquila purchased a dot of Memory at the end of last session, so I ran a brief flashback for her to kick off this session. She remembered being in China around 1900. There was a confrontation between her Cultists and colonial forces. She tried to force the Europeans to back down, but then she heard someone shouting orders at them. A Cultist brought her a weapon, a Roman Gladius that whispered to her as she drew it from its sheath. And then everything ended in blood.<br /> <br /> In the present, Aquila decided she needed to rally help for her struggle against Sem-Huf. Sesu Ra didn't appear to be all that interested, but she was able to persuade Luca to help her in return for not mentioning whatever it was that had broken Sesu Ra so badly back in the 40s. It was clear that Luca remembered the events perfectly, and he was quite troubled at the threat. Aquila then decided to go and wake Akenakhi and remove him from the prison she remembered building for him. She stole a boat (no sign of any Cultist driving one, their last had just been killed a few hours back by Sem-Huf) and travelled out to the island. There she was attacked there by the lion-headed bull creature they had last seen in the first session. Still healing from her resurrection, Aquila burned through all of her pillars in short order in an effort to get away. She barely made it, and ended up underground without any pillars left at all. She waited there for a little while, letting the lethal wounds heal, and then realised her mistake. Dust Beneath Feet had worn off, she was out of Pillars, and she was buried underground without any way to move.<br /> <br /> Not too far away, inside his tomb, Akenakhi was woken for his Sothic Turn. He found himself trapped beneath the ground inside a collapsing old tomb. After spending some pillars to destroy chunks of the wall to try and find a way to escape, he ended up being able to smash his way up through the ground (Sekhem 10 Mummies can do that kinda thing) and found himself on a deserted island and no idea how he came to be here. He vaguely remembered coming to Jakarta in his last descent, but that was it. Disorientated and confused, he was attacked by the jackal-headed snake monster and drained of his remaining pillars. The creature then disappeared.<br /> <br /> And then things got silly. Trapped underground as she was, Aquila needed to meditate to regain at least one Pillar point before she could get back to the surface. Not too much of an issue. She was Memory 4, so it should be easy enough to just wait an hour and then emerge.<br /> <br /> <i>Five days passed.</i><br /> <br /> Sesu Ra spent the time carrying out some investigations and trying to expand the Cult's operations in West Jakarta. At some point he was alerted by the Cult that Aquila had gone missing. Hearing about an incident at the docks, he went to speak to Sem-Huf. The two were puzzled about Aquila's complete disappearance. Sem-Huf confessed readily enough that he had attacked her and destroyed her body, but she should still be out there in some form or another. In the end, they agreed she's probably become scared and run away.<br /> <br /> During this, Sesu Ra saw a news report of Jakarta's National Monument. Someone had tagged it with an Iremite phrase, &quot;It will end&quot;. The sight triggered a flashback of standing alongside another Mummy named Rekhenaten, a fellow Tef-Aabhi. The two Mummies were watching the beginnings of construction at the monument's site. Sesu Ra remembered telling Rekhenaten that this building would be the key.<br /> <br /> He decided that this warranted waking Rekhenaten. The man's opulent tomb was at the centre of a golf course and country club on the outskirts of the city. Security was heavy, but the staff recognised Sesu Ra and let him enter without any obstacles. A conversation with one of Rekhenaten's priests persuaded him that the other Mummy needed to be woken.<br /> <br /> The conversation with Rekhenaten didn't yield much. Having just crawled from his tomb, Rekhenaten was effectively Memory 0 and had to make rolls just to remember who Sesu Ra was. The conversation wrapped up quickly with Rekhenaten saying he didn't know who might be behind the graffiti, but that it sounded like the Pelamat might be a likely suspect. He had no idea who they were or what they were up to, however. Sesu Ra was about to leave when Rekhenaten mentioned that he intended to return to henet shortly. Apparently, the other Mummy's Sothic Turn was fast approaching, and he did not wish to be mid-descent when it arrived.<br /> <br /> Finally, after throwing more than 20 dice at the attempt, Aquila scored a single success on a Meditation roll, activated Dust Beneath Feet, and rose from the ground to find Akenakhi waiting for her up above. Aquila explained that they were in Jakarta, it was the year 2012, and that they were allies. The two went back to the city. Akenakhi found that he had a tomb in the city, but that someone had built a restaurant on top of it.<br /> <br /> Aquila spent the rest of the session (we wasted quite a lot of time laughing over those meditation attempts) gathering together her allies. She brought Rom and two other Cultists over from the island, recruited Luca and Reza, and then sought out Yama-Het. She was looking for advice on how to tackle Sem-Huf. A Cultist brought Aquila to a community centre where Yama-Het had apparently made her base, and she spoke with the other Guildmaster briefly on the subject. The Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster suggested they meet the next night, at the centre, to discuss plans.<br /> <br /> Finally, Sesu Ra contacted Aquila and asked for her help with an important matter. He wanted to see if his old bypass project could be put back on track. They approached the construction site, which looked long-abandoned, at sunset. After exploring the area for a little while, they encountered Buk. The phenomenally powerful ghost hurled them into the fence encircling the site. Sesu Ra tried to gather what it was that Buk wanted, but only got the response that the ground was sacred. Aquila was on the verge of dying, and fled. Sesu Ra, taking a powerful telekinetic attack every turn, stayed long enough to ask a few questions. It seemed like Buk was perfectly willing to talk about itself, so long as whoever it was speaking to was able to withstand its attacks long enough to receive an answer. It wasn't long before Sesu Ra left the area as well, although at a more dignified pace.<br /> <br /> And that was where we ended it. I think we would have managed to get a lot more done if we hadn't spent so much time laughing at Aquila's player over those dice rolls, but hey, it was funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T22:33:06-07:00","id":255058,"title":"","content":"Session 7<br /> <br /> Aquila's allies gathered at Yama-Het's community centre the next night. She brought Luca, Reza, Rom, Izman, Ligo, Akenakhi, and Yama-Het along in order to hear their thoughts on her plans, and laid out her idea on how to get rid of Sem-Huf. She wanted to carry out a bank robbery, call in a bomb threat, leave evidence that Sem-Huf and his Sons of Gold Dust were behind it, and thus trick the authorities into raiding Sem-Huf's tomb. Ideally, she hoped to see him led away in chains, giving her a chance to raid his tomb and steal his canopic jars and relics. Well...<br /> <br /> Rom liked it. He suggested mounting an assault on the tomb to clear up any cultists that might not have been caught in the raid. Aquila shot him down, the point of the plan was to try and remove Sem-Huf without further bloodshed.<br /> <br /> Luca and Reza, the hardened criminals in attendance, weren't too fond of the idea. Involving the authorities just seemed far too likely to backfire. There was always a chance that the authorities could trace things back to the players or their cultists in some way. They preferred trying to work something out with Sem-Huf, some kind of arrangement that could lead to a ceasefire. Ligo supported them on this.<br /> <br /> Izman was tentatively in favour, but said that they had far too little information on the Sons to be sure that this plan would work. Odds were high, for example, that they knew cops who might leak plans for a raid to the Sons in return for a bribe. He said that they needed to gather more information, and ideally plant a mole inside the group.<br /> <br /> Yama-Het was really, really uneasy about the whole affair. Two Mummies fighting to the death in the streets is one thing, it doesn't do much more than temporarily inconvenience the loser. Attacking cultists is a pretty nasty escalation, but understandable under the circumstances. But actually entering another's tomb? Taking his canopic jars? That threatened a Mummy's continued existence. That was something only done to the vilest heretics. She urged Aquila to reconsider.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi revealed that he would quite like to seize control of Sem-Huf's cult. He said he would prefer some kind of arrangement that removed Sem-Huf from the equation, but left the Sons reasonably intact so that he could take control. The fact that he was the only character without a dedicated family appeared to be weighing on him. He also said he had no interest in carrying out a bank robbery.<br /> <br /> The meeting ended with Aquila declaring that she still believed that this was the right thing to do, and the group went their separate ways. The cultists returned to the island, while Luca, Aquila, and Akenakhi travelled to the Temple. There they found Sesu Ra, and a middle-aged Japanese man wearing a sharp business suit who they did not recognise.<br /> <br /> While the meeting had been dragging on, Sesu Ra had been meeting with Rekhenaten. The other Tef-Aabhi's Memory had been returning to him since he woke, and was now at a considerably more useful level than the Memory 0 he had been when he first arose. He said that he remembered Sesu Ra asking him to help briefly with a project in the Old Dutch Quarter several descents ago, something connected to the National Monument. Although he had to attend to a few final matters before he returned to henet, Rekhenaten lent his Sadikh, a Japanese man currently going by the name &quot;Tobi&quot;, to the cause.<br /> <br /> The group came together at the temple and agreed to help Sesu Ra discover, well, whatever it was that he'd been up to there. Sesu Ra questioned Luca to see if any of his, ahem, &quot;ancestors&quot; remembered this experiment, but Luca told him that he couldn't remember anything about it. The group hired some taxis and drove over. Almost immediately, Sesu Ra recognised that the area had been deliberately constructed to channel heka between two particular buildings. They were driving to where he predicted the first of these should be when Aquila spotted two men she recognised from their first confrontation with the Pelamat. The group got out of the cars and, thanks to the crowded streets, tailed the pair until they ducked down an alley. It turned out the Pelamat had been stalking someone themselves, and after the group quickly dealt with them (two mortals not really putting up much of a fight against two Sadikh and three Mummies) they met a man named Hendry who recognised Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> Hendry exclaimed, to everyone's confusion, that the cabal had continued to serve Sesu Ra's wishes over the decades. The holy texts he had given them continued to guide them, and the ritual was growing close to completion. He offered to take them to the high priest, Banek, and the group eagerly accepted.<br /> <br /> They were brought to an old, crumbling Dutch townhouse, and Sesu Ra could tell that this was one of the two important points in the region's geometry. Hendry claimed it was the cabal's temple, and the site of the ritual. They met Banek, a man with tattoos that resembled Iremite phrases cutting across his face. He explained that Sesu Ra had gathered them together to serve Manfred Schuss, a man he claimed was Sesu Ra's avatar. At the name, Sesu Ra had a momentary image of a desiccated corpse with a hole bored between its eyes. They were approaching the end of the ritual, but Banek could not properly explain what the ritual actually was. He claimed that its purpose had been kept secret by Sesu Ra when he established the cabal, and that they worked to complete the great working without any true understanding of what they were doing.<br /> <br /> Another piece of information emerged. Apparently, the Pelamat (Banek didn't know the name, but the group figured out who they were pretty quickly) had begun stalking other members of the cabal over the last week. Hendry was simply the latest in a line of victims found beaten bloody in back alleys.<br /> <br /> Well. Sesu Ra decided that this was clearly Tef-Aabhi business, and decided to get rid of the rest of the meret. He asked them, ever-so-sweetly, to return to the city centre and watch over the National Monument. After all, he reasoned, if the Pelamat were attacking Tef-Aabhi works in the city, then the linchpin would no doubt be in danger. In the meantime, he would stay and watch over matters here. The others acquiesced, and once they were gone Sesu Ra asked a few more probing questions about the &quot;ritual&quot;.<br /> <br /> To, really, no one's surprise, it turned out to involve human sacrifice. Unworthy men and women were delivered to Manfred, he killed them, and the energy from their deaths flowed through the streets guided by the arcane geometry of the district. A &quot;gateway&quot; stood at the other end, and would be forced open when the ritual reached its conclusion in three nights' time. Only three more sacrifices and the fifty year project would be complete.<br /> <br /> Banek then ordered Hendry to &quot;resume his post&quot;. Hendry, as it turned out, worked as a janitor at a museum of the VOC's occupation of Jakarta. From the conversation, Sesu Ra gathered that some kind of effigy was stored there and used to provide security for the cabal.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra, Luca, and Tobi stood guard that night. After a few hours, several blank-faced men and a rotting, zombie-like creature assaulted the building. They were driven back easily enough, the zombie-creature escaping and the others being dispatched without much bother. Sesu Ra earned a Descent Reset for killing one of them, apparently counting as those who commit crimes out of &quot;need or necessity&quot;. Banek announced that the sacrifice had been performed in the building's basement while the fighting took place, and secured a few of the still-breathing combatants to be sacrificed over the next two nights.<br /> <br /> Still trying to work out what the point of all this was, Sesu Ra decided to explore the area. After leaving the building, he was approached by a young boy who claimed his grandfather had told him to tell Sesu Ra that &quot;the experiment had gone awry&quot;. An old man named Jonas lived on the opposite side of the street to the temple. He told Sesu Ra that he was the only member of the cabal that still held the faith, that the others had been corrupted by Manfred and the ritual perverted. When Sesu Ra demanded proof, Jonas could only say that when he refused to swear loyalty to Manfred, the cabal cast him out. Sesu Ra did not consider this sufficient evidence and left, but not before telling Luca to remain behind and milk Jonas for all the information he could find.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra then travelled to the &quot;gateway&quot;, finding his way by the architecture and where his knowledge told him such geometry must lead. He found a row-house, which looked unoccupied from the outside, and entered it. The front door posed little resistance, and he found his way into a cellar where the walls were marked in Iremite scrawl. Down there, he five inverted obelisks, evenly spaced around a central point. Part of him knew that each obelisk represented a pillar of the soul, but he struggled to work out what the arrangement was meant to achieve. When he looked at the set-up under the light of Chthonic Dominion, he saw lines of pale fire running between each of the obelisks to form a pentagram. After a bit of thought, he decided that nothing looked out of place and returned to the cabal's temple.<br /> <br /> In the basement of the temple, he found a partly buried corpse of a long-dead European man. When he used Chthonic Dominion, the light revealed a distinguished gentleman dressed in a manner reminiscent of the 18th Century, who introduced himself in halting English as Manfred Schuss. Sesu Ra questioned him, trying to work out whether what Jonas had said had any truth to it, and only came to the conclusion that Manfred was eager to finally complete the project he had been working on for decades. He decided to wait there in the basement to watch the next night's ritual, and to keep an eye out for any sign of wrong-doing.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Akenakhi split up, having spent the night watching the National Monument without incident. Aquila returned to the island to speak to her cultists, and Akenakhi went to his tomb to meditate. Before he did so, he checked in on the restaurant above his tomb. Having picked up Indonesian recently, he could now read the sign, which just said &quot;Dartlan's&quot;. He went inside, and was met by a waiter who told him that the place was closed so early in the morning. Akenakhi shrugged, went downstairs, and tried to meditate.<br /> <br /> About ten minutes later, he heard footsteps on the stairs. The waiter from the restaurant walked in, looked at him, and attacked. The man's skin peeled off, organs unravelled, bones twisted and muscles reshaped themselves to turn the mortal into a gory monster. It threw itself at Akenakhi, who called upon the first tier of Revelations of Smoke and Flame to fight off the beast. It was a frenzied battle, forcing Akenakhi to seal his flesh and burn through most of his pillars to finish it off. When the creature finally collapsed, it reverted back to the unconscious form of the waiter, near to death. Akenakhi was able to keep the man from dying, and then gently removed him from his tomb and placed him in the streets outside his tomb when no one was looking. Thoroughly freaked out, he sealed the entrance to his tomb again and kept watch.<br /> <br /> Aquila, meanwhile, had returned to the island to find that several cultists hadn't woken up that morning. Phatri was the first, but there was also Pama Lehn's daughter and a few others. They appeared to be in comas, and none of her magical abilities appeared to be enough to wake them. She did find a few dead centipedes around, however. And that was when the jackal-headed winged snake-thing attacked her again.<br /> <br /> The following fight took a while. Aquila tried to use Soul Infusion to render the creature unconscious, but it didn't appear to care. Following that, she beat it quite severely, and it began to bleed centipedes. Mystery solved, but it phased away into Twilight when Aquila burned out the last of her Pillars.<br /> <br /> On the mainland, Sesu Ra witnessed the second-to-last element of the ritual. One of the captured men from the previous night was dragged into the basement and executed by Manfred's animated corpse. A surge of energy rippled through the district, but again, from Sesu Ra's limited understanding, the ritual appeared to be going correctly. Manfred returned to his grave, and we wrapped the session up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T08:14:54-07:00","id":255325,"title":"","content":"Oh man, Sesu Ra is going to wait until it's way too late isn't he...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T17:28:48-07:00","id":255682,"title":"","content":"His current thinking appears to be along the lines of, &quot;I have enough faith in myself to have set this up properly the first time I did it. There's no real evidence that anything wrong is going on. Let's see how this pans out.&quot;<br /> <br /> So... yeah. Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T21:15:47-07:00","id":255806,"title":"","content":"I looooove reading these posts. Such fun to see a different STs use of themes. Im eager to see what happens when the ritual is completed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T22:44:19-07:00","id":255850,"title":"","content":"Cheers mate, I'm glad you're enjoying the write-ups. We're really enjoying this campaign. I don't think I've ever seen my players so engaged with their characters before, and Mummy is a joy to GM for. I don't know, something about the Memory system seems to ensure everyone involved is a lot more interested in who the characters are (and who they were) than the norm, a lot more invested than they would be with any grand over-arching plot or anything.<br /> <br /> We'd have to get seriously side-tracked next session to not discover what is up with the ritual, so you should be satisfied on that count within the week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 09-13-2014, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T06:42:24-07:00","id":259734,"title":"","content":"Session 8<br /> <br /> This session was rather skewed. By which I mean was that this session saw Sesu Ra be declared the game's protagonist, with everyone else just filling supporting roles. His decision to exclude the others from Tef-Aabhi Guild Business meant he was off by himself doing active and exciting things for most of the session, which took up a lot of time. Just thought I would preface this with that. It was a seriously big session for him, less so for everyone else.<br /> <br /> We started with the session with Aquila returning to the mainland after her encounter with the jackal-headed beast. She went to the Temple, and found Mot-Tan meditating there. The reclusive Maa-Kep revealed he had left his territory to meet with Sem-Huf to discuss an issue arising in both their lands. After a bit of questioning, Aquila discovered that someone had killed one of Mot-Tan's cultists and implicated the other Mesen-Nebu in the act. However, upon further investigation, Mot-Tan found it was a lie. The actual perpetrator had been a third party, someone unknown, trying to provoke a war between Mot-Tan and Sem-Huf.<br /> <br /> At this, Aquila decided to recount the story of her conflict with Sem-Huf. When she reached the part about one of her cultists, a man named Ahumara and one of Ligo's uncles, being found staked outside her tomb, Mot-Tan interrupted her to ask if she were sure Sem-Huf was responsible. Aquila realised that she hadn't ever had any definitive proof of guilt, just having assumed it was Sem-Huf due to their conflict. Troubled by this, she asked Mot-Tan to question Sem-Huf about it, and then left quickly before her enemy showed up.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, meanwhile, was trying to proselytise to the mortals running the restaurant above his tomb. When the owner, a Mrs Dartlan, didn't seem to be taking him seriously, he unleashed the second tier of Revelations of Smoke and Flame. The resulting Terror Sybaris sent her and all of her staff fleeing the building. Not the greatest start. He then met up with Aquila, and they decided to try and work out a plan for the bank heist they'd been planning.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra waited through the day for nightfall. He was informed by Banek, the leader of the local cabal, that the Pelamat had been spotted entering the district with a lorry and a few motorbikes, presumably preparing for one last attempt at ending the ritual. Banek mentioned something about &quot;the guardians&quot; and how the cabal would bring them over to help with the defence. With Luca and Tobi besides him, Sesu Ra prepared for a fight inside the ritual chamber. Sure enough, just as the ritual was due to begin, the Pelamat attacked.<br /> <br /> There was the sound of fighting in the house above. It dragged on for quite some time. Finally, there were footsteps on the stairs. Banek came into view, saying that the guardians couldn't hold them off, and then a group of blank-faced construction workers, squatters, and other assorted people surged down the stairs with makeshift weapons in their hands. Luca picked up his rifle and gunned down three in a spray of automatic weapon fire, but the survivors seemed unfazed and threw themselves at the defenders. With the others distracted, the rotting, disfigured man from the previous attack appeared and charged Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> The fight was brief and exceptionally deadly. Everyone was rolling ludicrously well. Sesu Ra found himself nearly maxed out on lethal damage despite sealing the flesh, and largely survived his fight by using Dominating Might to keep his disfigured opponent knocked to the ground. Luca shot his opponents dead and came over to help. Tobi and Banek each killed a man. Finally, there was only the disfigured attacker left. Blow after blow rained down on him, but he kept struggling back to his feet. Luca picked up the sacral blade used to perform the sacrifices and lopped off one of the man's arms, but he continued unflinching. Finally, Sesu Ra pinned the creature to the ground and Luca drove the blade through its chest, and it lay still.<br /> <br /> At that point, Manfred possessed his corpse and walked towards the weapon. Sesu Ra decided that he couldn't risk the ritual being corrupted, and tried to ask Manfred to stop. The ghost pointed out that he had been given a command that he could not disobey, a command to perform the ritual. With that in mind, Sesu Ra punched Manfred and knocked him to the ground (Dominating Might is just amazing), tossed the sacral blade to Luca, and commanded him to execute one of the survivors of the attack. Luca did so.<br /> <br /> Luca lost two points of Morality and gained a derangement as a result of all this, I would like to add.<br /> <br /> As the blade claimed a mortal's life, Sekhem roared through the whole of the Old Dutch Quarter. Sesu Ra was transported back in time for a fleeting instant, to when he was standing in a temple in lost Irem with darkness clouding his eyes, a voice somewhere pronouncing that this would be the day he died. When his vision cleared, he was still in the present and there were animated corpses rising from the ground and bursting from the walls of the basement. Manfred declared that he had free will once more, and turned to Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> &quot;I did as you commanded, oh Unbending Spine. I claim this land as my reward. Be gone.&quot;<br /> <br /> With a veritable army of undead emerging from the woodwork, Sesu Ra decided to leave. As they left, they passed the carnage on the building's first floor. A dozen dead men, and in their midst two corpses that had taken an unbelievable amount of punishment. As they watched, these two corpses started to twitch and show signs of life. With Manfred's ominous words preying on them though, Sesu Ra decided it would be best if they left.<br /> <br /> He wanted to see what the ritual had wrought, however, and travelled first to the building the cabal had called &quot;the Gateway&quot;. In the darkness beneath the building, he found that the ground between the inverted obelisks had fallen away. A hole in the Earth stood there now. Standing at its top, Sesu Ra could hear the sounds of waves far below, but he couldn't see anything. Sekhem surged around him in waves, and he gained a descent reset as a result. Analysing the result of the ritual, he realised he could slow the descents of every Mummy in the city, if he used the National Monument as a linchpin and carried out some of the same designs on a larger scale. Sesu Ra told Tobi that he could return to Rekhenaten, his mission fulfilled, with the knowledge that the experiment had been a success.<br /> <br /> He had one final objective before he left the Dutch Quarter. He went to the Museum of the Dutch occupation, the place where the Effigy the cabal protected was being stored. It was late at night and the building looked abandoned, but for some reason the front door was unlocked. Sesu Ra and Luca went inside, found that many of the exhibits away from the main entrance were in poor condition, and eventually ended up in a room undergoing renovations. In the plaster dust on the floor, they spotted footprints. Sesu Ra cut his way through the doorway (Dominating Might again), and they found a ritual room with a few ominous bloodstains, mostly cleaned away and long-since dried. A trapdoor led down below.<br /> <br /> They descended, found an ancient stone door covered in Iremite hieroglyphs and three stone sarcophagi. Two were empty. When Sesu Ra tried to cut through the stone doorway, a piercing scream froze him in place. A European man with a noose around his neck and a young Indonesian woman with bones piercing through her skin appeared. When his khopesh passed straight through the man, Sesu Ra realised he was facing ghosts. With the man wielding telekinetic attacks and the woman stunning them with her cries, they were a challenge even before the third sarcophagi opened. A second woman, this one looking middle-aged and covered in scars, wearing clothes stained in places by dried blood, attacked them with an axe.<br /> <br /> Finally, Luca managed to use Chthonic Dominion to turn the European ghost on the corporeal attacker. She eventually went down after taking an unholy amount of punishment. The female ghost eventually stopped screaming and vanished. With the threats dealt with, Sesu Ra broke open the vault (so much use out of Dominating Might this session) and found a strange pedestal within. It was shaped like a man on his knees, with a cage made of rib bones placed on his back. Inside the cage was a single small item covered in a silk shroud, surrounded by a palpable aura that something here was not meant for mortal, or even immortal, eyes.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra took it and went back to his tomb. He noted that the woman he had killed was already beginning to heal, just like the men back at the cabal's temple. He went past her without trying to make sure she stayed dead. Once he reached his tomb, he removed the shroud to discover his prize. His natural affinity for Effigies enabled him to determine it was the Blasphemous Depiction, even as its curse struck him with the Vocalisation derangement. It was a maddening sculpture of the Judge Arem-Abfu, a horrifically blasphemous creation that bestowed the ability to perform a primitive version of the Rite of Return. By using it to bind ghosts into corpses, he could create near-indestructible undead beings and give them a single command, a command they would try to complete. The creatures were virtually feral, resorting to violence at the slightest provocation and without much in the way of intelligence, but they were also nigh impossible to destroy. Of course, the curse was that the sight of this relic was enough to shatter the psyche of those who looked upon it. All things considered, it was probably good Aquila and Akenakhi were not around, or else they would be suffering from Schizophrenia and Irrationality.<br /> <br /> He also ordered Luca to scope out the Dutch Quarter, keep the cabal under observation, and to find a way to kidnap Banek for leverage later. And that was about it for him this session.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi decided to camp out at the Arisen Temple to wait for Kotira. He felt it was probably best if he alerted his Guild's Guildmaster that he was in the city, even if it was a century late. Alerted by the Tomb Guardian, Kotira showed up a few hours later and formally welcomed him. She told him there was much work for the Su-Menent in Jakarta, blasphemy was everywhere and it needed to be rooted out. Many mortals were dabbling in things they should not, and she hoped he would have much success in serving the Judges.<br /> <br /> Aquila, in the meantime, went to talk to Mot-Tan to find out how his discussion with Sem-Huf had gone. The big revelation was that Sem-Huf denied any responsibility for killing Ahumara, which had been a serious driving force behind Aquila's desire for revenge. Mot-Tan felt it was pretty clear that something else was involved, and that by fighting the two Mesen-Nebu were playing right into its hands.<br /> <br /> Aquila went to Sem-Huf's tomb, that thought preying on her mind. She stood outside the main residential building and waited for his cultists to alert him to her presence. He came out to meet her alone. After a long, awkward silence, they talked through the situation. Although they each made it clear that they would be more than happy to kill the other one more time, there was clearly something bigger at stake. Until the mystery of these cultists' murders was resolved, they would cease their vendetta.<br /> <br /> With that ending the session, it was time for some descent checks. Sesu Ra has managed to score one every session for the past three sessions, so he was still at Sekhem 5 (functionally 6 thanks to the Talisman) when this one wrapped up. Akenakhi dropped from Sekhem 7 to Sekhem 6. Aquila dropped from Sekhem 4 to Sekhem 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T19:10:09-07:00","id":265875,"title":"","content":"Session 9<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra managed to get his Ren up to 5 last session, which means he can now chat with Luca telepathically. As a result, when Luca swung by the cult's island the next day and found every single one of them in a coma, he was able to point out this interesting development to his master. Sesu Ra gathered up Akenakhi and Aquila, Aquila said it was the jackal-headed creature doing it, and they all set off for the island.<br /> <br /> It took a while, but they eventually managed to lure the creatures in with the smell of their Pillars. They didn't seem prepared to take on three Mummies at once, but when Akenakhi split from the group they were more than happy to gang up on him. Both the small lion-headed bull and the jackal-headed snake with bird wings attacked him. He used a pistol borrowed from Luca, and killed the jackal-snake (sending centipedes everywhere), but proceeded to get thoroughly mauled by the lion/bull until the others showed up and beat it to death. Luca turned out to be fairly ineffectual in the fight for once, his attacks not seeming to do much to the hybrid monster, but the others were able to finish it off without much trouble. The one minor complication is that the blows sent up clouds of some kind of fungal spore, infecting the entire group.<br /> <br /> They decided, finally, that they should probably get some outside help. The infected Mummies were already starting to smell pretty rank. Aquila stayed behind to nurse the comatose cultists, while Akenakhi and Sesu Ra travelled back to the Temple. They waited there until dawn the next day, when Kotira Nahan and Yarikh arrived for a dawn prayer that, it seemed, was some kind of daily ritual for them. Akenakhi meditated alongside them, and when that was done Kotira left and they asked Yarikh if he knew how to deal with their fungal infection and how to wake their cultists. Yarikh finally gave them a name for the creatures that had been plaguing them, &quot;Amkhata&quot;, and told them they had been fighting relic-spawn (well, they knew that). He revealed that spending two points of Pillars and focussing on their own Sahu would burn out the infection, and that the cultists would wake over the course of the next few days. In the meantime they should keep them hydrated and fed as best they could.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Akenakhi sent Luca off to relay this information to Aquila, and then went to Akenakhi's tomb. Akenakhi's player got sick of having a Haunted tomb really quickly and had spent his accumulated experience buying back the Haunted drawback, so Sesu Ra descended into the tomb and used Chthonic Dominion to find a composite ghost made of the limbs, faces, and mutilated bodies of at least a dozen individuals nesting in Akenakhi's tomb. Every broken and bloody face in the creature's mass turned towards Akenakhi and screamed &quot;Murderer!&quot; For a moment, he had a vision of standing atop a pile of bodies in an underground chamber, perhaps his old tomb while it was being built. Before it could act though, Sesu Ra used the second tier of his Utterance to bind it with the command &quot;Protect me from harm&quot;, and then used the third tier to shift its anchor from Akenakhi's tomb to Sesu Ra's own body. Not only that, he erased the creature's memory of how it/they died.<br /> <br /> The next few days went by. Akenakhi went to Mrs Dartlan, owner of the restaurant above his tomb, and apologised for his earlier display. It turned out she had rationalised the experience of a flaming angel manifesting as the building catching fire, possibly from a thrown firebomb of some kind. Between that and one of her staff found beaten to a pulp in a nearby alley, she was quite convinced her business was under siege. He told her an ancestor of his lay buried beneath her restaurant, and had been responsible for originally constructing it. She seemed interested, and agreed to work with him on finding out more.<br /> <br /> Aquila burnt out her own infection, and spent the next few days caring for the cult. When Phatri woke, she used Healing Counsel to make sure the old woman was still in good health (at this point, we're pretty certain Phatri is being maintained at an effective Morality 10). Phatri seemed a little disorientated or delirious, and called Aquila &quot;Mother&quot;. A short chat teased out the fact that Aquila had raised Phatri from infant through a lot of her childhood.<br /> <br /> Once all that was sorted, Aquila and Akenakhi went off to put their bank robbing plan into motion. Akenakhi sat in the lobby with a newspaper and used the first tier of Palace Knows Its Pharoah to explore the structure and the bank vault. They found some gold they could steal and a few lock boxes with valuables in them hidden below the building, although Akenakhi failed a few Wits + Composure rolls and couldn't work out what a few of the strange electronic gizmos did. Just as he went to leave the bank, he was accosted by an energetic young woman who tried to persuade him to donate to wildlife charity battling to save many of Indonesia's endangered animals. He refused to subscribe to the newsletter, but swore he'd be back to donate money to the cause later.<br /> <br /> Aquila tried to work out a deal with a local charity to begin a massive campaign in one of the city's slums to provide food and support. The group was interested, but said they would like to get their lawyer to look at any such agreement. Aquila donated what money she had on her, and left.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra spent this time examining Jakarta's National Monument. He's tried to use it to reverse engineer a complete ritual, the second part that was meant to synergise with the experiment he found in the Dutch Quarter, but he all he could really tell was that the sacred geometries of the structure had something resembling his own signature style. He realised he must have known the end plan when he added his designs to it. The key must still be in his own memories.<br /> <br /> And that was really it for this session. Aquila picked up the Refined Purity of Purpose Affinity, allowing the rest of the group the enticing prospect of trading Memory for Resources. No one has taken her up on that offer, but in the meantime lots of unscrupulous individuals in the city are going to start getting a bit wealthier whenever she's in the area. And I forgot to get Akenakhi to make a Descent check. Have to remember to get him to do that next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T05:51:27-07:00","id":270744,"title":"","content":"Session 10<br /> <br /> Aquila called in the favour Sesu Ra owed her for guarding the national monument a few nights ago. She'd realised that her Haunted tomb was probably haunted. Up until this point her player had been acting as if the visions and visitations were largely in Aquila's head, with the assumption being that it was a sign of her going mad. Recent events, particularly the discovery of a ghost living in Akenakhi's tomb, made her suspect that there might be a ghost in hers. So they all went down to Aquila's tomb to toss Chthonic Dominion around and see what turned up.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, under the light of the first tier the ghost of a young Indonesian woman was revealed. She promptly through herself at Aquila and dragged her into Neter-Khetet. At first the ghost then fled from Aquila (following success on an Intimidation attempt), but when Aquila tried to be compassionate and understanding the spectre became furious. It screamed that Aquila was a child-taker, kidnapper, and murderer, and started attacking her. Eventually, Aquila was able to drain the ghost's Willpower to render it unconscious, but she took another point of aggravated damage from the accumulated attacks in the process. Sesu Ra was able to cast Chthonic Dominion Tier 2, giving it the command &quot;Make the bank vault appear full&quot; as he'd been asked by Aquila. He then turned Akenakhi's tie into an anchor.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Akenakhi then went off to chat with Yama-Het, apparently not terribly perturbed by Aquila's Twilight-bound state. Aquila, in turn, decided to make the most out of being stuck in Twilight and went to check out the building where she had first met Sem-Huf. She found a few interesting things, namely a false wall masquerading as an exit route in one of the apartments, but being out of phase with the world didn't really help her perception skills. After about an hour she returned to the real world. In the process though she witnessed two great mountains, one in the West and one in the East, and recalled a few myths from Irem about their presence and significance in Neter-Khetet.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, with Yama-Het, Sesu Ra announced that he was planning on instigating some Tef-Aabhi projects in her land in West Jakarta. The suburb was undergoing an urban renewal project, making it perfect for her purposes. He warned her that the Pelamat would no doubt try to intervene. She was reasonably accommodating, but in turn asked for his help dealing with some local Preman, an organised crime mob that she believed had kidnapped one of her cultists. She wanted him rescued with minimal bloodshed, and her associates were all known to the mob making it hard to gather information. The cultist, a young man named Ari, used to work fro the Preman in the district, and they'd tried several times to lure him back. This time, it looked like they were giving force a try.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Akenakhi then reunited and visited Rawa Bening, one of the largest gem markets in South-East Asia. Aquila revealed that she planned on using Equivalency Principle in conjunction with Refined Purity of Purpose in order to replace the gold she intended to steal in the bank heist. She would steal the gold, use it to gain Resources 5 with Refined Purity of Purpose, then spend 5 Resources to buy gems of a high enough value to be transmuted into gold bars, which she could then use to replace those she took from the bank vault. If she took less than a day, and Akenakhi kept the cameras from functioning, and the ghost maintained the illusion that the gold was still there, she could hopefully carry out the heist without anyone realising anything had ever gone missing. Then it would only cost her a single point of Willpower to replenish her Resources.<br /> <br /> In the process, they ran into Hague, Mot-Tan's European henchman. A brief chat revealed that there were a few vessels scattered through Rawa Bening, but that several undisclosed supernatural forces were vying for them in some kind of cold war. He cautioned them not to use magic in or near the building, and to steer clear of the vessels themselves. Most were likely Amulets, and thus his master's property, but it was proving hard to transport them back to Mot-Tan's territory without the courier mysteriously disappearing.<br /> <br /> And then it was heist time. Aquila, Akenakhi, and his tie (and companion ghost) travelled to the bank, went underground using Dust Beneath Feet from a few blocks away, and headed for the vault. Aquila anticipated that the ghost might try to be difficult, and left the tie wrapped around a bit of plumbing several hundred yards from the bank itself. Or at least, she thought she did...<br /> <br /> What followed was a confusing sequence of events, and none of the players were truly able to figure out what was real and what wasn't. Akenakhi shut off power to the vault, and kept an eye on the guards as they tried to work out what was going on. When in the lockbox room, Akenakhi and Aquila heard gunshots and felt bullets pierce their flesh, but there was no visible shooter and the guards outside the room didn't seem to react (Akenakhi was watching them through the walls thanks to Dust Beneath Feet). Aquila left Akenakhi behind to watch them, and entered the vault. She picked up a bar of gold, and then realised it was an illusion. A man-sized snake with the head of a falcon appeared in front of her, but she ignored it and grabbed some gold. Real gold, as far as she could tell. The enormous Amkhat then wrapped itself around her, and sucked out a point of Sekhem. Aquila tried to break free, but three failed attempts later and she was on the verge of death. Then she realised that the tie, with the ghost anchored to it, was still in her pocket and not tied to a bit of plumbing as she'd believed. She decided not to Seal the Flesh, figuring that if it was an illusion her damage would be gone and the creature would disappear. Instead she died.<br /> <br /> Unaware of what was happening, Akenakhi saw a squad of black-armoured troops rush down the stairs, haul the security guards away, and stick something square to the door. Then the falcon-snake Amkhat materialised behind him and grabbed him. He was able to resist the drain on his Sekhem, break free from the grapple, and slide away underground just in time to hear a muffled explosion. He escaped.<br /> <br /> Somewhere entirely removed from that debacle, Sesu Ra and Luca decided to interrogate the prisoners they'd taken from the Pelamat warehouse where they'd met Rangarni (or at least, the man they were calling Rangarni) all those sessions ago. They travelled to the Families' island and had the prisoners hauled out before them. When the first man refused to answer his polite questions, Sesu Ra killed him rather than even attempt an interrogation, then turned Luca loose on the others. This earned him a descent reset, and by putting his faith in Set-Qesu he avoided degeneration once again. The other men broke quite, quite quickly after that display.<br /> <br /> And that was it. Akenakhi dropped to Sekhem 5, joining Sesu Ra who is <i>still</i> Sekhem 5, not counting his Talisman. And Aquila is Sekhem 2, and that's before we even find out what happens in her Death Cycle. Which is another thing I have to write up. I... can't say I was expecting another from Aquila so soon, so we'll see what I come up with over the course of the next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 10-24-2014, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:25:41-07:00","id":270858,"title":"","content":"Exciting stuff! Though I'm not sue what the point of the bank robbery is. Especially if Sem-Huf is no longer viewed as a direct antagonist, that they've been manipulated into attacking each other. Seems like Refined Purity of Purpose would allow for a much easier way to get Resources 5 than that kind of convoluted plan...<br /> <br /> It seems a little like your characters are proceeding through this Descent very quickly (I realize that Aquila has had one death cycle and that has contributed to it, but she's also in her Sothic Turn, right? I thought that made most Descent checks happen more slowly). 10 sessions (chapters) just doesn't seem all that long to play to have dropped to Sekhem 5. Though I guess it depends on what the average length of a game session and the average number of sessions in your chronicle might be.<br /> <br /> In any case, what are your plans for if/when a character drops to Sekhem 0 and returns to henet? Is their cult able to immediately re-summon them, perhaps with the urging of the other members of the meret?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T17:33:54-07:00","id":271253,"title":"","content":"Well, Aquila is trying to get the &quot;free Resources&quot; aspect of Refined Purity of Purpose to trigger, and decided a gold bar would be the easiest way to do it. And in all fairness, all she really had to do was sidle into a bank and take one.<br /> <br /> Ten sessions actually feels like an incredible amount of time for Sesu Ra to still be Sekhem 5. From the top of my head, I'd expect most players to be Sekhem 6 after two sessions, Sekhem 5 after three. They are then making Descent checks every two sessions, with reasonable odds of success. We've found that players proceed through the early part of the descent at a rapid rate, but the lower levels (particularly 1-3) are far more forgiving. Dying doesn't help though.<br /> <br /> As for the player returning, they do need something to fuel the return. At present, Sesu Ra has two relics (he decided to bind the Blasphemous Depiction into his Lifeweb alongside his Talisman) that can be used to resurrect himself, so he has it easy. Neither Akenakhi nor Aquila have relics or vestiges on hand to use in that manner, and they're both currently on their Sothic Turns. If they end their descents, coming back could prove a problem.<br /> <br /> Even if they had relics though, I would likely rule that they had to stay in henet for a few weeks at least. A lot of the plans the group has, particularly Sesu Ra's, need time to come into fruition, and it would be a good excuse to fast-forward a little bit (although ideally not so far and fast that it triggers descent checks for everyone, at the very least I'd let those players play out attempts to stave off the descent). Ultimately, their cult will re-summon them, but it will cost Aquila the Memory dot she purchased and someone will need to acquire a relic or vestige to be consumed in the process. I don't want it to be something done lightly.<br /> <br /> And of course, if she does begin a new descent, that would be it for her Sothic Turn. She would come back with a purpose, and all the additional complications that imposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:07:08-07:00","id":271284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=271253#post271253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect most players to be Sekhem 6 after two sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems <i>nuts </i>to me, but looking back at the book and I suppose how many scenes one goes through in a given game session really depends on the group. Though I can also see how it might not be fun to drop 3 Sekhem levels in a single night. O_o<br /> <br /> Ouch, losing Memory to come back...sounds pretty harsh. What's your reasoning if I might ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T20:02:30-07:00","id":271340,"title":"","content":"Page 76 of the Mummy corebook, &quot;falling into Duat after a descent automatically lowers the Mummy's Memory by one dot (to a minimum of Memory 3) unless he rose in response to a disturbed tomb&quot;. Just a thing that happens, a way for the Judges to stamp down on any pesky individuality or something.<br /> <br /> As for the speed of the Descent, it's pretty clear that Mummies are meant to spend more time at the 1-3 range than, well, pretty much every preceding level put together. On a Sothic Turn a Mummy can last at Sekhem 1 right up until something kills it, and even when they are on the clock the &quot;story&quot; time frame they last for is &quot;an entire Chronicle&quot;. Depending on the length of your game, that could easily mean more time at Sekhem 1 than 2-10 combined. And it does make relic draining an increasingly tempting option.<br /> <br /> As I remember the first session, everyone was Sekhem 8 by the time the first session ended, and were making descent checks to fall from Sekhem 7 by the end of the second session. Sesu Ra did make his Talisman in the second session, so he was still effectively Sekhem 7, but everyone else was Sekhem 6 going into Session number 3. It's fast, but it actually informs play in a really beautiful manner. At high Sekhem, Mummies drive straight for their objectives as fast as they can with one eye constantly on the ticking clock. Once the initial surge of power has fallen away, they start to relax a bit and actually explore the world and the consequences of their previous actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T22:37:52-07:00","id":271420,"title":"","content":"Ten sessions to get to Sekhem 5 is <i>very slow </i>going, actually. Statistically, in a white room scenario, it's more likely to get to Sekhem 5 at session 5. My group was at Sekhem 5 in session 6.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the lower your Sekhem, the longer it takes to lose it. You can be at Sekhem 1 for an entire *chronicle*. Says so in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T23:44:11-07:00","id":271435,"title":"","content":"The Talisman means that he might as well be Sekhem 6, for that matter. And he just earned another reset, so it'll be two more sessions before he needs to make his next check. 12 sessions of Sekhem 6...<br /> <br /> The tragic thing is that, of all the characters, Sesu Ra is the one who could most easily perform at low Sekhem. His Talisman means he'll never drop below Sekhem 2, and that he'll always have access to all three tiers of his two Utterances. And Blessed is the God King Tier 3 means that, when he needs it, he'll be able to fight like a Sekhem 10 Mummy. Really, the only thing that would be annoying for him is that at Sekhem 2 you can only spend one Pillar a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T07:11:07-07:00","id":271604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=271340#post271340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 76 of the Mummy corebook, &quot;falling into Duat after a descent automatically lowers the Mummy's Memory by one dot (to a minimum of Memory 3) unless he rose in response to a disturbed tomb&quot;. Just a thing that happens, a way for the Judges to stamp down on any pesky individuality or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch. Guess I overlooked that rule! Makes sense though, but still ouch.<br /> <br /> So I am guessing Aquila doesn't rise much, her Cult lacking a vessel to bring her back with. And Akenakhi has been in that vault for a few years at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=271340#post271340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the speed of the Descent, it's pretty clear that Mummies are meant to spend more time at the 1-3 range than, well, pretty much every preceding level put together. On a Sothic Turn a Mummy can last at Sekhem 1 right up until something kills it, and even when they are on the clock the &quot;story&quot; time frame they last for is &quot;an entire Chronicle&quot;. Depending on the length of your game, that could easily mean more time at Sekhem 1 than 2-10 combined. And it does make relic draining an increasingly tempting option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great reason to <s>steal and/or misappropriate</s> recover existing talismans held by people of lesser virtue than yourself. With Talismans and Entombed Glory, one could maintain a decent Sekhem rating at all times, and a relatively high one (+5 for Defining Pillar, +1-3 for Talismans, depending on Guild Status) inside one's Tomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T07:37:22-07:00","id":271613,"title":"","content":"I'd usually just assume a single Talisman, as counting on being able to grab and hold onto more than one is a risky prospect. It makes it hard to build a character for. One is easily achievable though, and does allow you to maintain an effective Sekhem 7 when necessary. Choir unleashings are also quite useful once you start to hit the low levels for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> There's also the Jar of Clay Utterance from Guildhalls of the Deathless. As far as I can tell, it basically allows you to decide what Sekhem you want to be and to maintain that indefinitely for a slight Pillar cost. Heck, it's a first tier unleashing, so you could basically do it for free once a scene if you have a Talisman on hand and spend from your Defining Pillar. Every time you place a point of Sekhem in your organs you fall to a new Sekhem rating, starting the descent clock afresh at the new rating. But then you can suck the point of Sekhem back and be at the level you were before, except now you've only just reached that level, effectively earning you a descent reset. It's hard to see how a Mummy with Jar of Clay could ever go below Sekhem 7. Sekhem 8 might be hard to maintain, since you have to go to a canopic jar and do the ritual every three scenes (but not impossible, particularly if you carry a jar around with you), but it's tricky to imagine a session ever going past without a player finding time to do this.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, you're pretty much correct about Aquila. She was last awake in the 1990s, from memory, and her activity over the last century has been pretty rare (three separate risings in the last 100 years, if I remember right). Sesu Ra, meanwhile, has been active every 3-5 years, sometimes for more than a year at a time. And Akenakhi was last awake in the 1940s. Access to a relic allows for a pretty big step up in activity, but Sesu Ra couples that with a personality and goals that require frequent activity. Sekhet Bastet also has a relic, but she hadn't been seen since the 1970s. As a Sheut Mummy, she believes her place is in Duat. And from the cult's perspective... Bast isn't necessarily a person you actually want to have around. Great if you want a whole lot of people dead, but otherwise probably best to leave her where she is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T13:38:08-07:00","id":271716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=271613#post271613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd usually just assume a single Talisman, as counting on being able to grab and hold onto more than one is a risky prospect. It makes it hard to build a character for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's easy to imagine a couple of Guilds having members possessing out-of-Guild Talismans (they work, albeit in a lessened state) and then imbuing new Guild-aligned relics as Talismans...it'd take quite a bit of work though, but would pay off. At least until your Judge got mad at you for doing it, which could always happen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=271613#post271613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the Jar of Clay Utterance from Guildhalls of the Deathless. As far as I can tell, it basically allows you to decide what Sekhem you want to be and to maintain that indefinitely for a slight Pillar cost. Heck, it's a first tier unleashing, so you could basically do it for free once a scene if you have a Talisman on hand and spend from your Defining Pillar. Every time you place a point of Sekhem in your organs you fall to a new Sekhem rating, starting the descent clock afresh at the new rating. But then you can suck the point of Sekhem back and be at the level you were before, except now you've only just reached that level, effectively earning you a descent reset. It's hard to see how a Mummy with Jar of Clay could ever go below Sekhem 7. Sekhem 8 might be hard to maintain, since you have to go to a canopic jar and do the ritual every three scenes (but not impossible, particularly if you carry a jar around with you), but it's tricky to imagine a session ever going past without a player finding time to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, I hadn't thought of that. Though as Four-Jar Magic it also seems very Su-Menent proprietary (and the Guild Status prereq is quite high). That is the biggest limitation, it seems, since you can't get a friend to use it on you (nor do I suppose you want even long-term friends handling your organs...too risky).<br /> <br /> I suppose it'd be a good thing to do in general though. I had no idea it was that exploitable. And the Sekhem remains in there even if you return to henet, right. Since you always return at Sekhem 10, regardless of Talismans or other effects...one could spend multiple Descents imbuing organs with Sekhem and then have 8 Sekhem just kind of stocked there for a big emergency. Or, as you said, play the Sekhem shuffle and stay at high levels virtually forever. I'll have to think more about that, it's intriguing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T16:13:01-07:00","id":271814,"title":"","content":"Yeah, only a Status 4 Su-Menent could pull it off (Sekhet Bastet could buy the Utterance, but she ultimately decided it didn't suit a character who actually wanted to be spending time in henet). With a Talisman you could be Sekhem 8 pretty easily, since you descend as if you were Sekhem 7.<br /> <br /> One minor thing though. If you have a Talisman , you start the descent at Sekhem 9 instead of 10. You put a permanent sliver of your power into it. Any Mummy who loses a Talisman is going to be permanently disadvantaged, but also have a permanent connection to that Talisman. Hence why it's very, very hard to ever get your hands on more than one. You can only ever make one, the others have to be stolen from people highly capable and motivated at getting it back. It's possible (see Sabola in Cursed Necropolis D.C.), but exceptionally difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T22:20:46-07:00","id":272740,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Sekhet Bastet...<br /> <br /> Interlude 1<br /> <br /> In spite of Bast's player being out of the country, we've been staying in contact and working through some things Sekhet Bastet has been up to since that departure. We recently concluded a flashback sequence.<br /> <br /> Bast found herself on a rainy island, carrying a spear and shield and hunting some kind of unspecified quarry. She was there alongside a fellow Su-Menent, a woman named Nenheta. After some discussion, they decided that Bast would explore some nearby caverns near the ocean, while Nenheta and her leopard Beast Companion explored the abandoned village that sat upon a nearby hill.<br /> <br /> Exploring the caverns took a while. The rain hadn't let up in more than a week, and Bast found that the caverns actually connected to the ocean. It was high tide, and a lot of the area was flooded. Not a big problem for a Mummy, mind you. The darkness underwater was more of an issue than any other potential problem, like not being able to breathe. As she delved deeper into the caverns she discovered a place with a palpable aura of occult magic, and then was attacked by a Chthonic Being. The ensuing fight was long and drawn out, as Bast and the creature burned through nearly all their power regenerating damage. When Bast finally struck the killing blow, she only had one Pillar left (and couldn't use it to seal the flesh, as she'd already spent one from that pillar earlier), and only two points of health not filled with Aggravated damage. Those two points were filled with lethal instead. On the Chthonic Being's part, it had been forced to use every spot of Essence it had, but ultimately it just wasn't quite enough to stop Bast from killing it.<br /> <br /> Exhausted and drained, Bast retreated to the cavern's entrance. A bit of exploration in the upper levels discovered a cache containing several vestiges. To the present day Bast's distaste, her past self drained one of the vestiges to regenerate a few Pillar points. She decided to rest for several hours to recover from the fight, and then set off to try and find Nenheta. The sun was setting at this point, and the fellow Su-Menent was not at the agreed upon meeting place. Bast trekked across the island and reached the village. In the middle of the street she found the gutted remains of Nenheta's leopard, and saw a bonfire burning in the distance. She reached it, and found herself on the steps leading to the temple where the mortal's worshipped their false god. She lit the tip of her spear on fire and went inside, and found a sobbing Nenheta within.<br /> <br /> The scent of Bast's Sekhem drove Nenheta into a frenzy. She attacked Sekhet Bastet, who realised her fellow Su-Menent had become a Shuankhsen. Their quarry had trapped her and turned her. Luckily for the badly injured Bast, the process had not left Nenheta in a good state either. The very first blow &quot;killed&quot; Nenheta, and then it was just a matter of beating her down into the ground repeatedly until she could no longer Seal the Flesh.<br /> <br /> The memory ended with Bast staring at the crumpled, burning corpse of her ally. When she woke in the present, she decided the vision was a sign. The Shuankhsen must be at large in Jakarta, and she was going to find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:03:11-07:00","id":276280,"title":"","content":"Session 11<br /> <br /> Aquila's latest Death Cycle took her back to a gully surrounded by injured soldiers and damaged equipment. She was doing her best to care for the men, when a messenger arrived to announce that Yarikh's men were coming. He had only just got the words out when an arrow struck him and a host of armoured soldiers charged down the slopes to overwhelm Aquila's men. She found that in this prior life she didn't know the Dust Beneath Feet Utterance, but that she was familiar with Harvest the Divine Flesh. In the end, Aquila managed to kill one of her attacks before the rest bore her to the ground. Alongside most of her soldiers, she was bound and led away in chains.<br /> <br /> It took four days for Aquila to complete that Death Cycle. In the intervening time Sesu Ra and Luca managed to map out the everyday routine of Banek, the leader of the death cult in the Old Dutch Quarter. Luca was dispatched to kidnap him, and the next day told his master that Banek was locked away in the increasingly permanent holding pens on their cultists' island.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi spent the time recovering his pillars following the encounter with the Greater Amkhat, and drinking a lot at Darnton's.<br /> <br /> After Aquila returned to life she sought out and gathered her meret. They decided they needed more information on the larger breed of Amkhata before they tried to hunt it down and figure out what it was doing in a bank vault, so they sent cultists to request Yarikh meet the lot of them at the Temple. They ended up meeting just before the Su-Menent dawn service. Yarikh told them that Greater Amkhata were made, not born from broken relics, in a perverse ritual that required access to Sekhem and liberal amounts of human blood and animal body parts. Sesu Ra immediately suspected a fellow Arisen, pointing out that they had the easiest access to the Sekhem requirement. Yarikh suggested he speak to Kotira instead, since she knew of matters he was not at liberty to discuss himself.<br /> <br /> Aquila then dragged Yarikh off to one side to discuss her Death Cycle. After being a little cagey for a while, Yarikh added a few details to the story. They'd been fighting in the Third Servile War, side by side, each of them moved by their empathy for the slaves at the time. As the tide turned against the rebellion, Aquila and her followers were cornered. Yarikh was marching as fast as he could to help her, but by the time he arrived she was gone and most of her men were dead.<br /> <br /> The group approached Kotira after the morning prayers, and she revealed that there had been a marked increase in Greater Amkhata sightings in Jakarta in the last two decades. She had been trying to get to the root of the problem on and off, but the revenants she created for that purpose kept killing the leads they discovered. The men and women they killed had been employed at a variety of different multinational corporations, but she hadn't been able to draw a convincing link between them to give herself a single suspect. What she did know was that after each assassination, a cultist of hers would be slain. She had enough evidence to suggest it was the Amkhata doing this each time.<br /> <br /> When asked about why such a creature might be found in a bank vault, Kotira revealed that she suspected whoever was behind it might be able to detect the use of Utterances and other obvious manifestations of Sekhem. She didn't know if it was something magical in nature or not, but she did know that the coverage was not total and that it instead tended to be around locations where an Arisen might logically find something of interest. A bank vault would be a prime example.<br /> <br /> The party then decided to rob the bank again. This time they did things a lot more simply. Aquila put Dust Beneath Feet on all of them, they burrowed into the vault around midnight, cut off the power and turned the gold into an enormous diamond for transport. They then fled as fast as they could, without spotting any sign of trouble. Luca drove them away, and thanks to a multitude of poor Wits + Composure rolls they were unaware that they were being followed.<br /> <br /> When they stopped at a desert part of the docks they were attacked by the black armoured men Akenakhi had seen during the last robbery attempt. Aquila nearly died again, she was still badly damaged from her most recent death, and had to flee into the ocean with only one health not filled with aggravated damage. The ghost from Akenakhi's tomb obeyed Sesu Ra's standing command to protect him, and possessed one of the attackers and turned him on the others. The soldiers began to retreat, but Luca and Sesu Ra ran them down. One man fired a flare gun into Sesu Ra's stomach. Two attackers escaped in the end, one was left in the meret's hands but on the verge of death, and the other three died. We ended with the group saving the life of their new prisoner just before he bled out from his wounds.<br /> <br /> It was one of those sessions where a decent amount of stuff actually happened, but it doesn't look like much when I type it up like this. We had a lot of long roleplaying discussions, and then the fight against the men in black dragged on for quite a while. It's left the group pretty beat up though, and the trap Sesu Ra was setting for the Pelamat is about to spring, so it'll be interesting to see how they decide to run things next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:52:38-07:00","id":280912,"title":"","content":"Session 12<br /> <br /> In the aftermath of their fight, Akenakhi and Sesu Ra bundled their new captive aboard a stolen boat, along with the corpses of the dead men. Aquila hunted through a fish gutting station near the docks, found a suitable bowl and water, and absorbed the wealth of the gold she'd stolen through an alchemical mixture to grant herself Resources 5. As her meret mates headed inland, Aquila went to check out the gem market. At this point it was very early morning, and the place was still closed. Frustrated, she realised that a cheque made out using her new resources would actually serve to transmute back into gold to replace that which she'd stolen. She hurried back to the bank, waited for it to open, went through a rather lengthy procedure to have a cheque written for 5 Resources worth of wealth. She negotiated the hurdles easily enough, withdrew the money from the large account she suddenly had (or had always had) with the bank, travelled a short distance to transmute it into gold, and then placed it in the vault. The bank would likely find some issues with the video camera later, namely the discovery that dirt had somehow gotten into its wiring. With any luck, she hoped, that would be enough to stop the theft being noticed.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra had the corpses embalmed, so that he could use them with his Blasphemous Depiction later, and had Luca transport one of them to his tomb. He then went to the graveyard outside of Sekhet Bastet's tomb, dominated one of the ghosts there, and took it back with him (using Chthonic Dominion to turn himself into its anchor). He then created a proto-mummy creature with the task to defend his infrastructure in Yama-Het's territory, and the whole group proceeded to rest for a few days. Aquila camped out in the Temple, the others mostly stayed in their tombs.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi had a brief conversation with their new, impassive captive. The man looked Caucasian, was fit and well-built, and remained completely silent in the face of questioning. Conceding that he wasn't all that good at milking information from suspects, Akenakhi went and joined Sesu Ra and Luca in staking out the new projects that were being started in West Jakarta. Not too much time later, three Pelamat attacked. The fight was brief, the group drove past just long enough to hurl molotovs at the group and at the scaffolding put up in preparations for modifications to an existing building's facade, then drove away. As they were fleeing though, Akenakhi used Obedient Clay to turn one of their motorbikes into liquid. They grabbed the man and hustled him off to Yama-Het's community centre for interrogation. The Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster was not in attendance, but the cultists let them take a room upstairs.<br /> <br /> After some interrogation from Luca, the man revealed he'd been sent by Rangarni. The compartmentalised nature of the Pelamat continued to frustrate the players, as he didn't have any information about how to track down the leader. They did find that the guy had a phone with Rangarni's phone number, which could prove useful. And they did learn that the Pelamat were apparently purchasing real estate in South Jakarta. After that, Sesu Ra killed him and earned yet another Descent Reset. This time though, putting his faith in Set-Qesu was not enough. He dropped to Memory 2 and gained the False Incarnation derangement (we wanted to play around with one of the new Mummy-specific derangements).<br /> <br /> This session was really quite short, so we had to end there. I was feeling pretty wrecked, and I think most of the others were kind of out of it as well. Hopefully things will have improved next week, but it still had a few fun scenes. Aquila healed enough so that she now &quot;only&quot; has five aggravated damage, and Akenakhi dropped to Sekhem 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:55:36-07:00","id":281099,"title":"","content":"How long do your sessions go on for and how many 'scenes' generally take place in each one (like for the purposes of Sekhem drops)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:23:39-07:00","id":281656,"title":"","content":"The first few sessions were about six hours long, but we've since dropped to five hours (including a half-hour break in the middle for dinner). Scenes vary a lot. When the players were at a high enough Sekhem that scenes actually mattered for the Descent, they tended to spend as much time in each scene as possible. Things have become a bit more relaxed since we reached the session metric instead.<br /> <br /> I do know that the first session we had was only four scenes long. Sesu Ra missed the first scene, so he was Sekhem 9-10 for the entire first session, while the others dropped as far as Sekhem 8. After that the pace picked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T00:02:30-07:00","id":282009,"title":"","content":"Ah, cool! I really like how, even when there's some flashbacks, the big bombs only get dropped during death cycles. Poor Aquila - what's her Sekhem now? Is it 1 yet? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T00:22:03-07:00","id":282018,"title":"","content":"I try to have death cycles and cases when the players purchase a dot of Memory be big, significant flashbacks. Aquila has had a good few so far as a result, yeah, but Sekhet Bastet also had one when she repurchased Memory 3 and I suspect the same will happen to Sesu Ra (he currently has 8 Sebayt experience, so rebuying Memory 3 seems likely) shortly. I'm really enjoying running them.<br /> <br /> And yes, Aquila is Sekhem 1. It's not been her proudest Sothic Turn so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T02:55:21-07:00","id":282126,"title":"","content":"Can you or your players 'feel' the discrepancy between having both a Mummy at Sekhem 5 and one at Sekhem 1? I'm not sure I'll ever get around to having more than one PC for my <b>Mummy</b> game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:12:31-07:00","id":282149,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty marked difference. No access to Tier 2 and 3 Utterances, only able to spend 1 Pillar per turn, and even then only gaining one attribute point per Pillar. It doesn't help that Aquila is nearly full on Aggravated damage as a consequence of her most recent Death Cycle and subsequent fighting. Sesu Ra and Akenakhi have noticeably more options in combat, and what they do has more of an impact. Sesu Ra in particular, as the most combat orientated of the group now that Bast has left, still feels confident enough to stride headfirst into dangerous situations without any preparation. Aquila, meanwhile, is constantly on the edge of triggering Dust Beneath Feet Tier 1 and just hiding underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:08:28-07:00","id":282530,"title":"","content":"Would you mind giving a run-down of the Relics/Vestiges each player has possession of?<br /> <br /> I really like what you did with the Blasphemous Depiction, by the way. I noticed that the book description leaves it very open-ended so an ST can empower the Depiction as they see fit for their chronicle and your interpretation is awesome.<br /> <br /> Seems like it's too late for Aquila to make a Talisman, so she's basically stuck at Sekhem 1...at least she won't have to worry about a timed Descent roll since it's her Sothic Turn, but wow...she was only able to be active for a few weeks this time up to this point, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:57:39-07:00","id":282843,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sure. Akenakhi and Aquila are both relic-less, although Aquila knows the location of a relic sword that was once hers.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra has two relics. One, filling the &quot;from Ancient Irem&quot; slot in his lifeweb, is the Blasphemous Depiction. As I mentioned earlier, it allows the wielder to perform a mummification ritual on a corpse, bind a ghost into the body, and create an Abmortal with a single driving Purpose. Once the Purpose is complete the Abmortal stops healing damage. As a rule the creature acts like a Memory 0 Mummy, defaulting to violence to solve its problems and largely bereft of personality. I do love the Depiction's rules in the core book and the options it gives you. You could have it make vampires, sin-eaters, prometheans, revenants, restore humans to life, Shuankhsen, generic zombies, or whatever you want your chronicle to have. It's a brilliant piece of work. And as Sesu Ra's player pointed out, once you're suffering from the curse you could quite easily use the thing as a weapon. Your curse can't get worse, and it could be fun to inflict Schizophrenia and Irrationality on your enemies.<br /> <br /> The other, in his lifeweb under the &quot;Any number of relics made by your own hand&quot; category, is a three-storey obelisk called the Strength of Anut. Anyone who deals with him while he is in the &quot;seat&quot; of his power treats him as though he were Status 5 in an appropriate organisation. It's incorporated into the structure of his tomb, and its effects count the entire skyscraper as the seat of his power. He has turned the obelisk into a Talisman with two Manifestation dots in Blessed is the God King and one in Chthonic Dominion.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet has the Pale Brood uter, taking up the &quot;from Ancient Irem&quot; slot in her lifeweb. She has also turned it into a Talisman, containing one Manifestation dot of Secrets Ripped from Skies, one dot from Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, and two dots from Jar of Teeth. She also has a vestige (Hope and Justice fetters, I think) in the form of the cowboy hat being worn by one of the Faithful leaders.<br /> <br /> As for Aquila, it turns out getting killed is a very efficient way to speed through a Descent. She could reclaim her Sekhem point if she could track down and kill the Amkhat that stole it, unless the creature's master has already used the Sekhem for some other nefarious purpose. If it is gone, and she does decide to try and make a Talisman, she's going to have to drain a relic or something to boost her Sekhem back up a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T06:52:10-07:00","id":290476,"title":"","content":"Session 13<br /> <br /> This session started out with a bit of confusion. Sesu Ra and Akenakhi tried to track down Yama-Het's missing cultist, Ari, but weren't sure how to go about it. They ultimately ended up heading to Ari's apartment, where they'd heard he was kidnapped from. One neighbour suggested that she heard a visitor of his say words that sounded like &quot;taken to the country&quot;. So they reported back, asking if Yama-Het knew whether any of the local Preman owned land out in the countryside. They did some research, digging through all the information Yama-Het's cult could gather while trying to ignore the party going on in the downstairs room of the community centre. Akenakhi narrowed the field down through Muhammad's lieutenants to find a man named Awei Mohallem Wasi, who seemed to be the most likely culprit to actually have committed the kidnapping. More cultists were dispatched to find out if he had a house outside Jakarta.<br /> <br /> After that, they toyed with the idea of bribing some police to try and track down the Pelamat, but ultimately decided against it (informed by the fact that Aquila was the only one with money to spend). Instead, they returned to the island to interrogate the man they captured from the soldiers who attacked them. They found him inside a hut, strung up and being beaten by a younger cultist under the supervision of Pama Lehn. Apparently, the man had tried to escape. Sending the cultists outside of the room, Sesu Ra settled in for several hours of near-torture and interrogation.<br /> <br /> Finally, they got some details. The man worked for &quot;L41Secure&quot;, a security firm owned by a pharmaceutical giant called LDI. They were an acquisitions team sent out to capture &quot;targets&quot;, powerful immortal beings for study in LDI labs, but apparently surveillance had screwed up big time on this op. They hadn't realised there were three priority targets all working together, and had come expecting only a single supernatural foe. They found out that he had used to work for a PMC, before being recruited. He'd taken part in two previous acquisition missions, one in Afghanistan and another in Peru. The players were outraged, and were quick to make sure that he had no idea who the Faithful were.<br /> <br /> As they went to leave, however, the man mentioned that the full weight of LDI and its security forces would come down on the group. He seemed confident that they would have tracked down the cult, and that the villagers here would soon be massacred.<br /> <br /> The group's preparations for conflict lasted the rest of the session. Three days passed in which Akenakhi had cultists dig trenches and foxholes. He seemed a little confused by the suggestion that World War I tactics were no longer applicable. He did have a brief flashback to the Great War in the process, earning him a point of Sebayt experience.<br /> <br /> The others took it in shifts to go back to the mainland to mediate at their tomb (or the temple in Aquila's case), while debating a lot over how best to prepare for a fight. Aquila set Resa to track down one of his smuggling contacts, a man called Kudava Jav, to obtain a set of riot gear. A few arguments were had about the viability of explosives, of turning the entire cult into zombie-monsters using the Blasphemous Depiction and the small host of ghosts outside of Bast's tomb, and whether it would just be simpler to move to a different island. Ultimately, women and children were evacuated to the smuggler island Resa had once used as his base. Many, many ideas were offered up, and this sequence easily took far more time than anything else this session. In the end Sesu Ra did create a zombie using a body he'd embalmed earlier and a ghost from near Bast's tomb, commanding it to &quot;Protect the cult's island&quot;, but I don't believe any other grand strategy arose outside of it. Luca and a few men did take the accumulated prisoners, particularly Banek and the interrogated soldier, to an entirely uninhabited island, where they sheltered themselves from aerial observation..<br /> <br /> During this time, Akenakhi made a few trips to Dartlan's. Mrs Dartlan's husband had apparently just returned from France, but was quite sick. He tried to offer to buy the restaurant. She told him that her husband owned the restaurant, but was too ill from all his travelling to receive visitors just yet.<br /> <br /> On one shore trip, Aquila found one of Yama-Het's cultists waiting for her. He told her that Awei had a brother who owned a farm in the countryside. They decided that they would finally set off and rescue Ari, hoping no attack would happen in the meantime and leaving Luca behind on guard. Aquila used Dust Beneath Feet once they came within sight of the farm in order to take herself and Resa along. Resa, with no Ka or Sekhem rating, was completely blind underground. At Sekhem 1 and Ka 1, Aquila wasn't a whole lot better. They managed to navigate their way into the basement and found Ari inside, but their emergence provoked Terror Sybaris. Aquila desperately intimidated him while wishing she'd brought Akenakhi along with his ability to bestow the Witness merit. They managed to shepherd him underground, using Dust Beneath Feet Tier 1 on him as well, and get back to where the others were, before they were discovered. They headed back to town by hitching a lift in the back of a passing truck.<br /> <br /> And there it ended. An extra point of experience was awarded, because it was the first time in quite a while that the players had actually succeeded in wrapping up a story, albeit it a pretty minor one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:03:02-07:00","id":290836,"title":"","content":"Wait, so what's the deal with Ari?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:21:53-07:00","id":290841,"title":"","content":"Looking back, it looks like I forgot to name him. Back in Session 10 Sesu Ra struck a deal with Yama-Het, agreeing to help her find a cultist of hers. That cultist was Ari. He's ex-Preman, but had &quot;found god/s&quot; (or &quot;found Yama-Het&quot;, to be entirely correct) and left to join her cult. He was then kidnapped by his old associates, after they made several unsuccessful attempts to pressure him into coming back to them.<br /> <br /> I tend to write these right after the session finishes. The advantage is that the events are, supposedly, fresh in my mind. The downside is that I'm tired enough for that not to matter. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:27:47-07:00","id":292574,"title":"","content":"Interlude 2<br /> <br /> While all this has been going on, Sekhet Bastet has been on the hunt for Shuankhsen. After waking from her memories, she gathered a few cultists and told them to look for signs of the creatures' presence. She knew enough about Shuankhsen from her memories now to say that large numbers of missing people were the most likely sign of such a monster's presence. After deciding that it would take too long to trawl through each of Jakarta's many slums in search of vulnerable people, she chose instead to look into places with transient populations. A combination of Sybaritic Omens and mundane investigation led her to an enormous bus terminal in East Jakarta. This place had come up on the players' radar before, not being all that far from the old warehouse where they first encountered Rangarni, and because it apparently had a problem with missing persons. Dragging a cultist along to translate for her, she went in to investigate.<br /> <br /> The terminal was enormous, resembling an airport in scale and layout. People thronged its corridors, including a sizable number of foreign backpackers. Bast wandered up and down for a while, getting a feel for the place and trying to find something out of the ordinary. In the end, it took about a week of patrols before she ran into something of interest. Most of the departure lounges were packed, the hard plastic seats perpetually full. Today, one of them was completely empty except for a single woman with red hair and pale, badly sun-burnt skin. The glass walls of the lounge made the absence of anyone else quite obvious, and the fact that the woman was arguing with a security guard piqued her curiosity. The man was clearly trying to keep the woman inside. He said something, and the woman backed away and took a seat.<br /> <br /> Bast wandered over. She told her cultist to tell the guard that she was some kind of investigator and just strode past him, ignoring the attempts he made to stop her. She sat down next to the woman, who was looking at her in surprise, and waited for her cultist to catch up. Then, through her translator, she asked what was going on.<br /> <br /> The woman, named Lauren, turned out to be an English backpacker on a solo trip across the country. She was meant to be heading to Bali later in the week, but the bus to take her out of the city hadn't materialised. Instead, she was told there was a problem and to wait here, even when the rest of the passengers were cleared out of the room. That was a while ago now, and she's been getting more and more worried.<br /> <br /> When Bast looked away, she saw that there were now three guards outside all looking at her with unfriendly expressions. Past them, she could see a fourth man watching the proceedings with clear interest. She got up, told her cultist to tell Lauren to follow, and more or less bulled her way past the guards. They seemed largely helpless to prevent it. The watcher, meanwhile, had started to walk away, but Bast hurried to catch up with her gaggle of mortals in tow. When they did catch the man, he was asking a ticket seller about someone who had previously bought a ticket to Semarang. Bast, her cultist, and Lauren followed the man outside, with Lauren at this point looking more worried than she had when she was being held in the room.<br /> <br /> In the smoke-filled passageway between two of the terminal's buildings, the man they were following turned around and addressed to ask why they were following him. Bast, instead, demanded he say why he was watching them. Eventually, she learned that he was a guide, named Keiichi, and was looking for two of his clients. They were meant to travel to Semarang together, but as far as he could tell the pair had left a day early without telling him. He was watching because he'd wondered at first if Lauren was one of his clients, she looked a little similar. He's been getting a bit worried, a few other people in the business have told him that there have been a few tourists vanish rather than meet with their local guides.<br /> <br /> He does give Bast her next lead, however. Apparently, the guard keeping Lauren in the room, Ali, is a little bit notorious. He has a criminal background and martial arts training, a combination that means he's probably linked to organised crime. Bast leaves Lauren with Keiichi and heads back, eventually tracking down Ali and shadowing him from a distance. When he goes to head through a &quot;Staff Only&quot; door, Bast slips in behind him, closes the door, and grabs him. A brief struggle ends with Ali on the floor. Bast sends her cultist to find somewhere secure to interrogate the man, and he comes back to tell her that there's a security terminal manned by a single guard just around the bend. Bast strides in, grabs the guard before he can speak (silencing him with Grip of Death), and then beats his head against every available surface until he stops moving.<br /> <br /> Ali is then dragged in, and Bast waits for him to regain consciousness. A short interrogation breaks him, and Bast finds exactly what she is looking for. Ali is a cultist, a member of a family that has served a creature called &quot;Gator&quot; for generations. He, and a number of other staff in the building, all worship the creature. They conspire to send it regular meals, generally picking on tourists without a set schedule, people who could go missing at any point in their trip and no one would really know where to start looking. Lauren was intended to be its latest.<br /> <br /> Bast demands that Ali take her to the entrance to the creature's lair. A door leading to an underground maintenance system turns out to be the answer. When it opens, however, a pair of human corpses can be seen lying at the base of the stairs. They struggle to their feet when Bast enters, and in the dim light she can see that they have bloody holes in their chest, right where their hearts should be.<br /> <br /> Bast's response to the walking dead is to throw Ali at them. The creatures ignore him, and instead charge at Bast. The fight takes a long, long while. The creatures are incredibly strong, bolstered by lurking near their master's tomb, and won't go down until their health is full with aggravated damage, and Bast has no way of doing anything more than bashing. When she pauses to Seal the Flesh, the Terror Sybaris infects Ali and he starts to beg for mercy in the background. When she finally does finish off the Awakened Servants, tearing off their limbs one by one, she looks down at Ali and decides he's useless to her. She kills him, earning a Descent reset and passing her Degeneration check.<br /> <br /> Leaving her cultist behind, Bast explores and locates an altar room. A variety of bodies, in varying states of decay, lie on the ground around a central plinth. Some look quite recent, others have been there for years. Every single one has a hole where their heart should be. The place stinks of decay. There is a door on the other side of the room, a large stone door that looks distinctly out of place after the far more modern environs of the maintenance tunnels.<br /> <br /> Then, one by one, the bodies start to animate and get to their feet. Bast makes a break for the stone door, slamming into it with her shoulder. She rolls really, really high, and something breaks inside the door. She forces it open, and finds herself in a much smaller room. There is an opening in the middle of the floor. Although she can't read them beyond recognising the picture of a raindrop, there are signs around saying that there's a large water tank here. Bast closes the door behind her, walks over to the tank, and leaps down.<br /> <br /> It's quite a long drop. She takes a few points of bashing damage and is knocked to the ground, but Grip of Death pulls her to her feet a moment later. The only lighting at the bottom of the tank comes from above, putting Bast in the middle of a shaft of illumination. She hears something moving, and then a voice from the darkness speaks to her. She sees a huge shape in the darkness. It looks like a man, but then its head changes. The jaws grow longer and the head splits, until it looks like the jaws of a crocodile. Backing into the darkness, Bast triggers Ancestry of Forgotten Stars to assume her demon form just before the creature charges.<br /> <br /> When it comes through the light to attack her, she gets her first good look at the Shuankhsen. He's an enormous man, absolutely dwarfing her. He has dark brown skin, discoloured a reddish-bronze in places, and covered with tattoos of blue hieroglyphs in others. The hieroglyphs on his neck and head are impossible to read, stretched and elongated by his crocodile jaws, and she doesn't get a chance to look at the others.<br /> <br /> Then the Shuankhsen is on top of her. Even with Ancestry of Forgotten Stars and Seal the Flesh, she starts taking a lot of bashing damage. Her own attacks barely seem to phase her attacker. She grapples him, and the fight from that point is eerily quiet (both participants have Grip of Death). The Shuankhsen goes into a frenzy. Every strike that does 5+ damage stuns Bast for a round. She gets torn to pieces, the creature biting out huge chunks of her body and swallowing them, taking a point of Sekhem with it. She breaks free, recasts Ancestry of Forgotten Stars (it expired a round or two back), and, with only one health not filled with Aggravated damage, teleports to the nearest Geometry 4+ location. Luckily, that happens to be Sesu Ra's tomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T06:45:36-07:00","id":297069,"title":"","content":"Session 14<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra was partway through meditating to restore his Pillars when Sekhet Bastet appeared in the room, missing parts of her head, neck, breast, arms, and clearly on the verge of entering a Death Cycle. After a stunned pause, he demanded to know what had happened. &quot;Shuankhsen,&quot; she said. She demanded the meret be gathered to mount an immediate assault on the place. Not hugely in favour of rest and recuperation, Bast.<br /> <br /> Luca was summoned telepathically, and ordered to bring the rest of the group with him. Aquila and Akenakhi were returning after delivering Ari to Yama-Het. Aquila had tried to get some assistance for her cultists against the inevitable LDI attack, but Yama-Het was reluctant to send her cultists out without her blessing, a blessing that would require them to return to her within a few hours. That wasn't exactly feasible given the several hour boat trip required to get to the island where the Families lived, but she did promise to help if they needed help mounting their own offensive. Luca ran into them on their way back to the cult, and told them Sesu Ra was summoning them all on an urgent matter.<br /> <br /> Although Aquila and Akenakhi were reluctant to leave the cult undefended, they decided that a Shuankhsen close to one of their own bases of operation needed to be removed immediately. They headed for the bus terminal, pausing long enough for Sesu Ra to call up an impressive number of cultists to help them with the attack. Aquila sunk beneath the ground upon their arrival, carrying the party's weapons so they could move through the crowds without suspicion. Bast was wearing heavy clothing, both to disguise her injuries and prevent recognition. The group walked through the bus terminal following Bast's lead, reaching the &quot;Staff Only&quot; door. Aquila was able to open it from the inside. The door had just closed behind them when a pair of security guards confronted them. Sesu Ra's response was to use Chthonic Dominion to reveal the ghostly bodyguard following him, the composite spectre made up of dozens of dead men, women, and children. The guards promptly fled.<br /> <br /> They reached the maintenance tunnel that Bast had found, and Aquila handed Luca and Sesu Ra their weapons. Akenakhi used Palace Knows Its Pharoah to scout ahead as they walked, making sure they weren't ambushed. At around this point, Sekhet Bastet's player was able to skype in and take over for the rest of the session.<br /> <br /> When they reached the altar room, it was occupied by three cultists. They attacked the meret, and the corpses around the room started to rise. In all, six Awakened Servants and three cultists beset the party. Aquila and Bast both held back at first, Aquila hiding underground, while Luca and Sesu Ra both unleashed Blessed is the God King (Luca first, then Sesu Ra the next turn) and started boosting their Attributes right to the upper limits.The tight corridor meant that their own cultists couldn't join the fight at first, and the party had to actually push through the zombies and into the room before everyone could pitch in.<br /> <br /> When Sesu Ra's ghost possessed one of the enemy cultists and Luca gunned down a second one, the sole surviving man bolted for the next room and screamed for his master. Aquila scooted forward, still underground, to watch what happened. First came a hollow booming sound, as something climbed up from the pit. Aquila couldn't see what, as the water tank's walls were made of plastic or similar material. Until, that is, the Shuankhsen emerged. Aquila felt a sense of deja vu looking at the reddish-bronze discolourations on his flesh, and decided not to attack him.<br /> <br /> Back in the altar room, the fight was getting pretty bogged down. The immensely strong Awakened Servants were tearing Akenakhi apart, but were having a hard time touching Sesu Ra and Luca due to their high strength and added protection from Blessed is the God King. Bast, along with the three cultists, put one of the zombies in the dust. The ghost spun its mortal body's form into something that resembled an enormous, fleshy praying mantis with rib bones serving as scythe blades. It dismembered one of the Servants attacking Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> The Shuankhsen stormed into the chamber. It saw its tomb under attack by Arisen and roared out a challenge, as its head deformed into crocodile jaws. Sesu Ra answered, storming up and nearly cutting the creature in half with a single blow. Then the Shuankhsen threw itself into Sesu Ra, biting deep and keeping the larger attacker off-balance as it bit again and again, each strike doing enough to deny Sesu Ra his next action. Between Stamina 10 and Living Monolith (bound as part of Blessed is the God King thanks to Ren 5), Sesu Ra was still feeling reasonably confident, until his health filled with lethal damage and the Shuankhsen bit out a chunk of his Sekhem. Sesu Ra fell to Sekhem 4 (effectively 5).<br /> <br /> The rest of the party slowly finished off the Awakened Servants. Bast walked up to the only living enemy cultist and mummified him on the spot. Akenakhi and the allied cultists made sure that the non-zombie corpses around the room were decapitated, preventing them from rising to help. Aquila sung out with Healing Counsel to keep Sesu Ra on his feet. At the sound of her voice, however, the Shuankhsen stiffened. It turned its head back and forth wildly, and roared out a name. &quot;Emerset!&quot; For a moment, Aquila was back in Irem. She was being handed a rod of office, and being congratulated by a priest on her new station. &quot;Guildmaster Emerset,&quot; he called her. Aquila made sure she stuck far underground after that.<br /> <br /> With only the Shuankhsen and one of its servants still standing, the group focussed all their attentions on the Shuankhsen. Luca and the ghost grappled it. Sesu Ra and Bast began stabbing it repeatedly. Akenakhi, who had been using Revelations of Smoke and Flame to attack for most of the fight, switched to a pistol and threw a couple of shots in. With the creature weighed down by so many allies and clearly on the verge of death, Aquila rose from the ground and punched it. Her blow failed to connect, however. Sekhet Bastet struck what should have been a killing blow, but the creature's animating magic had enough juice in it for one more strike.<br /> <br /> Ignoring Luca and the ghost, the Shuankhsen lunged at Aquila screaming &quot;Emerset! Give back what you took from me!&quot;. It bit down hard, before the others hauled it off her. And then it collapsed, having taken too much damage for it to sustain itself any longer.<br /> <br /> The group quickly destroyed the final Awakened Servant. The Shuankhsen's cultists were out, one mummified, another dying from gunshot wounds, and the third having taken horrific damage while ridden by Sesu Ra's pet ghost. The group took stock, and Aquila felt something foul taking root in her soul. That last, final bite had infected her with something. A craving for human hearts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 10-31-2014, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:45:54-08:00","id":311118,"title":"","content":"Session 15<br /> <br /> Akenakhi purchased a dot of Memory at the end of last session, so it was flashback time. He found himself standing in the ice and snow, staring mournfully out into the blizzard. Then a door opened somewhere behind him, he felt the warmth of a fire, and another Arisen joined him. He remembered her name, Nenheta, and that she was an acolyte of the Su-Menent. Like him, she was a seeker of knowledge, looking for Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> They were both bitter about the storm. It was going to ruin the ritual they were set to perform, they were sure of it. In spite of that, Nenheta told Akenakhi that he had best head inside before he froze over completely. They entered the crude, wooden lodge where their cultists waited, and tried to call on the wisdom of the stars to reveal their path to freedom. For a moment they thought they saw sand, stone temples, and white cotton robes. Then it was gone.<br /> <br /> Thinking it had failed, the pair slumped into the carved, stone seats, thrones that seemed quite out of place surrounded by the wooden hut and fur-garbed cultists. Then the fire surged, and spoke. Eyes opened in the fire, and lips of ash parted to reveal glowing coals for teeth. It told them that it knew the knowledge they sought, the path to Apotheosis, but that it would only do so for a price. There were sixteen youths who had not yet seen fourteen winters living in the village. Feed them to the fire, and it would tell them how to break their chains.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi agreed, despite Nenheta expressing doubts that the creature could be trusted. She only watched as he fed the children and infants to the fire, a sequence he remembered only as a frenzied procession of tears and screaming and heat. When it was done, the flame spoke again.<br /> <br /> &quot;You must sunder your soul to break the Judges' hold. Let Devourer's Banes claim heart and shadow, so that you may be free of the Rite. With your master gone, restore your spirit to climb Sutek's ladder.&quot; <br /> <br /> Back in the present, Bast teleported out of the Shuankhsen's altar room carrying the mummified body of one of the creature's cultists. She interrogated him to extract as much information as she could, getting a list of fourteen names of fellow cultists employed at the bus terminal, the location of a safe house near Aquila's tomb, and a few facts about Shuankhsen and the way they resurrect. Namely, their enemy would be up and walking about in a day or two, probably inside someone else's body.<br /> <br /> The rest of the group walked out of the terminal without any problems, Aquila carrying their weapons underground once again. Luca and Sesu Ra went back to Sesu Ra's tomb, where they found Bast during her interrogation and pitched. in. Sesu Ra was interested in the enemy cult's presence around the Aquila/Sem-Huf territory, and they quickly discovered that the Shuankhsen had been responsible for fostering tensions between Aquila, Sem-Huf, and Mot-Tan by killing their cultists in ways that implicated one another (that cultist staked outside Aquila's tomb, which she blamed on Sem-Huf, was one prime example). Sesu Ra also found out that the Shuankhsen's followers called it Gator, something Sekhet Bastet had known for a while but I don't think anyone else in the party had discovered.<br /> <br /> The pair then discussed the situation with LDI, and how the cultists' island was likely in danger. Words that proved to be prophetic, because meanwhile...<br /> <br /> Aquila and Akenakhi reached the docks to find that their cultist there was in a panic. Several helicopters had landed on the cultists' island. While most people had been evacuated to Reza's old smuggling island, four, including Quil Mayehi (the man Aquila had resurrected when he was a stillborn infant) and Vania, the cult's historian and one of Phatri's daughters, had been taken prisoner.<br /> <br /> The two headed out immediately. They met up with Reza on the smuggling island, and quickly formed a plan. They'd walk in underground, locate the cultists, inoculate them against Sybaris using Akenakhi's make-a-Witness power, and then help them escape using Dust Beneath Feet.<br /> <br /> They meditated to restore some pillars as they waited for dusk, and then went in under cover of darkness. The few glimpses they saw of the island from underground were daunting, the place was absolutely swarming with black-clad soldiers, and there were at least three helicopters. They got lost trying to locate the cultists, but eventually found them in one of the larger buildings. Akenakhi darted off and caused a distraction, luring their guard away, and then hurried back to render them witnesses (Quil, thanks to one of the perks of resurrection via Gift of the Golden Ankh, already was one). However, he only had enough Willpower for two of them. The third would be a problem.<br /> <br /> Aquila used her Utterance on two in a quick succession, but just as she was moving up to bless the third a Greater Amkhat appeared in the room. A hulking lion with a jackal's head, bees crawling in and out of its nose and ears. Aquila and Akenakhi reacted first. Aquila blessed the third cultist, who scored a whopping six successes to resist Sybaris and so could function normally. They all threw themselves into the walls of the building, then down underground. They continued underground until they reached a neighbouring island, where they popped up again to board the waiting boat. Izman Lehn was the driver, and they were just getting aboard when he shouted and pointed behind them. The Amkhata emerged from the jungle, only metres away, and a helicopter roared overhead seconds later.<br /> <br /> Neither Akenakhi nor Aquila were any good at driving, so they couldn't do much more than hold on for dear life as they went on a hair-rising chase, weaving between islands in an attempt to lose the closely pursuing helicopter. After some truly stellar work from Izman, they were able to hide up an overhung stream while the helicopter passed them, then set off for the smuggler's island to rejoin the cult.<br /> <br /> They arrived victorious, all of the captives safe from harm. Immediately, Aquila ordered this island evacuated as well, everyone to be ferried off to that warehouse the party seized from the Pelamat in eastern Jakarta. She was worried that they might be followed. There was no sign of any LDI forces by the time the move was completed though. Aquila rode with Phatri, finding out that she'd raised the old woman from infant until she was seventeen, preventing her from marrying the whole while (Phatri made a snide joke about making up for lost time since then). Phatri never knew her birth parents, and Aquila had never told her about them.<br /> <br /> With the cultists all set up, Aquila travelled to the nearby bus terminal. After a bit of political jockeying and being passed from secretary to secretary, she eventually used her power as a Mesen-Nebu Guildmaster to simultaneously coerce and bribe the terminal's management into replacing a lot of their staff with loyal cultists. As she hadn't got her hands on that list of names Sesu Ra and Bast had discovered, she didn't know if there were still any of Gator's people on the payroll. It was enough to secure the district as under their control though, so the Families of the West edged a bit closer to gaining their next dot of Reach.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra went to the Temple in the meantime, and had a long discussion with Kotira Nahan about LDI. She'd been fighting them for a while now, ever since they forced her to pull out of the crusade against the Faithful. It turned out the rash of murders in the Golden Triangle had been down to this conflict. She sent ghosts and revenants to take out any high status, executives and public allies of the corporation that she could find, without arousing untoward suspicion, and they retaliated in kind by siccing Amkhata on her most visible cultists. The police hadn't quite put the conflict together, in part due to the supernatural nature of the crimes, and in part because Kotira's banking interests didn't seem to have any logical conflict with LDI's pharmaceutical works. She was able to tell Sesu that the best way to get rid of them was to make staying uncomfortably expensive for them. In that respect, targetting the shipping quarter down near the docks would be the best route. LDI owned their own ships, docks, and warehouses down there. Finding some way to remove them would go a long way to rendering the corporation's existence in Jakarta unsustainable. Kotira and Sesu Ra agreed to coordinate their efforts against LDI in future, before Sesu Ra moved out.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Bast rejoined, alongside Luca, to mount an attack on Gator's cult's safe house near Aquila's tomb. There was only a single cultist on guard, but Luca gunned him down. Inside they found evidence of the group's attacks on Aquila, including signs that they were planning to do another one in the near future (there was at least one pole, perfect for impaling a dead cultist, that was probably going to be used to try and incite violence between her and Sem-Huf again). There was a large amount of cash lying around, and a letter written in hieroglyphs neither of them could read. Sesu Ra grabbed the pole and impaled the dead cultist on it, sticking him up outside. The trio then scarpered before a mob could form.<br /> <br /> We skipped a couple of days, allowing each player to get back a decent amount of pillars and heal a point of aggravated damage. Reza returned with two suits of riot gear, procured through his smuggler contacts and purchased using Aquila's wealth. Aquila decided to take on Ligo as her personal assistant, having learned about this kind of &quot;modern slave&quot; concept during her political bribery efforts earlier in the session.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Bast ended the game sitting down at the table in the city's Temple, resolving to try and decode the strange piece of paper they'd recovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T01:28:12-08:00","id":318081,"title":"","content":"Session 16<br /> <br /> The meret mucked around for the first half of the session, making sure their relocated cultists were safe and doing some of their own projects. Aquila waited in her tomb for its ghost to show up. Akenakhi went to chat with the Dartlan's, but found the restaurant closed. Bast decoded the message hidden in the piece of paper they recovered, and handed it to Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rotlung grows impatient. I am not so sure I can restrain him without your supervision, lord. He is like an animal, and every day I catch him making more of the walking dead.<br /> <br /> As for the men of Chika, the other bosses are yet to come around to my way of thinking. I fear I may need to show them a miracle.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra began trying to track down Shuankhsen's cultists, using a list of names provided by the captured cultist Bast interrogated. Unfortunately, it quickly became apparent that they had been forewarned that he might be coming for them. A message left on the phone of one such vanished cultist revealed that Gator had already returned to life, and ordered his servants to abandon the area.<br /> <br /> Aquila called on Sesu Ra to help her with her ghost. It hadn't shown itself, even after 24 hours of sitting in the tomb. Sesu Ra used Chthonic Dominion destroy the extra anchor they gave to the ghost during the bank robbery, forcing it back to the tomb. Then he used the first tier to have it reveal itself.<br /> <br /> When the ghost flew at Aquila, screaming its usual babble about murder and kidnapping, she silenced it with a declaration and a promise. She would take it to see its daughter, Phatri, so long as it calmed down and stopped trying to kill her. Boosting her Presence and spending Willpower, Aquila was able to completely dominate it. When it agreed, she asked to hear its story, to explain what had happened.<br /> <br /> Phatri's mother revealed that Aquila killed her, and her husband, and most of their village. They were living out in the islands, and had no ties to the supernatural that she knew. They were innocent, when she appeared in the village and began to kill. As the ghost described the events of her death, a series of rapid flashbacks ran through Aquila's head. She saw herself standing over dismembered bodies, dispatching pleading injured victims as they tried to crawl away, decapitating Phatri's father and running through her mother, until she heard the sound of an infant crying. She remembered her gladius dropping from her hand, the sound of it striking the floor, and the vision ended.<br /> <br /> Shocked and disturbed, and more than a little confused at her own actions, Aquila had Sesu Ra bind the ghost into a knife so she could carry it to Phatri. By this point, Sesu Ra was getting a bit grumpy at the constant drain on his pillars, so Aquila offered him something in exchange. A painting depicting events of his prior life, that she had made long ago.<br /> <br /> (For those in need of a reminder, this was a reproduction of the stele Aquila remembered tracking down in order to give to Sesu Ra so that he could destroy it, back during the period when he was actively seeking to annihilate his own memory.)<br /> <br /> They took the knife to Phatri and told her that the spirit of her mother wished to speak to her. However, the group wasn't entirely abreast on ghost mechanics, so they failed to account for the fact that the presence of all the other cultists would mean that the ghost would be functionally unable to manifest. After nothing happened for a while, Aquila left to arrange for more permanent accommodation for the cultists, since the warehouse was increasingly proving unsuitable.<br /> <br /> Before she left, she had the time to locate the painted image for Sesu Ra. He looked upon an stylised depiction of himself, according to the accompanying Iremite script, working on the completion of an immense statue. It triggered a very brief flashback (truncated by Sesu Ra's Memory 2) of standing among a crowd in ancient Irem, slaves and fellow craftsmen all around. The sky above shimmered with magic, as the walls fell away to reveal the masterpiece he had toiled upon for so many years. The vision ended before he could get a proper look at the statue, however.<br /> <br /> At the end of the session, Akenakhi managed to avoid successes on his Descent check. The session did have to be cut a bit short, and we've ended up rescheduling our weekly game to the weekend. It'll be a bit longer than usual until the next write-up, as a result. On the plus side, I hope to have something interesting to post up between now and then, but it will probably deserve its own topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T15:41:18-08:00","id":320223,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say thank you for posting these, as a new Mummy ST...this has been very helpful in settling the game foundation and just an amazingly interesting series. I'm about to run myself and I hope i can be half as interesting as yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T15:44:37-08:00","id":320226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfrantz2361</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=320223#post320223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say thank you for posting these, as a new Mummy ST...this has been very helpful in settling the game foundation and just an amazingly interesting series. I'm about to run myself and I hope i can be half as interesting as yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw shucks. That honestly means a lot. I really hope you'll take the time to share your experiences with the game once you start running it. I love reading what other STs have been up to, particularly in Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T16:02:50-08:00","id":320233,"title":"","content":"I will gladly. Please thank your players on my behalf too. I only have one player right now so it will be a small focused story, but we usually can tell a very personalized and intimate story that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4371-mfrantz2361","name":"mfrantz2361","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T16:20:33-08:00","id":320237,"title":"","content":"It sounds very interesting. I've never tried to run a game with only one player.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the Deceived game I'm about to start only has two at the moment, so it's close. Even that is smaller than what I'm used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T05:24:09-08:00","id":325211,"title":"","content":"Session 17<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra accessed the computers in his tower (his relic making it easy) in order to discover the significance of the phrase &quot;men of Chika&quot; from the last session. He quickly found one, Chika Productions, a motorbike, autorickshaw, and car manufacturing plant in East Jakarta. He called up Luca and sent cultists to find the others, certain that this business must be in some way tied to Gator.<br /> <br /> Aquila, meanwhile, was checking in with the cult. She'd arranged for most of them to move in to new apartments in the area surrounding the warehouse base. Phatri still hadn't received any ghostly communication from her mother, but Rom Mayehi reported that he'd been suffering from terrible dreams. He was reluctant to speak about them, and Aquila virtually had to interrogate him to find out what they concerned. It became apparent that Rom had been involved in some anti-Chinese riots/pogroms some years before. He'd killed one or two people, but the event hadn't ever bothered his conscience before. Now though, every night for the past week he'd been plagued by nightmares. Aquila was appalled to hear of the behaviour of her cult's hierophant, but calmed her initial rage by remembering that she herself had done some terrible things.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi arranged for some cultists to form contacts and allies among the police, justification for spending experience on those merits.<br /> <br /> And then everyone gathered at Sesu Ra's tower for a briefing on the situation at hand. He explained that the note led them to Chika Productions, and the group, along with Luca, headed there immediately. They were initially treated with a mixture of puzzlement and suspicion by the men there, who weren't used to seeing well-dressed foreigners walking around their rather filthy and dangerous production plant. The closest thing to authorities on sight were the work crew bosses, so the group persuaded a man, Tega, to take them to meet one of those bosses. Aquila became furious when Tega laughed off her initial intimidation attempt, especially at the patronising way he treated her after that, and fumed quietly when Sesu Ra was able to persuade him quite easily to let them inside.<br /> <br /> They met two of the plant's bosses in a quick succession, Donny and Dimah, both middle-aged men in charge of shifts at the plant. The plant itself was a mess, ancient, dangerous machinery, terrible working conditions, no real safety clothing for anyone but the bosses themselves, and with many of the workers showing signs of exhaustion and previous injury. Donny wasn't much help, but Dimah implicitly confirmed some information when he went on the defensive and swore that he'd never met Rotlung. Sesu Ra waited until his shift ended, tailed Dimah home, and ambushed him in his house alongside Luca. They were able to intimidate him easily, helped by Sesu Ra's use of Dominating Might to smash down the front door with his bare fists, tie him to a chair, and interrogate him. A third boss, Ratger, had told Dimah that there was a lot of money to be made if they followed the instructions of a mysterious benefactor. In addition, a man named Rotlung would be around to handle any problems that might arise. Sesu Ra decided to gag Dimah and leave him tied to his chair, figuring that he'd eventually be rescued, and walked out.<br /> <br /> Aquila was mucking about trying to find the plant's fourth boss, Yayian Masari. She'd heard he was Tega's immediate superior and was hoping to get him fired. A few failed rolls though, and she was forced to concede defeat in the face of stubborn and patronising workers who refused to tell her where to find him.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Sesu Ra and Luca returned to tell the group that Ratger was manning the late shift and wouldn't clock out until midnight. They camped within sight of the compound's entrance, but by 1am he still hadn't emerged. The group went to investigate. The compound seemed abandoned, no security or anything, until they entered the main plant. Akenakhi was scouting ahead with Palace Knows Its Pharaoh and spotted an Awakened Servant walking a patrol. Luca charged in and beat the thing to death, ripping off limbs with his bare hands, much to the admiration of the watching Arisen.<br /> <br /> There were two warehouses left to explore, so the group split. Luca and and Aquila headed for the closest, Akenakhi and Sesu Ra went towards the other. However, as Aquila and Luca were halfway to the second warehouse when motion sensors kicked in and lit them up with floodlights. Then, the door of the warehouse opened and a huge horde of zombies spilled out. The group counted about twenty in all, too many for them to easily fight. Aquila dropped beneath the ground. Sesu Ra and Akenakhi hid off to one side, and Sesu Ra telepathically ordered Luca to draw the zombies away. Luca ran for it, running back into the manufacturing plant and using the overhead walkways to keep out of reach of the zombies as they chased him. He finally leapt out through a second story window to escape, made it to the car, and drove a safe distance away to wait for the others.<br /> <br /> With the zombie horde busy, the rest of the group headed for the warehouse. Aquila was ahead of the others, not having to wait for the zombies to move, so she snuck in and found two men inside. One matched their description of Ratger, a man wearing a doctor's mask, hard hat, long-sleeved clothing and pants, and a set of gloves. Only the skin around his eyes was easily visible. Dimah had said under interrogation that he started wearing the heavier clothing and mask around the plant a month or two ago, complaining about a chest infection from the fumes. The other she assumed was Rotlung, a disgusting creature that was barely recognisable as human. Every inch of skin seemed to be cracked, weeping, oozing, or coated in scar tissue. When he spoke, his words were slurred as he hissed through broken teeth. He was wearing nothing but a pair of tattered shorts. The two were arguing, Ratger saying their instructions were to flee when someone matching the description of the Arisen showed up. Rotlung said he would rather bring their heads to his master.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra hadn't brought his khopesh, so he made do with a massive wrench he found in the main plant. He walked up to the warehouse, banging the wrench against the wall as he went. The sound clearly worried Ratger, but it gave Rotlung time to get his knife out. When Sesu Ra and Akenakhi entered through the front entrance, Rotlung smiled at them, licked his curved blade, and said, &quot;I have waited long to taste Arisen flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> The group started combat. Aquila failed to drain Rotlung's Willpower, Rotlung successfully gave Phobia (Rotlung) to Sesu Ra, Sesu Ra was able to resist the Phobia triggering and unleashed Blessed Is The God King, and Akenakhi used the second tier of Palace Knows Its Pharoah to throw a moped into Rotlung. Ratger found a hammer lying around and watched nervously. Then Aquila rose from the ground and struck Rotlung from behind. He spun around, saw her, and seemed both surprised and pleased. He hissed something about taking her head back to his master and stabbed her with his knife. When it did aggravated damage, the group realised that all the rolls I'd been making them do (that they'd failed) were Kepher rolls, and that they were up against a relic.<br /> <br /> Ratger charged at Sesu Ra to try and slow him down. Aquila, not wanting to die again, hid beneath the ground to avoid further aggravated damage. Rotlung responded by charging Akenakhi, who had dealt a considerable amount of damage by throwing first the moped, and then a long javelin-esque pole of metal at him. In a single blow, Rotlung carved into Akenakhi and filled his health with aggravated damage. It was at this point that Sesu Ra's player got a bit exasperated at the fact that he was the only character who ever bothered to boost Stamina before a fight.<br /> <br /> Since he was the only one standing against the two combatants, and his ghost protector was apparently not intervening, Sesu Ra put his priorities on Rotlung. Akenakhi was able to stay functional by Sealing the Flesh, using Revelations of Smoke and Flame to scour Rotlung with blasts of smoke and ash. Mostly though, Sesu Ra kept Rotlung knocked to the ground with repeated blows from his massive wrench. Rotlung's retaliation was to scream obscenities and stab Sesu Ra repeatedly in the leg and foot from where he lay, while Ratger tried to club Sesu Ra from behind. They weren't able to make it through all of Sesu Ra's temporary health, however, before Sesu Ra leapt onto Rotlung's back, overpowered him, and turned the relic knife against its wielder to slit Rotlung's own throat. Seconds later, Akenakhi's attempt to Seal the Flesh expired and he died.<br /> <br /> Rather than face Sesu Ra alone, Ratger ran for it. He bolted out the front door the warehouse, but Sesu Ra ran him down. The motion sensitive floodlights came on again, providing stark lighting for the tableau that unfolded. Despite his sobs and screams and fighting like a cornered animal, Ratger wasn't able to stop Sesu Ra from knocking him to the ground and beating him with the wrench until his skull caved in and he lay still.<br /> <br /> Aquila was a bit annoyed at Sesu Ra for not leaving anyone alive to interrogate. Sesu Ra shrugged off the criticism. Aquila briefly explored the other warehouse, found it contained two more Awakened Servants, and backed out quickly. She made it back to the first warehouse to find Sesu Ra examining the relic knife. Thanks to his Model Lifeweb Affinity, Sesu Ra determined that it was a weak Uter, a komodo dragon's claw set on a haft of wood. Those struck by it started bleeding out, just as if their health was filled with lethal damage, causing them to take a point of bashing damage every minute until treatment. Its curse was something Sesu Ra had already experienced. The claw thirsted for blood, granting a bonus to anyone who grappled its wielder and used it to turn the blade back on the user. Sesu Ra pocketed it, intending to give it to Sekhet Bastet at the earliest opportunity.<br /> <br /> The zombies that had chased Luca were returning. Sesu Ra made some hasty preparations. He found everything flammable he could, rigged the warehouse to burn down, and grabbed Ratger and Akenakhi's bodies. Rotlung's he drenched in flammable liquids, hoping it would prevent the creature from returning to life. They waited then until the zombies entered the warehouse, Aquila blessed Sesu Ra with Dust Beneath Feet, and they dove underground as the building, with all the zombies inside, began to burn.<br /> <br /> They met up with Luca, Sesu Ra sending a telepathic order to come and pick them up. Searching Ratger's body, Sesu Ra found a reply to the earlier message he'd discovered. &quot;Rotlung is your elder, slave. I expect you to follow his commands, not question them. As for the miracle, I expect my Fasad to succeed in their tasks without my help. Fail, and I shall replace you.&quot;<br /> <br /> And on that note (heh), we wrapped up. First thing next session, another Death Cycle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-30-2014, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T04:08:04-08:00","id":329993,"title":"","content":"Awesome story! This definitely helps to highlight the themes of Mummy, and is very helpful for spawning new ideas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:21:12-08:00","id":330637,"title":"","content":"Thanks man. I'm really happy people are getting some real use out of these write-ups.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any critiques/criticisms of the game so far, I'd love to hear them. Any ideas that might make it better are wholly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T05:02:54-08:00","id":332153,"title":"","content":"Session 18<br /> <br /> Aquila's player couldn't make it to this session. We started out with Akenakhi's Death Cycle. After meeting with Anpu, he found himself in France, reading a libellous pamphlet slurring a member of the aristocracy. It wasn't the content that interested him, however, but rather the code he recognised. It was from someone he had known, someone he had loved, but all he could glean from the work was that it was telling him to seek out more books of the same type.<br /> <br /> So he did so. He wandered to a nearby back alley bookstore he knew, where he found a Dutch man arguing with the owner. They were speaking a language he didn't understand, but he noticed an Iremite symbol tattooed on the neck of the Dutch man. Intrigued, Akenakhi slipped a knuckle bone he owned into the Dutch man's pocket. He would be able to track the item, so he waited for the Dutch man to leave and found the book he was looking for, &quot;Scandals of the Scarron Dynasty&quot;. Then he took off, tracking his mark.<br /> <br /> He followed the man through the streets until they reached the large opening to a man-made cavern. Black-shrouded caravans were rolling through the door, and the Dutch man wandered in. Akenakhi snuck in after him and observed him talking to someone else in the same language from before, one he didn't know. He accosted the target after the meeting, demanding to know the meaning of the tattoo on his neck. The huge blonde man seemed a bit bemused by all this. He said some friends had given him the tattoo when he served aboard a naval vessel, but he was willing enough to show Akenakhi the tattoo in more detail. It turned out that it read &quot;Heart of Nenheta&quot;. Akenakhi discovered that the man now served with the East India Company, and asked about Nenheta. For a moment the man looked stricken, and then the memory dissolved.<br /> <br /> The next part of the memory took place some days later. Akenakhi managed to decode the message within the book he bought. It listed three places. The first, the catacombs. The second, he couldn't remember, the word appeared blurry in his memory. The third, Batavia.<br /> <br /> He woke in the present to find that Sesu Ra had wrapped his body and placed it within his sarcophagus, shortening his Death Cycle to just half an hour. He immediately meditated to regenerate some lost pillars.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra had been doing the same. When he emerged from his tomb, he sent a cultist to ask Yarikh to meet him at the temple to discuss the meaning of the word &quot;Fasad&quot;. His own attempts to research the word, at least beyond its modern meaning, frustrated him. As he was leaving, his False Incarnation derangement triggered, and he found himself pursuing a man on motorbike by jumping in a nearby taxi. He ended up outside a large, closed down building, watching the man duck beneath the tape closing off the entrance, and got out to follow.<br /> <br /> Inside there was a large squatter settlement. Sesu Ra seized the man he was chasing and dragged him back outside. He was convinced that the man had been a slave of his back in Irem, working on the construction of the monument he had remembered unveiling. He was demanding to know what the &quot;slave&quot; knew of his projects, when the man started sobbing and said that he'd just been paid to keep an eye on Sesu Ra by a woman concerned for his safety. Apparently this woman was just upstairs, so Sesu Ra dragged his new slave up two flights of stairs and...<br /> <br /> Found himself staring at a dozen Pelamat, some of whom he recognised from previous encounters. Both sides were somewhat stunned. A long moment passed, and then the Pelamat snatched up their weapons and Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed Is The God King.<br /> <br /> The following fight was absolutely gruelling. Sesu Ra strode through the horde of attackers like a Bronze Age hero made manifest, cutting down a man with nearly every blow. His ghostly protector possessed one of the gun armed Pelamat, and distracted two other men in a fight that ended in the death of both the possessed character and one of his opponents. Sybaris took four of the Pelamat out of the fight, but the remaining eight were nearly enough to kill Sesu Ra. Despite being Size 7, Stamina 10, and temporarily manifesting Living Monolith with Ka 5, he ended severely damaged by the time he cut down his final opponent. He'd taken 17 aggravated damage. The gore-splattered room was quiet for a moment, and then he quickly dispatched the cowering, Sybaris-infected survivors. The man that had been the subject of his False Incarnation derangement had long since fled. By some Judge-given miracle, Sesu Ra was able to avoid failing his degeneration check for this act of mass murder by putting his faith in Set-Qesu.<br /> <br /> There was a door to the next room. From behind it, Sesu Ra could hear someone playing music, jazz, loud enough to drown out the sound of the fight. At least, that's what he hoped. Still resplendent in God King form, he threw open the doorway and strode in.<br /> <br /> The room he found himself in was filled with contrasts. It had all the hallmarks of an abandoned building, from exposed maintenance work, a lack of wallpaper, and a general sense of incompleteness. Someone had chosen to decorate it with luxury furniture, including a truly opulent lounge. Curled up like cats at the base of this lounge were a pair of naked men. Reclining above them was what appeared to be a young Indonesian woman, tapping her foot in time to the music.<br /> <br /> Then the record ended, Sesu Ra moved, and the woman looked up and met his eyes. In that moment, Sesu Ra felt a rush of emotions. Hatred, love, shame, and a horrible, aching sense of loss. The woman flinched back, looked out towards the room's balcony, and screamed, &quot;No. No, no, no, no, no! Rangarni!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra demanded to know who she was. He spotted the tell-tale flickering of a khat moving beneath the sahu, a sure sign that she was some form of Mummy. She refused to answer him, babbling instead that he wasn't meant to be here and studiously avoiding further eye contact. Then Rangarni walked in from the balcony. He looked different from the last time Sesu Ra had seen him, sporting open, weeping sores on his face and hands, and a definite discolouration of his skin. He looked nervously from Sesu Ra to the woman and back.<br /> <br /> To Sesu Ra's frustration, no one seemed interested in answering his question. The woman demanded that Rangarni remove Sesu Ra. Rangarni quietly asked the woman, calling her Iwseck, to follow him out of the room. The two naked men seemed oblivious to the proceedings, watching on with blank, staring eyes.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Iwseck and Rangarni backed out to the balcony. Sesu Ra made one last demand that they tell him why the Pelamat had been so determined to kill them. The woman looked straight at him, and he saw she was crying. She spoke an Utterance, manifesting great wings of smoke and flame. Rangarni followed suit a second later. Then the pair leapt over the balcony and disappeared. Blessed Is The God King ended moments later, and Sesu Ra felt fate's curse settle on him for squandering its majesty. He sent a mental message for Luca to come and find him, and stood among the wreckage as he waited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:09:00-08:00","id":333740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=320237#post320237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, the Deceived game I'm about to start only has two at the moment, so it's close. Even that is smaller than what I'm used to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there annnnnnnnnny way for one to get in on this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:15:33-08:00","id":333761,"title":"","content":"A time machine capable of getting you to Australia two days ago would be a good start <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You can live vicariously through the players though by reading the other Actual Play thread I'm posting in this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T05:07:38-08:00","id":338963,"title":"","content":"Session 19<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra waited for Luca to show up at the squatter's building where he had confronted the Pelamat. They searched Iwseck's room together, and found a collection of photographs inside her dresser. They ranged from black-and-white to digital printouts, all of Sesu Ra in a variety of locations scattered across the past century. They searched a little more, didn't find anything else of interest, and then caught a ride back to the Temple. Sesu Ra met Akenakhi there, and shared the story of his fight and the strange conversation he'd had with Iwseck. A short while later Aquila showed up, and together they all waited for Yarikh.<br /> <br /> The Speaker to the Thrice-Dead showed up at the appointed time, and the group started bombarding him with questions about the various supernatural terms they had uncovered over the last little while. Sesu Ra discovered that Fasad were the Shuankhsen equivalent to Sadikh, but that Yarikh had heard rumours that a single Shuankhsen could manage multiple Fasad at a time. Aquila learnt a few interesting facts about ghosts, their corpus, and ways they could be destroyed/persuaded to pass on. And then Akenakhi asked about the phrase &quot;climb Sutek's ladder&quot;. Yarikh shut the conversation down. He curtly informed them that he hadn't ever heard the phrase, but that Sutek was held, according to mythology, to be the deity responsible for Azar's death and subsequent ascension to the throne of Duat. Akenakhi seemed satisfied by this response, but when Yarikh wasn't looking he cut off part of one of his own fingers and dropped it into Yarikh's pocket, letting him track where the other Mummy went.<br /> <br /> When Yarikh had left, Aquila asked Sesu Ra to use Chthonic Dominion so that she could converse with her ghost. She was perplexed about why it hadn't yet appeared to Phatri. When they did so, the exasperated ghost explained that she hadn't been able to touch manifest in the presence of so many mortals. Since Phatri had been moved out of the warehouse and into a new apartment, they took the ghost there immediately. The three Mummies waited outside while Phatri and her mother spoke, leaving the ghost in the room along with the ghost-light from Chthonic Dominion. After about an hour, they heard Phatri called to them and walked inside. The light was still there, but the ghost was gone. Phatri said that she had simply faded, and asked that they leave her alone for a little while. She had a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> The group went back to their warehouse to discuss what to do next. Aquila wanted the cult to move away from its tribal foundation, to become a legitimate enterprise dedicated to improving the lives of the lower classes. The others had no particular objections to this, neither caring all that much about what activities their cultists were engaged in. Akenakhi couldn't trust any of them due to his personal pursuit of Apotheosis, and Sesu Ra generally considered his cultists to be rather beneath his notice. Ligo was dispatched to see about laying the groundwork for the shift.<br /> <br /> They waited a bit over a week, allowing their bodies to heal a little from the confrontation with Gator/Rotlung and to gather some information on their next move. Aquila began working as a volunteer at a medical clinic in a West Jakarta slum, the opposite side of the city to the slums ruled by Mot-Tan and Sem-Huf. She had a few initial problems with local medical personnel noticing strange quirks about her undying state, but she gradually got better at emulating vital signs. Sesu Ra, meanwhile, was using Luca's connections and spying skills to find out about two potential targets, an LDI owned section of the docks and the ghost-worshipped cult in the Old Dutch Quarter of Kota. He'd decided that the threat posed by each of them needed to be removed, but wasn't sure which one to strike at first.<br /> <br /> He discovered that a massive tanker, the <i>Sethis</i>, was due into port in the next few weeks. It was owned by LDI, and would be carrying a cargo of medical supplies alongside certain items that the company had secured permission to bring into the country without first clearing customs. It presented ample opportunity to demonstrate to the company that continued operations in Jakarta would not be a profitable endeavour. Security would be exceptionally tight, of course, and they would have to be careful about how they went about it if they wanted to avoid bringing a city-wide manhunt down on their own heads.<br /> <br /> In Kota, the Temple the cultists used to worship Mannfred was obviously the main target. It was a symbol of their faith and presumably either was, or contained, Mannfred's principle anchor. Destroying it would be a great blow to the ghost, and killing the ghost himself would rob them of their supernatural backing. They'd already lost the Blasphemous Depiction, so they wouldn't be able to replace any zombies that they lost either.<br /> <br /> After a bit of debate, Sesu Ra declared that Kota would be the target. It seemed like the softer option, they all still had a bit of damage from their trials, and it presented the opportunity to add a few more ghost servants to Sesu Ra's menagerie in preparation for the larger confrontation.<br /> <br /> They went to back to the museum first. Sesu Ra recalled dominating one of the ghosts there on his last visit, and was interested in recruiting it. The group entered the museum in daylight hours, snuck into the rooms under renovation, and broke into the ceremonial room where the Blasphemous Depiction once was used. Sesu Ra sent his ghost-light into the chamber beneath, and saw the female ghost (the one he hadn't dominated) staring back. He immediately guessed that it must have destroyed the ghost he had controlled, it wasn't likely that the pair could be co-existing after he commanded the male one to turn on its allies. On the plus side, that meant he would be able to seize the creature with the banshee wail.<br /> <br /> There was a surge of movement, and the zombie he fought last time lurched out of the hole to attack. Sesu Ra kept it knocked to the ground, although the wailing spirit proved to be a bit of a pest as it caused each of the characters involved to lose at least a single turn of combat with its banshee screams. When the zombie finally stopped moving, they bundled it up in sheets from the renovation equipment and crept out, after Sesu Ra was able to bind the ghost to himself and force it to protect him from harm.<br /> <br /> The others had their cultists take the zombie's remains to be burnt continuously for the next 24 hours, while Sesu Ra returned to his tomb. Selecting one of the corpses he'd had preserved, the corpse of a member of the LDI acquisition's team, he used the Blasphemous Depiction to bind the banshee into it. He commanded it to guard his tomb and protect it from intruders, thinking that its scream Numen would help it against larger numbers.<br /> <br /> That night, the meret assembled near the temple for its assault. Aquila and Reza showed up wearing the riot gear they'd had smuggled to them. Sesu Ra and Luca carried the best weapons they could bring from their selection. Akenakhi had spent some time regenerating his pillars in preparation for the confrontation, and temporarily made Reza a witness.<br /> <br /> We called an end to the session just before they began their attack. It was good to have a session to plan, heal, and take stock, and we decided we could easily leave the next big fight until later. When &quot;later&quot; will be, however, is another matter. We'll all be pretty busy for the next two weeks, but hopefully there'll be time before the new year to have one more game. If not, I guess we're back in January.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T04:27:02-08:00","id":365319,"title":"","content":"Session 20<br /> <br /> &quot;Let's see who's been paying attention.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi has reached Memory 5, so we ran a flashback for him. It seemed to be taking place during at the time he first arrived in the city, believed to be 1916/1917. Unlike most of his flashbacks, this one was particularly abstract and vague. He remembered an item, the Rod of Tjesh, that he had made in life and passed to another. He remembered walking through the city streets, but they were shrouded in mist and seemed to curve in on themselves. Everyone he spoke to was faceless and spoke in a seemingly androgynous murmur, their exact words a mystery. And always, in the distance, was a glow that he knew indicated the place of the Rod. He wandered aimlessly, until he heard a snarl.<br /> <br /> He was attacked by a hulking, cat-like creature with the head of a worm. Rings of teeth glinted in the dull light. It leapt at him, and he dove out of the way. It faded into the mist.<br /> <br /> Then he heard Aquila's voice calling. He stood torn. He heard her promise oblivion, safety, and a chance to mourn. But the glow of the relic beckoned stronger still. He chose the relic over safe oblivion. The vision faded, to be replaced with the sound of a storm. Waves as high as castle walls were accompanied by the sound of splintering wood. The relic had been lost at sea.<br /> <br /> We cut back then to the group on the verge of storming Manfred von Schuss's hideout. Aquila scouted out the area first, and alerted everyone that the basement walls were packed with corpses, probably for use as zombies. They figured that Manfred's corpse was likely his anchor, and that they could just go in via Dust Beneath Feet, drag it underground, and pulp it. Akenakhi and Reza waited outside while Aquila, Luca, and Sesu Ra went in underground.<br /> <br /> The plan didn't go as expected. Luca was detected trying to grab the corpse, and the ground seemed to come alive with grasping hands. He leapt out of the earth and triggered Blessed is the God King, transforming into the form of an immense bull-headed being just as the zombies surged from the walls. Sesu Ra joined his Sadikh a moment later and started to battle the zombies, while Aquila rolled her eyes and kept firmly underground.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, meanwhile, felt the surge of Sekhem from the unleashing and charged inside, to be confronted by a group of four cultists. He unleashed the second tier of Revelations of Smoke and Flame, driving three of the cultists away in the grip of Terror Sybaris and inciting the remaining one to attack him. In the frenzied fighting that followed he nearly killed the man by flaying him with the Utterance's first tier. He struggled to decide between helping his meret mate and staying behind to treat the man, but ultimately decided that retrieving Aquila would give him better odds of keeping the man alive.<br /> <br /> The fight against the zombies was going slowly. The grasping hands fell inert, and Sesu Ra unleashed the first tier of Chthonic Dominion to reveal Twilight dwellers locked in combat. Sesu Ra's ghostly guardian was grappling with Manfred, a battle that mirrored the fight against the zombies. Knowing that the animate corpses wouldn't be slowed terribly by mere lethal damage, Sesu Ra and Luca both chose to fought with manifested weapons of light and darkness granted by their God King status. They drove poisoned rot into the flesh of their undead enemies as the ghostly battle raged on.<br /> <br /> Finally, Manfred gained the upper hand. He seemed about to overwhelm Sesu Ra's guardian when Sesu Ra turned away from the zombies he was fighting. The Arisen raised a hand and called on the third tier of Chthonic Dominion to strip away Manfred's Anchors. Manfred was an old, old ghost, almost impossibly hard to effect with the Utterance, but by a stroke of luck it worked. Anchors severed, Manfred vanished. The zombies crumpled the moment he was gone.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Akenakhi went upstairs, where Aquila used Healing Counsel to restore the injured man. Sesu Ra wandered across the road, after returning to his more mortal-seeming, to speak with the old man Jonah who had once been a follower of his. He told Jonah that the Families of the West would be moving into the area, and they expected his help in securing the architecturally important sites like the district's museum. Jonah was happy to help.<br /> <br /> The player cult went up a point of Reach from this acquisition, bringing them to Reach 2, Grasp 2.<br /> <br /> After the fight, the meret left to restore their pillars and rest. Aquila had noticed something was up with Rom, however. He hadn't been sleeping well, and there had been more than a few instances of strange behaviour. After a period of intense semi-interrogation on her part, she managed to persuade him to cough up some unpleasant details about his involvement in anti-Chinese race riots in his youth. He said he'd been dreaming about the event a lot recently, it seemed to be plaguing him. While more than a little discomforted by the knowledge that her hierophant was so prejudiced towards others, Aquila was also convinced that he was being literally haunted by a spectre from his past. She called in Sesu Ra for some help with the matter.<br /> <br /> The two Arisen spent the night with Rom, probing his room with the werelight from the first tier of Chthonic Dominion, but no spirits were in evidence. At last, as dawn broke, Rom woke screaming. Sesu Ra mulled over the situation a little, and pointed out that the symptoms could be explained by the use of Dreams of Dead Gods. Or perfectly mundane trauma, but the two Arisen dismissed that option more or less out of hand. They didn't know of any Mummy in the city with the Utterance in question, but Aquila was willing to venture a guess. There was one Mummy in Jakarta known to dwell in the ethnically Chinese sections of the city, who might have been wronged by Rom's actions in the past. Hetenatra, the Lady of the Broken Stele.<br /> <br /> When they gathered the next day, Akenakhi had exciting news that temporarily drove the matter from their minds. He'd located a shipwreck using Kepher, the resting place of a relic just off the coast of Jakarta and somewhere in the Thousand Isles. The group took a boat and headed out.<br /> <br /> They found the island, a large, uninhabited place covered in jungle, without too many difficulties. A bit of digging on the beach found the ship's figurehead buried in a mound of sand, but the rest of the ship was beneath the waves. Not much of an obstacle to undead beings. They went for a walk.<br /> <br /> That was when it became apparent that it was going to be a bit more difficult than a mere walk. A small group of reef sharks set upon them as the light began to fade. As the group fought them, they saw something huge approaching. Already in danger of being overwhelmed, they slipped beneath the sand one by one as Aquila passed on the blessing from Dust Beneath the Feet. Sesu Ra was the last to go, and saw what the approaching monstrosity actually looked like. It was a great swarm of fish, an impossibly great school of hundreds of different species. The host bore down on the group, but they were under the sand and away before they could be reached.<br /> <br /> They came to the shipwreck before long, guided by Akenakhi's Kepher. Locating the relic among the collapsing ruin was more difficult than expected however, especially when the fish school arrived. It swept through the shipwreck, battering the group into walls. They raced for what was left of the hold, and barred themselves in. Sesu Ra held the door shut against the fish, who were busy battering themselves senseless on the doorway, and Akenakhi found the relic lying in what remained of an old chest, long since rotted. The group smashed their way out of the shipwreck as the fish, joined by the sharks, came through the door. They slipped beneath the ground and got away, heading back to the island.<br /> <br /> When they arrived, they found crocodiles draped across their boat. A growl came from the jungle. A swarm of seabirds circled in the sky. As the animals closed in, they heard a voice speaking Iremite.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who dares trespass?&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi had already slipped beneath the ground at the first sign of danger, and missed the words. Sesu Ra strode forward and declared himself, &quot;the Unbending Spine, Guildmaster of the Tef-Aabhi.&quot; There was a pause, and the animals dispersed. Then, from the jungle, came a human figure and a large tiger.<br /> <br /> The woman looked like a pale Chinese woman in her early thirties, but it wasn't long before the group noticed the signs of unlife that marked her as a Mummy. She introduced herself as Nenheta, a hermit of the Su-Menent. The Rod of Tjesh was hers, she said, and they had no right to rob her.<br /> <br /> That was when Akenakhi emerged from the ground. The two stared at one another, stunned, for several long moments. Akenakhi recognised her, despite her changed features. A frenzied conversation in French followed, each expressing their amazement at seeing the other after so many centuries.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi made things different, Nenheta said addressing the group at large. The Rod was his, after all. The other two returned to Jakarta, saying they would send a cultist with a ship back to pick up Akenakhi. The two spoke of earlier times, and of their respective hunts for Apotheosis. Akenakhi shared that he was sure Yarikh knew something that they didn't, and Nenheta cautioned him. Su-Menent collecting information on Apotheosis could be dangerous, themselves notwithstanding. It was all too possible that he was using the information to seek out heretics, a fanatic ready to destroy them at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> During this conversation, she revealed that her plan had been to live as a hermit as long as she could out in these islands. No other Arisen in Jakarta knew she was out here. She begged Akenakhi to not let his friends reveal her presence to any others.<br /> <br /> After he agreed, something seemed to startle her. She left with the words, &quot;Goodbye my love. I could not be more pleased that you are here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Back on the mainland, Aquila was meditating again at the temple. She'd chosen to abandon her tomb near Sem-Huf's territory, planning on building a new one, but she didn't want to abandon the people to his rule. She'd heard of a woman who was leading some kind of resistance to the Sons, Sem-Huf's cultists, and resolved to meet her.<br /> <br /> A search of the slum led her to the doorstep of the old widow Wuldanri. Her grandson, a big, burly man named Pukta, answered the door. He didn't want to let her in, immediately suspicious of Aquila based on her look and fluent grasp of Indonesian, but she talked her way past him. Wuldanri, in turn, proved to be an old, hunched over woman who eyed Aquila with hostility from the very start. She didn't know what Aquila was, but she had no doubt that she was related in some way to the unnatural thing that lurked at the top of the tower the Sons called home.<br /> <br /> Aquila didn't deny this. Instead, she offered knowledge and help. She would provide funding, and weapons, to anyone Wuldanri could gather to fight this creature. She would even provide her own powers to heal the injured. She revealed that fire would help vanquish it. Meanwhile, the Sons could be broken by building new homes in the area, she thought, stealing away their grip on shelter and employment in the region. If they tried to fight back, automatic weapons and body armour could be made available to the locals.<br /> <br /> A good deal, Wuldanri called it. Ever since Pukta had returned to her after working for the Sons, telling stories of sorcerers and spirits, she had been afraid for her friends and family. For the first time, she had hope that she could vanquish the monster. With Aquila's backing, the Arisen would be driven from this corner of Jakarta...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 01-11-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T12:25:22-08:00","id":365613,"title":"","content":"And for those interested, the following is the full write-up of the relic they discovered:<br /> <br /> The Rod of Tjesh (3 dot Uter)<br /> Size 3, Durability 3, Structure 6<br /> <br /> <i>The Rod of Tjesh was wielded by those of the Su-Menent who needed to pass unnoticed. It appears to be a slim bone rod, about four feet long. Its head is wrapped in golden wire and topped with a stylised scarab. Beneath this ornamentation it is flat and featureless, except for the very bottom of the rod. It has been capped with mother of pearl, and impressed with a single hieroglyph that no one can read. Looking it it too long gives the unpleasant sensation that something is crawling behind one's eyes.</i><br /> <br /> Power: The Rod of Tjesh bores into the mind of the one that wields it. It feeds on everything that makes the wielder who they are, leaving them faceless, nameless, and almost impossible to notice. When its power ends, the wieldder recovers their identity... but not always entirely intact.<br /> Activating the Rod requires the user to forfeit all their current Willpower points. They must have at least one point to sacrifice, the Rod will not work for those who have nothing to give. So long as it is active, the bearer has no Virtue or Vice.<br /> In return, the bearer gains anonymity. They will pass unnoticed in any crowd. Guards will not notice them on their rounds. Sentries will let them pass unchallenged. This works only as long as another &quot;group&quot; is allowed in the area, a category of people outside of those assigned to protect it. Any guards will assume the bearer belongs to that group. Witnesses and magical beings are immune to this effect.<br /> The effect lasts one scene.<br /> <br /> Curse: At the end of the scene, the Storyteller rolls a Chance Die. On a success, the bearer regains a Willpower point. On a Failure, nothing happens. On a Dramatic Failure, the bearer loses a Willpower Dot.<br /> Su-Menent roll an ordinary die instead of a Chance Die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T13:03:25-08:00","id":373702,"title":"","content":"Session 21<br /> <br /> Aquila rose to Memory 5, and so began her next flashback. She was back in Ancient Rome, in a slave\u2019s quarters, and discussing the upcoming rebellion with a young gladiator. For a moment, the version of her that was watching recognised the young man. She\u2019d seen him spitted on Roman blades in one of her earlier flashbacks. Both of them were excited, tonight would be the night they slipped their chains.<br /> <br /> After the gladiator had left, Yarikh spoke from somewhere in the room behind her. He warned her that this was doomed to fail. Aquila shrugged. She had to try. With a heavy sigh, Yarikh told her that she knew where he stood, and left.<br /> <br /> The vision skipped forward. In the distance, Aquila could hear the escaped slaves praising Spartacus\u2019s name. She was ambushed by a patrol of Roman soldiers, and unleashed her powers to drive them off with Sybaris. She was seen by a slave, however, who fled back to camp screaming of monsters and magic in the woods.<br /> <br /> The vision moved forward again. Alongside her followers, Aquila had been almost entirely ostracised from the slave army\u2019s camp. Wherever she walked, she was regarded with suspicion and whispers of magic. The rumours were enough to see her seen as bad luck at best, a curse on the rebels at worst.<br /> <br /> Aquila\u2019s mind returned to the present. She gritted her teeth. \u201cThis time will be different.\u201d<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Sekhet Bastet had been chewing her way through Gator\u2019s cultists. After tracking down and killing another half-dozen, she finally ran out of leads. The only thing left to her were cryptic comments about a rot in Aquila\u2019s heart, put there by Gator, and the corruption that would inevitably come.<br /> <br /> She decided to turn to the skies for help. Leaving the city, she performed Tier 3 of Secrets Ripped from Skies to ask for guidance. She received this message:<br /> <br /> \u201cThree wolves circle the flock. The White Worm, the Gold Crocodile, and the Beast-Who-Is-Fire. They appear apart, but are together. Find one, find them all.\u201d<br /> <br /> Concluding quickly that this referred to Gator as the Gold Crocodile, and that the others must thus by Shuankhsen, she went to Sesu Ra\u2019s tomb to deliver this message to him and the rest of the meret. Sesu Ra greeted her happily, and handed her the Dragon\u2019s Claw. The Uter, he said, was rightfully hers.<br /> <br /> They discussed what had happened since they last met. Bast shared her prophecy, and Sesu Ra stated somewhat cryptically that he thought he knew the identity of the Beast-Who-Is-Fire. As for the other, the White Worm, he didn\u2019t know. The message was clear though. The city\u2019s Shuankhsen were coordinating, working together.<br /> <br /> Then Bast brought up her concerns, beginning with Aquila. She wanted to know if anything strange had been happening to the other Mummy, anything that might indicate that she was slipping towards the Shuankhsen. Sesu Ra didn\u2019t think so, however.<br /> <br /> And then it was Sesu Ra\u2019s turn to ask the questions. Seeing as Nenheta had introduced herself as one of the Su-Menent, he asked Bast if she knew anything about her. At that, Bast froze and demanded to know where he had heard that name. The whole story of Akenakhi\u2019s relic and Nenheta on the island came out quickly. Bast declared that they had to find the others, and they went to the Temple.<br /> <br /> Both Akenakhi and Aquila were in attendance, replenishing their pillars. Bast stormed in and demanded to know where Nenheta was. Akenakhi was quite upset. Nenheta had specifically asked that her presence go unknown, but Sesu Ra replied simply that he trusted Bast a helluva lot more than Nenheta. Or Akenakhi, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet decided she needed to meet with Nenheta. She wasn\u2019t sure, herself, how reliable her own memory was. The news that Nenheta was apparently Twice-Arisen was concerning, but not completely damning in its own right. It was possible that she hadn\u2019t been entirely corrupted in their last encounter, and that the other Su-Menent had been cured of the affliction by the fire Bast had wielded to end her.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra offered to accompany her, and Akenakhi demanded that he come as well. Aquila chose to remain behind, wanting to visit Yama-Het instead.<br /> <br /> As the others set off, Aquila went to West Jakarta to speak with her friend. When she walked into Yama-Het\u2019s private chambers, the other Mummy greeted her by name. She was sitting at a writing desk, her back to the door, and writing with a brilliantly coloured red and orange quill. Before Aquila could say anything, Yama-Het confessed that she was worried. There were too many attacks on the Arisen cults, too many strange magics at play. The gem market in East Jakarta had seen several cultist guards killed, and the potential relics therein were left entirely at the mercy of the perpetrator. No one could investigate, the police were refusing to allow anyone in. Mot-Tan and Sem-Huf\u2019s cultists, responsible for the protection of the site, were forced to watch and wait.<br /> <br /> Aquila chose to add to these concerns. Her meret balanced on a knife edge, she said, and her hierophant was afflicted by a curse of dreams. She wanted to know how to remove it. Yama-Het\u2019s advice was simply that a great show of will on his part would be the cure, or the use of an Utterance such as Rebuke the Vizier. Unfortunately, she lacked that particular knowledge herself.<br /> <br /> Out in the Thousand Isles, the other three Arisen were hauling their boat up and onto the land. They could see no sign of Nenheta, and so they entered the jungle. Once inside, Akenakhi got to work. The only one with any knowledge of tracking was Sekhet Bastet, but Akenakhi did his best to use lies and misdirection to prevent her from noticing the right way to go. The others put it down to incompetence, and it was ultimately unsuccessful. They made their way through the jungle until they came across a crude wooden hut.<br /> <br /> Nenheta emerged from the jungle. Bast stepped up to confront her, demanding to know if Nenheta remembered her. Nenheta looked from her to Akenakhi and back, and said in a broken voice, \u201cI said I wanted to be left alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Akenakhi stepped up to her and put his hand on her shoulder. He glanced back at the rest of the meret. Then he put the Rod of Tjesh in her hands and told her, \u201cRun.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nenheta took off. Bast unleashed the second tier of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, letting her slip through the cracks in reality. Akenakhi hurled himself at Bast. Sesu Ra whirled around and struck Akenakhi, throwing him to the ground. Bast gave chase, and Akenakhi and Sesu Ra grappled with another. When Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed is the God-King, Akenakhi conceded and slumped to the ground.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the jungle, Bast dogged Nenheta\u2019s heels. The other Mummy knew the terrain far better than her pursuer, however, and managed to slip out of sight. Having lost her quarry, a furious Bast returned to where Akenakhi and Sesu Ra were waiting.<br /> <br /> They explored the hut, and found it full of small animal bones. Food for the tiger, presumably. They demanded to know why Akenakhi had done what he did, and he said simply that he didn\u2019t want to see his love killed by them. They protested that they just wanted to talk, but Akenakhi raised an eyebrow and pointed to their respective track records.<br /> <br /> When the pair escorted Akenakhi out of the forest, they found their boat was missing. Cursing in frustration, Sesu Ra called for a new one while Sekhet Bastet tried to intimidate Akenakhi into giving up Nenheta\u2019s location. They knew that with Blessed Panoply, Akenakhi should have no problem tracking the Rod of Tjesh.<br /> <br /> When Akenakhi refused, Sekhet Bastet took matters into her own hands. A Kepher search located the relic, in Nenheta\u2019s hands and descending into the bowels of an old Dutch fort. Sekhet Bastet interrogated Akenakhi, stripping away his willpower and breaking him, to milk him for all the information he had on Nenheta. All she really learned was that they had been together for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> The three, ferried by the cultist who had come out to retrieve them, returned to Jakarta. There Bast took off, hunting Nenheta. Sesu Ra and Akenakhi followed close behind. They came to the Dutch fort, and one by one they slipped past the security and descended into the fort\u2019s tunnels. Bast reached Nenheta and her tiger before the others were even in sight.<br /> <br /> The brief conversation was bitter. Bast pointed out that, once, she and Nenheta had been friends. She had tried to save Nenheta from her fate. She just wanted answers to her questions, about Nenheta\u2019s nature. Nenheta\u2019s response was scathing. \u201cYou tried to save me? You failed.\u201d<br /> <br /> The next few moments passed in a frenzy. Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 2. Nenheta and her tiger lunged forwards, grappling with Bast. Bast, the Dragon\u2019s Claw in hand, nearly tore Nenheta in half. Sending her tiger away, Nenheta threw her head back and a many-toothed worm tore from her throat and dove into Bast\u2019s flesh. It burrowed in deep, but not deep enough to save its creator. Bast pinned Nenheta\u2019s arms down and waited. When she ran out of Pillars available to Seal the Flesh, Nenheta died.<br /> <br /> There was movement in the approaching passages. Sesu Ra and Akenakhi were approaching. Bast barely noticed though. To her absolute horror and disgust, the worm was inside her. She was infected. The Bane Affinity Wormheart had forced its way into her soul.<br /> <br /> The others arrived and demanded to know what had happened. Bast replied that she had found the third Shuankhsen, the White Worm. Akenakhi seemed to go into shock. He couldn\u2019t believe it, didn\u2019t want to believe it. He and Bast just stared down at the body on the floor, in silence.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra, on the other hand, began to look around the tunnel. It was a dead end, but it didn\u2019t take long before he found the switch at the base of the wall that opened a secret passage. He took one step inside\u2026 and stepped on a pressure plate. The resulting spears ran him through, but he sealed the flesh and continued on. Inside, he discovered a simple little tomb. The plain stone sarcophagus faced a wall where Iremite hieroglyphs were written in a cipher he and Bast recognised. It wasn\u2019t long before he translated them, and read out the following pledge:<br /> <br /> \u201cWe three, by the source of the river\u2019s curse, do swear on the Devourer\u2019s Jaws that the works of Irem shall fail.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bast and Sesu Ra waited there by the tomb in silence, to see if Nenheta returned. Akenakhi went back to his own tomb, having collected the Rod of Tjesh from Nenheta\u2019s corpse. He poured his being into the item, taking his mind from events with the creation of a Talisman. On the other side of the city, Aquila showed up to her volunteer shift at a slum\u2019s medical clinic, working through the night to keep mortal lives from fading.<br /> <br /> None of them felt like the dawn would bring anything better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:01:22-08:00","id":386175,"title":"","content":"Session 22<br /> <br /> Bad habits involving an upcoming election and arguing over politics sort of stopped us from making too much progress this session. Ah well, once we got distracted by the game it all went well.<br /> <br /> The day after their confrontation with Nenheta, the group pottered off to pursue their own interests. Sesu Ra eventually left Bast to guard Nenheta's tomb, and journeyed back to meditate. Aquila made the rounds among her cultists, sounding people out as they made the gradual transition into becoming an Enterprise cult. She spent a while speaking with the young Quil Mayehi, both about his lost father Richard and his education as a fisherman. Akenakhi... mostly just settled in for a long day of non-stop drinking. They each whiled away the day, before Aquila called them all together to meet at the temple the next morning, before dawn.<br /> <br /> That morning, they assembled there. They weren't the only ones. Kotira Nahan, Yarikh, Sem-Huf, and Yama-Het were all in attendance. Kotira was quite pleased by this apparent show of piety from every waking Mummy in the city, save for Sekhet Bastet and Mot-Tan. Bast's own piety wasn't really in doubt, and Mot-Tan had long been considered a lost cause.<br /> <br /> After the morning's prayers and meditations, the group began to talk. Sem-Huf and Aquila circled the gathering, staying on opposite sides of the crowd to one another. Yama-Het was truly perturbed, and extremely interested, in some of the stories about Shuankhsen that the group had encountered. Aquila quizzed Yarikh and Kotira about anyone they might know with the Rebuke the Vizier Utterance, so that she could have the curse from Dream of Dead Gods removed from Rom. Neither of them knew, however. Akenakhi and Sesu Ra explained most of the information they had gathered on the city's three Shuankhsen, but it seemed most of the others had been lucky enough to avoid any direct contact with the beasts. Aquila, still feeling the gnawing desire for human hearts, kept a low profile at the mutterings about &quot;vile beasts&quot; and the need to cleanse the city of their ilk.<br /> <br /> After the meeting, Aquila turned to Vania, the historian of their cult, for any information she might have on a Mummy with access to Rebuke the Vizier. Vania turned up a blank, although she did mention in passing that some documents might have been left behind on the island during LDI's attack. When Aquila wondered aloud how such a thing might be possible, Vania mentioned, a little reproachfully, that many documents had been hard to catalog because they had been written in languages Vania herself couldn't read. However, the conversation did quickly distract Aquila from that subject, as it turned out many of the older men of the cult were suffering similar nightmares to those suffered by Rom.<br /> <br /> Aquila gathered Sesu Ra and they set out for West Jakarta, the place they had heard was home to Hetenatra. The district was filled with examples of Chinese architecture, but it was also terrifically poor. It seemed clean and respectable at first, but the alleys were full of racist graffiti sporting anti-Chinese slurs and filled with rubbish and makeshift homes of the homeless. It was a place of desperation and no hope of improvement. They found, by asking a homeless man named Suharno who appeared to be suffering from polio, that there were a variety of places in the area regarded as supernatural. The old bridge was meant to be lucky, the community library was popularly considered spooky, many streets were thought to be haunted by the wandering ghosts of those killed in the Communist Party Massacre, and occasionally a mysteriously vigilante would kill Indonesian youths who had come to stir up trouble among the district's Chinese population.<br /> <br /> Eventually, they arrived at the community library. A wizened old man with thinning hair, a white moustache, and a cane introduced himself as Imeni, and almost immediately addressed them as Arisen. He asked if they had come to visit the Lady, and when they said they had he shuffled out the door and beckoned for them to follow. Carefully locking up the library behind him, he led them only a few doors down to a grocery store, where he introduced them to Yanar, the high priest of Hetenetra.<br /> <br /> Introductions took a little while. Yanar seemed awed, she had never seen an Arisen, while Imeni seemed a bit more at ease. When they were asked if they could raise Hetenatra so that the characters could speak with her, however, she got quite flustered. Eventually, Aquila coaxed the story out of her.<br /> <br /> Imeni, Yanar, and two others were the only ones left of Hetenatra's cult. Yanar had only been an infant when the Communist Party Massacre shattered the lives of Hetenetra's followers. Imeni helped her mother escape with her, along with a few others. None of them had been truly well versed in the ancient rites, however. They had only a few vague ideas of how to summon their Lady, and none of them had panned out. They had been told to never provoke the wrath from beyond the grave, so disturbing remains were out. And to cap it all, they had no relic or vestige by which to summon their mistress.<br /> <br /> The group was baffled. They had never seen an Arisen's followers reduced to such a state. Agreeing to help the broken cult, they resolved to begin a hunt for a suitable vessel to restore the Lady of the Broken Stele to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T00:36:51-08:00","id":398549,"title":"","content":"Session 23<br /> <br /> The group was in need of a vessel, but not particularly sure how to get their hands on it. They spent the five days recouping their strength, and Aquila spent some time building the new Enterprise foundation of the cult, to be called Asa Corp. Every moment of spare time she spent volunteering at the medical clinic at the edge of a West Jakarta slum, burning through pillars to keep her unlife masked by the medical staff.<br /> <br /> Luca returned to Sesu Ra with news that, according to contacts involved in drug crime in South Jakarta, the Pelamat were out. Some were in jail, others on the run or split into different gangs, but the upshot was that Iwseck's followers weren't looking to be much of a threat in the near future. <br /> <br /> In the end, rather than try and persuade Sekhet Bastet to give up her vestige, Akenakhi decided to go for a chance die Kepher attempt to simply locate a random vessel. He succeeded and was given a momentary vision of a strange-looking bathtub, as well as the identity of a woman named Barbara Sullivan. She was an American expat living in a prosperous suburb renowned for its large expat population, not far from Jakarta's Golden Triangle. The meret decided to track her down, and showed up on her doorstep later that day with Luca and Quil Mayehi in tow.<br /> <br /> Barbara's home was a large, well-kept house of almost manorial proportions, and Barbara herself proved to be a rather gossipy middle-aged woman who seemed instantly friendlier upon hearing Sesu Ra's almost American accent. Aquila had to stay out of the conversation in the end, as the only one of the three unable to speak English. Akhenakhi asked her rather bluntly whether she'd heard anything about a bathtub, and she rather readily said that it had shown up at a neighbourhood auction. Very creepy thing though. Someone had started a rumour that its supports were made from human bone, and there were strange, leathery drapes instead of shower curtains. Other than that it seemed like a functional, albeit large, bathtub. She said that the last she'd heard of it it'd been sent to the Butcher's a few blocks over. &quot;Johnny&quot;, an attendant at the store, was a big, strong fellow and did odd jobs like moving large bits of furniture for others in the area. He'd probably been hired to move it to its new home.<br /> <br /> So the group headed over to meet Johnny. Barbara had told them that it wasn't his real name, but no one really knew what he was called. He didn't speak much, and someone with a cruel sense of humour (her words) had taken to calling him John Doe. And now everyone called him Johnny. Big guy, mixed heritage, you'd know him when you saw him.<br /> <br /> Well. The group arrived at the Butcher's. Sure enough, a large, heavily built man was behind the counter, chopping meat. The group tried a variety of ways to get him to talk. Akenakhi tried to strike up a conversation, and even draw the words out of him with Words Summoned Forth, but Johnny remained quiet and impassive. Aquila tried to bribe him, laying out money on the table and saying she could offer a whole lot more than whoever had paid him, but Johnny seemed unmoved. Finally, Sesu Ra delivered some rather choice threats in both English and Indonesian, but Johnny's response was to point at something that had appeared behind the group.<br /> <br /> Alternating between snorts and growls, a jackal-headed Greater Amkhat had materialised between the group and the doorway. It charged, bowling over Luca. The group drew their weapons, but Akenakhi used Pillars to reinforce his attributes and for a moment revealed his khat to Johnny. For the first time, something brought an obvious reaction from the man. He bellowed, hefted his meat cleaver, and rushed at Akenakhi.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Quil moved to intercept, draining some of Johnny's Willpower and trying to hold him down. Knowing that a bleeding wound would break him momentarily free of the grip of Sybaris, Quil stabbed Johnny with a knife. It may have ended one spell, but it started another. Johnny turned on Quil and promptly struck him down with a heavy blow from the meat cleaver, leaving the cultist bleeding on the ground. The moment that was done Johnny seemed to relax, going limp in Aquila's arms.<br /> <br /> Quil's situation didn't get better. Sesu Ra, Luca, and Akenakhi all turned their attentions to the Amkhat. As they tore into the creature's flesh, scorpions came piling out. They swarmed across Quil, stinging him repeatedly, as well as hurting the rest of the group. Finally, with its body starting to come apart, the Amkhat retreated back into Twilight. Aquila rushed to Quil's side and used Healing Counsel to bring him back from the brink of death, and the group began to realise just how very loud the fight had been. Gunshots and screams and the aberrant noises from the Amkhat had completely broken the peace reigning over the affluent neighbourhood. Any moment now, they were going to be hearing sirens...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:17:34-08:00","id":407369,"title":"","content":"Session 24<br /> <br /> Akenakhi's player couldn't make it to this session, so he took something of a back seat in the events that followed. But on the other hand, Sekhet Bastet's player has returned from a six month tour of Europe, so we have the whole party together again! <br /> <br /> The police closed in on the butcher's shop, and the group hastened to barricade the store. They declared they had a hostage, the butcher, as Aquila worked like a demon to save Quil's life. In a moment's split decision, she decided the best way to save him would be to make him a Sadikh. He had promised her his loyalty before, and she knew his name, so I decided that would be enough for her to perform the Rite of the Engraved Heart on the dying cultist.<br /> <br /> By the time the police made their move, the group was gone. Johnny, the Butcher, lay near comatose on the floor of the room. There was no sign of the Amkhat they'd been facing. Aquila burned through all of her remaining pillars to help herself, her meret, Luca, and the newly risen Quil escape underground. Quil seemed a little delirious and didn't seem to understand what was going on. The group did observe, as they passed unseen beneath the feet of the assembled police force, that there were a lot more police present than they would have anticipated so short a time since Akenakhi fired his gun.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Akenakhi returned to his tomb to meditate and recover from his injuries. Aquila and Sesu Ra tracked down Sekhet Bastet, still keeping watch on Nenheta's tomb. They needed a new lead, and from their descriptions of the bathtub she was able to gain a Kepher vision of a new lead. Carrie Whitson was another expat, a lawyer, and the group gained knowledge of the location of her law firm HGB.<br /> <br /> After finding that they couldn't get in without an appointment, the group chose to just lurk about outside Carrie's work until she left for work. She travelled to the Caf\u00e9 de Obel, a popular destination for office workers in the area. The group followed her, and when she took a seat they sat themselves at her table without invitation. Rather belligerently, Sesu Ra demanded to know everything she knew about the about the bathtub.<br /> <br /> Confused and a little scared, despite being surrounded on all sides by people, Carrie stammered out that she'd heard that Marcin Winski had made a rather large purchase the day of the auction. There were rumours that it might have had to do with the bathtub. That was enough for the group, so they left before she made too much of a scene.<br /> <br /> Marcin Winski, it turned out, worked in a ground floor office some distance away. Again, the group found that they couldn't get in without an appointment. They made a call to the receptionist, and made arrangements to discuss the recent sale. The receptionist mentioned that Marcin was taking these meetings outside of office hours, and that they would have to wait until tomorrow night. Tonight he was meeting with a different client.<br /> <br /> The group promptly decided to wait until tonight to see who went to meet with him. At 6:30pm, the receptionist closed up and left. A light was still on somewhere in the office. A few minutes later, they saw it flicker off and on. Luca was sent inside, Sesu Ra watching proceedings through his eyes, to investigate. The front door turned out to be unlocked, and he snuck through the office without making a sound. They were able to listen in on the conversation... but somehow only Marcin's side of the conversation could be heard. Whoever else was speaking didn't seem to be audible to anyone except Marcin.<br /> <br /> Marcin himself was a handsome man in his late fifties. Despite the oppressive heat and humidity and the lack of air-conditioning in the office, he seemed entirely unaffected. He was making arrangements to meet someone at &quot;the discussed location&quot;. The figure of a million dollars US was mentioned, a payment to hire a single use of the discussed service. This seemed to meet the satisfaction of his client. Curiosity overcame Sesu Ra, and he had Luca use Chthonic Dominion to scan the area for a ghost. He didn't see any... but he did immediately spot three hulking Greater Amkhata in the room, including the jackal-headed bull they had fought in the butcher's shop.<br /> <br /> Marcin was clearly shocked by the beasts suddenly visible. He bolted from the building, as the Amkhat tried to find Luca. The Sadikh was able to slip out of the building, while Aquila and Sesu Ra tried to stop Marcin getting to his car. They didn't succeed, but Aquila used Dust Beneath Feet to sink into the ground and grab hold of the car's suspension, being dragged along behind the car as it headed off.<br /> <br /> When Marcin got home, she popped out of the earth to badger him again. She offered to protect him from the monsters, in return for the bathtub. He responded by snapping out something in Polish, and moments later the three Amkhata appeared around her, one by one. Aquila ducked beneath the earth before they could set upon her.<br /> <br /> After some discussion, the group decided they would keep their meeting with Marcin the next day. He'd seen Sesu Ra and Aquila, so they would send in Sekhet Bastet and Luca to act as her translator. Aquila would provide the million dollars required in payment, and they would see what this mysterious service was.<br /> <br /> The next night, Sekhet Bastet and Luca turned up at Marcin's office. He seemed to assume they had learned of the service through something called &quot;the Black Gold&quot;. Bast's seeming ignorance of what the service entailed momentarily aroused Marcin's suspicion, but Luca was able to soothe him. Speed and discretion apparently being Marcin's watchwords, they agreed to carry out the service the next morning.<br /> <br /> Bast was driven to a pre-arranged address. It was a large, seemingly uninhabited house, flanked on either side by houses with &quot;For Sale&quot; signs that seemed to have been standing for quite some time. She was led to the front door, Luca escorting her. A polite young man let her in and handed her a white bath robe. Bast looked at it, wrinkled her nose, and shrugged out of her clothing without making any move to take the garment. The man told Luca, who was studiously observing the ceiling, to wait in the outer rooms.<br /> <br /> Every room of this house seemed entirely devoid of furniture. There was the occasional sound of movement in adjacent rooms as Bast was led deeper into the building, but she never saw anyone save for her guide. Finally, she scented Sekhem nearby, and was led into a small, tiled room. Her guide waited outside.<br /> <br /> In the centre of the room was the bath from her visions, full to the brim of a thick, viscous red liquid. She walked up to the bath and trailed her hand along it, using Name the Thing to discover the relic's powers. She quickly learned that it was called the Red Bath, and that it was clearly something to be prized. The one who bathed in it would hold off aging for another twenty years, if they were mortal. If they were Arisen, however, it would immediately cause them to gain a point of Sekhem. It just required a mortal's life, and blood, to fill it. Either way, the act of bathing was itself a Morality 1 Sin.<br /> <br /> Bast decided there was no point in letting this service go to waste. She sank into the bath, feeling her power swell with it, and dropped again to Memory 2 despite putting her faith in Her-Uru. She gained the Suspicion derangement in the process.<br /> <br /> It all seemed to go smoothly from there. Once she was reunited with the rest of the group and Bast described it as a source of perpetual Sekhem, they decided the relic was far too valuable to sacrifice resurrecting Hetenatra. Instead, Bast volunteered the use of the cowboy hat Vestige she had retrieved from one of the dead Faithful, so long ago. The group travelled to Hetenatra's cultists, alongside Yama-Het. The Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster and Hetenatra's hierophant proceeded alone, since the exact location of Hetenatra's tomb was not something her cult wanted the meret knowing.<br /> <br /> Some time passed, before Yama-Het emerged. She said that Hetenatra was waiting for her memory to return, and seemed a little shaken. When pressed by Aquila, Yama-Het confessed that her subordinate had always unnerved her a little. She left before elaborating any further.<br /> <br /> After about an hour, the group heard a clicking sound approaching. Hetenatra came into the room, moving with the help of her hierophant and crutches. Her flesh was shrunken and withered, but even by the standards of Sekhem 10 Mummies she was not a pretty sight. Her legs were a shattered ruin, dragging uselessly behind her. Her mummified skin looked burned in places, and she collapsed thankfully into a chair prepared by her cultist at the earliest opportunity. She then turned her eyeless gaze to the meret, one by one. It looked as if the mummified skin near her mouth twitched a little at the sight of Sekhet Bastet, but that was it.<br /> <br /> The conversation that followed was tense and unpleasant. Hetenatra was not impressed by Aquila's plea that she lift a curse, given that its targets were chosen by Fate and thus surely the whim of the Arem-Abfu... and possibly the lesser judges as well. She was positively insulted at Aquila's offer of a trade, of help for her broken cult in return for mercy being shown to Rom and his fellow sufferers. She declared that each member of the meret, save Sekhet Bastet, had sinned against the Judges. Until they atoned, they would not receive an ounce of help from her.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra was a bit puzzled by this, although Aquila seemed to take it for granted that she'd probably done something to displease the Judges at some point. Hetenatra told the Unbending Spine to visit a zoo in South Jakarta to witness the product of his heresy. He shrugged, and began to make things very difficult. He didn't like the idea of having to appease a lesser Mummy just for the chance of being allowed to make his case. The Lady of the Broken Stele left rather than cave in to his demands, seemingly unconcerned by his promise that unless she lifted the curse, she would have made an enemy of him, and his Guild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:44:55-08:00","id":428665,"title":"","content":"Session 25<br /> <br /> Bast bought her Memory back up to 3 using up what Sebayt experience she had left, so we kicked off the session with a flashback.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet remembered towering over her followers as they dedicated themselves to the judges' service. She was somewhere steeped in thick jungle, her limbs darkened by the paint daubed upon them by her followers. They were celebrating the defeat of an enemy, an enemy whose body lay broken and unrecognisable at the centre of the clearing. All about her were her cultists, a group of mortals she had perfected in body and soul so that they were wholly given over to the Judges' service. Generations of indoctrination had rendered them into perfect slaves, without any goals beyond furthering the Judges' wishes.<br /> <br /> There was a darker edge to this worship, however. At the edge of the clearing was a pit, an inverted pyramid lined with human blood. Her defeated enemy had created something in this pit, something she hadn't had the strength to fight. In the end she had sealed it inside its birthplace, reluctantly conceding that starving it to death was the only sure way of ending its existence.<br /> <br /> As the ceremony dragged on, Bast was drawn inevitably towards the edge of the pit. When she reached it, keeping her face impassive despite the sensation of corruption rolling from the pit in waves, she looked down met the all-too-human eyes of the Amkhat lurking in the depths. There was a pause, and then the Amkhat spoke.<br /> <br /> &quot;Come to gloat, priest? No matter. Even with the death of my master, you have not won.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the brief, terse conversation that followed, Bast made a pact for the life of her cult. By feeding the Amkhat her own Sekhem, she would gain mastery over it... for a week or two, anyway. In return, it would help her save her cultists from the rot that had begun to spread in their midst. The very jungle seemed to be sickening and turning against its inhabitants, and she needed to end it.<br /> <br /> Upon feasting on her Sekhem, the Amkhat rose from the pits. Bast could not quite remember exactly what the creature looked like, but she did know that its appearance was markedly more decomposed and humanoid than that of most Amkhata she recalled encountering. It led her through the forest to the edge of a river. The river's surface seemed covered by an oil-like shimmer, and those cultists who had drunk from it had reported that it had been unpleasantly warm and greasy, making the drinker sick to their stomach for days afterwards. Bast moved to enter the river and follow the Amkhat, when the spirits of her past cultists appeared before her. They appeared as they had in life, save for their heads that were bereft of flesh. They told her that entering the river would end them, casting away their final ties to this world. Bast paused, thanked them for their sacrifice, and entered the river. One by one, the 42 spirits lined along the river's edge began to blink out and fade away.<br /> <br /> The river seemed to fight Bast, currents winding around her limbs and trying to drag her under. She bulled her way through it. As she emerged out the other side, she noticed the water was behaving like something alive. Rather than lapping against the river banks, it was pulling away from the bank opposite and surging against the bank closest to her. To her eyes, it seemed as if the river was reaching out for her, specifically.<br /> <br /> She plunged on, pushing through the jungle. The Amkhat had disappeared, but the Scarab's Path told her that the source of all this corruption, an Uter relic, lay nearby. She walked into a clearing, and there it lay.<br /> <br /> It wasn't like any Uter she had ever seen before. It was not a piece of worked flesh and tanned hide. Although Uter was built from the dead, most examples Bast had encountered had showed some semblance of skilled craftsmanship in their construction. This Uter was nothing like that. It was a rotting mound of viscera, swarming with flies. It seemed like a large animal had simply died in the wilderness, and its carcass become invested in enough Sekhem to turn it into a relic. Bast took a step towards it, and then everything changed.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the relic, the clearing, the jungle itself was gone. She was standing in the midst of a blackened wasteland. Mounds around her turned out to be toppled trees, some of them blasted apart by whatever had caused the devastation. She took a step, and something crunched a foot. A glance down revealed that she was walking on bones, and she somehow recognised them as the bones of her cultist. Looking around, she saw a bone dry ditch a short distance away, and realised that she was still in the jungle.<br /> <br /> Then she heard the first footfall. The sound was of something massive moving. The &quot;footsteps&quot; were incredible thuds that shook the ground, but they were interspersed with other sounds. Once, the boom of an enormous wing beat. Then for a second the sound seemed to be that of a great snake slithering. But despite the fact that it was loud enough to drive Bast to her knees, and that the sounds were drawing closer, she could see no sign of what was approaching. And then the sounds stopped, very close, and a voice hissed, &quot;Ah, the loyal one.&quot;<br /> <br /> The voice presented Bast with a choice. She could accept her chains, and trust in her Judge to save her. Or she could run, and see if freedom would be enough. When Bast looked down, she saw chains at her feet that lead away until they disappeared into the ground. They were chains of Sekhem, descending all the way to Duat, she felt, and ending in the hands of her Judge. Without a pause, Bast leaned down wrapped herself in her chains.<br /> <br /> The voice snarled that she would burn a slave, and flames rushed towards her just as the memory came to an end.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the group was discussing how to proceed. Sesu Ra was reluctant to discover what it was that he had done that had so offended the Judges, much to Aquila's exasperation. Stymied in her attempts to have the Dream of Dead Gods curse lifted from her cultists, she instead suggested they begin rallying the city's Arisen against LDI. They decided to contact Mot-Tan first, because if they could lure the reclusive Maa-Kep out of his territory he would be the natural diplomat to help them bring the rest of the city together.<br /> <br /> Some hours later, the cultist messenger they had sent to Mot-Tan's territory returned saying that no one had come out to meet him. He had come back rather than risk straying into Mot-Tan's territory uninvited. After some discussion, the party decided to take that risk. They wandered into Mot-Tan's riverside slum, noting that the residents kept well clear of them and avoided all eye contact with the obviously foreign group in their midst. They reached Mot-Tan's home on the edge of the river and entered, finding the door unlocked. Inside, they found a bloodbath. There were decomposing bodies of several of Mot-Tan's cultists, and a large scorch mark in the middle of the room with what looked like a few scattered remnants of human remains at their centre. Aquila recognised the body of Mot-Tan's young wife, and felt a rush of anger. Flies were everywhere. Whatever had killed them had clearly come and gone some days before. The group wondered whether LDI had been responsible, until they found a message written in blood on the wall. &quot;No one is safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> They could find no sign of Mot-Tan or his tomb nearby, so they left quickly. They began to interrogate the mortals in the area about what they had seen. They stumbled across a homeless woman, covered in bruises and cuts, who whispered in a fragmented mix of several languages a garbled message about different faces. They took her back with them when they left the slum.<br /> <br /> They put the woman up in a hotel in the city, where Aquila cared for her and treated her injuries. She recoiled slightly every time either Akenakhi or Sesu Ra came near her, so it was left to Aquila to try and work out what was wrong with her. She never settled on a single language for more than a few words at the time, switching between everything from Russian to Japanese to Arabic in a constant flow that made even the multilingual Arisen's head hurt. She even spoke Iremite once, when Bast asked what was wrong with her. &quot;I lost something,&quot; she replied in the same language.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Akenakhi did some digging, using connections Akenakhi had been building with local police to see if they could find anything. They discovered that she was a semi-famous socialite who had gone missing a few months previously. She was the daughter of a prominent conservationist, whose father was employed at the very zoo Hetenatra had told Sesu Ra to visit. That was enough of an excuse to persuade Sesu Ra, so they headed off to the zoo.<br /> <br /> The moment they stepped through the front gates, it became very apparent what Sesu Ra had done. The zoo had been built in 1966, and it had clearly been laid out according to Iremite geometries. The four Arisen were immediately overwhelmed by memories, giving each of them Sebayt experience. Sesu Ra, with the lowest memory, saw a few brief mirage-like images. He saw himself crying over a broken statue, the greatest effigy he ever built. He had once had a memory of its unveiling in the days of Irem, but this seemed to be centuries later, his very first Sothic Turn. The statue was bereft of its head, rendering it inert. If he could find that head though, he realised he might have the power to make his dreams for Jakarta come to fruition.<br /> <br /> The other Arisen were all struck by memories of their life in Irem. Sekhet Bastet saw a brief flash of herself leading a group of Su-Menent Shemsu. All she remembered was that they were about to denounce a heretic. Aquila, with her higher memory, was trapped in the past for several minutes. She saw herself watching a group of slaves by the river's edge. She picked out a particularly large, muscular specimen, and had him taken away. Some time later, she was washing blood from her hands. The slave was being dragged from the room, still moaning and twitching from the alterations done to his body. One of the Mesen-Nebu Guildmasters, an impassive Shan'iatu, offered her the congratulations due to a mortal master of the art.<br /> <br /> When she regained consciousness though, the group realised that Akenakhi seemed well and truly trapped in his memories. At Memory 6, he was more severely effected than any of the group. The group decided to sit him on a park bench and leave him there until he regained consciousness, while they tried to track down the conservationist they had come for.<br /> <br /> Inside his head, Akenakhi was working with the Maa-Kep. The Rod of Tjesh allowed him to sit unnoticed among a meeting of traitors. They were discussing a plot to overthrow the Shan'iatu, the height of heresy. He rose from the meeting and left, informing the Maa-Kep of what had happened. As the soldiers closed in and screams rose from the chamber, he found himself facing a being that seemed to be his Judge. This wasn't a vision from the past, it was something in the present. Six baby asps addressed him from their burrows in the flesh of their mother, asking him calmly why he forsook the gifts offered to him. Akenakhi declared that his life was his to live, and refused to bow before his master.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the group found an office belonging to the Killwarden Memorial Conservation Fund. They were allowed inside once they relayed the fact that they had discovered the daughter of one of the chief conservationists. They were led inside, noting the four large glass cages, all empty save for some bloody remains on the floor of one of them. Their guide seemed nervous and was sweating profusely despite the air-conditioning. When they came upon the doctor (for the life of me, I cannot remember his name. I'll edit it in once I have my hands on my notes again) he demanded to be taken to see his daughter immediately. The group was only too happy to comply, because they were quickly coming to suspect that this place might have a connection to LDI. The combination of the technology on display and the access to rare animals made it seem all too likely.<br /> <br /> They took the doctor back to meet his daughter (whose name I have also forgotten). After a brief reunion, in which the daughter refused to acknowledge her father and spoke in a mixture of languages that he swore she couldn't possibly understand, they took him to a different room. There, Aquila and Bast sat down to interrogate him. They started slow, asking him whether they knew the circumstances of his daughter's disappearance and subsequent affliction of speaking in tongues. He didn't, saying she had just disappeared out of nowhere months ago. It took him a while to believe what had happened, since his daughter was 30 years old and hardly ever spoke to her father, and her disappearing on strange trips wasn't unheard of. Then they began to ask about his work, and had their suspicions confirmed when he mentioned LDI as one of several companies who backed the work he was undertaking. Then they began to press him, using Bast's Fearsome Soul Affinity to break his will. It took a while, but just as he began to speak an Amkhat appeared in the room with him. In the state he was in the doctor was helpless to prevent the creature from tearing him apart. The Arisen began to activate their powers, calling on Ancestry of Forgotten Stars and Blessed is the God King (Tiers 2 and 3 respectively) to fight it, but it responded by fleeing.<br /> <br /> Furious, Bast and Sesu Ra decided to have their revenge. They knew the <i>Sethis</i>, an LDI-owned freighter, was due in port soon. They travelled to the docks... only to hear from dock crews that the ship, due in that day, had apparently been delayed indefinitely. Everyone seemed quite puzzled, because the only possible situation seemed to be that the ship was anchored offshore somewhere. Bast and Sesu Ra decided they didn't want to wait, so they had a cultist arrange a boat and headed out to locate the <i>Sethis</i>.<br /> <br /> Jakarta was fading into the distance behind them when an Amkhat appeared in front of their boat. Their engine died on the spot. It wasn't a normal Amkhat, however. Rather than appearing like a blasphemous chimera made from the parts of several animals, it looked as if its composite form had been knit from human bones into the shapes of those animals. Its entire form was constantly shifting and reforming, bones combining and separating, splintering and merging together, to make parts of its body take on the shapes of lion, jackal, falcon, snake, and bull. But its head, a distended human skull, stayed as it was. Its bones, including its skull, were draped in places by raw flesh, which separated and pulled back into something like a smile on the creature's face. It looked at Bast, and spoke in a mocking voice.<br /> <br /> &quot;It has been many centuries since I saw you last, master.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 03-05-2015, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T21:17:59-07:00","id":435232,"title":"","content":"Session 26<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet rose to the prow of the boat and demanded that the strange Amkhat submit itself before her. When it laughed in her face, she poured out her Sekhem for it to feed upon, binding it to herself as she enslaved it to her will in the name of Her-Uru. She avoided losing Sekhem to the subsequent Descent roll for feeding an Amkhat in such a manner, taking this as a sign that her Judge was not too displeased with her actions. Her fellow Arisen, however, were another matter. She had told the story of her encounter with the creature to Sesu Ra before, and he accepted her reasoning that enslaving the creature was the only way to deal with it until they could seal it away to starve once more. Akenakhi, however, felt that it was necessary for his Su-Menent credentials that he display at least a modicum of disgust at her blatant heresy (I forgot to mention it at the end of my last write-up, but Akenakhi tagged along for the attack on the <i>Sethis</i>). Bast shrugged it off, stating that it was the only possible course of action, and then set to interrogating the Amkhat.<br /> <br /> It revealed that it had been following her through the centuries, using its freedom to feed on mortals and keep itself material while avoiding the attention of Arisen and the like. And then it noticed that a growing number of Amkhat were following the meret, which attracted its interest. It followed, but the other Amkhat became alerted to its presence and fled. It turned out that even Amkhat tended to avoid this creature like the plague. Curiosity piqued, it decided to reveal itself to Sekhet Bastet and see what was happening.<br /> <br /> Bast demanded the creature seek out the city's Shuankhsen, drain their Sekhem, and return it to her. If it could not defeat them, it should at least return and tell her where to find them. The Amkhat bowed its head in supplication and disappeared.<br /> <br /> The sun set and the stars rose over their vessel as they closed in on the <i>Sethis</i>. The freighter was dark, no lights, no sound of engine, just a black mass outlined against the heavens. The stars gave Bast a message about an evil in the bowels of the ship ahead, so they decided not to risk it boarding the ship. Instead, she called upon the full force of Secrets Ripped From Skies, summoning a meteor shower to smash the <i>Sethis</i> into pieces. She left the choice of targets up to Fate, and Fate rained fire down upon the LDI vessel. Holes were punched in the ship's deck, and the glow of spreading fires illuminated it against the darkness.<br /> <br /> All was quiet afterwards, for a single long moment. Then swirls of spiralling corpus began to boil up and out of the holes in the ship's deck, avoiding the flame, before plunging into the ocean. Sekhet Bastet recognised a Chthonic Being. It surged through the ocean towards them, smashing through waves seemingly without noticing them. Bast leapt to the prow of the boat, summoning the Secrets Ripped From Skies to throw meteors at the creature once again. Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed Is The God-King Tier 3, and Akenakhi summoned up the Revelations of Smoke and Flame Tier 2 and took to the air.<br /> <br /> A meteor struck the creature head-on, and it responded by diving deep beneath the water. Sesu Ra dove overboard and Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 2, allowing her to walk on water. She stepped off the boat, moments before a second meteor struck the boat and blasted it to splinters.<br /> <br /> Underwater, Sesu Ra was gripped in combat with the Chthonic Being. A surge of strength had them up near the water's surface, and Bast leapt onto its &quot;back&quot;, for wont of a better word. Akenakhi transmuted the fragments of their boat into oil using Obedient Clay Tier 3, and then a third meteor struck the Chthonic Being. Fire scorched Sesu Ra and set the oil aflame, prompting the Chthonic Being to flee. The last they saw of it, it was diving deep trailing shreds of corpus, diving out of sight just as several meteors more slammed into the ocean after it.<br /> <br /> Bast then raced to the damaged <i>Sethis</i>, running on water, while Sesu Ra swam and Akenakhi flew after her. The three Arisen clambered aboard and began to explore, dodging patches of fire. They found a great deal of evidence of the Chthonic Being's activities there. The crew had been torn apart, their ghosts presumably devoured as well. Even with the light of Chthonic Dominion, no spirits were in evidence.<br /> <br /> Down in the hold, they found the supplies LDI had been transporting. The Chthonic Being had left them untouched. Among a variety of different medicines was a box that smelled faintly of the familiar aniseed and honey that marked the presence of Sekhem. Sesu Ra identified the drug inside as a kind of steroid. There was enough inside for ten uses, but to the best of their knowledge it would have no effect on their undead physiology despite the magical nature of the drug. The party claimed it as a prize, and then stole one of the ship's lifeboats in order to return to Jakarta. Thankfully, there was one unharmed from the meteors and fire, and they quickly left the burning ship behind them.<br /> <br /> Back ashore, Aquila had been trying to uncover as much publically available information as she could on LDI. For the first time, a member of the group found the organisation's real name, Last Dynasty International. She was troubled by the information she uncovered on their philanthropic activities in Africa, using what she could only presume was Sekhem-augmented drugs to treat HIV with great success. Their involvement in environmental conservation drew a more sceptical response, given the number of Amkhata that seemed to be at LDI's beck-and-call. Regardless, the scope and success of the organisation's philanthropy weighed upon her.<br /> <br /> When the group returned, Aquila had Sekhet Bastet organise a visit to the blood bath for her. Of course, Bast hadn't told her what the bath actually entailed, so she had no warning of the sight that would great her when she arrived for her appointment the next day. Like Bast, she was met by a young man who presented her with a white robe. Aquila put it on and followed him through the large house, noting with a tad of apprehension that the building was made of wood. Her favourite escape technique, Dust Beneath Feet, would not be available here.<br /> <br /> She entered the room with the bath, and her guide shut the door behind her. The lights came on, and she stared in horror at the gory sight that greeted her. She came to a decision quickly. She couldn't possibly use such an abomination, but she should still get the power she had come here for by draining the relic of its power. She stepped forward, reaching out for the bath, when she realised something had changed.<br /> <br /> There were now two Greater Amkhata in the room with her. She recognised them as two of the three she had seen protecting Marcin Winski when she followed him to her home, but that recognition came and went in a flash as she realised her predicament. Sealed in a room, alone, at Sekhem 1, and outnumbered two-to-one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:33:23-07:00","id":451375,"title":"","content":"Session 27<br /> <br /> Aquila raced to the bath and began to drain its Sekhem, frantically trying to increase her power before the Amkhata drained her of her remaining scraps. One of the creatures fell upon her and began to drain Sekhem from her as fast as she could draw it from the relic. The other leapt upon the relic and drained some of the Sekhem for itself. When the relic was completely gone... the forced Descent checks for that act of blasphemy cost Aquila her final points of Sekhem and she immediately dropped into henet. Her Sothic Turn was over.<br /> <br /> The next morning, the meret began to gather to try and locate this relic from Sekhet Bastet's vision. They had the cult charter a boat and prowled the Ciliwung. Bast sought out with her Kepher, was only able to get a fleeting image of pipes pumping waste into the river. Sadly, as they observed on their boat ride, that was not an uncommon sight.<br /> <br /> The days passed slowly. The group tried to contact Aquila, but couldn't find her. They wanted her resources to help them secure land where they could build and Amkhat pit to consign the creature Bast had enslaved to an eternity of starvation. When she didn't materialise, they became increasingly worried. She'd never returned from her appointment with the relic.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet spent the time between searches building her control over Mot-Tan's former territory. She found many of the people there had already seen Mot-Tan as something akin to a spirit or minor deity, he had come perilously close to open rule rather than just showing his true self to his cult. It was easy for her to bring them into the fold of the Judges. She chose to keep this gain separate from the rest of the cult however, instead building a cult entirely of her own.<br /> <br /> When the meret convened, they decided to investigate the site of Aquila's disappearance. They headed to the address Bast gave them, but they found the house almost completely deserted. When they entered the room where the relic had been kept, they found the crumpled ruin of the bath and a man sobbing over it. He was the one who had given Bast her robe and escorted her on her night. Under interrogation, he told them that Aquila had arrived last night, the &quot;Guardians&quot; had been forced to act, and that the miracle, the immortality at the centre of the Black Gold Society, had been destroyed. When asked who commanded these Guardians, he told them that Marcin was responsible and gave them the address of the office they had already visited. They left him there to cry over his ruined dreams.<br /> <br /> The group went back to the cult and began asking where Aquila's canopic jars were. It turned out that, after quitting her tomb, she had given one to Phatri and one to Ligo. They had each secured them in separate locations. The group checked on them, but they were both in place. Since Aquila had hidden one of her deaths from them, the group assumed she must have a third one somewhere and that there was nothing they could do but wait to see if she made it through her Death Cycle.<br /> <br /> Instead, they went out to an isolated island and began building an Amkhat pit using the blood of cultists. Sesu Ra completed it over the next two days, using his mastery of geometries to finish it quickly. Bast kept the Amkhat busy, sending it on missions. It located Aquila's sword for them, being held in a tower in the Golden Triangle under heavy security. At least five Greater Amkhata patrolled the building, although they scattered before the creature. Apparently, there were two other relics each being held on different floors. The group began to consider an assault with Kotira's help.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, meanwhile, found that the restaurant above his tomb had gone on sale. He had the cult purchase it, giving him a source of revenue, and then spent some time expanding his connections among Jakarta's police force.<br /> <br /> Finally, Bast ordered her enslaved Amkhat into the pit, and they left it there to starve despite its pleas. As they left, with the sun rising over the ocean, it roared blasphemies at them in Iremite. They didn't look back.<br /> <br /> And in henet, Aquila felt her remains disturbed. She came roaring back to life at Sekhem 10, to find herself confronted by a mortal's corpse and an enormous, burly man with discoloured skin. She used Dust Beneath Feet at Tier 2, but the man seemed unperturbed and grew an enormous set of jaws to attack her with. The mortal's corpse came to life and grappled her, while he tore massive chunks from her body. When her health filled with lethal, despite being Size 9 and Stamina 10, he swallowed a large chunk of her flesh and tore a dot of Sekhem out along with it.<br /> <br /> Aquila's response was to end Dust Beneath Feet Tier 2, and activate Tier 1. She used the momentary reprieve to transmute the bed in the room into an axe, and then, as her attackers smashed their way through the statue, she leapt from the stone with her axe swinging. She landed several solid blows, but his flesh started to knit together as fast as her own. Two more dots of Sekhem were devoured in short order, and the battle swung against her. Held down by the animate corpse, she was torn apart by her attacker.<br /> <br /> She plunged into a death cycle. Anpu beckoned her into her past, and she found herself standing on the docks as a city burned. Rifle shots indicated battles between colonial marines and local militia. The uprising was being slaughtered. Her cult was preparing her way out of the city, readying a ferry to take her to a waiting merchant vessel that would send her to the Pacific. She heard a patrol approaching, and chose to draw her blade rather than cower beneath a tarp with her cultists. The eight mortal men cowered before her majesty, and those that tried to fight were cut down. The last dispatched, she stepped aboard her waiting ferry as regal as any queen. The ropes were untied, the boat cast off. And then she realised she could taste blood upon her lips. She looked for her cultists, but her gaze found only blank, staring eyes, gashed throats, and a bloody carnage decorating the boat's deck.<br /> <br /> As Aquila climbed from her Death Cycle, she found herself with only two jars to reform around. One was Ligo's, the other the one that had been left in the bank vault and vanished after she was killed by the Amkhat waiting there. Figuring the later was no doubt being monitored by LDI and kept somewhere safe and secure, she reformed about Ligo's and found herself in his apartment. Ligo himself was sitting on his bed, and looked at her in astonishment. He had been crying. With a sinking feeling, Aquila put two and two together.<br /> <br /> Phatri was dead. Something had taken her heart. And worse, Ligo said. She was still walking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T22:15:22-07:00","id":456574,"title":"","content":"Wow, poor Aquila. She is either really not specced for combat AT ALL, Fate has a personal grudge to work out on her, or she just has the most rotten luck imaginable. Oh, now Phatri had her heart ripped out and eaten, and is still up and about. Okay, I'm going to go with &quot;Chew Toy of Fate.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T22:44:30-07:00","id":456575,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that she's not exactly specced as a combat character, no.<br /> <br /> Really, this past session was an unfortunate confluence of events. Aquila isn't alone in her tendency to wander into traps, but she does tend to do it on her own while the other characters are either far better prepared for combat (see Sesu Ra carving a path through a dozen Pelamat) or make sure to be in a group. And then the attack by Gator was... well, the Shuankhsen had been waiting for a chance to strike back for a long time now. It was hard to figure out a good way to squeeze them into a session though, because I didn't want to just arbitrarily slaughter the player cult and yet the players were spending very little time with their cult at all. Fuelling matters, the cultists had all moved into homes in Gator's former stomping ground, and ever since Aquila abandoned her tomb they'd been safeguarding high value items in the form of her remaining canopic jars. The Arisen have even been notified that certain cultists have been going missing, but haven't followed up on it.<br /> <br /> With all that in mind, an attack from Gator on Phatri or Ligo (torture of any member of the Cult would quickly lead to them as the highest ranking members of Aquila's cult, and Gator evidently has a grudge against Aquila in particular) was pretty much inevitable. And when Aquila's Descent ended, I thought I'd kill two birds with one stone by having Gator's attack also provide her with a reason to be back in the game in short order, rather than just sit out until the meret a) discovered she was actually dead, and b) found a reason (and a vessel) to summon her again.<br /> <br /> All it cost her was probably the most beloved NPC in the game. Besides Luca. I don't think any mortal love can eclipse the love Sesu Ra (or Sesu Ra's player, anyway) has for Luca.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thanks for the comment though! It's always nice to learn someone is reading these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 03-25-2015, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T01:49:33-07:00","id":459759,"title":"","content":"Session 28<br /> <br /> Ligo and Aquila went to Phatri's apartment. The door had been barricaded, so Aquila ordered Ligo away and began to remove the blockage. She forced open the door, to find Phatri standing in the middle of the room. From behind she could be mistaken for alive, but when her head swung around at an unnatural angle, revealing clouded eyes and a gaping, gory hole in her chest, it very quickly became apparent that she was not. She shuffled towards Aquila, mouth agape, and Aquila spotted the axe she had created during the fight with Gator. She snatched up the axe as Phatri buried her teeth in the woman she had once seen as a surrogate mother. Aquila rained blow after blow down upon the Lifeless creature, feeling her flesh tearing under the onslaught.<br /> <br /> She finally severed Phatri's head. As the energy of combat began to drain away, she took stock of what she had done. Then, slowly and carefully, she transmuted the corpse into a simple bracelet adorned with the word &quot;Daughter&quot;.<br /> <br /> When she came outside, she found Akenakhi and Ligo speaking. Akenakhi had encountered Nenheta, spotting her from the window while he was surveying the cult offices. When she saw him watching her, one of the phones rang. The terse message she delivered was that she wanted him to kill Sesu Ra. Akenakhi asked that they meet at Durant's, the new name for his restaurant, and she agreed to go there that evening. He had come looking for any sign of Aquila, as she was the only one he trusted to provide him with back-up in this situation.<br /> <br /> The pair swapped their stories, and went to the restaurant at the appointed time. Nenheta was waiting for them there, sitting at the back of the deserted restaurant. There was no sign of the building's staff, but no sign that any violence had taken place either. The Shuankhsen narrowed her eyes at the sight of Aquila, but didn't make any hostile moves. She said she wished Akenakhi had come alone, for she had things to say that were for his ears alone. Akenakhi tried to persuade her that it was too dangerous in Jakarta for her, too many fanatical Su-Menent willing to claim a Shuankhsen's scalp. Nenheta said it wasn't up to her, and then repeated her request that he kill Sesu Ra. Aquila stiffened at that, and Akenakhi tried to explain that he was no match for Sesu Ra in a fight, let alone if he had Sekhet Bastet to back him up. Nenheta considered this, and then told him to steal the other Arisen's Canopic Jars. There was a long pause... and Akenakhi agreed.<br /> <br /> Then, true to his status as a Ren Mummy, Akenakhi asked Nenheta to explain the nature of the Shuankhsen to him, so he could understand how she had come to fall so low. She just shook her head, and walked from the restaurant.<br /> <br /> Note: I knew in advance that this scene should trigger a Descent check for the players involved, but then completely forgot about it during the flow of the game. I'll let it slide this time, but I'll need to make sure to warn the players that their Judges are not happy. Not happy.<br /> <br /> Aquila told Akenakhi that he was in deep, even as he tried to explain that he had no intention of carrying through with his promise. Then she left as well, heading for the Temple to recover her pillars. When she arrived at the Temple though, she found it swarming with mortal humans. Close observation let her realise that they included several of Kotira's cultists, but it was very strange the way they were coming and going from the Temple itself. Kotira had rigidly enforced its status as hallowed ground, for the Arisen's feet alone. She approached a cultist outside to ask what was going on, and he seemed quite concerned. He said he couldn't properly answer that question, but the Keeper inside may talk to her.<br /> <br /> Into the Temple she went. The Tomb Guardian announced her presence, and she found that the round table that had once dominated the central space of the Temple was gone. There was a crowd of mortals in its place, carrying a variety of items. At the centre of the ground was a large, powerfully built Arisen. It was newly risen, its withered khat on full display, but its cultists seemed unaffected by the Sybaris that rolled off it in waves. Its followers were strapping plates of armour to its body, modern body armour laid over the top of steel plates. At its feet, a pair of cultists were reverentially lifting a helmet or crown made from a lion's skill, tatters of the creature's mane draped across the Mummy's shoulders. A surge of Kepher told Aquila that it was a relic.<br /> <br /> Another pair of cultists stepped forward once the relic was placed upon the Arisen's head. They handed it a strange axe with a haft that appeared to be made of ivory, and a modern-looking riot shield. Armed and armoured, the Mummy turned its eyes towards Aquila. In a voice that rasped like sound and echoed with the weight of ages, it asked Aquila if it had come to join its crusade. The Mistress of Bones had been taken, it, the Keeper, had been summoned to enact retribution. It intended to assault the front gates of those who had dared do this, before its power had any chance to wane.<br /> <br /> Aquila guessed that this was Aqhat, the Keeper of Sands and Shemsu of Jakarta's Su-Menent. She asked only that she be given a few hours to assemble her meret, and they would gladly storm LDI's Jakarta facility alongside it. It concurred, and she placed a few quick phone calls. Sesu Ra, who had been standing guard over the Amkhat Pit where they had sealed Bast's slave, assembled the cult's warriors. They had been given the drugs found aboard the <i>Sethis</i>, and the physically augmented warriors were made ready to join the assault. Three soldiers were gathered on short notice (not bad for a roll of 3 dice).<br /> <br /> Aquila decided she wanted her Judge's blessing for this. A darker self seemed to be taking over her, and for the first time she considered giving in to the urges of the Bane Affinity inside her. She left the Temple, telling a cultist that she would return soon.<br /> <br /> When she did, some hours later on the eve of the attack, flecks of blood adorned her clothes and lips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:27:57-07:00","id":469853,"title":"","content":"Session 29<br /> <br /> The assault on LDI begins with the meret boarding an armoured van, not dissimilar to the vehicle used by local banks to transport valuables. They prepare for the coming assault as they drive, joining together in a Unison casting of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 1 so that they may all see and interact with creatures in Twilight, giving them a valuable edge against the Amkhata they were sure to encounter. After that, they wait in silence. Aqhat doesn't speak, seemingly focussed on the fight to come. There are no windows, no way to gauge how far away they are from the target, until the van begins to pick up speed. Aqhat, Sesu Ra, and Bast remain standing and rely on their supernatural strength to maintain their balance, while the cultists, Aquila, and Akenakhi strap themselves into the waiting harnesses. Their vehicle crashes into something at high speed, the three standing Arisen are unmoved, and the fighting starts.<br /> <br /> Aqhat is the first out of the van. There were two security guards pulling night duty, but the waves of Sybaris rolling from the animate corpse attacking them prevent them from sounding the alarm in the critical moments that follow. Instead they charge forward to attack. Aqhat cuts the first man in half (I rolled 21 successes on his attack...) and the rest of the group easily overwhelms the second man. They leave the cultists and Luca behind to secure the exit. Akenakhi uses Palace Knows Its Pharaoh to begin searching the underground levels for any sign of Kotira, and the rest of the meret begins to scour the building.<br /> <br /> The lights are mostly off, and there isn't much sign that anyone is still working. They climb through five floors dedicated to the administration of a company called &quot;Integrated Transport Solutions&quot; without seeing a single other living soul. A few more floors later, and Aqhat kills a man wearing a cleaning uniform.<br /> <br /> The meret if halfway up the building and beginning to wonder if something that has gone wrong when the ambush is launched. They walk out onto a landing in time to be semi-blinded by floodlights. A net falls upon them, and a wave of gunfire begins to slam into them. Sekhet Bastet unleashes Tier 2 of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, phases through the netting and begins to cut into the black armoured men. Aqhat roars out Tier 3 of Rite of the Sacred Scarab. The swarm of scarabs throw the room into sudden confusion, a chaotic mess of shifting shadows and bright beams of light as they fly in front of the floodlights. Aquila transmutes the net into a lump of concrete for her to hide behind, and Sesu Ra unleashed Tier 3 Blessed is the God-King.<br /> <br /> Although the mortals attacking them throw a wide variety of different tools at them, from guns to knives to flare guns, they are rapidly overwhelmed. Sesu Ra's ghostly protector possesses one and turns him against his allies. Bast seizes one man and mummifies him on the spot. Aqhat and Sesu Ra kill a man apiece with every blow. When the fight ends, Bast releases her mummified target, Aquila drains him of most of his Willpower, leaving him open to Bast's Fearsome Soul as she tries to find out all he knows about Kotira and the relics LDI has been taking. All he knows, however, is that he is being paid to protect the vault. Bast kills him and dedicates the sacrifice to Her-Uru, who is pleased with her work. She gains a descent reset and manages to avoid losing Memory for the act.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Aqhat have ranged ahead, and located the vault door. The two Mummies, both possessing the Dominating Might Affinity, carve through the steel door in a few blows. Inside, they find a large variety of exotic, ancient, and valuable artefacts, but nothing with the tell-tale taste of Sekhem upon it. Disappointed, they continue climbing.<br /> <br /> By this point, Akenakhi has realised the police are beginning to encircle the building. He gathers Luca and the cultists and heads upstairs to find the meret. He calls Aquila to warn her of the problem, and she responds by telling him to make sure he gathers the weapons and armour of the dead guards on the vault level. She has a plan for them.<br /> <br /> Reaching the roof of the building, the group finds a small helicopter and a pack of four Greater Amkhata waiting for them. One is the falcon-headed snake that once killed Aquila, and the others are mostly constructed from lions and bulls. The Arisen and Amkhata pair off, four against four. The falcon-headed snake, clearly eager to repeat its previous success, charges at Aquila. It wraps itself around her and drains a dot of Sekhem from her, dropping her to Sekhem 5. Aqhat kills his Amkhat, a snake-headed lion, with one almighty strike that splits it apart, and then turns to kill the jackal-headed bull that was besetting Sekhet Bastet in the next round. When struck, both he and Sekhet Bastet send demon-scorpions weeping from their wounds to tear into the flesh of their Lifeless foes. Bast and Sesu Ra overwhelm the lion-headed bull attacking Sesu Ra, and finish it off in time to see the falcon-headed snake assault Aquila separate itself from her and dive over the edge of the building, sailing away on ragged wings of rotted feathers.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi joins them a short while later. The meret notes that LDI was clearly a step ahead of them, they can't even find any evidence that Kotira was ever even in this building, and the relics they'd been told had been taken here had clearly been moved. Using Model Lifeweb and by taking Luca's Drive skill, Sesu Ra is able to work out how to operate the helicopter. He and the mortals retreat to outside the city and circle back on foot, while the rest of the Arisen follow Sekhet Bastet as she opens a portal through Neter-Khetet to Sesu Ra's tomb using Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 2.<br /> <br /> Once Sesu Ra returns to release them from his resting place, the Mummies scatter. Aqhat leaves without a word to try and hunt down his guildmaster. His Sekhem is still apparently raging at its uppermost levels, having earned several Descent resets during the assault. Akenakhi receives a phone call from Nenheta, who criticises him for failing to deliver the canopic jars of Sesu Ra as promised. She threatens to reveal his heretical activities to the Arisen of the Jakarta Nome, but the threat seems to snap something in Akenakhi. He laughed at her. Before, he was hoping to find some way to ensure everyone came through alive, herself included. Now though, he was going to hunt her to the ends of the Earth, he told her.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet returned to the island where they had buried the Amkhat, and was relieved to find it still in place. It pleaded for release, promising secrets and occult lore, but she ignored it. On the other side of the city, Aquila is taking the weapons and armour stolen from LDI and delivering them to Wuldanri, the old woman trying to gather some resistance to Sem-Huf near the site of Aquila's old tomb. Wuldanri accepts the large arsenal happily, as well as the advice that fire, flare guns, and so on are the best way to combat Arisen. Sesu Ra finishes things off by observing with relief that the official story of the night's activities, that a group of robbers with unknown intentions had a violent encounter with nearly defenceless security guards, doesn't appear to offer any immediate links to the meret.<br /> <br /> And Akenakhi returns to his tomb to find that where his four Canopic Jars once stood, only three remained. The Shuankhsen move fast indeed, it seemed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T06:18:48-07:00","id":476854,"title":"","content":"Session 30<br /> <br /> Aquila tried to contact LDI through official channels, using Asa Corp as a cover. She found herself speaking to a man identified as Mr Thornton, who quickly informed her that they knew Asa Corp was just a cover for her meret. He offered to help her philanthropic works if she surrendered herself, coming alone and unarmed to the docks. They would take her in for a single &quot;operation&quot;, and afterwards she would be free to go. Aquila accepted.<br /> <br /> The group assembled at the docks at the appointed time, with Sekhet Bastet watching from offshore in a small boat and the others parked in a van within eyesight of the meeting point. Aquila left the van to head towards the meet-up, when a security guard ordered the others to leave. Reluctantly, they did so.<br /> <br /> Unaware that her helpers were gone, Aquila approached the meeting spot. A mortal Indonesian woman in her early 30s was there to greet her. She introduced herself as Syifa, a lawyer representing LDI, and presented Aquila with a contract and several nondisclosure agreements. The former agreed to provide significant financial and resource-based support for Asa Corp campaigns in the city's slums in return for Aquila's willing participation in an unnamed medical operation. The latter bound Aquila to secrecy regarding the nature of the medical operation and from revealing anything about the LDI facilities she was due to be visiting. Aquila signed both of them, pleased at the civility on display. Then, to the watching Bast's disbelief, she climbed into Syifa's car and the pair drove away.<br /> <br /> At this point, the meret was kicking themselves for not giving Aquila something of Akenakhi's so that they could track her with Blessed Panoply. Having lost Syifa's car, the meret retreated to discuss how to proceed.<br /> <br /> Aquila, meanwhile, was having a rather pleasant chat with Syifa. The woman had been supported through university thanks to the company's backing, and she was pretty enthusiastic about the good LDI did worldwide. The lawyer wasn't able to tell her much about the operation that awaited Aquila though, and after a while she handed Aquila a blindfold to wear until they reached the destination.<br /> <br /> Sometime later, they stopped outside a building and Syifa helped Aquila from the car. The Mummy felt air conditioning as they entered a building. When the blindfold was taken off, they were in a room made of non-earthen materials. A young-looking man, probably Greek or Italian by the look of him and dressed in business atire, approached her with his hand out. He introduced himself as Mike Thornton, and told her he was surprised at how civil the deal had been so far. The doctors would be looking after her from this point on, making sure she was in good shape before the coming operation.<br /> <br /> The doctors ushered Aquila away from her more corporate companions, and did what they could for her many Aggravated Wounds. Then, after many hours, they took her into a room with a large hole in the roof. As the sun approached its zenith, they told Aquila they needed to tie her down. She allowed it without struggling, and once she was securely bound they began to take out a number of mummification tools made from gold. Blasphemous, corrupted versions of canopic jars were laid out before her, and at noon the head doctor raised his arms to the sky and cried out a shockingly blasphemous chant in Iremite, decrying the Judges and declaring an intent to ruin their works in the corporeal world. He then sliced open Aquila's sahu in five ritually significant locations, before piercing her skull with a hollow tube. Sekhem flowed straight from her body, filling two of the canopic jars. The other two remained empty, and the doctors rushed to close the wounds and bandage up the damage done.<br /> <br /> Aquila was now down to Sekhem 3.<br /> <br /> She was then invited to join Mike Thornton in his office. Aquila posited that the two of them were not so different, that LDI's generous works in places like Africa replicated the kind of results that she herself wanted to achieve. She just wished that the group would forego their barbarous ways. In response, Mike pointed out the shocking bloodbath caused by the Arisen assault on LDI's corporate headquarters. Most Arisen were immortal brutes, he said, rushing through their lives with no thought for the mortals about them, their only thoughts for magical artefacts that were not theirs to steal anyway. They acted with violence and attitudes appropriate to ages long past. LDI couldn't deal with such monsters, they had to subdue them with force so that the magic within them could be channelled to produce products capable of healing even the most dire of diseases. And in the end, all of LDI's actions represented a mere minor inconvenience to the Arisen, a slight hastening of a Descent that caused no permanent harm to the Arisen.<br /> <br /> After some discussion, Aquila said she hoped a more peaceful arrangement could be made with LDI. She would reach out to the Arisen of the city, trying to persuade them to stop working against the group. She hoped to even rally some volunteers to offer their Sekhem, in return for the material aid from the company. But, as a show of good faith, she expected Mike to release any Arisen he currently held captive, as well as any relics he might currently be holding. Mike said it wasn't his decision to make, and in any case he needed an exceedingly strong demonstration that the Arisen would cease their violence before he undertook any such actions. He didn't want to be the target of a revenge-fuelled killing spree so soon after the last one.<br /> <br /> Then, as agreed, Aquila departed with a written guarantee that LDI would support her efforts in Jakarta's slums. She was blindfolded on the way out, but she made her way back to the Temple to meet with her meret without any major difficulties. She then decided not to divulge what had happened, merely saying that she had been drained of some of her power and then criticising the group for letting her get taken so easily.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet had spent the last twelve hours watching over their trapped Amkhat. In the final hours before morning, it began to fade. Cursing her in Ammut's name, it swore to her that Ammut's triumph was inevitable. No matter how many centuries it took, the Devourer would claim her. And then it died, collapsing into piles of rotting animal flesh... and the skeleton of a young child.<br /> <br /> The meret decided to chase down Akenakhi's missing canopic jars. Blessed Panoply led them out to the Thousand Islands, straight back to Nenheta's island. Sesu Ra activated Model Lifeweb to reveal anything that was pretending to be something it wasn't, and as Akenakhi led them through the jungle Sesu Ra's vision detected a tree stump that was truly a hiding spot for valuables. Tearing it apart, he revealed both Akenakhi's canopic jar and a book entitled &quot;Sutek's Ladder&quot;. Everyone present recognised the title as an allusion to Apotheosis, and Akenakhi snatched it up. He had brief, scattered visions that this book should have been lost while being transported to Batavia, back when he was following Nenheta's trail. The book was a chronicle of Akenakhi and Nenheta's joint efforts to pursue Apotheosis. The others, not knowing the contents, said that they wished to read the book the moment Akenakhi was finished.<br /> <br /> Frustrated at the lack of any Shuankhsen to fight, Sekhet Bastet used Secrets Ripped From Skies Tier 3 to ask for guidance. She received the following riddle:<br /> <br /> Beneath the floor of the Subtle Bazaar, the husks of souls who once were prey upon the sons of gold and the bearers of flame in the night. Shadows cloud glory and blind eyes until only foes remain.<br /> <br /> (Note: I had to make this up on the spot, so forgive its general clunkiness)<br /> <br /> Sharing this with the meret, Aquila mentioned that the Subtle Bazaar was a Mesen-Nebu concept and Sesu Ra pointed out that the Sons of Gold Dust were Sem-Huf's followers. They promptly decided to pay Sem-Huf a visit.<br /> <br /> And we finished there. With the experience from the session, Akenakhi bought his Memory to 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:57:44-07:00","id":492129,"title":"","content":"Session 31<br /> <br /> Akenakhi retreated to his tomb to examine the words of &quot;Sutek's Ladder&quot;, the book he had written about his quest for Apotheosis. He turned to the opening page, and found the following prayer inside:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I pay homage to thee, O divine ladder. Homage to thee, O Ladder of Sutek.<br /> <br /> Stand thou upright, O divine ladder, whereby Azar came forth to the Light Land.<br /> <br /> For I am thy son, Azar of Old, and thou shall give to me the Ladder of Sutek.<br /> <br /> I need plow no Earth, nor collect any offering, for that which I see and hear feed and nourish me when I appear in the Light Land by the Ladder of Sutek.<br /> <br /> I have gathered together my bones, I have collected my flesh, and I shall go quickly to the Light Land by the Two Fingers of great Sutek, god of the ladder.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> As he read the words, his vision began to swim. He remembered the streets of Constantinople, back during the Third Sothic Turn. The ravages of the Plague of Justinian. He was on his way to a gathering of local Arisen... but something changed. This wasn't a normal memory. He wasn't a passive observer inside his own skull. He was here. He could remember the future, Jakarta, the fight against the Shuankhsen that had plagued most of his fourth Sothic Turn. As his memory cleared, he realised he could remember many of the Descents between now and then, nearly every Descent he had ever had was open to him. The long course of history, his long quest for freedom, it was all clear. And he was here, in the past, in the streets of Constantinople.<br /> <br /> A cultist by his side, a well-dressed young man who he knew was the son of his high priest, asked if anything was wrong. Akenakhi avoided the question, and instead had them continue onwards to the gathering. He recalled that there were rumours of a time when the sky had been darkened and the reach of the Judges had been kept from this world. He had been in henet during this period, but he hoped to speak to Arisen who had been active to see if there were any clues he could ascertain about the time.<br /> <br /> They walk through streets largely devoid of travellers. The bustling streets have been cleared, and those mortals they see hurry past or cross the street to avoid them. The plague has made everyone wary of contact with strangers. Akenakhi recalls that the Su-Menent had a relic at this time which had been shared among the guild's cults, his own included, to protect them from the sickness.<br /> <br /> The pair arrived at the estate of a wealthy landowner. The mortal cultists were hosting a party among those of Constantinople's elite willing to risk such a large social gathering, but Akenakhi was shown down to the wine cellar by a poor, deformed servant who hissed that he should take a torch, head to the back, and press on the ibis to reveal the secret chamber. Sure enough, at the back of the chamber there was a mosaic depicting the pagan gods of Egypt, and a stylised ibis to represent Thoth. When it swung back, Akenakhi entered the hidden chamber where the other Arisen were gathered.<br /> <br /> Including himself, there were five others in attendance. Mekshonat, the Seal of Babylon, was a highly placed Maa-Kep and the host of the evening's gathering. His sister, Benerib the Penitent Falcon, was a Flail Bearer and warrior who kept to her brother's side at all times. Kor-Et-Udar, He of the Consecrated Flesh, was a badly scarred Sesha-Hebsu in close discussion with Ikapushet, Re's Hunger, a golden skinned Mesen-Nebu. Finally, at the back of the chamber, a mysterious Arisen known to the others only as the Tribune seemed content to watch from afar.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi chose to mingle. He knew from the rumours he had heard that Kor-Et-Udar and Mekshonat had been active during the time of darkness. He was able to lure some information out of Kor-Et-Udar by suggesting that the Emperor Justinian could have been involved. Kor-Et-Udar said that all information indicated that a calamity in the east was responsible, but that none of the searchers his guild had sent had returned.<br /> <br /> Then they heard the grinding stone that meant someone else had entered the chamber, and Sekhet Bastet walked in. She announced that she had run her quarry to ground and destroyed it, and Akenakhi recalled that a priest of some note had ordered Nenheta woken to pursue a dangerous quarry before he was woken by his own Sothic Turn. That must have been Sekhet Bastet. He offered her a glass of wine, which she quietly accepted but did not drink. Any attempts to lure out the location of Nenheta were met with cold silence, but with the knowledge of the future in his mind Akenakhi was quite sure he knew what had happened.<br /> <br /> As the party began to separate and leave, Akenakhi had the sudden realisation that he could recall every relic he had ever made in his mortal life. He knew, with equal certainty, that when he had first lived these events his Memory had not been clear enough to do so. His kepher sought out the relics. Most of his arts had been destroyed, consumed, or sent to Duat in the intervening years, but three still remained. The Rod of Tjesh, even now kept in the tomb he shared with Nenheta. The Withering Venom, currently somewhere in south Gaul. And the Serpent Named, in this very city. His kepher senses told him to seek out a ship's captain named Clodius for more information.<br /> <br /> But before he left, he took Mekshonat to one side and told the Maa-Kep about the Su-Menent's relic, and the cure to the plague it represented. He said his conscience had been weighing him down so far, but that he could no longer countenance the suffering of other guilds' cultists to protect his own guild's secrets. When asked where it was now, he speculated that Sekhet Bastet, as an active Su-Menent, could well be the one currently keeping it. Mekshonat gravely promised to investigate the allegations.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi knew that, when he had first lived these events, he had pursued Sekhet Bastet to find out more about Nenheta's fate. But he knew that now, as he knew of the existence of the relic known as the Serpent Named. He hurried towards the docks, ordering his cultists to assemble some warriors and follow him. They were able to locate Clodius as his men, preparing a ship to sail. Although the captain seemed initially reluctant to tell what he knew, Akenakhi spotted that one of his men was beginning to show symptoms of the plague. In return for ridding his ship of the disease, Clodius pointed out a strange galley at the end of the docks. A stranger from another land, a man much like Akenakhi himself, had been taking aboard plague victims with the claim that he could take them to a medicine man who could cure them. The ship was crawling with the diseased.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi and his men hurried towards the galley and boarded it. The putrefying smell emerging from the ship's hold almost overwhelmed the mortals, and as Akenakhi crossed the threshold to the stairwell, a surge of Sybaris sent his mortal followers fleeing into the night.<br /> <br /> The hold was lit by torches, illuminating the piles of bodies. Slight movement and groans indicated that some among the piles were still alive, but telling the blank and staring gazes of the living and dead apart was nearly impossible. At the back of the hold stood the Tribune, who ordered Akenakhi to begone. &quot;You shouldn't be here... you were never here,&quot; he said, sounding more than a little confused.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi said that he was here for the Serpent Named, and the Tribune removed the relic from the folds of his robes. It was a ceremonial flail, its haft wrapped around with a mummified snake. He couldn't take it, however. The Tribune said he had need of it still, to help those suffering from the plague. Spirits began to emerge from the shadows as he spoke, creatures of broken bone and torn corpus, the ghosts of the dead and dying. He had failed to heal their bodies, but he could at least remove their souls from beyond the corruption of the disease. And once his work was done, he would return the relic to his Judge.<br /> <br /> Obviously, that didn't meet with Akenakhi's hopes. He persuaded the Tribune that the Su-Menent had a relic that could cure the plague. If they worked together, they could retrieve it for him. In return, Akenakhi just wanted the Serpent Named. The Tribune agreed, and the pair headed immediately for the neighbourhood where Sekhet Bastet's tomb was kept.<br /> <br /> The neighbourhood was on fire when they arrived. Dead mortals dotted the streets, badly burned. They found Sekhet Bastet protecting a building near the centre of the district, armed with spear and shield and surrounded by the bodies of the dead. Akenakhi demanded that she allow the Tribune to enter and use the relic, but she replied that the First Prophet had ordered that only the Su-Menent should be allowed access. When Akenakhi suggested that the First Prophet be ignored, she attacked. Akenakhi threw himself onto her in an effort to restrain her, but she called on the Secrets Ripped From Skies to strike all three of them with fire from the heavens. The Tribune was hurled back into a building, body shattered, and struck a wall. In that moment the Serpent Named fell from his hands, and the relic mask he wore fell from his face. And Akenakhi realised that the Tribune was Aquila.<br /> <br /> Nearly consumed by the fire, Akenakhi sued for peace. Sekhet Bastet seemed torn as to whether she should accept or not, when the sound of stone breaking came from the building behind her. Without another word, she whirled around and charged inside.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi hastily gathered up the relics and ran. He made his way back to his tomb. As he entered, his vision swam, and he found himself back in the fourth Sothic Turn, seated at the table where he had been reading Sutek's Ladder. Except now, in his hands, he held the relics he had stolen from the past.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the city, Sesu Ra and Sekhet Bastet arrived at Sem-Huf's tomb to find a mob brawling with his cultists in the streets. There were brief glimpses of men with automatic weapons, but for the moment the fighting appeared to be non-lethal. The Arisen pushed their way through the mob, found a cultist to speak to, and ascertained that Sem-Huf was in his tower putting out fires that had been started. They headed there, bulled there way past the guards at the building who quickly caved to pressure from the Arisen, and walked up to speak to Sem-Huf.<br /> <br /> The Mesen-Nebu was wielding the Power of Re to put out fires in danger of consuming his estate. He told them that the fighting had started only a short time ago, apparently provoked by the deaths of some insignificant locals. They had blamed Sem-Huf for the deaths, although he'd had nothing to do with it, and attacked his tomb. His cultists had forced them back. Sesu Ra and Sekhet Bastet offered to finish off the mortal problem for him, and he accepted the offer gladly.<br /> <br /> With Luca by their side, the two Mummies walked out to where the two mobs faced one another. Sekhet Bastet smiled at Sem-Huf's cultists, and in a quiet voice told them to run and not look back. As the cultists fled, Sekhet Bastet struck the largest concentration of attackers with Secrets Ripped From Skies Tier 2. The Sybaris left nearly everyone who wasn't struck dead by the meteor begging for their lives, and they quickly crushed the last bit of resistance. Then they felt Sekhem flare in the tower behind them, someone unleashing an Epic Utterance. They left Luca to guard the prisoners and raced back to Sem-Huf's side. They passed the guards, torn apart by the teeth of a Shuankhsen, and raced into the chamber in time to witness Gator consuming the last of Sem-Huf's body.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed is the God-King, Sekhet Bastet unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 2, and Gator unleashed Dust Beneath Feet Tier 2. That took the Arisen off-guard for a moment, as it wasn't something they'd ever seen the Shuankhsen do before. As they squared off, the Shuankhsen demanded to know where Emerset could be found. Sesu Ra snarled out &quot;Silence beast, and die like a dog,&quot; and the two giants slammed into one another.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra fought with a khopesh made of light and shadow, while Gator had only his teeth and stone form. He tore massive chunks out of the larger Mummy, before Bast distracted him by digging her relic knife into his back. Given an opening, Sesu Ra landed several powerful blows with his blade, unleashing a mystic rot that ravaged Gator's form. Although he severely injured the two Arisen, Sesu Ra's attacks were too much. He said to tell Emerset he would be coming for her, and walked through the nearest wall to escape.<br /> <br /> The Mummies went back to their prisoners. Bast discovered both the location of the original killing, and the fact that their weapons and the knowledge that fire would harm the Arisen had come from an old local woman named Wuldanri. However, this attack had been a spur of the moment thing organised without her consent, a furious retaliation by the men of the slum against the deaths of their own. Bast left to speak to Wuldanri, and Sesu Ra and Luca executed the prisoners and left to fine the scene of the murders.<br /> <br /> Bast found Wuldanri's home guarded by a giant, heavily muscled man. When he refused to let her past, she unleashed Terror Sybaris and left him begging for his life on the ground. She walked in to confront Wuldanri, who demanded to know what she had done to her son. &quot;Put him on the ground, where he belongs,&quot; Bast said, before beginning the interrogation. Wuldanri was hard to break, but Bast's Fearsome Soul eventually broke her and she extracted Aquila's description and a fairly detailed knowledge of their intended plans for the district. That done, Bast spoke Wuldanri's name into the Pale Brood and left.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Luca, meanwhile, had found the site of the original killings. Someone had written the words &quot;No one is safe&quot; in the blood, using the hieroglyphs of Ancient Irem. It mimicked the site of Mot-Tan's death directly, suggesting that the killings might be connected. Luca did find that the &quot;handwriting&quot; was different, but they couldn't definitively determine anything from that. The style certainly seemed to indicate someone who had used Iremite in life, rather than a cultist who had discovered it at a later date, however.<br /> <br /> The meret assembled at the city Temple, where Aquila was waiting. Akenakhi had come to tell the others about his strange voyages through time, but he was pushed to the side by Sesu Ra and Sekhet Bastet who demanded a full explanation of Aquila's actions. She had set mortals against another of her guild, and allowed a Shuankhsen to consume one of the Arisen. Combined with the fact that she had refused to tell them much about what had happened when LDI kidnapped her, they were extremely suspicious. Akenakhi handed Aquila her mask, a one dot relic which mystically shielded the bearer's identity while worn, and the sight provoked a brief flash of memory in Bast who recalled fighting someone wearing that mask. That didn't help soothe tensions either.<br /> <br /> The argument raged for a while, Bast and Aquila hurling furious accusations at one another. Bast had no real evidence for her suspicions, and Sesu Ra seemed inclined to put the events down to Aquila's incompetence, which angered Aquila even more. Eventually, Sesu Ra grew sick of watching and walked out. Bast followed a little bit later, warning Aquila not to slip again. Aquila spat out that she was a Guildmaster of the Mesen-Nebu, and not accountable to either the Tef-Aabhi or the Su-Menent.<br /> <br /> Once alone with Akenakhi, the two swapped their stories in full. Akenakhi elaborated on his tale of being cast into the past, and told her the story of Constantinople and what had transpired there. Aquila shared what had happened when she had been taken by LDI, and how she thought they could align their interests with that of the organisation to break the hold of the more brutal Arisen on the city. Akenakhi, always happy to cause trouble to the guilds, agreed that it seemed like a good course of action. They didn't want to see any more of the kind of bloodshed their own meret brought in their wake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:16:28-07:00","id":492241,"title":"","content":"Oh, and the relics.<br /> <br /> The Serpent Named (4 dot Uter)<br /> Size 2, Durability 2, Structure 4<br /> <br /> <i>The Serpent Named appears to be a mummified snake, carefully coiled around the haft of a ceremonial flail. Its head, mouth agape and eye sockets staring, rests at the base of the haft. The presence of the delicate animal remains makes it impossible to wield the flail as a weapon, and it must be carried with care. It looks as if the bandages that bind it were once dyed a brilliant array of colours, but they have all but faded.</i><br /> <br /> Power: The bearer of the Serpent Named may project their soul through the relic, taking an instant action and a point of Willpower. It emerges like a whisper, a sliver of consciousness cast into the void of Neter-Khetet. They manifest in their soul-form, a mystic representation of their Decree animal. This spirit form is represented by a ghost. This ghost has a Power, Finesse, and Resistance of 1, an Essence Pool equal to their Decree Pillar (mortals get 0), and the Spirit Prowess Numen.<br /> If the bearer knows someone\u2019s true name, however, the powers become even greater. They can call out the soul of anyone whose true name they know as an instant action. A true named soul has its attributes determined in the normal fashion (Power equals highest of Strength, Intelligence, or Presence, Finesse equals highest of Wits, Manipulation, or Dexterity, Resistance is highest of Stamina, Resolve, or Composure). They get 10 Essence, the Spirit Prowess, Regeneration, and Old Age (always 10 for Arisen, partly because they\u2019re actually that old and partly because added protections layered onto their soul).<br /> In either case, if destroyed, the bearer is forcibly returned to their body and lose all Willpower and Pillars.<br /> As long as someone's spirit is absent from their body, their body cannot take any actions. Arisen seem to return to henet, their sahu vanishing and leaving behind their dead khat. No Sekhem can be detected in the corpse, to all extents and purposes they appear to have finished their Descent. Mortals appear to have fallen into a coma, and it is impossible to detect brain activity until their spirit returns. The spirit remains separate from the body until an akhet can be found in Neter-Khetet that will return the spirit to the corporeal world.<br /> <br /> Curse: The bearer\u2019s true name becomes vulnerable to other occultists. All attempts to discover it gain a +3 bonus.<br /> <br /> Note: Aquila realised that, based on Akenakhi's description of her actions as the Tribune and his description of what the Serpent Named could do, she must have at one point known enough about true name to determine the true names of the plague victims aboard her ship.<br /> <br /> Face of Deception (1 dot Regia)<br /> Size 2, Durability 4, Structure 6<br /> <br /> <i>This mask appears to have been cast from a gold and bronze alloy in the style of a Greek theatre mask. Beyond the wide, open eyes and mouth, there are no details that give any indication as to what the mask is meant to represent.</i><br /> <br /> Powers: While wearing the mask, the bearer has no recognisable features. Any who try to describe them will be unable to recall any details about their person that could lead to determining the wearer's identity, whether that be their height, skin colour, what they were wearing, even their sex or gender. It is still easy enough to remember the actions they take however, and nothing prevents someone who knows the wearer carries the mask from putting two and two together to figure out who this mysterious stranger might be.<br /> <br /> Curse: The bearer suffers a -1 penalty on all Memory checks, as it becomes harder to maintain a hold on their identity while hidden in such a fashion. Mesen-Nebu are exempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T06:55:47-07:00","id":500259,"title":"","content":"Session 32<br /> <br /> After the meeting with Aquila, Akenakhi returned to his tomb. As he turned into the alley approaching his tomb's entrance, he saw a woman sitting in the middle of the street in a pink sleeveless dress. She smiled up at him, and said &quot;Hello Akenakhi. I've been waiting to meet you for some time. My name is Iwseck.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi realised that she was holding something in her lap. With an impish smile, Iwseck turned it around so he could see that it was Nenheta's head. Her features were twisted in a rictus of pain and her hair matted with her own blood. &quot;She promised me something, Akenakhi. Something she couldn't deliver on. Now, I don't like violence, but I think she was protecting you. And I don't like my friends to lie to me like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> She climbed to her feet and tossed Nenheta's head into the nearby gutter. She explained that Akenakhi had failed her as well, but she wasn't angry. He couldn't have known he was working for her. But now, in no uncertain terms, she expected him to deliver Sesu Ra's canopic jars to her immediately. If he didn't, she would kill every mortal close to him and desecrate his tomb, and that would just be to make sure she had his attention. She wouldn't go as easy on him as Nenheta had. But, on the other hand, Akenakhi could use her help for his little experiment in freedom. Sesu Ra was part of the very establishment he hated, and she could always resurrect Nenheta to take the fall for him once it was done. Just so long as her own name stayed out of it, she would be happy. Akenakhi promised to deliver the canopic jars to her, and she walked away smiling.<br /> <br /> After that disturbing experience, Akenakhi turned his attention back to Sutek's Ladder. It didn't have much more to tell him than what he had already discovered through his own memories, thanks to his heavy focus on restoring his memories. What it did tell him was that he and Nenheta had never been lovers, that tidbit must have simply been a lie she thought would make him easier to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Sesu Ra did some digging around the docks and discovered that a company called Integrated Transport Solutions dealt with the transportation of sea and air freight for most of LDI's transport needs. He remembered the name from the attack on LDI's headquarters, where they had walked through the offices of a company by that name. He contacted them under the guise of a representative of Asa Corp, and was surprised to discover that they were quite genial towards him. Thanks to his familiarity with corporate structures, a combination of successful Politics and Persuasion rolls allowed him to secure a copy of the manifest of the next ocean-bound shipment.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet and Luca were spending the time trying to discover anything they could about local pirate activity. Their plan for disrupting all LDI's future shipment relied upon finding a group willing to seize any LDI ships that entered Indonesian waters. Their exploration led them to Gorijo, the man who had first put them in contact with Reza's smugglers. The middleman was still working near the resort where they had first met him, and after a brief discussion with Bast he caved and told them that Kudama Jav was the main underground figure engaging in maritime activity. He seemed quite terrified of the man, although he'd only met with him in person a few times. Stories said his enemies died under mysterious circumstances, found without a mark on their bodies but expressions of horror etched into their faces.<br /> <br /> They met up with Luca. Gorijo told them how to go about meeting with Kudama. He had tunnels beneath the fishing dock districts of North Jakarta, their entrances hidden as seemingly normal maintenance tunnels and sewer access points. There were buildings near each one with Kudama's men, who would watch these points and help potential business partners to enter them. They found these men without a problem, and Sesu Ra quickly convinced them that they were here to discuss business. They ended up in the tunnels, which started out looking very modern in appearance. Quite quickly, however, the pipes and lighting fixtures began to fade into the wall, and the concrete walls began to change colour to a yellowish sandstone of far more ancient origins. They realised that etched into the walls were Iremite hieroglyphs, telling the story of an Arisen called Thothekmet. He had pursued an undead abomination, the product of a failed experiment, to Batavia after the creature sought refuge with the Dutch. The first tunnel seemed to describe the journey to Indonesia. At that point, Luca draw their gaze to the shadows cast by the flaming torches placed at even intervals along the tunnel. The shadows thrown by the light seemed to suggest a lot more people were in this tunnel than just the three of them. When Sesu Ra unleashed Tier 1 Chthonic Dominion, it revealed that next to each torch was a figure in a dark robe, a scroll clutched in their left hand. The hoods of these figures turned to watch the three as they continued deeper into the maze.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra noticed a few other things as they continued. He realised that the maze wasn't conforming to regular geography, but was rather bending and twisting according to the dictates of magic. They would have been lost without his occult senses to guide them. On top of that, a brief study shared the sudden insight that the knowledge used to build these tunnels could be repurposed in his geometric network. Instead of creating a city in which Arisen descend more slowly, or one in which Sebayt experience allowed them to fight the grind of ages on their memories, he could create a Lifeweb spanning the entire city that would allow him to treat all of Jakarta as his tomb.<br /> <br /> He didn't share this revelation with the others. Instead, he led them to the centre of the maze, to the lair of Kudama Jav. They found smugglers, and a great deal of illicit cargo, in the central chamber. Kudama, a rake-thin man with wild eyes, seemed startled by their appearance and demanded to know how they had arrived. The Arisen avoided the question. They proposed a deal, agreeing to supply his group with weapons in return for their help attacking LDI's freighters and a promise to give them 80% of the loot. Both Bast and Sesu Ra realised during this conversation that the book Kudama was clutching was a relic. Bast queried whether he understood the writing in the tunnels. It had stopped three turns before reaching the maze's centre, ending suddenly with the words that Thothekmet was closing in on his quarry. Kudama appeared to have no idea what the words said, and was greatly interested to hear the story. The group left soon after that, finding their way out easily enough. Sesu Ra theorised that the tunnel network would be the perfect tool for smugglers. Mortal attention largely avoided it, as it was functionally a tomb with the Obscure merit. Even if police investigated, they would need knowledge of the occult to locate the &quot;stable&quot; rooms where the products were kept. The rest of the maze was constantly shifting, and they could be lost for all time if they entered without any idea of how to navigate. Meanwhile, the smugglers could use the tunnels to get anywhere quickly, as the maze could cut through seemingly impassible obstacles.<br /> <br /> With this agreement struck, the group decided to wait and focus on healing their wounds. Bast and Sesu Ra used the down-time to spend on Sesu Ra teaching Bast the Utterance Blessed is the God-King. They also gathered Akenakhi to mount another expedition to try and find the Source of the River's Curse from Sekhet Bastet's visions, but it was no more forthcoming than before. It was at this point that Akenakhi decided to share the information that one of the Shuankhsen was trying to get him to steal Sesu Ra's canopic jars. He refused to name the Shuankhsen, afraid she might have mystic senses that would detect him breaking his promise in that way, which made Bast somewhat suspicious. That, and the knowledge that the Shuankhsen might have some kind of leverage on him. He shared the true secrets in private with Sesu Ra sometime later, when they met together at the temple. He told the full story, saying that it was Iwseck behind it all, and that she knew he was a heretic. He explained that he was a student of Apotheosis and that she sought to use his studies against him. Sesu Ra wasn't particularly interested in the revelation of heresy, as it had little to do with his Guild's own projects. However, as part of his agreement to stay silent on the matter, he did ask to read Sutek's Ladder. Akenakhi delivered a copy of the book, after making a show of burning it before the meret so that Bast would not seek the same thing.<br /> <br /> Days passed. The group waited for word of Sem-Huf's awakening, but there was none. However, a messenger did arrive from Rekhenaten's cultists. Rekhenaten had awoken for his Sothic Turn, and had asked to speak with his Guildmaster. Sesu Ra was escorted to the Flesh Mason's lavish living quarters, and there the two Tef-Aabhi discussed their plans for the city. Rekhenaten said he had collected many vestiges to help anchor the arcane geometries Sesu Ra had spent decades constructing. They weren't far from completion, they just needed the missing head from Sesu Ra's memories and they would be on the verge of completion. That, and to discover what revelations the site in the East held. There had been one in North, South, West, and Central Jakarta, so there must be one last secret to discover. Having warned Rekhenaten to step up security against the Shuankhsen, Sesu Ra returned to his tomb.<br /> <br /> Bast spent some time with the personal cult she was growing in Mot-Tan's former district, a new attempt to create a cult dedicated wholly to the Judges. She met with Tio, a middle aged man with a milky white eye who seemed to have taken the role of policing the cult upon himself, Alex, a fifteen year old boy who was one of the many cultists showing signs of the same wasting sickness she remembered afflicting her old jungle cult, and Julie, a ragged, malnourished woman with a raw wound where her left ear should be. After complimenting Tio's willingness to cut open his own scars during a ritual devoted to her and dealing with Julie's request for retribution upon her husband, quickly accomplished by the use of the Pale Brood, she did some cursory investigation of the disease. It was afflicting those who drank from the river most strongly, and, oddly, her cultists were disproportionately affected even among the other slum dwellers.<br /> <br /> Iwseck, meanwhile, had grown impatient. She confronted Akenakhi at his tomb again, this time wearing a floral green dress. Akenakhi appeared unflustered by her sudden appearance, asking after the brand of clothing she was wearing. Iwseck told him to ask the woman who had worn it before her, and then asked if they could speak in his tomb, somewhere they wouldn't disturb any onlookers. Akenakhi agreed. Keeping her voice measured, she asked why he hadn't provided the jars yet. It had been several days, after all. Akenakhi tried to stall for more time, saying that he was on the verge of being able to enact his plan and that killing him would hurt her plans, not help them. It didn't work. Iwseck unleashed Blessed is the God-King Tier 3, turning into an enormous being sporting a desiccated lion's head. She picked Akenakhi and slammed him into the wall. He tried one more time to delay her, to convince her that this was a mistake. When they didn't work, he wriggled free and bolted for the exit. She was on top of him before he could make it, and tore him apart. He felt her teeth sink deep into his body and soul as he collapsed. As the last shreds of his Sekhem were torn away, his pillars were left vulnerable. Akenakhi lost not only his final dot of Sekhem, but also a dot of Ab to Iwseck's feasting. It was the end of his Descent, the last moments of his Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra was the first to discover the carnage. Days later, he entered Akenakhi's tomb to return Sutek's Ladder. He found the shredded remains of Akenakhi, left to lie in his tomb rather than be consumed, and a second copy of Sutek's Ladder lying beside the corpse.<br /> <br /> And that's where we ended it. Aquila's player couldn't make the session, but I have been informed that Aquila will be going to Memory 5. Sekhet Bastet is planning on getting Memory 4. And Akenakhi, despite dropping to Memory 6, should get a final flashback before his soul returns to Duat. So next session should involve a lot of time in the past...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 05-04-2015, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:41:47-07:00","id":505288,"title":"","content":"Let's do the Timewarp again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:46:05-07:00","id":516660,"title":"","content":"Session 33<br /> <br /> Akenakhi's death sent him plunging into the final Death Cycle of this Descent. He descended again into the swirling darkness of Neter-Khetet, a path beneath his feet leading him to an enormous vaulted arch. Hieroglyphs ran up the monument's sides, saying &quot;The Akhet Betwixt Two Titans&quot;. In the shadow of the gate, Anpu waited. He held a staff in his left hand, and gestured for Akenakhi to follow.<br /> <br /> Before long, the ground began to crunch under Akenakhi's feet. The darkness gave way to light, and he found himself standing atop a sand dune with Anpu by his side. The god handed him the staff, and a glimmer of starlight atop the object seemed to light a path for Akenakhi to follow. An impression of water and safety filled his mind, and he knew where he had to go.<br /> <br /> He never made it, however. The oasis promised in Anpu's vision never appeared. The red sun in the black sky above began to burn, and Akenakhi realised he was being hunted. Massive, bloated scorpions began to emerge from the sands, rising from his own footprints. The slaughterers converged on him, and poison filled his veins even as their mandibles sank into his flesh. He staggered and collapsed, and the pain seemed to last an eternity.<br /> <br /> When Akenakhi regained his sight, he found himself lost beneath the stars. In the far East was an enormous mountain, crested with sunlight. To the West was its twin, guarding the sun's resting place. They were the only landmarks he could rely upon. He was standing on a flat, desolate plain, but ruins covered the ground.They moved and changed constantly, like a mirage, the architecture changing through various cities he had known in his long life. He saw buildings from Jakarta, Constantinople, Paris, Irem, and others, all ruined by time and some kind of apocalyptic devastation.<br /> <br /> Then he heard the sound of marching feet. From the West approached an army, a legion of Irem's dead. Ghosts of slave-shoulders armed and armoured in the regalia he knew in life, their flesh peeling and rotting as they walked. Despite their ephemeral appearance, Akenakhi knew their blades would cut as surely as any mortal blade.<br /> <br /> He sensed a presence beside him, and looked up to see Anpu watching the scene impassively. Following the god's gaze, he saw in the East a howling mass rising from the ruins of the shattered city. Flaming spirits, the broken remnants of mortal souls, created and empowered to fight the intruders. They plunged down and crashed into the ranks of the legion of the dead. Fire turned the sand to glass, and Akenakhi felt himself drop through the glass into the darkness of Duat.<br /> <br /> Elsewhere, Aquila found herself meditating on new memories of her life just after coming to Jakarta. Her cult was small, just three mortals, but they had secured the gem she requested. They brought it to her, and she drained the Sekhem eagerly. For the first time in months, the world seemed to have colour again. She was invigorated, and rose to thank her servants for the duty they had performed.<br /> <br /> Then, heavy footsteps sounded, and a large man entered her tomb. In his arms he carried Hetenatra, the Lady of the Broken Stele. Aquila saw the judgement in her glare, and realised with a sinking feeling that the other Arisen knew what she had been doing to stay awake.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sphinx of Rome,&quot; Hetenatra addressed her, &quot;You have sinned most grievously against the Judges' will. Six years of heresy lie behind you. For the sake of a mortal child, you have forsaken your purpose, abandoned your fellow Deathless, and, most grievously of all, you have committed the heresy of despoiling relics to ensure your longevity. Do you contest these allegations?&quot;<br /> <br /> Aquila gritted her teeth. &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hetenatra ordered her cultists to bring in the child. Phatri was a beautiful child at six years of age, wearing a simple brown shift that Aquila had made with her own hands. The hem was stained dark, a sign that she must have been playing near the ocean.<br /> <br /> Quietly, Hetenatra explained that she could kill the child, and not a single Arisen in the city would say it had been the wrong choice. The very guild Aquila claimed to master would applaud the decision, once the full scope of her crimes became known. But, Hetenatra was willing to show leniency. She did not think Aquila was entirely given over to heresy. She could use a highly placed servant, and if Aquila swore to aid her in all her efforts to bring justice to heretics then judgement for her indiscretions could be postponed indefinitely. However, if she ever found that Aquila had devoured another relic, her doom would fly on wings of fire.<br /> <br /> Aquila's pride battled against her desire to see Phatri safe, but her love for Phatri won out. She accepted the offer.<br /> <br /> Hours later, she was sitting by the beach watching the sun set, Phatri curled against her side.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mother?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes?&quot;<br /> &quot;Are you going to go away soon?&quot;<br /> &quot;Soon, my love, but not just yet. And I will always return to protect you.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the darkness of her own tomb, Sekhet Bastet felt her own mind expand. She remembered another dark temple, long ago.<br /> <br /> <i>Fear the red-haired man. Exalt the square-eared beast.</i><br /> <br /> The cryptic phrase has dogged Sekhet Bastet through the centuries. It is, she believes, a clue to her True Purpose.<br /> <br /> She remembered the Crusades, and the end of a bloody campaign. A long lost temple to the Judges, hidden away in the mountains, was finally reclaimed. Even as the hymns of Christian warriors rose from the camp outside, the cults within the army had ensured that the holy ground remained sacrosanct and safe from the monotheists. The Su-Menent had gathered in the old temple, and each was taking their time to present a sermon. Bast remembered speaking herself.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is right to worship what one fears. Witness the Judges, in all their terrible glory. Their splendour is more than the mortal eye can comprehend, and their forms inspire emotions humans cannot readily accept. Terror and awe are simply signs that what we perceive is beyond our ken.&quot;<br /> <br /> Her words on the nature of worship, the necessity of fear, and humanity's need for an impending judgement are well received. As she descends once more to take her place among the black-robed masses, she spots something that makes her freeze in her tracks. Beneath layers of dust and the detritus of ages is a statue of a square-eared beast. As she peers closer to examine it, its eyes peel open and she finds herself staring into a gulf of stars.<br /> <br /> The statue doesn't move, but a voice appears to pour from the vista and sink deep into her mind. &quot;Your choice, She Who Is Power, remains the same as ever. You may choose victory in the arms of your enemies, or a violent death as you stand alone. The stars see the passage of your fate. You fight on so many fronts, against the heresy within, the Devourer's slaves, mortal treachery, and abominations that exist outside the natural order. And yet, your greatest victories will come when you allow one enemy to live so that you may hasten the death of another.&quot;<br /> <br /> The temple melts away. Bast finds herself on a barren rock in the midst of the void. Stars burn close, bolts of golden fire ripple across the cosmos, and she notes without surprise that her body has become that of a colossal jackal.<br /> <br /> Beyond the light, she senses her enemies on the move. Shuankhsen move like sharks, testing the water for the scent of Sekhem. Amkhata flock like carrion birds in their wake. The tiny motes of humanity are a constant irritant, needles against her skin. The stars themselves seem hostile, turning their malevolent gaze upon her, and she feels their will as a curse that seems to sap her energy and turn fate itself against her. Beyond even the stars, stranger things crawl, creatures that make her soul rebel even to consider the nature of their existence.<br /> <br /> All these foes descend, and Bast finds herself overwhelmed. Her skin tears beneath the onslaught, her flesh unravels, her very existence becomes a raw wound pulsing with agony. Against any single one of these enemies, she could prevail. But against all of them...<br /> <br /> In desperation, she remembers the words. She exerts her will, and her enemies turn upon themselves. And for a moment, Bast glimpses the Ladder of Sutek. With a wrench, she realises she has seen the path heretics walk towards Apotheosis. When she looks down, she sees her own feet upon it as well.<br /> <br /> The vision ends suddenly. Thoroughly disturbed, Bast tries to focus her thoughts on the Shuankhsen. Cutting herself to improve her visions, she seeks out the cursed Uter she has been hunting. Yet again, however, her visions lead to nothing. Just the same images of pipes pumping vile substances into the river.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra orders the meret to gather, and reveals the destruction of Akenakhi. Troubled by the death of their ally, they continue their hunt for the Shuankhsen. Bast and Aquila seek out Yama-Het, hoping that she might have more on the actions of the Shuankhsen. The Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster is disturbed, but has nothing of substance to offer. They ask her advice on the bloody writing found at the site of Mot-Tan and Sem-Huf's deaths, and point out that some force is preying on the isolated Arisen in the city. Unfortunately, she isn't able to make any sense of the events.<br /> <br /> The meret oversees dredging operations they set in motion, in the hopes that finding the cause of the river's taint will lure out the Shuankhsen. They find that some of the dredge contains a thick reddish sludge, with a tendency to stick to itself in lumps resembling flesh. From what they observe, no matter where in the river they dredge, those dredging operations manned largely or entirely by cultists discover this substance while those involving outside contractors don't seem to encounter any.<br /> <br /> A week passes largely without event, allowing Aquila to recover from her wounds. She spends some time away from the others, preying on the city's criminal population by targeting jails in order to gather the hearts she needs to heal. Dust Beneath Feet makes her a consummate predator, able to come and go without notice. Sekhet Bastet and Aquila each spend the time mastering a new Utterance. Bast draws on Sesu Ra's tutelage to learn Blessed Is The God-King, while Aquila mines her own memories to once again wield Harvest The Divine Flesh.<br /> <br /> At the end of the week, Bast and Aquila meet at the temple and find Aqhat there. With his flesh restored, he takes the form a blockish Persian man with light olive skin, a thick, curly beard, and a shaved head. He is wearing a simple linen wrap around his waist, dark kohl around his eyes, and has his axe in hand. They have caught him mid-practice. The weapon moves impossible fast as he goes through the movements, displaying a skill and speed no mortal man could ever match.<br /> <br /> The three have a quick conversation. Aqhat reveals that he has turned to outside help to locate Kotira. Allies are due to arrive at the airport tomorrow. He is glad to see the pair, because their meret proved themselves allies in their fight together. He asks their help. The newcomers will be vulnerable when they arrive, and he suspects LDI will be one step ahead. If they could secure the airport for the newcomers, he would be most appreciative.<br /> <br /> The pair agree. Bast asks who it is that Aqhat has summoned, and he says that the newcomers will be of the Maa-Kep. Their names are Benerib, the Penitent Falcon, and Mekshonat, the Seal of Babylon. Benerib has been a close friend of the Su-Menent for centuries, and long ago she and Kotira marked a mystic pact that should allow her to locate Kotira immediately.<br /> <br /> They inform Sesu Ra of the proceedings, and decide to wake Akenakhi. A Sekhem 10 Mummy would be good back-up if LDI does mount a serious attack. Investigating his tomb, they find that he has sealed his relics within his tomb using Palace Knows Its Pharaoh. There are two entrances to his treasury, and they are connected in such a way that entering the treasury through one causes the walker to exit the treasury through the other in the same instant. After some consideration, Sekhet Bastet uses Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Tier 2 to pass through the walls and snatch the Rod of Tjesh.<br /> <br /> The cultists, under Aquila's direction, then raise Akenakhi back to life. The Rod of Tjesh is drained in the process, becoming inactive for the next 14 weeks. He rises, and they give him the command &quot;Destroy the Shuankhsen&quot;.<br /> <br /> First, however, a quick detour to the airport (with Akenakhi carefully swathed in layers of clothes to avoid invoking widespread Sybaris). The meret, and Luca, arrived several hours before the plane was due and began scouting out the area surrounding the private hanger chartered for the use of the arriving Arisen. They discovered several signs in a quick secession that something was amiss. Luca noted the baggage handlers are not the ones listed on the documentation of those chosen for the roster that day. Bast found caltrops had been scattered across the driveway leading away from the hanger. Aquila put two and two together, and quietly excused herself. She called Mike Thornton, and warned him that he should call off any operations LDI was running near the airport that day. They were facing down an entire meret, at least. Mike quietly thanked her for the information, and hung up. Over the next few minutes, each one of the suspicious baggage handlers slipped away. Luca followed them undetected.<br /> <br /> The private plane arrived without incident. Benerib emerged, a handsome woman of clear Iremite origins wearing a formal suit and high heels. She greeted each of the group, although when Akenakhi asked if she remembered him she politely indicated that she didn't, to his disappointment. She asked that they wait until her brother could be off-loaded from the plane, and they watched as a large packing crate was loaded into a truck. Passing through customs was smooth, the group got the impression that Kotira's cultists must be at work, and before long they were heading for the temple. Benerib wanted to leave her brother there, and then immediately head for Kotira's current location.<br /> <br /> They picked up Aqhat at the temple, who was wearing his full battle armour, and piled into the truck again. Benerib's sense for Kotira led them straight to a hospital in West Jakarta. They asked Aqhat to wait while they investigated, and went inside. The topmost levels were where Kotira was. So, acting like they belonged there, the meret and Benerib walked straight for the elevator and headed straight for the top floor. The doors started to open...<br /> <br /> And we ran out of time, so I called the session there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:42:15-07:00","id":524292,"title":"","content":"You didn't mention my 10 minutes of back-and-forthing on whether or not Iwsek had stolen the Serpent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T06:35:07-07:00","id":533133,"title":"","content":"Session 34<br /> <br /> Akenakhi returned to Memory 7, and recalled a time from his first ever Sothic Turn. He remembered the days the River ran red and the Old Kingdom shook with the fury of a host of immortals, but most of all he remembered the priests of Iunu. He remembered how they, mere mortal men, defied the Judges and forged relics and Amkhata to fight off Arisen and Shuankhsen alike. He remembered the power they fielded to stave off Sybaris, and the way their veneration turned towards the sky and A'aru, rather than the depths of Duat.<br /> <br /> He found himself creeping through a temple complex at dusk, hiding from passing Amkhata and using the Rod of Tjesh to by-pass mortal guards. He met with a priest named Pohmet, somewhere in the inner sanctuary of the Temple of Re. There was an arch there, although the architecture was of a time and place he didn't recognise, but he could see that it was adorned with constellations from the night sky. In an alcove behind this arch was a scared and beaten young woman, maybe fourteen years of age, with her hands bound. She looked as if she were about to speak, but Pohmet silenced her with a sharp gesture.<br /> <br /> Together, the priest and Akenakhi stepped through the arch. The world seemed to crumble, buildings melting like wax. The roof came crashing down, passing straight through Akenakhi without harming him. The very Earth itself grew pale and seemed to fade away. Everywhere Akenakhi looked, there were only stars. He was standing inside a small sphere on a surface almost entirely transparent. Everywhere, above, below, and all around, were the stars. He could see the sun, the brightest of them all, burning in the distance. He noted, as he walked, that the gravity of the sphere changed such that no matter where he stood, the ground was beneath his feet.<br /> <br /> Pohmet and the young woman had come through with him. The priest handed him a knife, and told him that, &quot;Your people discovered the essential truth of magic. All power requires suffering.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi remembered his disappointment when faced with his Judge, the devastation upon awakening and realising the kind of existence he had given his life for. He took the blade and drove it into the woman's heart. He heard a whisper as she died, although whether it was from her or another source he couldn't say.<br /> <br /> &quot;Was it worth it?&quot;<br /> <br /> He realised the blood wasn't dripping down then, but rather falling up towards the centre of the sphere. Watching, he saw a glimmer of light, a glimpse of hieroglyphs floating there just out of reach above his head. The sight of it was like a searing brand against his mind, and the vision broke apart there.<br /> <br /> As Akenakhi opened his eyes, he saw the elevator doors opening. He was back in Jakarta, with Benerib and the rescue party for Kotira. They entered a hospital ward, white and sterile and smelling of formaldehyde, with a dozen beds hidden behind green curtains. Bast walked to the first one and pulled it open. A young woman lay there, staring blankly at the ceiling. She was quite, quite dead.<br /> <br /> The meret checked the other beds. All save the last contained the bodies of mortals. But there, in the final bed, they found Kotira.<br /> <br /> Her sahu was as withered as her khat, and she stared sightless at the ceiling. Her eyes had been torn out, the sockets around them broken by the trauma. She had a large hole in her forehead and several more punched in her torso. A black fluid was leaking from her ears as well, staining the white pillow beneath her head. She seemed to sense their presence, and started to murmur something beneath her breath. That was when the party sensed Sekhem, and the first of the corpses began to stir.<br /> <br /> The corpses were rising in pairs, two every round of combat. Aquila grappled one of the first, while Akenakhi turned the curtain rail of Kotira's bed into a spear. They had destroyed one attacker, only to see four more of the corpses rise, when Sesu Ra realised what was going on. Kotira was using Words of Dead Glory to create Nenitu. He yelled at Bast to silence Kotira (Grip of Death) and so prevent her from unleashing her Utterance. Bast raced to do so, while the meret and Benerib dispatched the remaining walking corpses.<br /> <br /> Aquila rendered Kotira unconscious, and they quietly stole her from the hospital in a wheelchair. They didn't face any further opposition. When they reached the van and spoke to Aqhat, trying to work out what had caused her to attack them, he examined her closely and said she'd been blinded and rendered deaf. She must have thought they were LDI and was trying to defend herself.<br /> <br /> The group drove back to the Temple, Aqhat ranting about the judgement he would bring down upon the mortals who had dared do this to a Prophet. The group left the van and began to carry Kotira inside.<br /> <br /> The world turned to fire.<br /> <br /> Aquila picked herself up slowly, on shaking arms. She looked around. The Temple had collapsed. The path they had been walking on was gone. Her meret's bodies were scattered across the pavement, blasted beyond repair. Benerib and Kotira could also be seen, broken almost beyond recognition. Aqhat and her were still standing, but neither of them were in good shape. She was trying to gather her senses when an enormous, bloated creature pulled itself from the rubble and charged at her.<br /> <br /> Before the attacker could reach her, Aquila unleashed Dust Beneath Feet Tier 2 to armour herself in Earth. It slammed into her then, attacking with razor sharp claws and teeth. Aquila responded by grappling it, turning one of its arms into gold in the process. She then began to fight with razor sharp teeth of her own, augmented by the Bane Affinity now that her meret was not around to see it. Aqhat staggered over to help, but their attacker seemed to just shrug off his blows. Finally, Aquila couldn't take any more. She broke the grapple and dove beneath the ground with Dust Beneath Feet Tier 1, hiding on the verge of death. Aqhat didn't take long to finish the fight then, striking the creature down. Before it died, she watched it gasp out some words she couldn't hear. When she returned to the surface, Aqhat told her what it had said.<br /> <br /> &quot;Master of the Pit is master no more.&quot;<br /> <br /> There was a shifting sound from the rubble that had once been the temple, and the two Arisen turned to face it as the rocks began to move.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in Neter-Khetet, those killed in the explosion seemed to find themselves bound together. They caught glimpses of the spirit-forms of the others, moving through the shattered terrain of the immaterial realm. They could sense the Nameless Jackal watching from on high as they descended through their Death Cycle, but they caught glimpses of the others. In each, they felt as if they had been the one to live through those events.<br /> <br /> They were all the one standing on a cliff, looking out at the ocean, as fire rained from the sky and the blasted wreck of an ironclad sank beneath the waves.<br /> <br /> They were all the one walking through the crowded streets, cheering, as men in red and blue boarded carriages to charge the enemy and save the city.<br /> <br /> They were all the one grappling with the roaring monster, all fang and claw and bleeding spiders, atop a mountain peak and the one who fell through that cold air, still locked in that embrace, to the cold earth below.<br /> <br /> And they were all the one who fell to their knees in the pouring rain, grasped the hand of a man beyond salvation, and watched the life and blood and tears fall away until they found his slow-beating heart and claimed it for all time.<br /> <br /> But as the Death Cycle continued, they slowly pulled away from one another. Bast remembered the battle at sea, of being ambushed aboard the deck of a ship, the knives of the enemy digging deep. She had called fire from the sky and ended the battle and her attackers, but now, as she watched the sun set, she wondered at her knew enemy. She turned to the sky and asked the stars for answers, and they replied:<br /> <br /> The Restless Stars linger and hate. The Hidden One seeks to shatter the crook, and let the reign of the Judges come to its final end. This foe will find you here and across the sea, today and in centuries yet to be born. And yet you share a flesh, and others hunger for it. The starving jackal may yet lead you to your quarry.<br /> <br /> For Sesu Ra, he remembered a night in New York when the sky roared and the rain fell so hard the street lights became pale glimmers in the distance. Three cultists with Tommy Guns waited with him in a dark alley. They were all blooded, feeling their life and warmth being leeched by the cold wind and rain, and they were all waiting to see if their enemy had found them again.<br /> <br /> Finally, an Italian-American, a newcomer to the cult, told Sesu Ra that they would hold the creature off. He needed to finish his work. Although it galled him to run, Sesu Ra agreed. The Empire State Building would be complete soon, and the final preparations needed to be made. He remembered leaving the storm and standing in the secret chamber, watching lightning course through the walls and arc across the room, as he performed the final ritual and sealed New York's fate with chisel, blood, and magic.<br /> <br /> When he returned, his cultists had been throw about the alley and torn apart like dolls. Only one, the man who had suggested this sacrifice, still lived. He was dying, and Sesu Ra demanded to know everything about the creature. In a weak voice, the man told him... but Sesu Ra of the present couldn't hear what was said. He could see the man's lips move, the blood trickle down his chin, hear the laboured breathing, but the words didn't make any sense. But he watched as his past life grabbed the dying man's mouth and force his name down the cultist's throat, before reaching into the man's chest and claiming the heart as payment for Luca's immortality.<br /> <br /> For Akenakhi's Death Cycle... we're going to need to wait for next session. We ended the game there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:46:58-07:00","id":542512,"title":"","content":"Session 35<br /> <br /> Akenakhi fell from the inferno into the streets of Paris. Men in blue and red were boarding cabs and rushing to the front, urged on by the cheering crowd. He joined them, thinking of his cultists fighting in the battle, but a part of him hoped the attack would fail. So much blood had run through the streets of Paris. Blood had power, what else could he achieve with the strength of a thousand more mortal deaths?<br /> <br /> He stopped that line of thinking. If there was one law he had learned in his long life, it was that power was a chain. If he wanted freedom, he needed to forsake it. Only at his weakest could he challenge the Judges.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, he couldn't count on himself to always remember this lesson. Below the city was the Carnal Gate, an incredibly powerful Uter. He would need to destroy it. His vision broke, and for a moment he remembered the time of Irem. Three Guildmasters sang and danced beneath the stars as their assembled priests screamed prayers to the Judges. Along with the others, Akenakhi approached the mummified corpse, its ribs splayed open. He cut his left palm and let his blood run out to fill the chest cavity. He trembled, his legs gave way, and he returned to the present as he watched the corpse fade from sight.<br /> <br /> The Gate would need more blood to manifest. He had very few cultists left in the city. This would take some time to arrange...<br /> <br /> Back in the living world, Aquila watched the pile of rubble shift. She dove beneath the ground again rather than face what was coming. She was just in time. A roaring pillar of flame slammed into Aqhat, overwhelming the Su-Menent in fire. She watched the Shemsu lash out blindly with his axe, and incredibly the blade seemed to sheer the pillar in half. A pale corpse toppled to the ground, a thick dark ooze leaking from the massive wound in its chest.<br /> <br /> It wasn't enough to lure Aquila out of safety, however. Sure enough, the moment Aqhat dropped his guard the corpse was on its feet again. Aquila saw it raise a chisel and slam it into the other Arisen's skull. The chisel began to pulse a dull red colour, and Aqhat sank to his knees.<br /> <br /> Using the fighting as a distraction, Aquila carefully retrieved the Pale Brood and Rod of Tjesh from the bodies of her fallen meret. The Dragon's Claw had been broken in the explosion, it appeared. She then fled underground rather than face what had emerged from the collapsed temple.<br /> <br /> Hours later, Sesu Ra was the first to wake from his Death Cycle. He found himself lying on a stretcher in a makeshift tent. In the tent with him were the bodies of the other Arisen, Benerib, Kotira, Akenakhi, and Sekhet Bastet. Seated on chairs were Aqhat and Rekhenaten, as well as a newly woken Arisen he didn't recognise. Rekhenaten saw him wake, and quickly explained. He had rushed to the site of the Temple the moment it exploded. He had seen fit to explain it as a demolition, and currently had his cult working to cover up what had happened. A gas main explosion, or preferably a demolition that hadn't alerted the appropriate authorities. There was a certain amount of confusion due to events that had played out between the emergency personnel and the newly awoken Mekshonat, the other Arisen in the tent, which Rekhenaten was confident would help resolve the matter and keep mortal authorities out of their business. After all, cultists and Arisen were the ones who had most frequently gone to the Temple, and an investigation could be inconvenient.<br /> <br /> They relocated the others via truck to Rekhenaten's private club, where they could discuss the attack. Kotira's Descent had clearly finished, her body would need to be returned to her tomb by her cultists. As for the others, they woke one by one. Akenakhi was the last to wake. After introductions, he noticed that Mekshonat's khat was rather different from what he remembered. For one thing, the shape of the skeleton seemed to be female, and the tone of skin, even after centuries of mummification, was quite pale.<br /> <br /> After a glib remark from Akenakhi, Mekshonat burned some Sekhem in order to heal the damage he had taken fighting Aqhat. The form he took once his flesh returned did not look much like the middle-aged Arisen Akenakhi remembered from Constantinople. He had pale skin, ash-blonde hair, and blue eyes, nothing like any Arisen born in Irem. His voice was high and clear, and he was most definitely wearing a female body. Between them, Benerib and Mekshonat explained that he had lost his body in the Middle Ages. Their cult, a rural tribe, had chosen one of the village virgins to be his new form, rather against his wishes.<br /> <br /> While this was going on, Rekhenaten drew his Guildmaster to one side to discuss the creature that had attacked Aqhat after the fight. He had retrieved its corpse. Sesu Ra demanded to see it, and the two left to observe the corpse where it was laid out in one of the building's kitchens. Sesu Ra felt there was a certain kind of similarity with it and some of the forms he had perceived during joint unleashings of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, and after questioning his guildmate closely he got Rekhenaten to confess. His experiments in human breeding had produced some interesting results. Working on some knowledge let slip by a Su-Menent many centuries ago, he had discovered bloodlines of great power and brought them together. Every now and again, such bloodlines produced mutant offspring. His cult generally tried to remove such creatures at birth, but some slipped through the cracks and he suspected there was a breeding population in the sewers. He asked Sesu Ra not to tell the Su-Menent, they would not take kindly to such meddling.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra suggested instead that Rekhenaten talk to Sekhet Bastet about it, although obviously not make the full extent of his involvement clear. Rekhenaten agreed, reluctantly. He lied to Bast, telling her that the creatures were simply pests his cult occasionally tried to remove to keep the city safe. Bast recognised the connection to mankind's demonic legacy almost immediately upon viewing the creature, but believed Rekhenaten's claims of non-involvement.<br /> <br /> Akhenakhi managed to get in contact with Aquila, using a phone provided by Rekhenaten. She had linked up with Quil had kept their Talismans safe. She arranged to meet and deliver them, and came over directly. She'd also received contact from Asa Corp. The head of one of their imprisoned cultists had appeared on the doorstep of the corporation, and investigations suggested that the other cultist was missing. They'd been collected by people who had seemed to have the authorisation to move them to a new holding cell, but they had disappeared from the map immediately after.<br /> <br /> The meret were all still badly injured, and needed time to recover and find out where their enemies had come from. Sekhet Bastet retreated to an isolated spot away from Jakarta's light pollution, and asked for guidance. The skies spoke:<br /> <br /> <i>Shadows crawl and time breaks beneath the rising stars. The twisted masters prey upon you and shattered slaves hunt the darkened streets. Amongst the blood and grit and darkness, only the one rendered less than what she was can lead you where you need to go.</i><br /> <br /> She described it to Sesu Ra, and together they pieced it together. This message, and the one she had remembered from her Death Cycle, clearly advised the same course of action. The &quot;starving jackal&quot; and &quot;the one rendered less than what she was&quot; were surely the same, and Sesu Ra believed the identity of this being was Nenheta. A &quot;starving Jackal&quot; could mean a Sheut Arisen, and the reference to being less than what she was combined with &quot;starving&quot; definitely suggest a Shuankhsen to Sesu Ra's mind. Perhaps, this was the clue. The Shuankhsen hunted for whatever had attacked them just as much as they hunted the Arisen. They could use one enemy to find the other.<br /> <br /> Aquila and Sesu Ra met briefly in a private spot to discuss the possibility of creating an Amkhat to fight the Shuankhsen. By draining the Sekhem from the creatures, they could render them ineffectual and hasten the eventual end to their Descents. Sesu Ra wasn't comfortable with the idea until LDI was finished and the Thousand Isles were safe again. He didn't want to build an Amkhata pit anywhere it might be discovered, but the Isles were currently being watched by the corporation and he couldn't risk it there.<br /> <br /> Aquila decided then that she had to put her proposal forward to Mike Thornton, to see if she could remove LDI from the equation. She asked him if they could meet over lunch. He took her to a favourite restaurant of his. Aquila wore heavy coverings to cover up the damage to her body from the explosion. Over the meal she outlined her proposal. First, she criticised what he had done to Kotira, saying the savagery ran counter to the moral efforts of the company in their efforts to combat disease and aging. Mike defended that by pointing out the Bronze Age attitudes of Arisen and by saying that she would recover from harm anyhow. Then Aquila brought up the threat posed by a united Nome all striking at LDI together. A dozen Arisen together could do damage he would not imagine in his worst nightmares. But she offered him a solution. If he appeared to dissolve the Jakarta branch of LDI, citing the recent attacks on their headquarters and fear for his personnel's safety, he could make it seem that LDI was gone. In reality, they could continue to operate as an R&amp;D branch of Asa Corp. They would receive regular donations of Sekhem from the more friendly Arisen, and they could work together to ensure the others didn't pose a problem. They could minimise the risk to themselves and continue to reap a steady flow of Sekhem. Aquila put all of her considerable charms into the proposal, and it definitely seemed to sway Mike. He promised to try and obtain permission to entertain the proposal, and said his lawyers would be in touch. He left Aquila with the bill.<br /> <br /> Bast, Sesu Ra, and Akenakhi all then went to check up on Sem-Huf. He had returned from his Death Cycle, very much weakened. He told them much of what they already knew. When the riot happened and his guards were distracted, Gator found him and consumed him. Gator was behind efforts to turn Mot-Tan, Aquila, and himself against one another, and clearly had a lot of influence in the area. Without any clear leads, they told him to share any information he found and that they would call on his help when they located the Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> The meret separated there. They each tried to put into action different plots to draw out their enemies, spending the next few days on the endeavour. Akenakhi sought out contacts in the police force for information about victims with missing hearts, trying to locate the Shuankhsen. In his spare time he tried to break through to Aulia, the mad girl who continued to speak in tongues, in the hopes she might have some information to share. Sesu Ra used his mystic status to have a tunnel maintenance operation put into action, hoping it would draw out the mutants. Aquila had Akenakhi get in contact with Nenheta. Akenakhi barely remembered the number (all the phones had stopped working after they were caught in that explosion...), but when the phone was answered it was Iwseck on the line. He claimed he was here to sell out Aquila, telling Isweck that she would be at Gator's old resting place beneath the bus station. Iwseck grew angry, saying it was Sesu Ra she wanted. Akenakhi explained he was working on it, and she hung up.<br /> <br /> Finally, Sekhet Bastet decided to speak to Kudama Jav again. The man agreed to meet with her outside his tunnels. Just like before, he was clutching a relic book close to his chest. Bast probed carefully to find out more about it, and was surprised when Kudama claimed it was his life's work. It allowed him to call up spirits to help him. He had studied the occult for years, and the process of making it nearly killed him. He recognised in Bast a fellow seeker of lost knowledge, and told her how impressed he was at her ability to navigate his tunnels. It had taken him years to find his way about.<br /> <br /> The two talked for some time. Kudama began asking about the company he had been contracted to attack. His men, he claimed, were being approached and offered money to turn on him. He wasn't sure if he could trust his lieutenants, not with the sums on offer. Bast told him that they were a ruthless organisation, but the rewards for his help would be considerable. She could offer many secrets. If he was loyal and swore to serve, she could even offer him immortality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:46:18-07:00","id":553990,"title":"","content":"Session 36<br /> <br /> The session began with the cult reaching out to each of their Arisen. Rom Mayehi wished to present the information they had found on the death of their cultist in person. The Arisen gathered slowly. Akenakhi and Sesu Ra were the first to arrive. They spoke with one another about Iwseck, Akenakhi explaining that he thought the Shuankhsen would make another try to kill him soon. He asked Sesu Ra's help in laying a trap with him. Unfortunately, Sesu Ra felt the threat of Last Dynasty International was too important for the moment. He suggested Akenakhi stay near him until LDI was dealt with. After that, he would turn his attentions to the Shuankhsen. Akenakhi was more than a little dissatisfied by this, but chose to stay silent as Aquila and Sekhet Bastet joined them in the conference room at Asa Corp's shiny new office.<br /> <br /> Rom entered then, and laid out the information they had gathered. The men who had removed the cultists from their cells had not had the appropriate papers to do so, but had apparently convinced the guard on duty to allow them to move the prisoners despite that. The guard had been under the impression that the papers would be sent to him shortly after their departure. As for those responsible, there was no information available as to their identity. After an internal review, Jakarta's prison system seemed quite sure that the men were not employees.<br /> <br /> The meret decided that they would begin their own investigation. Accompanied by Luca, they travelled immediately to the suspended guard's apartment (address provided by the cult's contacts). They barged into the man's room. Luca forced him to sit at gunpoint. With a supreme show of will, the guard resisted Sekhet Bastet's attempts to extract what he knew about the events. Aquila drained him of his remaining willpower, and he slumped unconscious in his chair.<br /> <br /> A brief discussion followed. Luca and Bast would remain and carry on the investigation when he woke. Sesu Ra, Akenakhi, and Aquila would head to the prison and obtain access to any video footage of the event. They were able to bribe their way into seeing the video despite the recalcitrance of the guard on duty, Sesu Ra manipulating Fate itself to get them the information they were looking for. They found a brief video clip of an Indonesian man speaking to the guard they were interrogating, and printed a picture for future reference.<br /> <br /> Bast and Luca picked up their interrogation when their captive woke. Without any Willpower, he broke quickly. They were able to get a brief description of the man he spoke to, but the conversation itself was oddly mundane. The guard had just been inclined to believe the man when he said the documents authorising the transfer would be along quickly. He couldn't say whether or not he would have normally been so trusting, mix-ups like that did happen.<br /> <br /> Disgusted, they frightened the man into silence and left. A brief attempt to track the car's license plate showed another dead end, with the plates being fake. Stymied, the group decided to move on to other matters.<br /> <br /> Bast then received a call from Kudama Jav. He had traced the money flowing into his organisation to do brothers, Ino and Ogi. They weren't exactly renowned for being able to get along though, so he believed that only one of them was plotting against him. He asked that they find out which one was responsible, without overtly interrogating them. That could turn the one who was still loyal, after all.<br /> <br /> The brothers owned a fishing vessel and an office not far from the dock where it was moored. Sesu Ra, Luca, and Bast travelled to the docks first, to gather information. They met with a man named Susil, an old fisherman missing most of his teeth, who spoke of seeing one of the brothers accept a briefcase with a strange lopsided pyramid picked out in gold on the side. He didn't know which brother it was, but if they found the briefcase all should become clear. From there, they travelled to the brothers' office. They heard a row going on inside when they arrived. It stopped when they walked through the door. The two brothers were very much alike, dark, older men with hunched postured and long, spider-like hands.<br /> <br /> Luca spotted something through a door into the pack, and Bast and Sesu Ra distracted the brothers while he snuck through. There he found the briefcase, laid out on a bench in the open. Looking through his Sadikh's eyes, Sesu Ra realised he recognised the symbol. It wasn't actually a pyramid, but a representation of a pile of dust. A symbol of the Sons of Gold Dust. They confronted the brothers about it directly, and Ino said he had just found the briefcase before they arrived. A man had approached Ogi with an offer to make some money on the side, running drugs out to international markets. Some group in the city's east that wanted to expand the reach of their operation. Assuming that the Arisen were working for Kudama, Ogi said he would submit to punishment.<br /> <br /> Not wanting to anger Sem-Huf by interfering with his business, Sesu Ra suggested they hide the matter from Kudama. Bast decided against that, however. She informed Kudama of everything they had learned, but suggested he take it as a new business opportunity. He decided it was a grand idea, and that he would only remove three of Ogi's fingers as punishment.<br /> <br /> After that, the meret separated again. They were still recovering from the attack on the temple, and many of them needed to heal. Aquila busied herself setting up a system at the hospital where she worked, one that involved bribing staff members and admin officers and providing donations to patients in order to ensure a flow of hearts. Under ideal conditions, she would be able to access a single heart that would not otherwise be suitable for transplants, and devour it. She kept this business scrupulously hidden from the meret, knowing how they would react.<br /> <br /> Bast spent much of her time in the northern end of Jakarta, looking for signs of Shuankhsen activity. She concentrated her attention around the train lines, remembering their preference for transient populations as a source of victims. While she didn't find any evidence of the Shuankhsen being in the area, she did find many trains transporting freight with LDI logos. Backtracking, she found they were moving items out of their warehouses near the docks to other locations in the city. Bast, Sesu Ra, and Akenakhi decided to investigate, but Aquila was too badly hurt still for them to consider contacting. They scouted out one of the warehouses, trying to see what the security was like. Some dogs and a few rent-a-cops, was all they could see. Sesu Ra was mid-sentence, suggesting they gather their men and attack, when fire began to rain from the sky.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet had spent entirely too much time being troubled by these mortals. She had wanted to end it quickly. Calling on the Secrets Ripped From Skies, she Unleashed a meteor shower guided by Fate to destroy every trace of LDI in the area. Flaming rocks smashed into the LDI warehouses again and again, while the rest of the docks saw smaller explosions and fires started by Unleashing. Chaos overtook the area, humans overwhelmed by the Sybaris that cascaded from Bast in waves. The words of the stars filled her mind as the fire fell around her, a simple message.<br /> <br /> <i>Watch the pretty fires burn.</i><br /> <br /> Akenakhi was appalled by the devastation. He tried to help, but his fellow Arisen tried to stop him. They didn't want LDI to see their faces, know it was them in the area. He evaded their clutches however, and fled. Once he was a safe distance away, he turned his efforts towards trying to save the lives of mortals injured and dying throughout the area.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet's memories were shaken by slaughter she had unleashed, and she dropped to Memory 3. Her mind was strong enough to resist gaining a derangement, however, and she felt power course through her body as her Judge bestowed its favour for her actions. Alongside Sesu Ra, she left the area as the emergency services began to arrive.<br /> <br /> Hours later, Aquila received a phone call from Mike Thornton, beginning with the words, &quot;What in the ever-living fuck?&quot; He accused her of mounting delaying tactics, giving her brethren time to engineer this latest attack. She angrily denied any involvement, pointing out that this kind of carnage was exactly what she had warned would happen if he did not agree to her plan. Mike said it would be hard, his superiors were finding it hard to believe that she hadn't known the attack was about to happen. Aquila asked if they could meet in person.<br /> <br /> Once they were face to face, Aquila laid out the information as she had gathered from Akenakhi. Bast had launched the attack on her own, after discovering the presence of LDI property by chance. It wasn't something pre-planned or conceived by the Arisen as a whole. She offered Mike immortality as a Sadikh if he could find a way to persuade his superiors of that, and convince them to take up her offer of merging the Jakarta operations with Asa Corp. Mike told her that he had his own way to immortality, but said he would do his best to convince the others that she had not taken part. As a gesture of good faith, Aquila added that Akenakhi had offered to donate his Sekhem to LDI. Mike gave her a street, and said that if he waited there LDI would collect him.<br /> <br /> Then, hesitatingly, Aquila asked if LDI could provide her with an Amkhat. The Shuankhsen were far too hard to destroy permanently. A direct confrontation might send them into a Death Cycle, but if they gained so much as a single dot of Sekhem in the process then they would be every bit as strong when they recovered, maybe even stronger. She needed a way to drain the Sekhem from them entirely. Mike almost laughed her out of the room, but she was able to convince him to let her use one of LDI's Amkhata pits to create her own instead.<br /> <br /> The next day, Akenakhi paid his visit to the doctor. He was collected by Suyifa, who had him sign some documents to the effect that LDI wasn't liable if anything happened to him, and had him blindfolded and driven to a facility where he was tied down and cut open. He had emptied almost all of his pillars, leaving only his Ren filled, at Aquila's suggestion. The power that flowed from him was little more than a trickle. All around, the LDI scientists recited their blasphemous chant decrying the Judges and all they held dear, much to Akenakhi's interest. When the power was done they helped him patch his wounds, and then he was escorted out the way he had come. Akenakhi fell to Sekhem 6.<br /> <br /> Bast and Sesu Ra were with Kudama Jav again, preparing his men for the attack on LDI's transport ship. The pirates had the weapons provided by the Arisen, and Sesu Ra offered to give material bodies to some of Kudama Jav's ghosts so that they could be the front line of the attack. After some consideration, the smuggler leader agreed. Sesu Ra took three of the hooded ghosts back to his tomb, and bound them into embalmed corpses using the Blasphemous Depiction. &quot;Destroy LDI's shipping&quot; was the instruction he gave them.<br /> <br /> Across the city, Aquila had cut apart a snake and bull. The LDI lab had provided her with a fungal heart for the False Ka. She stitched the bull's head to the snake's body with a needle of bone and sutures of sinew, and sacrificed her own Sekhem to the pit. The ritual took a day and a night, but there among the stench of rotting animal parts she brought forth a foul new life. Tetasu Xex was born, and for her blasphemy the Judge Qerrti struck at her Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Aquila was now Sekhem 2, but she felt she had nearly everything she needed to fight Gator. A Talisman would be the final piece of the puzzle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T00:36:16-07:00","id":557985,"title":"","content":"I must say, I'm loving the character development that we've seen so far, particularly with regard to Aquila. In the beginning she really came off as the &quot;sensitive one&quot; in the meret, but over time it seems like she's revealed herself to be as ruthless as any of the others, though she obviously has a very different set of priorities from most of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-17-2015, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T02:56:23-07:00","id":558047,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Aquila's player has definitely settled playing her as a once-peaceful character driven to violence and other terrible acts. The weight of centuries has really become too much for her. She remembers all her past attempts to raise up the lower classes, and yet is faced with the fact that little has changed in the modern world. Picking up Rouse the Khaibit was a pretty character-defining moment for her, and now she's turned to making Amkhat as a way to expedite victory. It's been a really fun arc to watch, and I can't wait to see the ultimate conclusion. Quil, her new Sadikh, probably offers her the best chance she has at a remotely happy ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:52:57-07:00","id":559816,"title":"","content":"Well, that's one problem with being immortal: you don't get to have <i>any</i> kind of ending, happy or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:26:10-07:00","id":560020,"title":"","content":"For the purposes of this chronicle, I guess?<br /> <br /> Quil certainly doesn't represent a long-term prospect of happiness. Aquila's conscience had her give him a detailed explanation of his condition, and Sadikh who know the exact details of their nature tend to burn out pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T03:56:42-07:00","id":562853,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Aquila's existence seems to have been a cycle of crushing depression made worse by brief periods of happiness. Remember when Aquila had a kid? Remember how happy she was? And when she was forced to return to sleep by the Lady of the Broken Stihl (who is an utter bitch, by the way), waking up to find her little girl had become an Octogenarian? And then was forced to kill said octogenarian?<br /> Yeah, the same thing's gonna happen with Quil. maybe not the exact same thing, but we're still going to see that cycle of horrific crushing despair being brought about by loss of one of the few sources of happiness available repeat a few more times, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:17:18-07:00","id":563596,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Session 37</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sekhet Bastet and Sesu Ra boarded Kudama Jav's ships, which took them out to the Thousand Islands to transfer to the open-topped longboats that would be used to board the LDI freighter. It would take nearly 24 hours to get far enough away from Jakarta to carry out the operation safely.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Back ashore, Aquila and Akenakhi (along with Tetasu Xex) were following up on a kepher vision of Aquila's. They found themselves in an old Red Light district, a place where the gap between worlds seemed remarkably thin. Although in recent years the brothels had been driven out of business, signs of the what the neighbourhood had once been were everywhere. Among the evidence of vice they were able to track down a woman from Aquila's named Adelaide Baron, a self-proclaimed spiritualist. Adelaide was a serious middle-aged woman who worked out of her home. She welcomed them in when they arrived, claiming she could sense a dark presence hanging over them. Aquila thought guiltily about Tetasu Xex, and decided to have him manifest at the earliest opportunity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A conversation followed in which Adelaide revealed that there were many among the people here who worshipped false gods and dark spirits. She had banished some of their so-called gods herself with her knowledge of exorcism, and said that her greatest battle was yet to come. The Arisen offered their help, thinking it might lead them to the relic they sought, and she accepted gladly. They were to head directly to the evil spirit's resting place, but Aquila begged to excuse herself. Once somewhere no one could see, she summoned Tetasu Xex.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To her horror, her Amkhat appeared with great wounds rent in its body, fungus oozing from a hundred cuts. The creature was clearly near death. As the Arisen wandered oblivious through the streets, there had apparently been a desperate battle taking place in Neter-Khetet that her newborn pet had only just survived. She ordered the creature to return to Asa Corp headquarters, where it was to remain in Twilight and lick its wounds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She then accompanied Akenakhi and Adelaide to an old, dilapidated home. It was clearly long-abandoned and dilapidated, its walls riddled with rot and paint peeling from every surface. They came upon a strange iron door that was at odds with the rest of the building, clearly new and well-furbished. It was carved with symbols that seemed to denote human sacrifice, and written in Indonesian across the top of the door were the words &quot;The Mindless Body&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They opened the door and stared into the darkness beyond. Just as they were about to step across the threshold, however, coils of undulating corpus began to spill out of the room. The Arisen realised quickly what was happening and turned to run. They weren't quite fast enough, as snapping jaws took chunks out of Aquila. They each spent pillars to boost their Physical attributes as they raced towards the exit, and Adelaide saw their true form. The Sybaris overwhelmed her and she fled, barely avoiding being caught by the Chthonic Being that chased them. They reached the street when they noticed that the Chthonic Being wasn't pursuing them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Adelaide demanded that they go away and leave her alone. She had seen them for the dead things they really were, and wanted nothing more to do with them. The two Arisen weren't willing to fight a Chthonic Being without the rest of the meret, so they retreated to nurse their wounds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Out on the ocean, the pirate ships closed in on the freighter in the dark of night. A blaring siren made it very clear their presence had been noticed. Boarding ladders were raised, while Sesu Ra drew his khopesh and cut through the steel hull like butter. At least one of the undying monsters he had created entered through the gap, while Luca, Bast, and he all followed suit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Once inside they could hear occasional gunshots up above. They heard movement coming towards them and hid quickly. When half a dozen crew emerged, Luca opened fire and gunned them down. That was when they realised the men were unarmed. By the time they reached the top deck they found most of the crew alive and held prisoner by Kudama Jav's men. There had been no armed resistance, no Amkhata, just a civilian crew without any defences. Kudama's men started stripping the ship of anything of value while the Arisen interrogated the ship's captain to find out if he knew anything about LDI operations. There wasn't much information forthcoming.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kudama and his men were quick and efficient. They abandoned the ship, leaving the Arisen aboard. Sesu Ra set a course that would take it into the damaged section of the LDI docks, and once it had run aground, Sekhet Bastet called down a meteor that blasted a massive hole in it. The burning ship should remove most useful evidence for them, and send a remarkably good message to their enemies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They linked up with the rest of their meret at the Asa Corp offices, who told them about the unusual spiritual activity they had discovered. With a relic on the table and Sesu Ra's normal interest in ghosts, they decided to destroy the Chthonic Being immediately. Before they left, Aquila gathered some cultists together to feed on their Willpower and restore her own. She found, however, that her cultists were already drained. Every attempt she made simply rendered them unconscious without any benefit to herself. She wondered at first if it was due to the dreams being inflicted upon them by Hetenatra, but it turned out even cultists unaffected by the dreams were feeling drained and demoralised. She deduced then that it must be due to the presence of Tetasu Xex. The cultists were being weakened by his presence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The meret travelled then to the place Akenakhi and Aquila had visited with Adelaide. When they arrived at the residence they found an old man waiting for them. He demanded that they leave. They were trespassing on sacred ground, on a resting place of the God-In-Three-Parts. The Arisen brushed past him, Aquila pausing to drain his Willpower until he was rendered unconscious.<br /> <br /> The iron door was closed once again. They pushed it open and the Chthonic Being began to ooze forward. Aquila tried to seize the creature and turn a chunk of it to gold, but it shrugged off the magic easily. Bast, wielding bone knives made for her by her cultists, began to carve into its essence doing terrific damage to the creature. It roared and struggled, to little avail. Sesu Ra tried to will the power of Blessed Is The God-King forth from his Talisman, but his Sekhem was so low that, by the time he completed the Unleashing, the Chthonic Being had been torn apart by Bast's attacks.<br /> <br /> The cavern beyond turned out to be bereft of any relic, however. After a brief consultation they decided to check out the church from the original kepher vision. It was an old, dilapidated building that had a greater resemblance to local architecture than any classical church imagery. They asked the priest, who assumed they were tourists, for a brief tour of the building. They managed to milk him for information in the process, finding out that there was a local preacher who had been poaching from his congregation to gather people in the worship of a strange God. Outwardly, this preacher seemed to adopt the trappings of Christianity, but the priest had visited his temples and seen some very strange and worrying things.<br /> <br /> The meret didn't need any more detail than that. They found the location where this other congregation met, and drove there immediately. The building was one of the more modern buildings in the area, a shining example of the progress the district was making. They walked in, and that was when the ghosts began to materialise around them.<br /> <br /> There were close to a dozen of them. Terrible, twisted things of shredded corpus, many eyes, and unnatural physiology. Many were close enough to human to tell their origins, but others looked almost entirely alien. A mortal man walked towards them through the spirits, clutching a metal box under his arm. He said his name was Ancilo, the leader of this congregation, and told them to leave immediately.<br /> <br /> As the others tried to persuade the man that they meant no harm, Aquila's eyes were fixed on a tall fluted pillar on the other side of the chamber. It was the relic they'd come here seeking. Finally, the meret decided that conversation wasn't getting them anywhere. They attacked.<br /> <br /> Ancilo fled the moment the fighting started, Akenakhi close on his heels. Bast waded into the ghosts, cutting them apart with her bone knives, but they singled her out as the greatest threat. Many of the creatures were able to become physically manifest, and they tore into her with fangs and talons of corpus. Sesu Ra used Chthonic Dominion Tier 2 to dominate one of the spirits, turning it against the others, while his ghostly protector joined the fight to attack the ghosts that were striking at its master. Aquila summoned up armour from the earth with Dust Beneath Feet and rushed towards the pillars, two of the spirits clinging to her back and tearing out chunks of flesh. She reached it, and used Name the Thing to determine its power and if it was in any way responsible for the attackers.<br /> <br /> Behind her, her allies were struggling. Bast felt herself coming apart under the spiritual onslaught. Akenakhi was nowhere to be seen, having pursued Ancilo down the street but failing to catch the man. And then, forming from a black cloud that seemed to spill out of the altar. It was a tall, insectile thing, with a torso nearly seven feet long, eight bladed limbs, and a head that was nothing but eyes. It speared Aquila with one limb. Bast, on the verge of death, decided to rush the creature and put it in the ground. Her blades tore into it, causing it to screech and strike at her. The blow should have killed her, but instead it opened her eyes.<br /> <br /> She realised that most of her wounds weren't real, that they had been struck by phantoms. Of the many spirits attacking them, only three appeared to be real. Most were illusions, causing her allies to flail at the air while their real enemies struck at them in relative safety. She redoubled her attacks on the strange monster, killing it, and directing her allies against the real foes. They were soon alone in the chamber, torn corpus gently dissipating into the air around them.<br /> <br /> The cult was called to bring a truck so that they could move the pillar. Aquila had determined that it was a Minor Djed, and was almost certainly responsible for the corrupted nature of the ghosts. Sesu Ra used Chthonic Dominion to set himself as an anchor for his newly enslaved servant, having given the creature the command &quot;Protect the Tef-Aabhi&quot;. Even the brief exposure to the relic had caused visible effects on his existing protector.<br /> <br /> Although many of their injuries were phantasmal, Bast and Aquila were happy to retreat and lick their wounds. They had retrieved what they had come for anyway. The meret returned to their tombs (the still tombless Aquila returned to Asa Corp).<br /> <br /> When Sesu Ra reached the lobby of the skyscraper where his tomb was concealed, a heavily shrouded figure asked him to come with him. He chose to send Luca after the man instead, and returned to his tomb. The man flatly refused to speak to Luca, even when Sesu Ra seized control of Luca's voice and spoke through him as a puppet. He demanded they meet in person, somewhere quiet where they could be alone.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra gave in. Leaving Luca behind, he met with the figure in an empty corridor of the building. The man removed the hood and shrouds that concealed his identity. Beneath the rot, the diseased skin stretched tight across a malformed skull, the wounds and sores visible in his flesh, Sesu Ra recognised Rangarni, Iwseck's Fasad.<br /> <br /> &quot;I need you to help me die,&quot; he said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:48:06-07:00","id":572037,"title":"","content":"Session 38<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra's player only arrived about half-way through this session, so my efforts to remember the in-game chronology versus out-of-game chronology might go a bit wonky. Apologies for that in advance. I'll try to prioritise the in-game sequence, but I make no promises.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra said he was more than willing to kill Rangarni, right there and then. He could even have Luca come and do it, if that would be easier. Rangarni grew a bit frustrated at that. He didn't need help being killed. The problem was staying dead. Iwseck could raise him from the dead if he died, and Rangarni couldn't think of any way to stop her. But she would listen to Sesu Ra. He could convince her to let her Fasad die. Rangarni hadn't realised what he was signing up for when he agreed to Iwseck's original proposal, and as his flesh rotted and his mind frayed he wanted, more and more, to die before the man he had been was completely gone.<br /> <br /> The idea seemed a bit far-fetched to Sesu Ra. He asked Rangarni why he thought Iwseck would have any interest in what he had to say. Rangarni told him that Iwseck was helping him, that she had always been trying to help him as best as she could. More disturbed than reassured, Sesu Ra asked they should arrange a meeting.<br /> <br /> After a bit of thought, they decided that they could lure Iwseck out by having Akenakhi pretend to have finally come through and delivered Sesu Ra. Rangarni and Iwseck would encounter Sesu Ra alone, but somewhere public where a supernatural battle was less likely to occur. Unbeknownst to Rangarni or Iwseck, Luca would also be lurking nearby in case things went south.<br /> <br /> The next day found Sesu Ra waiting in a crowded street in the town centre, watching Iwseck draw closer. She and Rangarni were making attempts to blend in with the crowd, as if they were shadowing him. When they finally drew close enough, Sesu Ra spoke first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Fasad is a traitor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Iwseck started, and whirled on Rangarni. Rangarni swore violently at Sesu Ra and looked as if he were about to run. Before he had the chance, Iwseck ordered him to shut up and be still. Mystically compelled by the ties binding him to his master, Rangarni had no choice in the matter. Reduced to throwing dirty looks in Sesu Ra's direction, he could only stand and watch the conversation that followed.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra wanted to know more about this &quot;help&quot; Rangarni seemed to think Iwseck had been offering him. Iwseck dodged the questions though, asking him how much he remembered. When it was quite clear that his memory was even more degraded than usual, unable to even remember his previous descent, she looked quite upset. Sesu Ra pressed her, pointing out that her minions had attacked his guild projects. He was nothing without his guild, he did not consider that &quot;help&quot; in the slightest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your guild betrayed you!&quot; Iwseck spat at him in response. Then, taking a deep breath, she offered him a deal. When his memory was high enough to remember her, to understand what she was talking about, she would give him what he desired the most. The head of a certain colossus...<br /> <br /> Set-Qesu was most displeased at his servant's display of lenience towards a foul spawn of the Devourer. As the two parted ways, their agreement struck, Sesu Ra felt the pillars of his soul shake at the forced Descent check. He was able to cling to his last scraps of Sekhem, however, and did not fall into Henet.<br /> <br /> The rest of the meret had a busy few days. Sekhet Bastet approached Kudama Jav, and asked for his decision on her offer of immortality. He accepted. With great ceremony, she broke his ribs apart and carved her name into the flesh of his heart, and then watched the flesh heal itself as he became her Sadikh. Across the city, Aquila returned to the site where her relic blade had once been kept. It had the required geometry for a tomb, and she began the process of mystically claiming it as her (Geometry 2) tomb. That done, she installed the Minor Djed and poured her power into it, creating a Talisman containing a dot of Harvest the Divine Flesh and the Prepared Keyword. And Akenakhi, commemorating the day his Cult died on the fields of France, took a lot of glasses to an old war memorial. He filled each glass with brandy, one for every cultist, and sat there for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> The next few weeks passed in a hurry. Sesu Ra meditated upon the revelations gleaned from his conversation with Iwseck, wondering how to broach the subject with Rekhenaten. Bast and Kudama spent some time familiarising themselves with the new situation, and Bast discovered details on the Relic Text Kudama had created, and how it allowed him to ensnare the souls of the recently dead to create ghosts bound to his service. And Aquila began to consume hearts donated to her hospital program, rapidly healing the injuries she had sustained in the explosion. She had cultists fill in the entrances to her new tomb with concrete, so that only someone using Dust Beneath Feet could enter. As part of her final preparations, she sealed the second tier of Dust Beneath Feet into a ring using the Silenced Utterance Vessel Affinity.<br /> <br /> Then she approached Akenakhi with a proposal. She could render him unconscious and remove a little of his excess Sekhem. She would return it the moment she was done. Akenakhi was torn. His studies of Apotheosis had suggested that Sekhem was a chain more than a blessing, but he was in no hurry to hasten his descent until he had all the knowledge he needed to escape his Judge. He agreed to let her take &quot;some&quot; (one dot, in game terms), although he queries why she had to knock him unconscious first. Aquila responded vaguely that the process required him to be unaware. Trusting her, they met at a small room in the Asa Corp building, where he surrendered his Willpower to her and collapsed unconscious.<br /> <br /> Aquila then summoned Tetasu Xex, having him drain Akenakhi of every drop of Sekhem he had, barring the few dregs required to keep him out of henet (Akenakhi fell to Sekhem 1). Tetasu Xex then delivered the Sekhem to her, raising her to Sekhem 4 (5 with her Talisman). She ordered Quil to keep Akenakhi unconscious until she returned, and used Akenakhi's phone to send a message to the Shuankhsen. She would meet Gator and fight him in single combat, without either of their merets to interfere, if he so wished. The site would be the bus terminal where they had first fought.<br /> <br /> Gator was waiting there for her, armoured in Earth. Aquila, wearing a suit of riot gear she had obtained many weeks ago, declared that she would not be such easy prey this time. As she spoke her flesh turned to gold and the earth began to swirl around her, layering armour upon armour until she felt near impervious to harm. She was preparing to reach out with Harvest the Divine Flesh and turn Gator to gold, but he was faster. He thundered across the intervening space and slammed into her. The two titans struggled in the dark corridors beneath the earth, a fight that took place entirely in silence. Gator's powers rendered Aquila unable to speak, to pronounce the utterances that might have given her an edge. He was stronger than she had anticipated, his teeth able to breath the layers of mystical defences to tear into her flesh. Desperate, she cancelled the unleashing of Dust Beneath Feet. For a moment she was ensconced within the statue, no longer bound in silence by his grip. She lashed at him with Harvest the Divine Flesh Tier 1, but her mystical attack wasn't able to gain a purchase. And then his arms moved through the statue like it was made of water, grasping her by the throat and lifting her out. Without that armour to protect her, Gator's attacks were unstoppable. He tore at her again and again, swallowing enormous chunks of her flesh whole. She tried in vain to break free, but as she grew weaker his strength only grew. Her stolen Sekhem was swallowed, until at last she dangled from Gator's arms, a ruined wreck.<br /> <br /> &quot;You cannot harm me,&quot; the Shuankhsen said, leaning in close so that she could see his toothed maw even with her fading eyes, &quot;you cannot even scratch me.&quot; His form seemed to flicker, and she felt fear of him sink into her bones. And then his jaw distended, opened wide, and swallowed what was left of her whole.<br /> <br /> (Aquila lost 2 Sekhem to the fight, dropping her to Sekhem 3)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T21:28:45-07:00","id":572169,"title":"","content":"The relic Kudama brought with him was the following, as far as Bast could determine:<br /> <br /> The Book of Dead Names (3 dot Text)<br /> Size 3, Durability 2, Structure 5<br /> <br /> The Book of Dead Names looks like a large, heavy book with iron clasps on its covers. When opened, its pages are filled with tiny, cramped scrawl that appears to have been written in the native tongue of the reader.<br /> <br /> Power: The bearer of the Book of Dead Names may take an instant action to call a ghost to their presence, so long as they are in proximity to one of the ghost's anchors. If in the presence of someone who has died since the last sunrise or sunset, the bearer may spend a point of Willpower to turn them into a ghost anchored either to the immediate area or the bearer themselves. This ghost always appears wearing a cowled rob and carrying a scroll in their left hand, and always has a compulsion to protect the bearer.<br /> <br /> Curse: The bearer develops a fascination with death and the book's own powers. Any time the bearer is in the presence of the recently deceased, they must roll Wits + Composure. If they fail, they must spend a point of Willpower to use this relic's power. If they do not have any Willpower, they develop a new derangement (normally Fixation or something similar appropriate). Mummies of the Sesha-Hebsu do not suffer this Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:40:44-07:00","id":580430,"title":"","content":"Session 39<br /> <br /> Rom Mayehi must really hate his job sometimes. Today he had the unenviable task of calling Sekhet Bastet and Sesu Ra and informing them that Aquila's Sadikh and Akenakhi were holed up in a room at Asa Corp, with Akenakhi unconscious and Quil apparently keeping him that way. That job done, he very quickly removed himself from the situation.<br /> <br /> The two Arisen arrived and ordered Quil to stop what he was doing. Under questioning, he revealed that Aquila had instructed him to keep Akenakhi unconscious until her return, but that she should have returned hours ago. The Arisen ordered him to stop what he was doing, so that Akenakhi could reveal what he knew of the events.<br /> <br /> It would be a few hours until Akenakhi regained consciousness. Sesu Ra had Vania, the cult's historian, dig through her records to find out if Aquila had any history of acting erratically. He plumbed his own memories while he waited, probing at the hole in his mind.<br /> <br /> He remembered the sound of the doctor's hammer, driving the chisel deeper into his eye. He considered the tools being used, comparing them to the ones he used in his own trade as a mason. Another blow, and the blade shifted deeper. The doctor sat back, a self-satisfied smirk on his face. Behind him, Sesu Ra could see his new Sadikh, Luca, watching. He waited. He should have felt something by now, but it hadn't worked. He stood up. The doctor's expression turned to one of shock. Deaf to the admonishments that he should lie down, be still, continue the pretence of being an anaesthetised patient, Sesu Ra reached out and grabbed the man's head, twisting it right around. There was a sense of resignation as he left the room. If he couldn't physically purge the memories from his mind, he had only one other choice.<br /> <br /> The memory broke, reforming some time later. A bloody khopesh was in his hand. The boats from Ellis Island had stopped flowing. It had worked, although he no longer had a clear grasp of what &quot;it&quot; was. He had to leave now, this city was too familiar, too liable to provoke memories better left buried. Passage had been booked to a new city. A city without history, he had told Luca, and so a Dutch trading post in the Pacific had been chosen. The voyage would begin this very night.<br /> <br /> Another break. He remembered the dark and the pain. Somewhere, a woman was crying, great heaving sobs. He heard a door open in the distance, letting in the sound of jazz music for just a brief moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;They're coming for you again.&quot; His modern self recognised Iwseck's voice. &quot;Do you think you'll break this time?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra gritted his teeth. &quot;I will never break.&quot;<br /> <br /> Soft hands removed his blindfold. Iwseck looked different in this life, although some of her features shone through the flesh of the poor white girl she was wearing. The room was lit by candlelight. One of his eyes was crusted shut with blood. On a chair on the other side of the room, a small wrapped bundle could be seen. Iwseck smiled down at him. &quot;So strong,&quot; she murmured. &quot;Let me help.&quot;<br /> <br /> His pain ended. The vision faded shortly afterwards.<br /> <br /> Vania's records, about a century's worth of Aquila's activities, did not seem to provide any explanation for her current behaviour. Of course, Sesu Ra was aware that a mere hundred years was an insufficient time scale on which to get a gauge of an Arisen's character.<br /> <br /> He returned in time to witness Akenakhi regaining consciousness, and the explosive swearing that followed. When the Fog of Torment finally calmed down, he revealed that Aquila had taken nearly all of his power. He told the others that he had offered to allow her to take a small measure of his Sekhem to help her, but that she had repaid his kindness by stealing everything he had. He didn't know how she had taken his Sekhem, but he did know why. She had gone to fight Gator.<br /> <br /> On Akenakhi's information, the meret travelled to investigate the bus terminal where Gator had made his lair. They found signs of a fight, cracked earth indicative of a fight between two creatures the size of elephants and armoured in stone. Luca found evidence of a shattered statue that could have been Aquila, but there was no sign of an equivalent one of Gator. He proffered the opinion that Gator had walked away from the fight. Aquila had not.<br /> <br /> The meret had rumours of murders in nearby slums that matched Gator's heart-devouring MO. The squatter settlement that hid Sekhet Bastet's tomb was not far away, so they started there. Bast retreated to her tomb to make sure everything was in order, and then began to ritually cut her flesh with a bone knife. The pain honed her Kepher visions to a startling accuracy, finally allowing her to locate the Uter relic she had been hunting for so long. She saw visions of rusting metal drums, a long neglected chemical plant, and a red sky burning beneath the heat of a black sun. A pressure in her mind told her where she needed to go to find this place, hidden up the river from her tomb.<br /> <br /> She told the others, but they decided they were too weak to mount an assault on the lair of the Shuankhsen. Sesu Ra in particular was cautious, asking that they wait until his current descent had finished. As he pointed out, his Sothic Turn was imminent. With that power, he would be of far greater help in any attack. The rest of the Nome should be alerted and their aid sought, although Sesu Ra was of the opinion that only Aqhat could be counted upon to help them.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Sesu Ra realised that the final part of his geometric network should be in the area. Following his directions, they were driven downriver until they reached a swathe of long-abandoned towers and apartments. The entire area was abandoned, the buildings clearly damaged by flooding. There weren't even any squatters to be seen.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra led them through the area to a crumbling hotel, built in the classic colonial style. The windows were clouded with filth, some of them damaged and missing. Inside, the room was entirely bereft of furniture, and there was a build-up of detritus against the walls. In the centre of the room were four pillars, looking entirely out of place.<br /> <br /> This was the heart of the area's geometry. They explored the room, noting hieroglyphs cunningly hidden among the scrollwork and finer details of the hotel's greeting hall. Then Sekhet Bastet stepped between two of the pillars in the room's centre, and vanished. Sesu Ra rushed over, and followed immediately.<br /> <br /> They found themselves in a place outside of the world, in the void of space. Above, below, and all around them were the stars, constellations that they recognised, mixed with glowing symbols and hieroglyphs marked out in golden light. They were standing where the Earth should be, but the Earth itself could not be seen. The room was like a transparent sphere, suspended in space, and no matter where they stood gravity always seemed to make &quot;down&quot; beneath their feet. Surrounded by the stars on all sides, Sekhet Bastet unleashed the third tier of Secrets Ripped From Skies, asking the heavens for help.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Radiance would end Solar's reign and break the ties of Fate. The Restless Stars must stand, lest the world fall.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi followed the other two a few minutes later. As he appeared within the sphere, another being appeared alongside him. It had the shape of a woman, her features picked out in tiny motes of glowing starlight. She looked like a moving constellation, impossibly vast even in human form. Akenakhi recognised her. He had cut her throat, more than four thousand years before.<br /> <br /> &quot;Was it worth it?&quot; She spoke a dialect of Ancient Egyptian, sounding like a badly butchered version of Iremite barely understandable to the Arisen.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi was shocked, and shook his head. &quot;No,&quot; he said, on the verge of tears, &quot;no, it wasn't. I am sorry.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra was eyeing the apparition, trying to come to a decision. Satisfied that what he was looking at was, indeed, a ghost, he decided to unleash Chthonic Dominion Tier 2, commanding the ghost to tell him everything she knew of the magic of this place.<br /> <br /> The command settled upon the ghost, binding her like iron. She screamed with rage and turned on Sesu Ra, appearing in front of him and plunging her hands into his chest. Although he felt no physical pain, his pillars began to spiral rapidly out of him, drained from him by her magic. His Ren disappeared first, and then he began to feel his flesh wither under the assault.<br /> <br /> Yet, despite her anger, the ghost could not stop herself from speaking. She spoke of the magic she had been killed to reveal, telling them that there was a magic in the name of stars they could not even comprehend. This magic had long been hidden from the world, and could only now be seen by those who had already wielded it. She spoke of the eternity she had endured, bound here beyond the world, bare and open to the gaze of the malevolent stars.<br /> <br /> Worming her hands ever deeper, now stealing Sesu Ra's Sheut, she spoke of a light she had seen. Scientists called it a quasar and knew it to be the brightest thing in the universe, but she knew better. It was like a living thing, coursing through the stars. It would devour all other light, and feast upon the hidden magic.<br /> <br /> Those final words said, she sealed her mouth tightly shut. Sesu Ra endured her onslaught a little longer, but when it was apparent there was no more information forthcoming, the meret found they could return to the world simply by willing themselves away.<br /> <br /> The meret decided they needed to tie up any loose ends regarding the ghost cult they had encountered. Akenakhi and Sesu Ra went to meet with Adelaide to see if she had any help she could offer, while Luca and Sekhet Bastet found that the cult's meeting place now had a sign declaring it Condemned. They were able to track down the home of Abilo, the cult leader, and were met at the door by a pretty young woman who introduced herself as Calisto. She told them that her father didn't want to see them, and when they tried to push past her she stabbed Luca in the neck with a knife.<br /> <br /> More men, including Abilo, came rushing from the house. Ghosts began to materialise around them. Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, revealing her demonic form. The men were overwhelmed with Sybaris, flinging themselves to the ground. Only Calisto was entirely unaffected, shrugging off the supernatural terror with a supreme act of will. Luca bludgeoned her unconscious, while Abilo went to flee. Bast walked after him, flitting through walls and dancing across the impossible angles until she was standing in front of him. Before he could react, she reached out seized him by the throat. His flesh withered away and he was mummified, a frozen scream distending his face.<br /> <br /> Luca stayed on watch to see if the brief struggle had alerted the authorities, but it seemed that no one in the neighbourhood had raised the alarm. The cultists were tied up, along with Calisto. Exploring, Bast found the iron box she had seen Abilo carrying in their last encounter. It contained a human skull, missing its lower jaw. When she touched it a creature appeared in the fog of Twilight, a ghost consisting of a floating skull and a writhing mass of tentacles that appeared to be made from vertebrae. It was unable to harm her, however, so she ignored it until it disappeared.<br /> <br /> Calisto surged to her feet then, rushing at Luca. She snatched his pistol from his waistband. When he seized her, she put the gun to her own head and fired. In the struggle, however, the shot did little more than graze her. They subdued her again, struggling to understand how she had escaped her bonds.<br /> <br /> Back at Adelaide's home, Sesu Ra and Akenakhi had managed to get through the door and were now waiting for Adelaide to get home. She did, saw them, and went pale. She demanded that they leave. Akenakhi tried to talk her down, saying that they were here to help, but she pointed out that she had made her feelings towards the undead very clear the last time they spoke. The two Arisen left. Sesu Ra, being able to witness the events playing out through his Sadikh's eyes, didn't mind overly much. It seemed the situation was under control.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi returned to the abandoned suburb. He remembered the priests of Iunu calling this place the Vault, and stepped through to speak with the girl he had killed. She appeared and attacked without speaking, taking from him his Ab. He stayed as long as he could, begging for forgiveness, and left before he was destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 07-05-2015, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:14:51-07:00","id":588724,"title":"","content":"Session 40<br /> <br /> Aquila fell ever deeper into Neter-Khetet. She remembered standing on a hill on the day the city fell. The gates were opened from within by treachery and starving citizens, trapped between a desperate warlord and a mad emperor. It was the end of the only empire since the days of Irem she considered worthy of the title. She wondered if this was what it would have been like to watch Irem die.<br /> <br /> The barbarian horde swept through the city. They had cut her off from her cult, her temple. She was making her way back to her people when she was struck from behind. The blow sent her sprawling. It was the first time in more than two hundred years that anyone had dared raise a hand to her, and she rose brimming with fury. The man gave her an insolent smirk, wearing the armour of the invaders. She had seen how men behaved in the aftermath of conquest, and Qerrti compelled her to act.<br /> <br /> She unleashed Harvest the Divine Flesh, unveiling her true glory. Rather than cower from the Sybaris, however, the man's smile only widened. His comrades formed a loose semi-circle around them as he levelled his spear at her and thrust, driving the blade deep into her body. She raised a hand to strike back, and heard a voice shout out, &quot;Stop this madness!&quot;<br /> <br /> An old man interposed himself between the fighters. He moved with the vigour of youth, but his hair was grey and his face lined. He apologised to Aquila profusely, speaking Latin with a thick Gothic accent. His men had heard stories, he said, and were much too eager to test themselves against one of the gods. Aquila sneered, expressing her surprise at hearing a barbarian speak the civilised tongue, but said that he spoke well for what he was. The man's effusive thanks for her compliment mollified her, and she Sealed her flesh to knit the wounds she had suffered back together.<br /> <br /> The man explained that he had come with a message, not for her but for the one who would one day remember these words. He locked eyes with her, and she fancied she saw bright lights in the depths of his gaze. &quot;Fate hates you,&quot; he said. &quot;It loathes you. It twists the world against you and brings ruin to all your endeavours for no reason other than that you are what you are. But Fate can be broken, its chains smashed, and what must be need not come to pass.&quot; In every Sothic Turn, he explained, Fate could become mortal. If they destroyed the bonds of Fate, then, at last, they could know peace.<br /> <br /> The vision ended, and Aquila awoke in her tomb. Her last canopic jar was gone, her body reformed around her talismanic spirit organ. She had only the last dregs of Sekhem remaining, and she realised what that meant. She had nothing to give back to Akenakhi, no price to pay that would lessen her betrayal. Overcome with shame at her hubris, she sank to the depths of her tomb and nursed the growing hatred for the hand Fate had dealt her.<br /> <br /> On the surface, the Arisen were being stirred to a frenzy of activity. Sekhet Bastet had rallied the Nome. With news that she had located the nest of the Shuankhsen, she had arranged for every active Arisen in the city to gather at Rekhenaten's tomb. The Master of the Pit was not terribly happy with this arrangement, and made it clear that he expected neutral territory to be used for all future gatherings of this nature, but he was happy to play host this one time. He had no intention of becoming the next Temple, however.<br /> <br /> The Arisen began to arrive. Only Aquila, hiding in her tomb, and Mot-Tan and Kotira, currently in henet, did not make an appearance. Rekhenaten had arranged for a lounge room on his estate to be used, a large room filled with armchairs and lavish carpets. Yarikh joined them first, but chose a corner of the room to stand in. The siblings Mekshonat and Benerib were next, escorted by Rekhenaten's cultists who had been helping to arrange new tombs for them in Jakarta. Hetenatra arrived seated in a wheelchair, pushed by her cultist Imeni. Sem-Huf chose a chair close to where Rekhenaten himself was seated, while Yama-Het and Aqhat chose to stand.<br /> <br /> Rekhenaten dismissed his cultists before the meeting began, and ceded the floor to Bast. She spoke of the vile nature of the Shuankhsen, of their parasitic lust for Sekhem and the need to destroy them like the rabid dogs they were. If left to fester, there was the danger they may create more of their kind, maybe even from among those Arisen in this chamber. She had tracked a relic they had in their position, and believed she knew the location of their primary stronghold within Jakarta. She called upon the Nome to put together a combined crusade to destroy these creatures.<br /> <br /> Aqhat stepped forward immediately, before any others could react, to offer his services. Mekshonat was next, volunteering his sister's help in destroying these creatures. The others were more measured, but every Arisen present offered some kind of support. Sem-Huf, though too weak to fight, said he would dispatch as many of his cult's soldiers as he could spare. Yama-Het would send her chosen warriors, augmented with her magic, but cautioned that they should be returned to her the minute the fighting was done lest the magic rend their bodies asunder. Yarikh offered as many Awakened Servants as he could create on short notice, while Hetenatra offered to come in person and ensure that judgement was brought down upon the wicked. Finally, Rekhenaten said he would send his Sadikh, Tobi, a capable fighter with the power to call upon Rekhenaten's own magic.<br /> <br /> Decision made, the Arisen moved quickly. Asa Corp arranged for vans to transport the Nome's forces, sending them around the city and to gather the army at Asa Corp. Sem-Huf's mortal cultists were chosen as drivers, as they would be of little use in actual combat in the face of so many sources of Sybaris. Sesu Ra chose to retire to his tomb and send Luca in his place. He had no interest in fighting the Shuankhsen in person while his Sekhem was so low.<br /> <br /> Below the city, Quil alerted Aquila to the cult's movements. The interest drew her out of the depths. A strike against the Shuankhsen interested her greatly. A chance for revenge, perhaps. However, she dared not show her face openly, not until she could repay Akenakhi. She summoned Tetasu Xex, knowing that the ability to drain Sekhem would be vital if they hoped to destroy the Shuankhsen with any kind of permanency.<br /> <br /> That was when she found that she had a message from Mike Thornton. She called him, and after he finished berating her for being out of contact for so long, he told her that LDI had come to a decision. The attacks on their port facilities had done a lot of damage, and they were retreating from the city. Only a few projects would remain in place, which would be folded into Asa Corp as &quot;research divisions&quot; of the smaller company. They were going to trial a less intrusive presence, to see if the donations of Sekhem from willing Arisen could make up the potential shortfall. Aquila contacted loyal members of her cult, arranging for this merger to take place without her direct supervision, hiding LDI's presence within the cult from the rest of her meret.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, this gave the cult the Compartmentalised advantage.<br /> <br /> The vans began to move out, the Nome's army inside. Aquila, Quil, and Tetasu followed in a van of their own at a discrete distance. They wound through the city, following the kepher trail illuminated in Sekhet Bastet's mind.<br /> <br /> The chemical plant was located in the industrial quarter of the city, along the banks of the river. As they arrived, Bast realised why a mundane search had never found the place. There was a distortion of the air lying across the entire property, giving the impression of a mirage. Any attempt to notice it, to see it as something significant, failed. The eye simply drifted away from the plant, finding other, more important things to focus upon. Without the scarab's path telling her that this was where the relic lay, she would never have paid it any attention.<br /> <br /> The front gates were padlocked shut, but a blow from Aqhat tore the very gates themselves from their hinges and sent them crashing to the ground. Beyond was a long gravel driveway, littered with construction equipment and rusting steel drums. At its end was the plant, two long wings extending up and downstream on either side of a central tower. Bast's kepher unerringly pointed forward, to the top of the tower.<br /> <br /> The vans disgorged their contents. Kudama Jav, his book in hand, summoned forth his spirits to aid his master. Awakened Servants shambled out to form a vanguard of undead flesh. Then came Yama-Het's warriors, a man and a woman who had been greatly altered by her magic. The man had the head and claws of a lion, while the woman had a falcon's head and a great pair of wings spreading out behind her. The skin of both almost seemed to shimmer with a golden aura, a palpable manifestation of the magic inside them. Tobi, bearing a Japanese officer's sword from the second World War, summoned Rekhenaten's magic to armour himself in earth. They each crossed through the gates, the Arisen in their midst.<br /> <br /> Stepping across that threshold filled even the mightiest of the assembled Mummies with a sense of nausea. The world beyond was broken. A black sun burned in the midst of a sky mottled like a purple bruise, surrounded by dark stars. The ground cracked underfoot, and through the cracks could be seen flesh oozing like an open wound. Bast, looking into the world beyond with Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, realised something else. Twilight did not exist here, Neter-Khetet had been folded into the physical world. Kudama's ghosts manifested physically, every bit as real as the creatures around them.<br /> <br /> The group advanced on the factory. That was when Akenakhi spotted the lesser Amkhata. A host of them, almost all with the heads of falcons or jackals, descended on the group. During the fighting, several could be seen fleeing back towards the main building. The Arisen army overwhelmed their attackers easily enough, having more trouble from the scorpions, bees, and centipedes that spilled from the creatures' wounds than from the Amkhata themselves.<br /> <br /> Hetenatra announced that she would remain outside, to summon her magic as needed. Akenakhi muttered something snide beneath his breath at that, about avoiding the danger and claiming all the glory. Bast had Kudama stay with Hetenatra, while the rest of the group advanced on the main tower. Aqhat smashed down the front door, and they all filed inside.<br /> <br /> There was a large circular room at the base of the tower. Three doors led off in different directions. Bast's kepher only told her that she needed to go up, and there was no way to tell which door was the correct one. Akenakhi unleashed Palace Knows Its Pharaoh to try and discover the correct route, and had to bite back a scream as the information flooded his mind. The interior of this building did not conform to normal physics. His mind could not make sense of the barrage of information, of the way rooms lay within smaller rooms and down became the same as up. He had a sense that the central door was the one they wanted, but more than that he could not determine.<br /> <br /> The door led to a staircase, which wound up and up and up for an interminably long length of time. As they grew weary of the climb, they smelled something foul in the air. A moment later a hissing, toxic liquid came pouring down the walls and stairs. The more nimble of the invaders were able to avoid being hurt too badly, but the Awakened Servants lost much of their flesh to the corrosive fluid.<br /> <br /> They rushed to the top of the tower to confront the source of the attack, but as they charged the stairs began to change. The stairwell's walls became craggy stone, and one by one the other members of the group disappeared from view. Bast and Akenakhi each found themselves alone in a canyon they recognised. The shadows formed jackal-headed demons carrying bone knives, and oversized scorpions emerged from the sands. They realised slowly what had happened. Somehow, they had fallen into Duat. There was nothing they could do except run.<br /> <br /> The canyon maze was hard to navigate. Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars to make herself faster, easily outpacing her pursuers. Akenakhi was not so fortunate, suffering cuts and stings from the demons who dogged him. Neither of them fell, however, and they emerged into a burning sky for a moment before they fell into a chamber beneath the earth. Like the first chamber they had entered, it was round, but this one had a sloping floor that fell towards a large grill in the middle. They were back on Earth and in what looked to be a waste disposal chamber.<br /> <br /> Aqhat was there already. The lion-headed warrior emerged from the walls seconds after they did, and they were joined by Tobi moments after that. There was no sign of Luca, nor any of the others.<br /> <br /> A rumbling came from the pipes leading into the chamber, along with a high-pitched wailing. The group stood back to back as a host of the dead emerged. They mostly appeared to be workers from the chemical plant, badly scorched and broken by whatever had killed them. They crawled on shattered limbs as they spilled like a flood of flesh towards the intruders. The lion warrior tore into them in a frenzy, joined by Bast and Tobi. Akenakhi and Aqhat stayed back, noting with dismay what little impact the attack was having on the enemy's numbers. Aqhat strode to the central drain and smashed it open, calling out for the others to follow him. Then he leapt down into the depths.<br /> <br /> When Bast pulled her way out of the horde to follow, she experienced the disconcerting knowledge that she was getting closer to the relic above her despite the fact that she was going down and ever sense told her that she needed to go up. The Arisen and their allies emerged in a neat, grey corridor. The walls were cracked like the ground outside, the flesh within festering with nests of maggots. Akenakhi poked one with his spear, and grimaced when it burst.<br /> <br /> They heard the sound of fighting and rushed to the nearest door. It flew open at a touch and they piled into the room. Benerib was there, one arm missing and her body shattered beyond any Arisen's ability to heal. As they watched, a being with the head of a diseased lion, who Akenakhi recognised as Iwseck, tore her apart and swallowed the last few chunks. With her was Gator, armoured in stone with his flesh coloured gold and his eyes made of jewels. Behind them, Nenheta lurked near the back of the room. An Amkhat with the head of a lion and the body of a serpent roared a challenge, and a group of Gator's Fasad, led by the one the meret knew as Rotlung, rallied at their master's side.<br /> <br /> There were no speeches or declarations. The two sides charged. Aqhat rushed the Amkhat, severing its head from its body in a single blow. Scorpions flooded the room, spilling from the thrashing body as it died. Rotlung charged Bast, tearing at her with his oversized teeth. She seized him by the throat and cut him apart, her blessed bone blade easily parting his Lifeless flesh. Before she could recover, however, wounds began to appear on her body as if from nowhere. The assault came from Nenheta, her hand outstretched to strike at Bast's shadow. To her left Akenakhi battled one of Gator's Fasad, keeping the savage creature at bay with his spear. The third Fasad vanished under the lion warrior's claws, limbs and chunks of flesh flying as Yama-Het's soldier demonstrated the strength of his blessings.<br /> <br /> Aqhat went to the defence of his fellow Su-Menent, knocking Nenheta to the ground and embedding his axe in her chest. She spat out the power of the Kiss of Apep as her death curse, infecting his body with a mystical poison and robbing him of his ability to heal. Then Iwseck leapt on him from behind. Her lion jaws sank deep, ripping him apart. The great Shemsu of the Su-Menent fell. As he died, the entire room shook, and shook again. The roof collapsed, bringing with it fire and the wrath of the Judges. Meteors struck at the Shuankhsen, and Sekhet Bastet realise it must be the work of Hetenatra. The attacks were carefully placed, hitting only those enemies who were not so close to the Arisen as to risk harming them. Bast took advantage of Iwseck's sudden injuries to revenge Aqhat's death, striking a blow that almost ripped Iwseck's jaw from her head. The Shuankhsen rounded on her in a fury, her jaws biting out chunks of the of the Arisen's flesh. Ancestry of Forgotten Stars saved her from losing Sekhem to the creature, but she could not maintain the spell for long.<br /> <br /> Gator had seen the earth-clad Tobi and, seeing him as the closest thing to Aquila, had bulled his way through the melee to attack the Sadikh. His massive jaws kept Tobi staggered and on the defensive, doing horrific damage to the Sadikh despite his armour. Akenakhi, trying to help, rushed over and laid a hand on Gator's body. The earthen armour ran from Gator like water. Furious, Gator rounded on the Fog of Torment and readied himself to strike.<br /> <br /> That was when Aquila burst from the wall and barrelled into him. Quil rushed out to attack the Fasad who was preparing to attack Akenakhi from behind. Tetasu Xex coiled in the air, waiting for a clear target. Akenakhi threw himself on Gator as well, trying to hold him down. Gator seized Akenakhi first, and ripped the last Sekhem from his soul. His Descent ended there, and Gator feasted on his Ab. Then he fastened his grip on Aquila, who stared at him with horror.<br /> <br /> The rain of meteors had stopped. Ancestry of Forgotten Stars faded. Iwseck launched herself at Bast with renewed vigour, tearing Sekhem from her body. Her teeth did horrific damage to Bast's Sahu, taking her beyond the point where she could maintain her form. She fell into her Death Cycle. As she died, she summoned a final meteor with Secrets Ripped From Skies as her death curse. The Utterance struck Iwseck. Both Shuankhsen and Arisen were consumed in fire.<br /> <br /> Outside, Kudama Jav received instructions from his master. He picked up Hetenatra and carried her from the field. They left behind them the smoking corpses of the Amkhata who had tried to attack the Lady of the Broken Stele, thinking a wheelchair-bound Arisen to be an easy target.<br /> <br /> The remaining Fasad squared off against Quil and the lion-headed warrior. With a wicked grin, the creature lunged at Yama-Het's servant, plunging its hand into the man's chest and ripping out his heart. The man's body didn't fall. Instead his eyes clouded, and he turned on Quil as an undead abomination. Tetasu dove from the sky to help, coiling around the Fasad.<br /> <br /> Aquila was the only Arisen remaining in the room. She threw everything she had at Gator. Rendered silent by his grip, she was unable to wield Utterances herself. She had prepared for that, however, and called on the power she had stored in one of her rings to try and turn his head to gold. Gator shrugged off the spell, however, and split her open. As he had done moments before with Akenakhi, his teeth reached deep and devoured the last of her Sekhem. Soul exposed, he shredded her Ba and claimed it for his own. Aquila ordered Quil to run with her final thought, but was gone from the world before she could see if he managed to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 07-13-2015, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T18:26:48-07:00","id":596380,"title":"","content":"Session 41<br /> <br /> The assault on the chemical plant was a disorientating experience for Sesu Ra. He tried to keep up with events by watching through Luca's eyes, but the images he received were strangely disjointed. They lost track of the others after the chemical spill. Luca battled his way through a horde of horrors, his strength and speed augmented with Blessed Is The God-King. He ended up trapped in a room where Awakened Servants poured from every entrance. They dragged him down, his magic failed, and everything went black.<br /> <br /> For Sesu Ra, it seemed as if only seconds passed before Luca's vision swam and he returned to consciousness. He was bound in chains, and Iwseck was squatting in front of him and banging the side of his head as if she were trying to get an unruly television to work.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sesu? Are you in there?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra chose to stay silent rather than speak through his servant. Instead, he asked for a report on the situation. Luca, much to Iwseck's annoyance, started to rattle off a description of his situation. He was alone, had no contact with the others, and didn't like his odds of getting out alone.<br /> <br /> Frustrated, Iwseck declared that all the other attackers had been killed. She'd feasted quite well. Luca was still alive though, because she knew that he meant something to Sesu Ra. She'd kept him hidden from the other Shuankhsen, and she intended to set him free. She wanted something first though. She wanted to see Sesu in person. No teeth involved, she promised.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra agreed, speaking through Luca's mouth. When she tried to ask him to meet her at a house she'd prepared, however, he refused. The two stared at one another, at loggerheads. Iwseck backed down. Sesu Ra asked that instead they meet at the abandoned building where they had first encountered one another. Iwseck agreed, but requested that he give her an hour to get the place ready.<br /> <br /> When Sesu Ra walked through the door of the building, it was deserted. The homeless it had played host to were gone. Instead, there was a man and a woman standing just on the inside of the doorway waiting for him, blank expressions on their faces. The man asked for Sesu Ra's coat and shoes. Sesu Ra glared at him and told him to go away, and the man complied.<br /> <br /> The smell of incense became very strong as Sesu Ra climbed the stairs. He reached Iwseck's room and walked inside. The smell was almost overwhelming, a particular flavour that reminded him of something he had lost. Sitting on a bed against the far wall was Iwseck. She was wearing a new body, that of an Egyptian woman in her late twenties, but her features had a strong resemblance to the Iwseck he had known before. She was dressed in a simple cotton shift, tied at the back of the neck with a knot. For a moment the sight and smell sent Sesu Ra's mind back to his mortal days, to a small home on the river's banks, and Iwseck's smile as he walked through the door.<br /> <br /> He was snapped back to the present by her voice. &quot;You came!&quot; Iwseck was on her feet, hurrying towards him and babbling in her excitement. &quot;I have a gift for you. Gifts. I fed well in the attack on my home. I can use it. I can tell you secrets, secrets the Silence would keep hidden.&quot; As she said those words, her face went pale and she swayed on her feet. &quot;Ooooh, She didn't like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra demanded to know what she was talking about. Iwseck shook her head and muttered to herself, something about not missing this chance. He asked what she had done with Luca, and she said she had already released him, on the other side of the city. Sesu Ra checked, peering through Luca's eyes, and saw it was true.<br /> <br /> Iwseck said that she would help him to remember. And then her eyes lit up. She would speak of the gifts he had given her. &quot;My gift to you will be your gifts to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> She stepped close to Sesu Ra. He could smell her beneath the incense, a smell like dust and honey with something foul and rotten underneath. She spoke of the Pharaoh's Name Day feast in her sixteenth year. Sesu Ra gave to her a necklace, made in secret, to spare her from the whips of the slavemasters so that she could labour with the other slaves without fear.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra remembered it. A relic, made by his hands in the dark of the night when the rest of the Guildhall was silent. A tiny square shield, hammered from a little sheet of bronze and inscribed with Iwseck's name, encircled by a protective cartouche.<br /> <br /> His mind returned to the present. Iwseck was walking around him, trailing a hand across his chest. She spoke of the day they wed, when he gave her freedom. She was still a slave, but he had her brought to the Guildhall to fetch and carry for him alone. She was freed from the duties of other slaves, free in every way save name.<br /> <br /> Again, Sesu Ra's mind flashed back to the past. He remembered that day. He was rising quickly through the ranks of the Guildhall. His skill had been recognised. He stood trembling before one of the great Shan'iatu, and the master asked if he required anything to help him in his work. He spoke Iwseck's name without hesitation.<br /> <br /> Iwseck stopped walking. She lifted a hand to touch his cheek. &quot;And when I told you I was with child, you gave to me a promise. You would find a way for our love to last through all time, to watch over our children forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> A mountain stood in the Guildhall, waiting to be carved. The Shan'iatu had spoken of a great task it would give him. The power of the relic would be formidable. Only his skill could bring it forth. Sesu Ra listened, and in his deepest, most private thoughts a different plan presented itself. He could use it to protect his family instead. Simply change the form, and anything could be possible.<br /> <br /> Iwseck kissed him. Gently, firmly, Sesu Ra pushed her back. &quot;Iwseck, how can I be with you when your hands are at my throat? You feed upon my friends.&quot;<br /> <br /> Iwseck looked hurt. It was self-defence, she said. They had attacked her.<br /> <br /> That wasn't enough. Sesu Ra pointed out what she had done to Akenakhi, her involvement in Richard Mayehi's death. He demanded to know why she had helped the Faithful to steal his body.<br /> <br /> Slowly, hesitantly, Iwseck explained. She could remember everything, all six thousand years. He could not. If she made him like her, a Shuankhsen, then he would lose those memories forever. He needed to have his memory rebuilt, so that he could remember her, what she meant to him. That wouldn't be enough. The Judges would punish him for being with her, his Descent would come to a swift end, and his memory would be ground down through time. She needed his memory restored, and only then could she complete his transformation. He would become a Shuankhsen, his memories intact, and they would be together for all time.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra kissed her. Iwseck's dress fell away before they ever reached the bed.<br /> <br /> Set-Qesu brought down its judgement as the sun rose the next morning. For its servant's sin, it stripped away the last of Sesu Ra's Sekhem. He fell into henet, the last of his meret to fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Season 2 begins (Aquila's player thought it would be fun to look at it like the start of a new season of a TV show)<br /> <br /> The light of Sothis drew him back from Duat. Opening his eyes, the Arisen found himself in his own body, in his own tomb. A part of him was a little bemused by this, but he could not remember why. He opened his sarcophagus and stepped out into the light.<br /> <br /> There was a mortal in the room with him. Bowing and scraping, the man introduced himself as Rom Mayehi. He was Sesu Ra's hierophant, the head of Asa Corp and a devoted servant.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra's memory slowly began to return. He recalled his last descent, and the way it had ended. He noted Rom had grown a beard, and asked how long it had been since he had been awake.<br /> <br /> &quot;A year,&quot; Rom said. &quot;We knew your Sothic Turn would be upon you soon. I came to speak of what has changed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Over the next few hours, Rom outlined the situation. Not much had been seen of the Shuankhsen. Their stronghold was under siege, encircled by Hetenatra's fire spirits and Aqhat's servants. The hope of the Nome, with so many of their warriors weak or vanquished, had largely rested on preventing the Shuankhsen from feeding. For the most part, this appeared to have worked. There had not been many direct confrontations with the Shuankhsen since the siege was put in place.<br /> <br /> Aqhat and Hetenatra had both returned to henet. Mot-Tan and Kotira had not yet returned to activity. Yama-Het and Rekhenaten were still awake, and had become involved in a feud that had seen many of their respective cultists killed. Mekshonat and Benerib had established proper tombs, secreted somewhere in the city. Yarikh was still awake, and reclusive as ever. Of Sem-Huf, little had been heard.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of the meret, Sekhet Bastet lay in her tomb awaiting her own Sothis rising. Akenakhi had sealed his relics and canopic jars within his tomb, linking the doors together in such a way as to render physical entry to the tomb impossible. Aquila, meanwhile, had closed the entrances to her tomb with a barrier of concrete. The cult had found it impossible to raise either of them as a consequence.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra wasted no time. He had himself taken to speak to Rekhenaten. The Master of the Pit's Country Club looked much the same as ever, but security had certainly been increased. There were now two guards on the front gate instead of one, and they carried automatic weaponry with an authority that suggested they had all the correct permissions to carry, and even use the weapons in defence of the property.<br /> <br /> Inside, cultists, direct Sesu Ra through a baffling sequence of doorways to reach Rekhenaten's chambers. Eventually, the stairwell down to the basement led him smoothly into Rekhenaten's preferred receiving room on the second floor. There, the other Tef-Aabhi was waiting.<br /> <br /> Rekhenaten was more than willing to explain what had happened. Rekhenaten had been attacked by groups trying to disrupt some of his connections in organised crime. The criminals were useful in his people smuggling operations, so he moved in resources to retaliate. When Tobi was burned alive where he lay recovering from the attack on the Shuankhsen, Rekhenaten realised that something supernatural was at play. Then animal-headed creatures began assaulting his men, and he knew the culprit. The fighting had become quite vicious, but now that he and Yama-Het were approaching the tail ends of their respective descents it had settled down into an uneasy stalemate.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra asked if the Vestiges were safe. Rekhenaten took him to them, located in a hidden chamber within his building. There were six of them, ranging from a waterlogged book to a pair of police issue handcuffs. Sesu Ra admired them, and resolved that a danger to them could not be countenanced. He offered to do what he could to help destabilise Yama-Het.<br /> <br /> Over the next day he made arrangements regarding the building he had constructed inside Yama-Het's territory, originally used to lure out the Pelamat. He organised for the local criminal groups opposed to Yama-Het's cultists to have access to the building as a safe house, and began to funnel money into helping prop them up.<br /> <br /> With those arrangements made, his Sekhem dropped to 8 (9 because of his Talisman). He used the opportunity to Kepher for the necklace, whose existence he had discovered from Iwseck. To his shock, and more than a little frustration, Yama-Het's face appeared in his vision.<br /> <br /> He hadn't intended to wake any other members of his meret so soon, but he decided he could not approach Yama-Het with any expectation of a civil discussion, under the circumstances. He gathered cultists, went to Aquila's tomb, and used Dominating Might to smash apart the barriers she had erected with ease. He ordered the cult to raise her, using the life of a beggar Luca had bribed to descend into the crypt.<br /> <br /> The Black Caul lifted. Aquila woke, Sekhem roaring back into her new body forming around her Talisman. Her purpose filled her mind. &quot;Bring the Unbending Spine his relics.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra didn't wait to speak to her. Seeing the ritual performed successfully, he left the cult to explain what had happened.<br /> <br /> Aquila's memories returned quickly. She mustered her power and sacrificed it to raise to life the man who had died to summon her dropping her to Sekhem 8 (effectively 9). She understood the purpose she was bound to, but could not bring herself to act without first making reparations. She travelled to Akenakhi's tomb, and summoned Tetasu Xex. To her relief, he appeared. She sent him to enter the tomb through the walls, by-passing the spells Akenakhi had put in place, and ordered him to bring her the Rod of Tjesh.<br /> <br /> Tetasu returned quickly. Aquila performed the necessary rituals to raise the Fog of Torment, binding him with the command to raise Asa Corp to the heights of power, so that they might help as many people as they could. In game terms, it was a command to lift the cult to Reach 5 before the end of his descent.<br /> <br /> As Akenakhi stepped from his tomb, Sekhem thundering in his ears and his mind still wiped clean of any memories, Aquila felt the tug of her Purpose. She had neglected it for too long.<br /> <br /> At the end of the session, Sesu Ra raised his Memory to 4 and Akenakhi's player repurchased Memory 7 (since it had dropped back down to 6 at the end of his last descent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T22:40:27-07:00","id":605302,"title":"","content":"Session 42<br /> <br /> For Bast, the experience of a Death Cycle trapped in the Shuankhsen's tower was disorientating to say the least. She was trapped inside her own khat, unable to descend to Neter-Khetet in a place where that realm and the physical one appeared to overlap. She watched as the last of her allies were destroyed, and witnessed Quil flee the tower in the company of an Amkhat. And then she was alone, as Gator picked up her body and dragged her somewhere dark to hang by her wrists.<br /> <br /> She had no idea how long she was left alone in the shadows. And then she sensed movement, out there in the dark, and Anpu came towards her. He pressed one hand to her cheek and her vision was filled with memories of a life three thousand years lost.<br /> <br /> She was alone among the dead. It was not an unfamiliar experience. Even among the priests of the Su-Menent, Sekhet Bastet had always been one to whom the darkness of the next world and the terrifying secrets of the afterlife were familiar. But at this time, she had not seen a living being in three hundred years.<br /> <br /> She meditated at the top of a round, smooth stone. It rose from the desert among the dunes. She had watched the sands change shape over the years, moving like an ocean. The dunes never came close to the stone. Nothing ever did. The stone appeared impervious to seeds, offered no shade for lichen or moss to grow. The sun killed all life long before it reached this place. She had chosen it for this reason. It was not a place of life or death, because nothing had ever lived to come here. It was the promise of what came before. It was pure, untouched, entirely apart of the cycle through which all living things must endure.<br /> <br /> Her cultists had tried to join her on this journey. One by one they had perished, long before they came to this place. Their souls were anchored to her body, a cult of the dead to raise her with the power of the Pale Brood whenever her power failed her and she fell once more to henet. She needed to keep her vigil. For her own part, she endured. The sun burned her skin, but she would heal when the night came. The freezing wind was as nothing to her in the darkness. She waited.<br /> <br /> Finally, the air spoke with forty-two voices, in a language she didn't know but could somehow understand. The voices praised her devotion, and asked why she had come.<br /> <br /> &quot;The square-eared beast is gone,&quot; Bast said. &quot;I have failed in my purpose.&quot; The words tasted like bile in her throat. &quot;Why do I yet endure if my purpose can never be completed?&quot;<br /> <br /> There was silence for some time, and then the voices told her. They spoke of the corpse of the dead beast, and how it may yet be raised to exaltation. It would rise as a shadow of itself, but perhaps a shadow is all she would need.<br /> <br /> The vision ended, and Bast felt the last of her Sekhem dwindle away. She returned to henet, until she felt Sothis begin to rise in the skies above.<br /> <br /> When Bast rose, she rose to find herself still trapped in the Shuankhsen's dungeon. She was suspended by her wrists. With all the might of a newly woken Arisen, she tore the chains from the walls and battered down the door of her cell. She strode out into the halls. The corridor began to change then, shifting in form and shape until she was walking along a narrow metal walkway high above a factory floor. Vats of bubbling chemicals stood on either side, and as she watched Awakened Servants began to appear on either end of the walkway, blocking escape.<br /> <br /> Bast unleashed Blessed Is The God-King, become an enormous jackal-headed being. Then she charged, rushing the Awakened Servants in front of her. At the last moment she leapt, sailing above their heads, and hit the ground behind them without breaking stride. She could still feel the uter that had first drawn her to this place, beating a steady drum in her mind. It led her up a spiral staircase. She was half-way up when Gator tried to ambush her.<br /> <br /> She saw him waiting for her, and summoned to her hands a spear of light and darkness. The Shuankhsen looked sickly, weak. He rushed her, dodging beneath her defences and sinking his teeth into her chest. She unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, adding demonic attributes to her divine visage and making her harder to hurt by far. Then she pinned Gator to the wall with her spear, and let a mystic rot eat away at his tissue. He struggled, but he was quickly consumed.<br /> <br /> Just before he died, he stopped fighting. His arms fell limp. Looking up at her balefully, Gator told her that she should have been a feast to restore the Shuankhsen's strength. If it hadn't been for the Child up above, he would have been there when she woke. As he spoke his final words the last of his flesh was eaten away, and he collapsed at Bast's feet.<br /> <br /> She stepped over him and continued her advance. The resistance was considerably more mild than she had experienced on the first assault, although the impossible architecture of the plant was still a challenge to navigate. At last she emerged at the top of the tower. There were many more holes blasted in its walls than she remembered, but the relic was definitely here. It wasn't the only thing.<br /> <br /> It took her a few seconds to realise that she wasn't alone. There was a strange shimmer in the air of the chamber, a mirage-like ripple that moved in ways that made her think of a coiling snake. She stepped towards it and reached out a hand to touch it. As her hand made contact she was thrown across the chamber, her body wracked by conflicting gravitational forces. Her bones felt like they were being pulled apart from the inside even as her flesh and eyes were crushed under waves of pressure. She pulled herself to her feet, summoned a spear, and charged. The thrust felt like it was plunging into rotten, pulpy fruit, and the forces that struck back were stronger than the first. She unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars again, to protect herself, but as she did the coils suddenly stopped moving. Bast felt a voice speaking in her mind.<br /> <br /> [i]You are one of our heritage,[i] it said. <i>Do you seek the star's light?</i><br /> <br /> Bast was confused and asked what it meant, but it only told her that if she was not here for the star then it had no quarrel with her. It said that it was the Coils of Apophis, that it was a child of the light, but beyond that it would share nothing.<br /> <br /> Frustrated, Bast turned her attention back to the relic she was hunting, and realised that it was beneath her feet, behind the walls, literally grown throughout the building. She smashed open the floor and plunged her hands into the pus and blood that seethed beneath it. She intuitively knew how to remove the relic, and pulled it from its resting place.<br /> <br /> The World's Wound was in her hands. As she straightened, the world around her shuddered. She sensed Neter-Khetet and the material world separate once more into their ordained places. The Coils of Apophis was gone, she noted. The world was no longer broken here. There was a spiral of spidery black runes on the ground where she had removed the Wound, but other than that there was no sign of the terrible changes it had wrought on the world around it.<br /> <br /> Fire spirits began to materialise around her, introducing themselves as servants of Hetenatra. They had been maintaining the siege of this place. They offered to take her to her meret, transported in secret by a Witness cultist of Aqhat so that the Sybaris of her form would not overwhelm the mortals here. Bast accepted, and left with her prize.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the meret, Akenakhi had spent some time exploring the residential area where Yarikh made his home. He had decided that the best way to keep to his mission was to expand the cult's influence into Yarikh's territory. The other Su-Menent in the city were all in henet, if he could remove Yarikh then he stood a good chance of pursuing his research into Apotheosis without further interruption. He discovered a vestige at the local textile market, a strip of cloth with ornate markings picked out in gold, and purchased it for a pittance from the oblivious mortal.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra had focussed on his memories. He remembered being sealed beneath the earth, and he remembered the day he returned to the world and saw the promise of Jakarta. He marshalled his forces, had Rekhenaten bring him materials, and the Tef-Aabhi acolyte Thothekmet was put into action placing the foundations for the new geometric networks. Thothekmet had become a warrior, a crusader over the course of the centuries, and Sesu Ra noted how the Arisen burned his Sekhem fighting to uphold his purpose and his guild's business at the same time. Ultimately, it left Thothekmet weakened, and that was how Sesu Ra found him in the Tef-Aabhi guildhall beneath the city centre. He met him there, and when Thothekmet greeted him he pulled a golden chisel from his clothes and told the acolyte that he had one more duty yet to perform.<br /> <br /> Months later, watching the pit be filled in, he was asked by a cultist if he wanted an access tunnel to remain open. In a moment of mercy, Sesu Ra agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:56:53-07:00","id":619562,"title":"","content":"Completely forgot to post this. The following is the World's Wound, as stolen by Sekhet Bastet:<br /> <br /> The World\u2019s Wound (5 dot Bane Uter)<br /> <br /> <i>The World\u2019s Wound appears as nothing more than a pile of decaying viscera. Attempts to examine it find that it appears to be from a mix of different animals, strangely fused together during decomposition. The smell coming from the mouldering flesh is disturbing, but worse are the sensations conjured up through proximity to the Uter. It mixes lust and hunger in equal measure, an appalling desire for more. What it is that the watcher craves isn\u2019t clear, even to them, but it can drive them to commit the basest of acts in an attempt to fulfil it.</i><br /> <i>Whenever the World\u2019s Wound is moved, a gruesome task by any measure, those who examine the ground where it rested find trails of black and red gore laid out in the shape of spidery runes. They seem to swim and shift before the eyes of the onlooker, but their shapes sear themselves into the memory of those who witness them. Although they write in no language ever spoken by mortal men, all who see them know they promise madness and the death of all things.</i><br /> <br /> Power: The World\u2019s Wound tears the line between reality and unreality, forcing space and time and the otherworld that is Neter-Khetet to bleed together. But before it can rend the laws of the universe so thoroughly, it requires a sacrifice. Forty-two innocents (defined as anyone of Morality 7 or higher) must be sacrificed to the Wound in order to activate its power. The blood of these sacrifices seep into the Wound\u2019s rotten flesh, and a spectral wail can be heard as their souls are condemned to an eternity of agony.<br /> The Wound\u2019s power creeps forth with the death of the final sacrifice. It claims the site of the sacrifice as its domain. The definition of a \u201csite\u201d is arcane, but generally it is along the lines of a large building and surrounding grounds, or an arbitrary amount of land of approximately equal size. Mortals are driven from the area in fear, and from that point forward they will be unable to notice or enter the site of their own free will. Anything that takes place there will go unseen by onlookers, even if the chosen site is an open field. Witnesses and those with an appropriate Unseen Sense feel revulsion and horror from proximity to the area.<br /> For supernatural beings, they see a strange shimmer when looking at the area of influence from the outside. It makes the area appear to be a mirage. It is hard to focus upon, and bringing oneself to believe that there is something of note there is quite hard without knowing of the relic\u2019s existence.<br /> Inside the bounds of the relic\u2019s influence, the world is broken. The state of Twilight seems to cease to exist, causing Amkhata and ghosts inside the area to be manifested physically. The manifestation modifier of the area rises to +5, overriding any other effects that may alter it.<br /> The corruption bleeding from the Wound alters the nature of the surrounding area in a variety of other unpredictable ways. Cracks in walls reveal pulsating, infected flesh, weeping trickles of blood. The view through windows shows unfamiliar stars in a strangely discoloured sky, mottled purple like a bruise. It alters the layout of buildings and leads to twisted and alien architecture that defies reason, from vaulted halls built for colossal beings of inhuman biology to tunnels that burrow through the walls and twist in on themselves endlessly.<br /> The Wound seeks to protect the one who performed the sacrifice, and intruders can be subjected to any one of a different number of effects. These range from visions and illusions, the creation of demons and strange spirits to destroy intruders, or attempts by the very land itself to elimate the intruder. Treat it like Retributive Curse\u2019s narrative level obstacle, except that whatever obstacle is chosen should have a good chance of killing the intruder. Each intruder who comes with ill-intent towards the one who performed the sacrifice triggers an obstacle of their own, although an individual obstacle may be dangerous enough to destroy every such attacker at once should they enter as a group.<br /> Utterances and other magic unleashed within the bounds of this territory can only affect the territory, their effects do not go beyond and remain unnoticed by any potential onlookers.<br /> This relic cannot be drained for Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Curse: The Wound feeds on the Sekhem of the surrounding area. This has a corrupting effect on mortals, causing them to sicken and die in droves. For regular mortals, this could be mistaken for a minor outbreak of a serious disease, from malaria to pneumonia. It strikes randomly, and its effects are usually survivable.<br /> The exceptions are those mortals who have been touched by Irem. Witnesses are almost certain to die, some dropping from heart attacks after prolonged exposure to the relic\u2019s influence (spending more than a week within a mile radius of its location). Next are the Cultists, who will be guaranteed to be infected by the disease. Individuals who have had other contact, particularly being subjected to Sybaris, simply have a higher rate of infection.<br /> The exact impact of this curse\u2019s effects on individual NPCs is up to the Storyteller. As a rule, all cults within ten miles lose a dot of Reach or Grasp every month. The plague may spread further than that, carried in the water, in vermin, or by the diseased themselves, but will have a lesser impact on cults outside of the region.<br /> The cultists of Shuankhsen are immune to this Curse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:41:13-07:00","id":619760,"title":"","content":"Wel, Bast should do everything in her power to completely destroy this relic if she is smart. One lesser amkhat is a perfectly acceptable price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T06:53:30-07:00","id":619970,"title":"","content":"It's juuuuust harmless enough when it isn't active that her current plan seems to be to keep it locked in her tomb until her Descent ends and it can be sent to her Judge.<br /> <br /> I see no way this could end badly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T16:21:28-07:00","id":620678,"title":"","content":"So intelligence isn't the highest Stat I see lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T23:15:12-07:00","id":621913,"title":"","content":"Session 43<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra's exploration of his own memories took him back to the days of Irem, to his mortal life, and the years he spent working in his Guildhall. It was the happiest time of his mortal life. He lived with Iwseck and worked under the tutelage of a Shan'iatu Guildmaster, among the finest masons of Irem. His skill was such that his master chose him, alone, to create an effigy of unsurpassed power. It would be a mighty statue, a representation of the master himself, and so long as it stood the Shan'iatu's power would be beyond any challenger.<br /> <br /> He worked for many days and nights. The <i>heka</i> of Irem flowed into his work chamber, and even to his mortal senses the statue's power became clear. He began to carve, creating the form of a Shan'iatu in full regalia. He worked upon it in secret, accepting no help from the Amulet Bearers of the Maa-Kep, spurning even his fellow masons.<br /> <br /> There was not enough power in the city's energies alone for what was needed. The Shan'iatu sent him slaves, and they died by Sesu Ra's hands. Their blood stained the statue's feet red, even as their Sekhem infused the effigy with untold majesty. It was his finest achievement, his life's work. But something was wrong.<br /> <br /> He recalled a night in his chambers, Iwseck by his side. She was worried about him. All he could think about was the feeling of the knife in his hands, watching today's slave die at the statue's feet. It had been a young man today. The day before, a woman, Iwseck's age. He remembered wondering how long it would be before Iwseck suffered such a fate. Irem was not kind to its slaves.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra made his choice. He returned to work on the statue. The head had yet to be carved, and required only the slightest modifications for what he intended. Form was power, and he knew best how to change the form to garner the power he needed.<br /> <br /> The day of the unveiling came. He stood proud among the crowd, knowing what was to come. As the statue was bared to the assembled masses, a sudden stillness came across the square. The statue wore the regalia of a Shan'iatu Guildmaster. It contained all the power Sesu Ra had promised. But rather than the mask of a Shan'iatu Guildmaster, its face was Iwseck's.<br /> <br /> They were in the temple. The Shan'iatu's guards kept Sesu Ra on his knees.<br /> <br /> &quot;For your skill, you will become one of our immortal servants,&quot; the Shan'iatu said. The master spoke of the thousand lifetimes he would live in glorious service to the Judges. A great honour, worthy of a craftsman of his talent.<br /> <br /> &quot;For your treachery, a price must be paid.&quot; That was when Iwseck was dragged, struggling, into the chamber, and the Shan'iatu spoke of the need of lives to power the Rite. He gave Iwseck a golden cup and whispered something to her, too low for Sesu Ra to hear. Her eyes fixed firmly on her husband, Iwseck drank, and he watched helplessly as black veins rose up her neck.<br /> <br /> The last thing Sesu Ra remembered, watching Iwseck die, was the order being given to have him prepared for the Rite of Return.<br /> <br /> Back in present day Jakarta, Sekhet Bastet and Akenakhi each made the effort to reconnect with their cultists in Asa Corp. Through them they discovered the others had returned from henet. Although the Sphinx of Rome was absent, the other three gathered together in the one place. Akenakhi had managed to discover a second vestige in his exploration of the textile market in Yarikh's neighbourhood, although the location of the rival Arisen's tomb still eluded him. Sesu Ra noticed the vestige and became extremely interested. He asked Akenakhi if there was anything he could offer in return for the items, as he needed them for a great ritual for his guild. Akenakhi magnanimously declared that he would offer them freely, a gift to his meret. Sesu Ra accepted happily, and began to share the information he had gathered on the state of Jakarta in 2013. Most importantly, he mentioned that Yama-Het had somehow got her hands upon a relic he had made in his mortal days, and that he intended to get it back. Aquila had been raised for this purpose, but he was growing quickly impatient.<br /> <br /> The three Arisen set off then to speak to the Sesha-Hebsu guildmaster. Akenakhi and Sesu Ra had lost power enough that they could pass for human, but Sekhet Bastet was asked to keep to the back of the van where no one could see her. Luca drove them to Yama-Het's community centre, where they found her cultists. Sesu Ra was refused access by her cultists, who said their master did not want to have a Tef-Aabhi within her quarters while the tensions were so high.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi and Bast went in without him, Bast grudgingly agreeing to be concealed in heavy clothing to prevent her from driving Yama-Het's cultist mad with fear. Akenakhi asked Yama-Het about the relic, and she confirmed that it was a trophy she took from defeating a Shuankhsen in battle many years ago. She did not see any reason why she should give it up. When Akenakhi suggested that she part with it so that Sesu Ra could make peace between her and Rekhenaten, she grew angry. Rekhenaten attacked her. She was not going to give up her property to buy peace. If anything, he should lend his resources to helping her rebuild. Neither of them had any significant advantage over the other, and he was in the wrong.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi left to report this to Sesu Ra, but Bast remained behind to ask Yama-Het some unrelated questions. She wanted to know about the &quot;square-eared beast&quot; and the significance of red-haired men. While Yama-Het wasn't able to tell her anything about the latter, she did mention what she knew about the shah, Sutek's Beast, a group of relic-creatures created with the components of relics from each of the five Guilds. These creatures were destroyed during the first Sothic Turn, either by the Shuankhsen or simply over time as their power drained away. Bast mentioned her belief that her true purpose was related to one, and that she felt she needed to return a shah to life. She asked if Yama-Het knew where she could find the remains of one, but the Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster was unable to help.<br /> <br /> Bast left, but she wasn't the last of Yama-Het's visitors. Luca had stolen past her guards and entered her chamber. She looked up when he entered, and Luca informed her that his master wanted the return of his possession. The relic she had taken as a trophy was his. Yama-Het merely folded her hands and said that she would not be making any deals until the conflict with Rekhenaten was over and reparations had been made. Sesu Ra chose that moment to step into his servant's place, swapping positions. They each knew that, in a fight, the drained Yama-Het wouldn't have a chance against the newly risen Tef-Aabhi Guildmaster. Sesu Ra made some veiled threats about entering the conflict on his subordinate's side, and Yama-Het told him she did not think he wanted to make this a guild affair. If he left, however, she would make sure to tell her cultists not to shoot him on the way out.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra decided to leave, although he was sure he had no intention of order Rekhenaten to make peace with the Sesha-Hebsu. The Arisen took a moment from there to go and speak to Aqhat's cultists in charge of monitoring the siege of the Shuankhsen to find out what had happened to Iwseck, Nenheta, and Gator. Nenheta had been killed by Hetenatra early in the siege during a breakout attempt. She hadn't been seen since then. Gator had made several attempts to escape, even fleeing underground using Dust Beneath Feet, but the moment he left the protection of the World's Wound Hetenatra's flaming ghosts converged and burned him until he retreated. As for Iwseck, she hadn't been seen once. It was entirely possible that she had been trapped on the outside when the siege began.<br /> <br /> Without any clear leads, Sekhet Bastet asked her meret to help her track an uter she had discovered simply through allowing her kepher senses to roam. The Kepher led them to a Doctor Jameela, a GP working in an affluent neighbourhood not far from Akenakhi's tomb. Akenakhi was able to talk them past receipt to grab fifteen minutes with the doctor, who took one look at the Arisen and told them all that they should be dead. Bast responded to this by slamming the human against the wall and demanding everything she knew of a withered, mummified heart. With the help of her Fearsome Soul affinity, she broke the doctor quickly. Jameela confessed between terrified sobs that she had discovered the heart when she was young and travelling in the Middle East, and had brought it back to study. She had some passing affinity for the occult, and when her cousin Imelda started to die from a heart condition, she realised she could use the heart to save her. She transplanted it into Imelda's chest, and her cousin had been fine ever since.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi realised what Bast was about to do then, and tried to stop her. He wasn't quite fast enough. She pressed her hands against Jameela's throat and subjected her to the Withering Judgement, reducing Jameela to a mummified corpse. In response to Akenakhi's horrified protest, Bast pointed out that this would wear off in a few hours. It was just to stop the doctor from warning her cousin.<br /> <br /> The meret walked out before anyone discovered the body and went immediately to the address Jameela had given them. It was an old, stately colonial mansion, with a garden full of wildflowers, orchids, and weeds in equal measure. The facade was stained an off-white by exhaust fumes, but other than that appeared to be in good repair. Bast walked up to the front door. When no one replied to her knock she asked Sesu Ra to knock the door down. He declined. Akenakhi noted that there was a tall hedge wall around the property that made the building proper hard to spot from the road. He was forced to repair his damaged pillars, torn apart by the Shuankhsen, on the spot, and then unleashed Revelations of Smoke and Flame Tier 2. He flew up to the second story and punched a small hole in one window, allowing him to reach inside and open it.<br /> <br /> Bast narrowed her eyes at this, and kicked the door hard enough to break the lock. She didn't trust the other Su-Menent not to do something to spoil her efforts in retrieving the uter. She ran through the house and up the stairs, while Akenakhi raced along the upstairs corridor towards the only door with light coming from underneath it. They reached the top of the stairs at the same time, neck and neck, but Akenakhi was the faster one. He reached the door to the room and stepped inside, slamming it in Sekhet Bastet's face. She snarled and unleashed the Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, allowing her to phase straight through the door and appear in Akenakhi's face in her demonic form. She spat at him that she would not be denied her prize, at which point the two Arisen took stock of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> They were in an old woman's bedroom. The air was a little stale, but otherwise it was clean and respectable. Imelda was sitting in the bed with a pair of reading glasses on, looking only a little terrified at the flaming angel and ghostly demon that had appeared in her bedroom, but apparently unaffected by Sybaris. Bast demanded that she give up the uter, her heart, and Imelda told her that she had no wish to do so. Bast rushed her and Akenakhi threw himself at the other Su-Menent, yelling at the old woman to run. Imelda went for her bedside table, moving too slowly for Akenakhi's comfort, and to his dismay pulled out a gun. She fired at Bast, but the bullets passed straight through the demon form without hurting their target. Laughing, Bast called upon the Jar of Teeth. Red smoke poured from her mouth and tore at Imelda, ripping the flesh from her bones. Akenakhi struggled in vain to subdue the stronger Mummy, and Imelda tried to run past them, firing the gun at the window, just as Sesu Ra walked into the room.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stop her!&quot; Bast screamed at him. There was a moment as everyone waited to see what the Tef-Aabhi would do, and then he struck Imelda with a casual, almost lazy blow that sent her sprawling to the ground. That was enough. Bast called up the Jar of Teeth one more time, and the power flayed Imelda alive.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi released her then. Not once looking at her fellow Su-Menent, Bast gathered the heart from Imelda's remains and identified it as the Heart of Sek-Bet, a relic with the power to turn mortals into immortal undead when placed within their chests. Her-Uru rewarded her with a descent reset for her achievement, and she left in triumph.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi returned to Jameela's office alone, and found it closed to the day. He was able to go to the nearest hospital and masquerade as a police officer, finding that Jameela had woken screaming in the morgue and that the desiccated corpse found in her practice had mysteriously disappeared. She appeared to be hysterical, but the hospital suspected some kind of hoax. Akenakhi was able to get access to her in a private ward, and managed, eventually, to persuade her to stop screaming at the sight of him. He told her, in broken tones, that he hadn't been able to prevent Imelda from being killed. His companion had wanted her heart.<br /> <br /> Jameela asked him if there was any way Bast could be killed. Akenakhi told her that it was possible, but it would be very, very hard. She asked for his help, and he promised to give it. Too many lives had ended at the hands of She Who Is Power, he told her. If he could put a stop to it, he would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T17:10:51-07:00","id":630473,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting to post these. Anyway, below is Bast's latest prize:<br /> <br /> The Heart of Sek-Bet (4 dot Uter)<br /> Size 1, Durability 2, Structure 3<br /> <br /> This dry and withered heart fits easily into the palm of one's hand. It is clearly dead and inert, but from time to time a dark, red liquid will seep from its closed valves.<br /> <br /> Power: The Heart requires a newly dead body to be used. It must be placed within the chest cavity of a dead mortal. This is a surgical operation, and requires a successful Intelligence + Medicine roll to properly stitch the heart in place. Once the wound has been closed over the heart will begin to beat, returning the dead mortal to life. They gain the following benefits:<br /> <br /> -Their Stamina rises to 6, and their Strength to 4 (provided it was not 4 or 5 already). They gain Iron Stamina 3.<br /> -They become undead. They no longer need to eat, sleep, or breathe. Their health must be completely filled with Aggravated damage before they die, and they do not suffer any loss of consciousness from bashing or lethal damage.<br /> -They no longer heal damage naturally. Instead, they must spend a Willpower to downgrade an Aggravated Wound to lethal, a lethal to a bashing, or a bashing wound to nothing.<br /> <br /> Curse: In order to give life, the Heart takes the vital energies of the one who performs the operation. This causes the one who uses the Heart to lose a permanent dot of Stamina. This is more temporary for the Su-Menent, who merely suffer a point of Aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T00:52:29-07:00","id":630790,"title":"","content":"Thanks for continuing to share these awesome actual plays! I'm really enjoying your writeups, but I have to admit that it's gotten a little difficult for me to keep some of the NPCs straight. Would you mind doing a quick rundown of the characters involved in the plot so far, for future reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T01:35:08-07:00","id":630854,"title":"","content":"Hehe, sure. There are quite a lot of characters buzzing around of various importance. At the moment, the big players are probably the following:<br /> <br /> Yama-Het, the Bloody Pen. Guildmaster of the Sesha-Hebsu, recently discovered to have an Effigy Sesu Ra made in his mortal life in her possession. Looks like a 16 year old girl.<br /> <br /> Rekhenaten, the Master of the Pit. A high-ranking Tef-Aabhi, and the only Tef-Aabhi in the city besides Sesu Ra himself. A member of the Flesh Masons and currently feuding with Yama-Het over disruptions to his people-smuggling schemes.<br /> <br /> Yarikh, Speaker to the Thrice-Dead, is a mid-ranking Su-Menent. A bit of an isolationist and popularly regarded, at least by the player meret, as a hunter of those heretics seeking Apotheosis. Akenakhi is currently conspiring to weaken his cult's influence and undermine his authority, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Rom Mayehi, the meret's hierophant, brother to the former (deceased) hierophant, and recently put in charge of a company which he probably has no idea how to run.<br /> <br /> Mike Thornton, the manager of LDI operations in the city. His current exact disposition is unknown following the withdrawal of LDI from Jakarta. American chap, pretty pally with Aquila.<br /> <br /> Iwseck, Nenheta, and Gator. The three Shuankhsen known to be in the city. Iwseck was Sesu Ra's slave/wife in life, Nenheta used to be an Arisen of the Su-Menent, and Gator died in some horrible experiment of Aquila's. The first two don't appear to be active at the moment, and there's a question mark over Gator.<br /> <br /> Most of the other Arisen in the city appear to be back in henet and not hugely plot-relevant at the moment, although some of the meret may take that opportunity to settle grudges they have formed in their last descent (I'm looking at the Aquila/Sem-Huf spat, specifically). The recently introduced Jameela, an older medical doctor who used the above relic to keep her dying cousin around, is probably going to become fairly important as she conspired with Akenakhi to put an end to Sekhet Bastet.<br /> <br /> Those are the really big characters, anyway. Are there any others giving you problems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T23:18:12-07:00","id":632017,"title":"","content":"Session 44<br /> <br /> It was Sesu Ra's turn to let his senses loose along the Scarab's Path, searching for anything that might lead to an Effigy or Vestige to help with his geometric network. Fate was with him and led him unerringly to a large shopping mall in the north of the city. The beacon of the Effigy was so great that it allowed him to locate it precisely, hidden in the desk of a manager's office on the fourth floor. Sesu Ra forced the door and smashed the lock on the desk, finding a small scorpion figurine carved of dark stone within. The rest of the meret had been given enough time to gather for this expedition, and Akenakhi was able to distract a large, heavily tattooed man who came to investigate long enough for the group to get clear.<br /> <br /> They didn't face any further opposition as they left the shopping centre and returned to Akenakhi's tomb, or rather the restaurant above it. Aquila met the others there, and an argument immediately unfolded between her and Bast over the use of an Amkhat in the attack on the Shuankhsen's stronghold. Aquila pretended she had merely tamed the creature, rather than created it, and pointed out that Bast had once done the same when faced with an Amkhat she couldn't destroy. Bast rather resented that, pointing out that she had done so in order to find a way to destroy the creature, not to use it, but it did take the wind out of her sails.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra tried to reign things in then. With the Shuankhsen apparently gone, the meret needed to work out their new priorities. LDI was apparently scattered to the winds, so their largest enemies no longer appeared to be in a position to hurt them. Of course, Sesu Ra's preference was for his meret to help him deal with Yama-Het. He didn't particularly care one way or the other if it was a violent or peaceful resolution, but he wanted his Effigy back immediately. Retrieving it was Aquila's purpose, so she didn't have much choice in the matter, but the others didn't have any interest in making another attempt.<br /> <br /> In the end, Aquila left on her own to speak with Yama-Het. The Sesha-Hebsu's cultists were welcoming enough, although Aquila could see at a glance that they were on guard. Her first sight of Yama-Het after a year showed just how tired and rundown the other Guildmaster had become. The two talked about the situation, and Aquila was worried at the way Yama-Het's version of events didn't seem to match up with Rekhenaten's. Each seemed to think the other had attacked them unprovoked, although Yama-Het admitted there was a chance she had killed some of Rekhenaten's people during her crusade against organised crime. Aquila's attempts to persuade Yama-Het to give up the Effigy she held were similar to Akenakhi's, and again Yama-Het resented the idea that she should give away her relics to stop a war she didn't start. She repeated her demand that Sesu Ra call off Rekhenaten. Only then would they talk.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Aquila tried to contact Mike Thornton. It seemed he had been transferred to an overseas posting, forcing her to dictate an email to an Asa Corp cultist requesting information on the disposition of her stolen sword. After that, she returned to report the news to Sesu Ra.<br /> <br /> When Aquila returned from her meeting Yama-Het without success, Sesu Ra began contemplating other options. His expanded memory offered up one possible option. He could remember being captured by a group of fanatical cultists once, men and women who had scarred themselves and painted spider-like runes across their bodies in blood. He had been held down as he watched a blasphemous perversion of the Call being performed. The memory ended with Iwseck waking, rising clothed in the flesh of a dead sacrifice. He studied the memory, and believed he could repeat the ceremony if need be. He dispatched Luca to find for him a recently deceased female body. If he had to, he intended to summon Iwseck and set her upon the weakened Yama-Het.<br /> <br /> The rest of the meret, meanwhile, discussed their options. They recalled rumours of a group that had taken advantage of the destruction of the Pelamat to secure the drug trade in the nightclub district close to Sesu Ra's tomb, back before they were even aware of the Pelamat's nature as a Shuankhsen cult. When coupled with the stories that the south part of the city, which included this area, had become increasingly hostile to the Arisen, the meret decided to investigate and see if the matters were linked.<br /> <br /> The group travelled together and chose to focus on the area's most popular establishment, Novus. Aquila's good looks and money got them through the door without a problem. Bast and Sesu Ra tried to mingle with the people on the first floor. Aquila and Akenakhi wormed their way onto the top level of the building. Rather more adept in this environment than their meret mates on the ground floor, they quickly learned that the building had come under new management over the course of the last year. From Aquila's many admirers they learned that the former owner, a man named Benjy, had disappeared mysteriously at the time of the change. It had caused a bit of the stir in the area, but it had actually drummed up a fair bit of business for the nightclub just from sheer curiosity. Probing further, they found that no one was really sure who the new owners were. They were very fond of live music, however, and had ensured a regular roster of performers were always available for the VIP lounge. One of the crowd that had formed around them mentioned that Daryat, the one-armed man in the bar below, was the manager and the best person to talk to. He was notoriously tight-lipped on the subject of the owners, however.<br /> <br /> Aquila left Akenakhi behind and went to deliver this morsel to the others. They located Daryat quickly enough, and eventually managed to catch his attention. Aquila bluntly tried to worm the names of the building's owners out of him, suggesting she had a lucrative business offer. Daryat steadfastly refused, but did agree to talk further in his office away from the music and the crowds.<br /> <br /> Of course, the moment they had him alone, Sekhet Bastet used Withering Judgement to turn him into a corpse and Aquila used Dust Beneath Feet to transport the meret, and Daryat, down into the sewers where no one could hear the ensuing interrogation. They returned Daryat to life, Aquila drained away most of his Willpower, and Bast immediately got to work using her Fearsome Soul Affinity to break him completely. To their absolute bafflement, however, Daryat remained resolute and refused to give up any information at all. Outraged at his defiance, Bast drew her knife and began to carve apart his remaining hand before Aquila dragged her off the man. She rendered Daryat unconscious with a light touch and used her powers to heal his wounds, then angrily told the other Arisen that she would take responsibility for the prisoner. In return, she demanded that Bast never touch him again. Bast wasn't happy about it, but she backed down.<br /> <br /> Transporting the unconscious man was difficult. Sesu Ra returned to the surface to collect Akenakhi, while Aquila smuggled him into a waiting truck and had him taken to Asa Corp headquarters where he could be safely quarantined.<br /> <br /> By the end of the session, everyone had dropped to Sekhem 7 (effectively 8, since they all have Talismans). Bast was the only exception, still at Sekhem 8 (effectively 9).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-21-2015, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:19:53-07:00","id":637503,"title":"","content":"Sesu Ra's new Effigy:<br /> <br /> The Black Scorpion (2 dot Effigy)<br /> Size 1, Durability 3, Structure 4<br /> <br /> This is a small carved figurine of a scorpion, made from an unknown kind of black stone. Those who hold it find it warm to the touch, no matter what the temperature of the room might be. Shadows grow longer in its presence, and the bearer quickly becomes convinced that they can see movement in the darkness, the scuttling of thousands of legs.<br /> <br /> Power: The Black Scorpion can reach into the depths of Duat and dredge up waves of crawling demons. These scorpion-creatures attack every single being within 30 yards, welling up and out of every nook and cranny to overwhelm their prey. Everything within range takes 1L damage a turn as a consequence of their attacks.<br /> <br /> Curse: The scorpions feed on the bearer's allies, and the bearer himself, just as much as their enemies. It is impossible to control them or prevent them from attacking everyone within range. They will never attack a member of the Tef-Aabhi Guild, however, even if the bearer might wish them to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T20:07:45-07:00","id":637649,"title":"","content":"Session 45<br /> <br /> Akenakhi knew well that he would need help if he ever hoped to kill Sekhet Bastet, and it seemed unlikely that an elderly doctor would be enough. After the events at the night club, he thought he knew of one, at least, among his meret who might help to put an end to her rampage. He met with Aquila in private, and asked her for her help. The Mesen-Nebu Guildmaster agreed that Bast was like a mad dog and that it would be safer, by far, if she were returned to henet as quickly as possible. Having her awake on a Sothic Turn was far too unpredictable, at least in future awakenings she would have a purpose to keep her attention away from causing indiscriminate harm.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the city, Sesu Ra visited Rekhenaten to deposit the Vestiges Akenakhi had discovered. He knew from observing Tobi fight that Rekhenaten had mastered the Dust Beneath Feet Utterance, and asked that Rekhenaten teach it to him. Rekhenaten agreed easily, and they began their studies.<br /> <br /> Bast remained in her tomb, meditating. She had organised a meeting with Yarikh to take place, along with Akenakhi. It was then that she found her mind moving back through the ages, to a strange vision of the world. She remembered walking through a thick fog, surrounded by a crowd of people whose features were blurred and impossible to make out. Words reached her mind. &quot;Do you fear the silence?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was silent, and it was terrible. It roared in her head, a raw and enormous void where sound should be. Neither the people nor her own footsteps made any noise. Even the voice had appeared in her head without passing through her She knew she was in a city, but it was impossible to tell which one. The silence was more than just the lack of noise, it was a lack of substance that permeated every aspect of this vision. <br /> <br /> As she walked, bright lights appeared in the fog around her, rising higher and higher until they met as arches above her head. Objects fractured and changed the closer she came, exploding into bizarre fractal patterns and shapes. Living people came apart, their skin peeling back and allowing her to see the five pillars of their souls woven into their flesh.<br /> <br /> Bast came to realise that she could not even perceive her own body. She seemed to be a disembodied consciousness, floating through the shadows. And then a man emerged from the darkness. He was a tall man, lean, with hard muscles visible beneath his skin. He had long red hair, although the shifting patterns of light in this place made it seem from time to time as if his skin were scaled, his hair a mane, his eyes yellow and slit like a serpent's. He approached Bast and gripped her chin, despite her lack of the body, to tilt her head back and stare into her eyes.<br /> <br /> The voice resounded in her head again, and Bast knew what she wanted to know. She asked about the Shah, and what she needed to do to return them to this world. The red-haired man smiled sadly, and told her that his beasts died a long time past, even their remains turned to dust on the wind. They had been stolen from the world by time. But they could yet be stolen back. There would be a time in this Sothic Turn when the stars above Jakarta would converge in such a way that the weave of time could be undone.<br /> <br /> The vision ended, and Bast awoke invigorated. When the time came, she went to meet Yarikh at the inner city cafe he had nominated as a meeting spot. She showed up early, before Akenakhi, and found Yarikh was already there. Eager to talk to him without the other Su-Menent looming over her shoulder, she sat down and launched right in. Her discussions with Yama-Het had suggested that her true purpose was to raise one of the Shah from the dead, and she wanted to know if Yarikh knew anything more about them, or about the process by which she could raise one. Specifically, she was hoping he could tell her about the stars, Sutek and if he could recall anything about the remains of a dead Shah.<br /> <br /> Yarikh's responses were careful and measured, and he told her that there wasn't much he could reveal beyond myths and rumours. The stars had been the province of the Lost Guild, according to legend, but the Artists were lost to history and he had never seen any evidence they existed in all his long descents. Sutek was the Nameless Serpent, responsible for Azar's death in Iremite's mythology, and had helped complete the ladder to Heaven. As for the Shah, he only knew that they were rumoured to have existed in the first Sothic Turn. He didn't know of any remains in Jakarta.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, accompanied by Aquila, showed up just as Yarikh was finishing, and Sekhet Bastet excused herself and left. The three remaining Arisen sat down, and Aquila began to chat amiably with Yarikh while Akenakhi struggled to work out how to get the information he wanted out of the other Mummy. He had just been informed that the cult had purchased the lease for the building where the textile market was. He felt reasonably sure that Yarikh's tomb was in there. He casually mentioned how impressed he'd been with the market during a lull in the conversation, but Yarikh's response was rather noncommittal. Akenakhi tried to provoke Yarikh in giving something away that would help his ambitions in undermining the other Su-Menent's influence in the area, but nothing much was forthcoming. They ended up parting ways without Akenakhi getting the information he was hoping for.<br /> <br /> Once they were alone again, Akenakhi briefed Aquila on how he had been progressing with his purpose. He explained that he was attempting to take control of Yarikh's territory and grow the influence of the cult there. Aquila didn't object to the plan, precisely, but she did suggest they try somewhere with less resistance first. They caught up to Sekhet Bastet and suggested they all head to the slum where Aquila had once worked as a volunteer for a health clinic. There had been rumours of fire spirits and other malevolent forces when she had last been there, and she was interested in investigating to see if she could enable Asa Corp to help the area against the frequent fires that caused so many fatalities in the area. On the mortal side, she began a long-term investment in establishing a group of volunteer firefighters while simultaneously trying to improve infrastructure, particularly electrical infrastructure, so that the spontaneous fires would be less frequent. On the mystical side of things, the three Arisen began to wander the streets looking for signs of the fire spirits they had heard of.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi chose to learn the Enlightened Senses affinity during this process, enabling him to see into Twilight and keep an eye out for the attackers. The group proceeded to the ruins left behind by the most recent fire. They found the large building was almost completely gutted, with several families still living in the ruins under makeshift shelters. Aquila had brought her Sadikh along, and it was Quil who found and alerted her to a strange patch of clean ground in the midst of an ash-filled room. This patch surrounded a small stone dog statue, something from a low quality ornamental garden. When Aquila touched it, flame leapt out and across her arm, burning her.<br /> <br /> Bast and Akenakhi caught up, and Akenakhi informed them that, to his new senses, there was clearly something inside the statue. Aquila needed no further prompting. She unleashed Harvest the Divine Flesh Tier 3, and struck it with the golden flail that Utterance provided. Flame struck back, struggling to break through the golden armour. When the statue finally shattered, corpus spiralled up to take the form of a girl of six or seven with a badly burned face. Aquila didn't hesitate. Before Akenakhi could protest, she seized the ghost and tore it apart.<br /> <br /> The two had a row over whether the ghost should have been reasoned with. Akenakhi pointed out that, had they waited for Sesu Ra, he could have used Chthonic Dominion to grant the Ghost Speech Numen. He was quite angry that Aquila hadn't even tried to avoid violence. Aquila replied that, had the ghost been the product of Words of Dead Hunger, which she thought likely, then it was a tortured soul and she had simply put it out of its misery. She said she and Quil would stay and stake out the place, in case someone came to retrieve the dog statue. If there was a sinister organisation behind this, it was possible that they had been using the ghost to burn down buildings, but they would need to come back for their tool now that the work was done. She sank into the earth using Dust Beneath Feet, while Quil set up a more mundane ambush.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi and Sekhet Bastet left, Akenakhi returning to his tomb, Bast heading out of the city as the sun set. She used the third tier of Secrets Ripped From Skies to ask the stars what her next step should be, but the stars were silent. Finally, she heard a discreet cough behind her. She turned to find a strange man standing behind her. His head was shaved bald, although patches of dark stubble were regrowing in a haphazard manner. He wore a fine silk shirt, white with golden chrysanthemums, that contrasted with his ragged jeans, poor quality sandals, and mud-stained toes. He wore a large satchel around his neck. The man introduced himself as the Prophet of Java, a servant of Fate. Bast asked him if he knew when the convergence of stars would be, the one spoken of in her vision that would allow her to step back in time to retrieve the body of one of the Shah. The Prophet sat down in the field and opened his satchel, pulling out a state-of-the-art laptop. He bade her sit next to him as he scanned through a variety of star maps, visions of the skies above Jakarta in the months yet to come. At last he stopped.<br /> <br /> &quot;This I can do for you,&quot; he told her. &quot;When the time comes, I will appear to you and we can undertake this journey. But there is something you must do for me, for the dictates of Fate itself. Retrieve the head of Apophis. Then this work can be done.&quot; And then the Prophet vanished.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra, meanwhile, decided to explore the tunnel he remembered creating in one of his older memories, the one leading to the resting place of Thothekmet. Its entrance was close to the National Monument, a long-sealed concrete tunnel. Dusty light bulbs lined the walls, but there was no electricity to power them. He lit his way with Chthonic Dominion, and came to a secret chamber buried beneath the monument. It was circular, with channels and grooves carved into the floor. These led into pipes that disappeared into the earth on every side. Suspended above the ground was Thothekmet himself, or at least his remains. He was pierced through by long spears, fixed to keep his limbs spreadeagled. Buried in his forehead was the golden chisel Sesu Ra remembered from his vision. As he watched, a single gleaming drop of honey-like liquid ran down the chisel and dripped into the bowl-like depression in the ground beneath him. It was filled with the same liquid, a rarefied form of Sekhem, and a slow, viscous trickle of the liquid ran down each channel to disappear into the pipes beyond. This, Sesu Ra recognised, was how he had created the foundation for his geometric network. Thothekmet seemed to be unaware and frozen in a state of limbo, if he was even still active. Sesu Ra left him there, idly wondering if the World's Wound could take the Mummy's place. He believed it would, but the ramifications for the Arisen and Shuankhsen of Jakarta were probably not worth contemplating.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet remembered that the creature calling itself the Coils of Apophis had made some cryptic comments about stars and light, and decided that the best place to go for advice regarding such things was the strange ghost in the Vault of Stars. She headed off to that abandoned slum, stepping between the pillars in the once-flooded hotel. As before, the world melted and ran like wax, and she found herself standing in a transparent sphere suspended in the void of space where the Earth should be. There was no sign of the ghost until Bast unleashed the first tier of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars. There she could see the ghost of a young woman, hard to discern against the backdrop of stars, whose body seemed to be made of the black vacuum of space filled with tiny pinpricks of light. The woman was curled up into a ball, hugging her knees, and did not respond at first to Bast's questions. When the name &quot;Apophis&quot; was mentioned, however, it caught her attention.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is one of the light's children,&quot; she said. &quot;I saw it come here, rippling through the void. It seeks to consume the light of the stars for its father, to feed until the Radiance overwhelms us all.&quot;<br /> <br /> At the same time, Akenakhi had decided he needed to assuage his conscience by making another attempt to apologise to the one he had sacrificed. He approached the Vault of Stars himself, not knowing of Bast's presence inside. He stepped across the threshold and froze. The two Arisen each demanded to know why the other was there, and neither of them were terribly forthcoming in their intentions. They were distracted, however, by the ghost speaking. It told them that if they wanted a glimpse of what was coming, they could step through the gates and see.<br /> <br /> This confused them at first. There were no features in the sphere in which they stood, let alone any gates. But Akenakhi, with the knowledge of Palace Knows Its Pharaoh in his mind, realised he could sense openings all around him. He unleashed the Utterance, leaving the destination up to Fate. Both of them felt the epic unleashing, and there was a moment of trepidation as they stood there. The portal was invisible physically, but they could each sense its outline. Akenakhi went first, stepping through. Bast hesitated on the threshold, but in the end her pride forced her across.<br /> <br /> They were somewhere very dark and very quiet. Their bodies moved strangely, not weightless, but certainly not as heavy as they were used to. They moved in the only direction that was distinct from any other, away from the portal and towards a soft greyish suggestion that light could be found on the other end. They could not see one another at first, and they found that any attempt to speak did not carry. It was about this point that they realised there was no air to breathe.<br /> <br /> Around the corner and they found themselves at the mouth of a cave. The vista beyond was not something they had ever seen, not in the six thousand years of their existence. It was a flat, dead world, pockmarked with craters. There were almost no shadows. It was hard to see. When they looked up they were blinded, and needed to seal the flesh to recover the use of their eyes. The sky itself seemed to be made of light. Only the very horizons seemed clear of it. Everywhere else they looked was an immense pillar, impossibly vast, like a star stretched out until it blotted out everything else.<br /> <br /> As they watched, the light seemed to... react. It pulsed and moved, and tendrils split away from its bulk and began to descend. These wisps of light or energy moved slowly, but deliberately. They began to converge on the cave where the Arisen were standing. Bast reacted first, summoning Secrets Ripped From Skies and hurling a meteor at the light. It was a powerful unleashing, but it was impossible for them to tell if it had any impact. At least, until the light expanded. A beam of energy tore through the planet they were standing on, and they were hurled violently as the ground came apart beneath their feet. Blasted, burned, and on the cusp of death, Akenakhi unleashed the second tier of Revelations of Smoke and Flame to fly back to the portal. Bast, in a similar situation, chose to use the second tier of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars. Akenakhi launched himself back into the cavern, dodging falling rocks and reaching the portal only moments ahead of a cave-in. Bast didn't even try to regain her footing. She stepped through broken angles to the nearest site of attuned geometry.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi landed back in the Vault of Stars. The flesh of his face was burned away, and it would be a long time before it healed. He waited for Bast to emerge, but she didn't. A small smile spread across his face as he contemplated the possibility that she was lost somewhere on the other side of the galaxy, trapped far away from Earth. But there was something more pressing. The ghost in here had attacked him the last time they met. If she did so now, he would die. He spread his arms wide and turned to her.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am at your mercy,&quot; he said.<br /> <br /> Bast, meanwhile, opened her eyes to a strange sight indeed. Her attempt to leap straight back to Earth had gone awry. She was lying on a bridge arching across a deep chasm. Two suns burned in a violet sky above. All around her was a city, but not one built by human hands. It stretched as far as her eyes could see, impossible architecture bending and twisting in complete disregard to the laws of physics. Cyclopean monoliths towered around her. She could feel the power contained within them. This was Irem writ large, she thought in awe.<br /> <br /> She followed the path she was standing upon, and descended into the depths of these aliens ruins. The city was still, without any sign of life. Whatever had created it seemed to have abandoned it, long ago. She walked through shadowed halls until she came to a great temple plaza, or something that greatly resembled one. There was still the matter of returning home, and she had no idea how to achieve this.<br /> <br /> The answer came to her. &quot;The Herald of Forgotten Stars&quot;. She wasn't sure where the thought had come from. It seemed nonsensical. It required help, other Arisen to create the Herald's body. Without a chorus it would be impossible to pronounce the being's true name to summon it, and even if she did, she was not sure how it could get her home. And yet the thought was insistent, and there was little else she could do. Within the shadows of that alien temple, she knelt and began to chant. Her voice echoed among the pillars, returning to her with distorted timbres and strange inflections. The sound swelled the longer she spoke, welling until it sounded like a thousand inhuman voices spoke with her in unison.<br /> <br /> And then the ritual was complete. Her body broke and twisted, and shadows welled from every side until the Herald rose up from among the peaks and spires of the strange city. Bast's consciousness was subsumed, but she felt the Herald step across the galaxy in a single fractured instance, tearing through time and space at unnatural angles. And then there was heat, and her memory dissipated.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, still in the Vault of Stars, witnessed her approach. A shifting monster of inhuman proportions appeared in the skies over Jakarta, becoming a burning star as it descended through the atmosphere. It flashed across in the city in a flaming arc, and struck the ground some miles away. Every Arisen in the city felt its presence and the waves of Sybaris that cascaded down from it.<br /> <br /> Bast regained consciousness alone in the middle of a large crater. She was near death, and had to force herself to her feet and return to the city on foot. She had no memory of her last moments as the Herald, but her time in the strange city was burned into her mind. She wondered if even the time's toll on her memory would be enough to erase it entirely.<br /> <br /> Back in the Vault of Stars, Akenakhi asked the ghost if there was anything he could do for her. Her response was a long time in coming.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stop the light. Stop it before it reaches us.&quot;<br /> <br /> A week passed as Akenakhi and Sekhet Bastet recovered from their injuries. Bast sacrificed a dot of Sekhem to speed up her healing, dropping to Sekhem 7, while the others all dropped to Sekhem 6. Aquila sent Tetasu Xex to dwell among Sem-Huf's cultists, materialising every now and then for momentary glimpses until their Willpower was gone. Towards the end of the week, she finally gave in to the urges of her purpose, and went to meet with Yama-Het to try and find out if there was a way the Sesha-Hebsu could be persuaded to give up the necklace. They largely rehashed the arguments from their last conversation, until Aquila asked Yama-Het's permission to deal with the organised crime problem in her area. If there was nothing for Rekhenaten to invest in, after all, there would be no point in continuing the conflict. Yama-Het gave her permission, and Aquila put her plan into action.<br /> <br /> She and Quil spent some time determining where the Preman in the area could be found. There was a local curry store that was quite popular with many of the higher ranking bosses, but Aquila didn't like the idea of striking somewhere so public. She also found that a building under construction in the area was frequently used by them for a variety of illicit activities. More specifically, it was the building Sesu Ra had invested in heavily when they had been hunting the Pelamat. She sent Tetasu Xex to haunt the place for a day, and then launched her attack close to midnight. There were only four men in the building. Alongside Quil, she emerged from the walls and drained the last of their Willpower. Allowing her darker self to take over, she used Rouse the Khaibit and then, methodically, slit the throats of each of the men. Quil watched, not having seen this part of his mistress before. When she stood up from her work she was smiling, the smile of a predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T20:38:41-07:00","id":646278,"title":"","content":"Session 46<br /> <br /> I know a couple of my players do visit this thread, so this first bit of the write-up is spoilered for those not involved.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As the days passed, Akenakhi felt the pressure on his mind growing. The strange vision of constellations and celestial movements he had received in the Vault of Stars weighed on him. He pursued studies of the night sky as his body recovered, noting how closely it mimicked the sight in his vision. At last, he knew where he needed to go.<br /> <br /> He wandered outside of the city one evening, following the path laid out by his vision. It led him to a rice paddy, an open field miles from Jakarta's outskirts. It was very quiet, and the stars shone bright in the clear sky.<br /> <br /> The moment arrived. He could sense nascent power in the air. Sekhem, like the presence of a relic, beat like a heartbeat throughout the surroundings. He could see no vessel, however, and had no idea how to proceed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your kind are blind,&quot; came a voice from behind him.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi turned around to find a man seated cross-legged on a nearby rock. He wore a white silk shirt decorated with golden flowers alongside ragged jeans.<br /> <br /> &quot;That may be true,&quot; Akenakhi allowed. &quot;What am I missing here?&quot;<br /> <br /> The strange man gestured towards the stars. &quot;There are wonders in this world that have been hidden from the servants of the Shan'iatu. Powers beyond that of text, amulet, uter, regia, and effigy. They are Fate's own wonders, hidden from those who have not possessed them. The Judges must not come by this power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi swore that the Judges would not get any power from him, and the strange man showed him what he needed to do, gave him a word he needed to pronounce. And then the man was gone, vanished into thin air.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi did as he was told. For a moment, as the last of the word passed his lips, he saw a glowing ball of hieroglyphs suspended in the air above his head. It broke apart and flowed into him, joining to his name. The sensation was not like anything he had ever experienced, and as he turned his eyes towards the heavens he felt a veil lifting from his sight. Were there more stars there now than there had been before?<br /> <br /> He had claimed his first Seba.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Bast and Sesu Ra came to an agreement to help Bast's burgeoning cult claim control of their old territory in the Thousand Islands. Since Last Dynasty International had apparently retreated from Jakarta, they did not expect the opposition to be fierce. With Kudama Jav in tow, they travelled out to the resort where they had first encountered the smuggling groups. Shortly after arriving, however, Bast recognised faces among the people at the resort. They had been employees with LDI. The two Arisen withdrew, apparently unnoticed, and sent Kudama to scout out the area and speak with the resort's owner.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Arisen took their boat around the island to find the smuggling dock they remembered being used nearby. They saw a much larger, sleeker motorboat heading in the same direction though, and stopped. The Arisen leapt into the ocean and proceeded along the ocean's bottom. What they found was a large operation, maybe twenty people in total, loading and offloading crates from the ship. They had their suspicions about the culprit even before Kudama, with a bit of surreptitious bribery, found out that a corporate sponsor had requested the discrete use of the land from the resort's owner. It looked like they had found an LDI base just outside of the city limits.<br /> <br /> The pair sat down to wait until nightfall, settling into the sand on the ocean floor. Towards the middle of the afternoon a second ship arrived at the dock, and the two Arisen sensed the presence of a nearby vessel. Sesu Ra made Bast wait long enough for the crew to disembark, and then they acted. Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, while Sesu Ra became a titan in stone with a combination of Blessed Is The God-King and Dust Beneath Feet. He loomed over the docks and summoned a blade of light and darkness to his hands.<br /> <br /> There were five men in total, one of them handcuffed to a long case which presumably contained the relic. Bast went straight for this man before anyone else could react, plunging her knife through his chest. He crumpled to the ground, and she had cut open a second man before anyone could react. The remaining men went for their guns. Sesu Ra brought his blade down, but he was in no rush to endanger his newly rebuilt Memory. The men watched in astonishment as their guns were cut apart. One man, out of Sesu Ra's reach, was able to open fire. Bast felt her body burn as the incendiary rounds ripped through her, spared from truly mortal wounds only by being slightly out of phase with reality. The two unarmed men fled, and she quickly killed the one who had the temerity to attack her. She passed her Degeneration check, putting her faith in Her-Uru, and it was rewarded with both success and a Descent reset.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra tore open the case. Inside they found an old, bronze gladius. Using the Model Lifeweb, Sesu Ra was able to conclusively identify it as Aquila's blade. He claimed it as a reward for helping Bast secure the area, which she willingly accepted. The two then retreated before reinforcements could converge on their position, giving themselves the breathing space needed to figure out their next move.<br /> <br /> They arrived back in Jakarta in time to receive an urgent message from Rom Mayehi, telling them that Asa Corp had been attacked. When they arrived they found that Reskan Lehn, a young cultist in the Lehn family, had been badly injured. He'd been standing guard outside Daryat's cell when he heard strange sounds coming from inside. When he went in to investigate, he'd found a tunnel running from the room and into the sewers. There were two women there helping Daryat escape. One of them he recognised as Yama-Het, the other he didn't know. She shot him in the leg and the three of them ran, the tunnel collapsing behind them.<br /> <br /> The meret weren't sure how to take this. Akenakhi argued that it didn't sound like Yama-Het's usual method, but Sesu Ra pointed out that it wasn't actually that far apart. No one had been killed, and she'd hardly been squeamish about violence in the past. The identity of the second woman was a puzzle. They retrieved a picture of her from security footage, but they couldn't match the glimpse they had of her face to anyone they knew. Bast idly floated the sensation that it might have been Aquila in disguise, having decided to whisk Daryat away and out of the reach of the rest of her meret. Although this idea wasn't given much serious consideration, it did catch the imagination of the others.<br /> <br /> Regardless, they needed to speak to Yama-Het about this. When they arrived, however, her cultists refused to allow them to see her. Bast grew quite angry at this, and loomed over the poor cultist on guard. In the end, he confessed that Yama-Het had returned to her tomb. It seemed that her descent had ended only hours before, and she now lay in the repose of <i>henet</i>. Sesu Ra shot down any suggestion that they wake her up purely to investigate, and the group returned to their respective tombs to meditate and think on events.<br /> <br /> Bast, at Sesu Ra's request, made a Kepher roll to try and help him track down a random Vestige somewhere in the city to help with the construction of his Geometric Network. She received a vision of a man named Idih, who looked like nothing more than a square brick of muscle, and the impression that the vessel she sought was somewhere in the fire-prone slum where Aquila did most of her charity work.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi, meanwhile, chose to follow up on Aulia. The damaged woman with a penchant for speaking in tongues was still being held by the cultists at Asa Corp, although a year's worth of help from psychologists had been unable to break through to her. When Akenakhi walked into her room, she greeted him happily in a babble of languages he didn't understand. When he asked after her health, she replied in a sentence that flowed from French to Iremite to Indonesian. &quot;Pretty bright lights in your eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi had a moment of inspiration then. Perhaps, with the help of one of his powers, he could free her mind and grant her a moment of clarity. He blessed her with the use of his Affinity.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Missionaries,&quot; she said, quivering with fear. &quot;The Missionaries of the Radiance, they're going to hurt us all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi wasted no time after that. He called his meret and requested they help him in tracking down the &quot;Missionaries of the Radiance&quot;, figuring that they must have something to do with the light they had been warned of. Bast and Sesu Ra had returned from their excursion into the Thousand Islands, and Bast remembered that Aulia had first been encountered in the area around her tomb. Akenakhi pursued legal channels, while Bast leveraged her cult's help in gathering word of mouth. Between them they found evidence of four others who had been afflicted in a similar way to Aulia, and all of them had something to do with a woman named Lia living on the edge of the slum.<br /> <br /> The Arisen decided to immediately confront this woman. They found Lia washing clothes in a tub in front of the hovel she had for a house. She was a petite old woman, but regarded them with confidence when they approached. They told her they knew she worshipped the Radiance, but Lia simply asked them mildly to leave. Akenakhi was able to persuade her to reveal a little of her allegiance, however. She confessed that yes, she did belong to the cult who worshipped the Radiance. She did so because its approach was inevitable, its hunger unquenchable, and that the Earth would be consumed in the end. She only wished to help feed it, sate it enough to delay the doom of this world long enough for her grandchildren to live and die. She did not say anything regarding the curse upon Aulia, and flat out refused to speak of any of the other members of her cult. The Arisen boasted that, between them, they had the strength to stop the Radiance, but Lia clearly didn't believe them. She gathered her washing and went inside, and Bast had to be restrained from going after her and beginning an interrogation. Instead, the Arisen decided to let Lia be, and see if they could come up with another way to get through to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-31-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T04:04:38-07:00","id":646509,"title":"","content":"Also, Akenakhi's new thing:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Sickle of Eternity (Cosmic Seba, 3 dot)<br /> <br /> Power: Decay is the order of the universe, yet Fate dictates that some things must remain inviolable. The Deathless themselves are examples of this, an act of sorcery preserving a fleeting mortal against the rigours of time. And yet Fate itself is not immune to the inevitably of destruction, and like all things it seeks to prevent its annihilation. This cosmic weapon is intended for its champion against the fouler Things That Must Not Be.<br /> This Seba can be activated at any time as an instant action. Stars appear in the sky behind the bearer, visible to them and those nearby. The light of these stars forms a mantle or halo behind the bearer, and collects in their hands in the form of a sickle.<br /> This blade is guided by the mind, not the body. Attacks roll Intelligence + Occult + 2, ignoring the target\u2019s armour. Attacks against Mummies do Aggravated damage as if they were made with a relic weapon, and the bearer is unaffected by target number increases. Attacks against enemies of Fate score successes on a 6 or more.<br /> <br /> Curse: Fate is inscrutable, and the bearer must struggle to work against its agenda. The bearer of this Seba gains successes on 10s when working towards an endeavour Fate does not approve of, whatever that may be. This occurs whether the Sickle is active or not.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:07:01-07:00","id":656113,"title":"","content":"Session 47<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet launched her assault on LDI's island hideaway. She had gathered several of her slum-dwelling cultists and her Sadikh, and Sesu Ra dispatched Luca to help her. They attacked in broad daylight, beginning with a meteor strike that blasted apart the boats and wharf on the island. There was a terrified exodus as unarmed men and women fled the small nest of buildings into the jungle, away from the attackers. The attackers were in a single small ship, driven by Kudama Jav, and were packed tightly together. When LDI did return fire, security men raking their boat with bullets, everyone aboard was caught in the crossfire. Riflemen opened up, concentrating their efforts on Luca and Sekhet Bastet, even as they each unleashed their Utterances. Luca grew to an enormous giant, while Sekhet Bastet revealed her demonic visage.<br /> <br /> Under the effects of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, Bast no longer had any need to worry about the bullets being poured into her body. She could, however, see into Twilight, and immediately noticed the two Greater Amkhata there. One, aloft in the skies above on falcon wings with a snarling lion's head, dove to attack her. In the moments before it struck she lashed out with her blessed knife, carving it apart in a single blow. Pieces of the Lifeless thing fell into the ocean in their wake. Seconds later she hurled a second meteor at one of the structures on the shore, silencing the riflemen there.<br /> <br /> They hit the shore. There were more than half a dozen LDI security guards, their bodies augmented and rendered immune to Sybaris. Some switched to flareguns and other incendiary ammunition in an effort to harm the spectral Bast, but it wasn't enough. She dispatched the second Amkhat in moments and tore into the men, tossing their bodies from side to side. Luca concentrated his fire on one particularly intransigent soldier camped behind the ruins of the wharf. In the end, Kudama Jav vaulted the barrier and laid the man out. Meanwhile, Bast's cultists charged into the fray with their shotguns and brought down two of the defenders.<br /> <br /> When the last man fell, the attackers were battered but alive. The encampment was on fire, and the bodies of the dead were strewn about. Bast took a moment to exult in her victory, and her faith in her Judge protected her Memory from harm. She ordered Kudama Jav to make preparations to secure the area, and was about to begin exploring for anything of interest, when she felt something terrible. Her Talisman had been removed from her tomb, robbing her of its strength.<br /> <br /> Back in Jakarta, Akenakhi and Jameela had been keeping a close eye on Bast's tomb. They waited for several hours after she left before making their move. Akenakhi carried several bags of sand into her tomb, while Imelda remained outside on watch. He scattered the sand around, and then transmuted it into gunpowder. He detected the presence of her many nearby relics and gathered them all into a bag, including Bast's Talisman, the Pale Brood.<br /> <br /> In the last few months, Bast's tomb had seen many new additions, expanding it and increasing its geometry. It was now possible for her to step across the intervening miles in a single moment. Unleashing Ancestry of Forgotten Stars again, she did so and appeared in her tomb, face to face with Akenakhi.<br /> <br /> Bast did not wait for explanations. She saw the desecration of her tomb, the theft of her Judge's property, and hurled herself at Akenakhi with a scream of rage. He burned his pillars to seal his flesh and reinforce his body, but her first blow almost tore him asunder despite his efforts. Scrambling backwards, Akenakhi summoned a sickle made of starlight to his hand. Bast was injured from her attack on LDI, he noted, and he hoped this blade would be enough to put her down. His first blow did leave a burning wound in her flesh, until Bast bulled into him and knocked him to the ground. With a single-minded focus she worked her knife through the flesh of his shoulder and tore his left arm, still holding the bag of relics, from his body.<br /> <br /> As Bast became aware of her surroundings, the smell of gunpowder filled her nostrils and almost overwhelmed her. It reminded her of previous lives in which she had seen the blasting powder in action, and hazy memories threatened to distract her. She left Akenakhi's body, damaged past the point of repair, and retreated with the precious relics a safe distance from the tomb. That was where she spotted Jameela.<br /> <br /> Akenakhi's body stirred. Still mobile thanks to the magic binding his body, he rose slowly to his feet and drew a lighter from his pocket. He dropped it at his feet and Bast's tomb was consumed in fire. A part of the tomb shuddered and collapsed, and every wall and edifice was scarred by the explosion. It wasn't enough to drop Akenakhi entirely, however. He walked burning from the tomb and stopped, staring at the tableau before him. Bast stood over Jameela's gutted body.<br /> <br /> The sickle returned to his hands, angel wings spread from his back, and Akenakhi descended on his fellow Arisen. Bast herself was forced to seal her flesh as Ancestry of Forgotten Stars flickered and expired. Akenakhi had nothing left to lose, doomed to a death cycle no matter the outcome of this fight. Bast was forced on the defensive, trying to stay alive until his magic failed. Nothing she tried seemed to stop the sickle in his hands. The blade fell with the inexorable force of Fate no matter how much strength she devoted to keeping it at bay, no matter what unleashings she used to protect herself from its edge.<br /> <br /> But it wasn't quite enough. Akenakhi's last dregs of magic fled his body and he crumpled to the ground. Bast still stood, badly wounded, but her body capable of repairing itself. She slowly placed her relics on the ground and looked towards her ravaged tomb. Her dazed mind slowly took in the scope of Akenakhi's treachery. Her canopic jars had been inside. Every single one had now been reduced to dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 09-09-2015, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T02:13:06-07:00","id":656276,"title":"","content":"I'm still upset that Jameela died. Should've really left her in the car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:47:38-07:00","id":657147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=656276#post656276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still upset that Jameela died. Should've really left her in the car.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Akenakhi is a traitor and an enemy against the Judges, he deserved to see her die really.. serves him right for working towards Apotheosis and making used of a cursed Seba lol. The tragedy is the loss of Bast's Canopic Jars, I was rather upset when I read that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:26:25-07:00","id":657175,"title":"","content":"Bast for Shuankhsen in 2015?<br /> <br /> Did I just hear the sound of an entire Nome dying in fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T12:40:43-07:00","id":658264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=657175#post657175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bast for Shuankhsen in 2015?<br /> <br /> Did I just hear the sound of an entire Nome dying in fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another reason why he's undeserving of the freedom of Apotheosis, if he ever deserved it. He's mad at Bast for killing people? She's violent yeah, but she works to glorify her Judge and by that logic she doing no wrong- simply being an exceptionally zealous Su-Menent. Akenakhi on the other hand has betrayed his people and his culture, attempted to steal a vast number or relics, devastated a fellow Arisen's tomb... not to mentioned has potentially damned Bastet to a fate far worse than being a servant of the Judges.<br /> <br /> He wants freedom, yet he's done something far more unspeakably cruel and evil in pretty much handing Bast to Ammut. I say he should be thrown into the Devourer's Jaws as well! Glory to Irem! lol.<br /> <br /> in all seriousness, you should jeopardize his chances of reaching Apotheosis, level the playing field as it were. makes it much more interesting than him getting away with destroying her tomb and her Jars by only suffering a death cycle ( though the loss of that Seba is a good start lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-09-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:50:50-07:00","id":658542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=658264#post658264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason why he's undeserving of the freedom of Apotheosis, if he ever deserved it. He's mad at Bast for killing people? She's violent yeah, but she works to glorify her Judge and by that logic she doing no wrong- simply being an exceptionally zealous Su-Menent. Akenakhi on the other hand has betrayed his people and his culture, attempted to steal a vast number or relics, devastated a fellow Arisen's tomb... not to mentioned has potentially damned Bastet to a fate far worse than being a servant of the Judges.<br /> <br /> He wants freedom, yet he's done something far more unspeakably cruel and evil in pretty much handing Bast to Ammut. I say he should be thrown into the Devourer's Jaws as well! Glory to Irem! lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the central dilemma Akenakhi has always faced is the question of how far he's willing to go for Apotheosis. Remember that time he had children burned alive for arcane secrets? Or that time he stabbed a slave to death for, well, much the same reason? He eventually came to the conclusion that he shouldn't hurt humans, but Bast, as a zealous Su-Menent, is probably his biggest obstacle to reaching Apotheosis at the moment. The inquisitor to his heretic, as it were.<br /> <br /> His actions aren't overly dissimilar to canon Arisen's quests for Apotheosis, I should point out. The sample Mummy adventure in the core book has a would-be seeker of Apotheosis slaughter his own cult, send gangsters to kill the cults of his rivals and steal their relics, and intended to abscond with their relics and use them to keep himself active until he could ascend. Akenakhi's plan was arguably more moral than that, since he didn't harm any of Bast's followers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=658264#post658264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in all seriousness, you should jeopardize his chances of reaching Apotheosis, level the playing field as it were. makes it much more interesting than him getting away with destroying her tomb and her Jars by only suffering a death cycle ( though the loss of that Seba is a good start lol)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fact that the <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Seba is functionally gone forever is probably enough punishment. He was Fate's chosen warrior against the Radiance. The Sickle of Eternity, as a cosmic Seba, would have waited a single scene to be reclaimed. Bast didn't have the requisite knowledge, so she couldn't pick it up. It would have subsequently launched off into space. It won't be back for several centuries, outside the scope of this chronicle, and even then it isn't likely to be Akenakhi who claims it. To quote one of my players, it's like Arthur losing Excalibur.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:27:52-07:00","id":658857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=658542#post658542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the central dilemma Akenakhi has always faced is the question of how far he's willing to go for Apotheosis. Remember that time he had children burned alive for arcane secrets? Or that time he stabbed a slave to death for, well, much the same reason? He eventually came to the conclusion that he shouldn't hurt humans, but Bast, as a zealous Su-Menent, is probably his biggest obstacle to reaching Apotheosis at the moment. The inquisitor to his heretic, as it were.<br /> <br /> His actions aren't overly dissimilar to canon Arisen's quests for Apotheosis, I should point out. The sample Mummy adventure in the core book has a would-be seeker of Apotheosis slaughter his own cult, send gangsters to kill the cults of his rivals and steal their relics, and intended to abscond with their relics and use them to keep himself active until he could ascend. Akenakhi's plan was arguably more moral than that, since he didn't harm any of Bast's followers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the fact that the <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Seba is functionally gone forever is probably enough punishment. He was Fate's chosen warrior against the Radiance. The Sickle of Eternity, as a cosmic Seba, would have waited a single scene to be reclaimed. Bast didn't have the requisite knowledge, so she couldn't pick it up. It would have subsequently launched off into space. It won't be back for several centuries, outside the scope of this chronicle, and even then it isn't likely to be Akenakhi who claims it. To quote one of my players, it's like Arthur losing Excalibur.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but destroying Bast's canopic Jars and trashing her tomb is just as immoral. Unless he was going to cannibalize the relics they could always be reclaimed, but there is no way to save her(Bast) soul from Ammut should she become a Shuankhsen. You may argue that losing the Seba is good enough punishment, I disagree. Cosmic Seba are still relics, and they are far less important pieces on the board than the Arisen and Deceived ( though they are safe from Ammut's hunger)- something the Judges and Temakhs both agree on ironically, such is their hatred for Ammut.<br /> <br /> But hey, if such a loss is considered equal to a player character's potential damnation, that's cool lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-09-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:03:36-07:00","id":658873,"title":"","content":"Wow, you're really passionate about this.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's far from just the Seba Akenakhi lost here - after this, I'd be surprised if Akenakhi wasn't being hunted by the entire Nome, likely blaming him for the Temple fiasco as well. This means is tomb is forfeit as well, as is his Meret (and by extension, possibly the secrets he has shared with one particular member of his Meret) and he now has extremely limited access to his cult, if any at all.<br /> Basically, he's gone ahead and lost everything again.<br /> <br /> Remember, though, the plan wasn't to damn Bast to Shuanksen-ness (although that was always a risk) but to remove her from the playing field until the next Sothic Turn. Remember, she did kill a lot of people, and NPCs have been damned for a lot less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:47:05-07:00","id":658903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=658873#post658873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, you're really passionate about this.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's far from just the Seba Akenakhi lost here - after this, I'd be surprised if Akenakhi wasn't being hunted by the entire Nome, likely blaming him for the Temple fiasco as well. This means is tomb is forfeit as well, as is his Meret (and by extension, possibly the secrets he has shared with one particular member of his Meret) and he now has extremely limited access to his cult, if any at all.<br /> Basically, he's gone ahead and lost everything again.<br /> <br /> Remember, though, the plan wasn't to damn Bast to Shuanksen-ness (although that was always a risk) but to remove her from the playing field until the next Sothic Turn. Remember, she did kill a lot of people, and NPCs have been damned for a lot less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's more I passionately despise pvp ( even if the players agree to it) than I dislike what was done, though it still was a horrendous thing to do from a mummy's perspective.<br /> <br /> And I know, though it doesn't matter what he intended, what he did is still unforgivable lol. And while losing &quot; everything&quot; is a problem, everything he lost in this nome doesn't mean his goals are too hindered, otherwise he wouldn't of taken this course of action. He was ready to make this sacrifice - hence why I believe his loss should be greater XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T22:19:15-07:00","id":658929,"title":"","content":"PvP has been an assumption of this game for a while, given the presence of the Deceived group running concurrently with it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't think I'm going to punish Akenakhi for his actions more than the natural consequences of those actions would allow. I think the story that is likely to evolve will be intriguing enough on its own merits without making it any harder for him.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, if Bast does become a Shuankhsen, there's a small part of me that would think it would immensely cathartic to see the carnage she might unleash on the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:20:54-07:00","id":659777,"title":"","content":"I'm curious: how are you dealing with the rift between the PCs? Does Bast's player duck out while Aquila and Akenahki scheme, or do they just sit and listen, but then act only on IC knowledge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:27:36-07:00","id":659784,"title":"","content":"It's usually just sit and listen and act only on IC knowledge, but we have had a few instances of getting the scheming done when the players of the rival characters are elsewhere (when, say, Akenakhi and Aquila show up early to a session). It hasn't been terribly consistent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:29:27-07:00","id":659881,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Akenakhi v Bast debate I feel there is one important question that needs to be addressed: At what point is flat out murder a virtue? <br /> <br /> Bast may have been following the will of her Judge and Akenakhi is not innocent from bringing merciless destruction down upon mortals. But at the end of the day one feels remorse for killing mortals and the other doesn't feel anything at all about the act. One regrets their last actions and wants to make amends and the other would even consider doing their past actions any other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:24:27-07:00","id":660026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=659881#post659881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the Akenakhi v Bast debate I feel there is one important question that needs to be addressed: At what point is flat out murder a virtue?<br /> <br /> Bast may have been following the will of her Judge and Akenakhi is not innocent from bringing merciless destruction down upon mortals. But at the end of the day one feels remorse for killing mortals and the other doesn't feel anything at all about the act. One regrets their last actions and wants to make amends and the other would even consider doing their past actions any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good point, though remember; they are a people who came from a time where murder simply wasn't frowned upon, especially if it was to glorify the Judges or Irem. Sacrifice was not just an necessity, it was honorable and just- a virtue that few others could match. And he may feel remorse and he's certainly free to do so, Bast is equally free to do what she does because from what she remembers of Irem and her culture at large, her killing of mortals isn't morally wrong because it's her sacred duty to the judges to perform such sacrifices. So to answer your question; flat out murder becomes virtuous if one's culture teaches that it is virtuous, cruel as that may seem - though that's a part of Mummy isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-10-2015, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T02:23:04-07:00","id":660530,"title":"","content":"<b>Korogra</b>, you do make a good point. However, that logic is a very slippery slope.<br /> <br /> The Judges and the culture of Irem adhered to very inhuman ideology. The Virtues of the Shan'niatu followed a morality that was fundamentally different from even the most bloody cultures in the real world. Claiming that the Mummies are exhemt from the mental weight of those acts due to their cultural heritage doesn't diminish the severity of said acts, for instance if one of the Arisen commited an act like that for little reason than because it was easy (which I remind you Bast has already done waaaay more times than I can count, and thus has like Memory 3 or 4) then it would be a breaking point for Memory. The fact that acting on the Judges behalf to negat the roll doesn't mean the act is just, only that the Arisen's masters use that reason to insentivise obediance. In fact I'm willing to argue that the reason Bast has any Memory left at all is entirely to the fact that some part of her still has human dreams and asparition very similar to Akenahki, because the sole &quot;Virtues&quot; of the Judges would leave any Mummy a 0 Memory shell of a being who obediantly serves their cosmic masters (which is the whole point I suppose.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Editing 09-11-2015, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:32:34-07:00","id":660610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=660530#post660530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Korogra</b>, you do make a good point. However, that logic is a very slippery slope.<br /> <br /> The Judges and the culture of Irem adhered to very inhuman ideology. The Virtues of the Shan'niatu followed a morality that was fundamentally different from even the most bloody cultures in the real world. Claiming that the Mummies are exhemt from the mental weight of those acts due to their cultural heritage doesn't diminish the severity of said acts, for instance if one of the Arisen commited an act like that for little reason than because it was easy (which I remind you Bast has already done waaaay more times than I can count, and thus has like Memory 3 or 4) then it would be a breaking point for Memory. The fact that acting on the Judges behalf to negat the roll doesn't mean the act is just, only that the Arisen's masters use that reason to insentivise obediance. In fact I'm willing to argue that the reason Bast has any Memory left at all is entirely to the fact that some part of her still has human dreams and asparition very similar to Akenahki, because the sole &quot;Virtues&quot; of the Judges would leave any Mummy a 0 Memory shell of a being who obediantly serves their cosmic masters (which is the whole point I suppose.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I argue that it's not all that slippery and is rather sound from a sociological standpoint, for better or worse. And you do have a point, but at the same time, the Shan'iatu ideology was no more inhuman than the religious practices of the peoples of Sumer, the Aztecs or the Mayans - all of which relied on human sacrifice as one of the highest acts of faith- again it's just an dark part of human history. And you are looking at things from our standpoint of morality, to many mummies it is just, and many callous mummies in canon have rather high Memory scores ( 4 or usually if I remember correctly), reflecting that either through faith or their cultural influence they are not overtly bothered by death or killing. Most mummies are fine with doing what needs to be done, it typically doesn't erode Memory that often from what I have seen/ experienced. Still like I said before it's perfectly fine for a mummy player character or NPC to be noticeably troubled by acts of violence or &quot;needless&quot; deaths for more compelling roleplaying opportunities ( as long as it doesn't risk pvp in my honest opinion)- it's just quite rare considering who the Arisen are.<br /> <br /> And of course there is something human left in her- it's what makes her so vicious and zealous lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-11-2015, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T13:19:18-07:00","id":661004,"title":"","content":"Good point, I'd only disagree in that even our most bloody human cultured truly believed that those sacrifices were necessary (albeit there were higher ups who used it as a means of population control but that's the nature of corruption in politics.) Even before the Storyteller section it's pretty clear that the Shan'niatu used the sacrifices of Irem to power their own ambitions. <br /> <br /> Other than that spot on analysis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:59:45-07:00","id":662418,"title":"","content":"Session 48<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra had been spending this time divining the location of Yama-Het's tomb. It was near one of the oldest buildings constructed under the area's gentrification area, in a small park containing a stone maze. Inside he found a staircase leading to a locked door. He ripped the lock out of the door and went inside.<br /> <br /> He was immediately assailed by a sense of dread, and had to force himself through. The curse lying on Yama-Het's resting place very nearly overwhelmed him, but he had just enough willpower to carry over the threshold. Once inside he found himself in a spartan room. In its centre was a tall stone pillar, covered in Iremite hieroglyphs. On the right were rows of locked safes. Sesu Ra activated Dust Beneath Feet Tier 1 in order to peer through the metal, and found them full of books. These books appeared to be centuries old in nature. Closest to the door was a safe containing video tapes, cassettes, and CDs. He figured they must be recordings of Yama-Het's descents.<br /> <br /> The pillar, meanwhile, turned out to be a description of Yama-Het's long crusade against the Shuankhsen. Nine separate hunts had been successfully concluded, each ending in the destruction of one of the Lifeless and the dissolution of their perverted cultists. Yama-Het's strategy was to transform her cultists into animal-headed warriors, allowing them to do the fighting without running the risk of feeding the Shuankhsen with her Sekhem. There seemed to have been five individual Shuankhsen, some of them had been destroyed multiple times. Sesu Ra noticed a mention of &quot;the Beast Who Is Fire&quot;, Iwseck, among the hieroglyphs.<br /> <br /> He continued through her tomb carefully, making sure not to disturb anything. The next room contained Yama-Het's vessels, each in an alcove positioned at a cardinal point in the room. The southernmost one was empty. He found the necklace he had come seeking there, as well as a quill he had seen Yama-Het use many times before, and a stone seal. Using the Model Lifeweb Affinity, he determined that the latter was a powerful Vestige with the Fetters of Temperance and Wrath, presumably conforming to Yama-Het's own Virtue and Vice. The necklace was called the Shield of Ptah and contained powerful protective magic, while Yama-Het's quill aided those who wielded in determining true names, and used that knowledge to spy upon them.<br /> <br /> Since Sesu Ra had no interest in facing off against a Sekhem 10 Yama-Het in the middle of her tomb, he withdrew before he accidentally triggered her awakening. He decided to pay a visit to Rekhenaten, and offered him a plan. He could guarantee that the local Preman would help against Yama-Het's cultists, the Sutra Watch, and he could make sure that they were unable to wake their mistress to defend them. Rekhenaten just needed to leverage his cult's formidable resources to wipe out Yama-Het's cult completely. The Master of the Pit, eager to see this stalemate end before his Descent finished, agreed eagerly.<br /> <br /> It didn't take long for the necessary preparations to be put into place. Rekhenaten used his considerable connections to ensure that the mortal police would be no obstacle. Sesu Ra sent Luca to persuade the Preman in the area that now was there time to take action. The two Tef-Aabhi sent their Sadikh, Tobi having been resurrected recently and in secret by his master, to the two most critical points. With the help of Dust Beneath Feet, Tobi hid in the basement of the Sutra Watch's community centre, their headquarters, to guard the secret tunnels there. Luca, meanwhile, hid within the maze leading to Yama-Het's tomb, using Dust Beneath Feet himself to spy through the walls and intercept anyone who came to awaken their mistress.<br /> <br /> According to official reports, a wave of criminal violence and rioting took place over the course of the day. The community centre was burned to the ground, and found to have failed to meet the fire safety code. Tragically, many of those inside, attending a meeting for a local community watch group, died in the flame. At the same time, several fatal muggings and assaults occurred, scattered over the course of the day. By the time night fell, the Sutra Watch was no more.<br /> <br /> Rekhenaten moved to consolidate his hold in the area. Sesu Ra had no problem with this. He sent Luca to retrieve a female body for him, and travelled out to the Thousand Islands with it. Luca had conspicuously little difficulty with the task assigned for him, and met his master there soon with the body of a beautiful local woman. Using the ritual he had learned from his memories, and sacrificing the Black Scorpion, Sesu Ra performed the Call to summon Iwseck back from Duat. He was nervous, wondering if she would return without memory and seek to devour him in her hunger, but that fear disappeared when he saw a brilliant smile spread across the dead woman's face.<br /> <br /> The two embraced, and Sesu Ra explained that he had delivered Yama-Het to her. He told Iwseck where to find the tomb of the Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster. He bade her go there and reclaim the Shield of Ptah for herself, kill Yama-Het, and consume her Canopic Jars. Leave her khat, however, so that Iwseck could devour her again and again for her Sekhem and pillars, and leave the other vessels for him. Iwseck had no problems with this, and after a quick kiss she was off to take her revenge on the Arisen who had hunted her down centuries before. Sesu Ra dropped to Sekhem 6 (effectively 7) due to his interaction with the Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> Luca was sent to watch how events panned out. He saw Iwseck enter Yama-Het's tomb, and then leave again a few minutes later. She looked bruised and injured, but clearly proud of herself. She carried a body presumabling containing what was left of Yama-Het's khat.<br /> <br /> Once the coast was clear, Sesu Ra entered the tomb. He found that the Shield of Ptah had been taken, Yama-Het's canopic jars and khat were gone, and that the safes full of her records had been melted to slag and ash. He found and took Yama-Het's quill, which he discovered was also a Talisman containing the first two tiers of a Sesha-Hebsu Guild Utterance, Inscriptions Upon Flesh. He also retrieved the Seal, which almost brought him to the total number of vestiges he needed to complete his Geomantic Network. He took the Seal to Rekhenaten and returned the Talisman to his tomb.<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastset remained near her tomb. She summoned her cultists and ordered them to set a watch on the surrounding slum. They were to prevent her meret, or any other Arisen, from entering the area without her express permission. Before they left to carry out their duties, she had them bring wood and oil, and burned Akenakhi's body before them.<br /> <br /> Aquila, meanwhile, was still haunting the building Sesu Ra had renovated for use by the Preman. Every time a group entered she would drop down on them, Harvest the Divine Flesh Tier 3 active, and slaughter them to the man. Those who tried to fight her were unable to harm her through the armour and their own fear. However, when one particularly large group filtered in, she overheard them talking about the destruction of the Sutra Watch's community centre. She wasn't able to get to all of the men as they fled, but she turned one man's legs to gold and interrogated him. He confessed that they had been given a list of names and addresses, and someone with a whole lot more influence than they had called off the police. The Sutra Watch was dead.<br /> <br /> Bast returned to Lia to find out more about the Radiance. Without Akenakhi to hold her back, this time she chose to go straight to the interrogation. She struck Lia across the face, but the woman seemed to melt away, fading out of reality. Even with the help of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, Bast found that she couldn't touch or harm the woman. Frustrated, she went to leave and found the Prophet of Java waiting for her.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Radiance bestows upon its followers blasphemous rites with which to sunder Fate's hold,&quot; the Prophet said gravely. When Bast asked what he was doing there, he told her that he had come to prepare her. She was one of the few willing to lead the fight against the light. There was a day coming where Fate's hold on the world would be weak, and the Radiance's servants would seek to tear reality asunder. The Coils of Apophis would be at their most arrogant on that day. She would have her chance to destroy it then.<br /> <br /> After this encounter, Bast decided that she needed to inform her meret of what had happened. Sesu Ra could not be reached, but she called Aquila and explained over the phone what had happened. Aquila pretended to be sympathetic. She suggested summoning Hetenatra to lay a judgement down on Akenakhi's actions, but privately she wanted the Lady of the Broken Stele awake to help her locate Yama-Het's tomb and return the Sesha-Hebsu Guildmaster to life so that they could deal with the attack on the Sutra Watch.<br /> <br /> On the way, Bast explained to Aquila what they had discovered about the Radiance, and the impending doom it represented for the world. Her mention of the Prophet of Java, an agent of Fate, greatly interested Aquila. She recalled what she had been told, long ago, by an old man. Fate would become mortal, and she would have a chance to break the never-ending cycle of failed revolution she had been condemned to.<br /> <br /> The two Arisen approached Imeni, one of Hetenatra's old cultists, and explained that they required Hetenatra to sit in judgement. She had set provisions in place for this occurrence, and he went immediately to perform the Call.<br /> <br /> Hetenatra emerged a short while later, her sahu withered from the strength of her Sekhem. Bast put forward her case against Akenakhi. By her count, he had broken two of the laws of the Diasporic Code, and may be guilty of a third. By striking at her tomb he had broken the Essence Law, and doing so without first seeking Sesha-Hebsu arbitration meant that he had broken the Spirit Law. He had also made her dangerously fragile in the process, close to becoming a Shuankhsen, so she asked Hetenatra consider him guilty of breaking the Shadow Law as well. Hetenatra gave these points due consideration, and agreed. By her judgement, Bast had the right, nay, the duty, to destroy Akenakhi's tomb in retaliation. In addition, every relic he possessed was now hers by right, and his right hand, the hand with which he had lifted a blade against her, was forfeit for the rest of his descent.<br /> <br /> Bast was ready to leave at this point, but Aquila brought up the attack on Yama-Het as needing Hetenatra's attention. Personally, Aquila believed Rekhenaten was responsible. His cult was by far the most powerful, and possibly the only one in the city with enough influence capable of ensuring the police did not get involved in such blatant assassinations. He was clearly taking advantage of Yama-Het's return to henet by breaking the stalemate. Hetenatra pointed out that there wasn't much to go on in that respect, and that in any case by acting through the Preman he had not clearly broken any laws of the Diasporic Code. Nevertheless, the reckless endangerment of her Guildmaster's ability to act in Jakarta was a problem. Without anyone to perform the Call, Yama-Het would not return until her tomb was disturbed or the next Sothic Turn occurred in some 1500 years. Aquila suggested she kepher Yama-Het's relic, the quill she was often seen carrying. Hetenatra had seen the relic before and, with her Sekhem as high as it was, bent her will towards locating it.<br /> <br /> The scarab's path was clear to her. She rolled an exceptional success. When she looked back at Bast and Aquila, her voice was subdued. &quot;This is disturbing,&quot; she said. &quot;The Unbending Spine has the quill.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bast's expression was first shocked, then devastated as the implications sunk in. Sesu Ra must have done to Yama-Het what Akenakhi had tried to do to her. Aquila felt something akin to a sense of triumph. She had always resented the Tef-Aabhi's Guildmaster's assumption of authority whenever the two were at odds, and now she had Bast on her side. She told Bast that they had to work together, they could only trust one another now. Bast asked that they wait before assaulting Sesu Ra\u2019s tomb, that they demand an explanation from him first, and then left to think on the matter.<br /> <br /> Aquila decided that she needed to prepare for the possibility of a fight against Sesu Ra. She used Silenced Utterance Vessel to store several of her combat Utterances, but she didn\u2019t feel it was enough. She had considered learning the Kiss of Apep for a while, but it seemed that of all the Arisen in the city, only Mot-Tan knew the Utterance to teach her. She decided to take advantage of all the confusion around Akenakhi\u2019s attack on Bast to send Quil into the area, intending to locate one of Mot-Tan\u2019s former cultists and extract knowledge of his tomb and how to summon him. Instead, Quil returned reporting his every effort had been blocked or intercepted by Bast\u2019s suddenly hyper-paranoid cultists.<br /> <br /> The only option appeared to be to fight fire with fire. Aquila called on those members of Asa Corp loyal to her personally, and dispatched them to do the task Quil had failed to perform. Unfortunately, with Bast\u2019s tomb nearby, her cultists proved too much of an obstacle for Asa Corp. It was worse than simple failure, however. A confrontation between the two groups spiralled into disaster, into violence, and the shocks sent reverberations back through the whole of Asa Corp. Its influence shrunk, dropping to Reach 2.<br /> <br /> Aquila knew how Bast\u2019s mind worked. She would take this event in the worst possible way. She rushed straight to Bast\u2019s tomb, only to be stopped at the edge of the slum by Bast\u2019s cultists. She was forced to wait there while a runner was sent to ask Bast what they should do with her. When he returned, close to an hour later, he instructed that Aquila be brought under escort to Bast\u2019s tomb.<br /> <br /> Bast was waiting outside, sitting cross-legged among the bodies of the men and women Asa Corp had sent to the area. Any hope that Bast might not have recognised them died at the look on her face. Aquila seated herself opposite and tried to explain her actions. She needed Mot-Tan\u2019s help, his knowledge, if she had any hope of overcoming Sesu Ra. Bast replied that the Maa-Kep would be a distraction they could ill-afford. At that, Aquila decided to take a risk.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat if he wasn\u2019t? What if I could make sure his descent was over quickly, and that the power that would have fuelled him could come to us instead?\u201d<br /> <br /> Bast\u2019s eyes narrowed as she considered what Aquila was suggesting. Aquila suggested that she might be able to locate an Amkhat, and use it to drain Mot-Tan to nothing once he had taught her what she needed to know. That Sekhem could be made to make the both of them stronger, which they might well need if the situation with Sesu Ra came to violence.<br /> <br /> Bast was horrified. Taming an Amkhat was the worst thing she had ever done, a blasphemy that still made her sick to contemplate. She had only done it because no other way to stop the creature could be found. What Aquila was suggesting was beyond the pale. She demanded that Aquila leave, immediately. The Mesen-Nebu Guildmaster did so, cursing the other Arisen for her stubbornness.<br /> <br /> Every member of her meret had betrayed her. Bast felt cold and very, very alone.<br /> <br /> She set her mind to the task she had been working on before all these events occurred. Her kepher had told her of a vessel on the other side of the city, in the slum where Aquila occasionally did medical work. She summoned Kudama Jav and went there on her own, seeking out the man Idrih she had witnessed in her vision.<br /> <br /> Her search led her to Block 94, a tenement building in the midst of the slum. It was well known among the locals as being a local Preman hideout, and Idrih appeared to live on the third floor. She located his room and knocked. He answered the door, a man who looked more like a cube of muscle wearing a singlet and cargo shorts. He stared at her for a long moment, and Bast demanded that he let her inside. She knew he had knowledge of an item of power, one not meant to be in the hands of mortals. At the word \u201cmortals\u201d Idrih gave a savage kind of smile, and welcomed her inside.<br /> <br /> There was a large slab of meat on his kitchen bend, beside an enormous meat cleaver. Bast had clearly interrupted him in the middle of something. Idrih said, in tones a lot more erudite than she would have expected from a man of his appearance, that he had heard of an item like the one she sought. However, he wanted something in return before he shared what he knew. A taste, just a morsel, of her divine flesh.<br /> <br /> Bast narrowed her eyes. She asked if Idrih knew of a group called the Faithful. He gave her an innocent smile and said that he had belonged to them once, but had left after a dispute involving his consumption of the hierarch. He had learned of the gods and spirits that walked among men from them, however, and he had partaken of the flesh of many beings. Never another Arisen, but he had consumed a chimera and many of those claimed by the souls of dead things who plagued this area.<br /> <br /> After some consideration, Bast sliced off a sliver of flesh from the ball of her thumb. She offered to him, saying she hoped for his help in the future. Idrih was amenable enough and quickly swallowed what she offered. He then explained that the Preman boss in this area, a man named Rahma, was known to wear a yellow pendant around his neck with strange properties. Rahma lived in an apartment at the top of this building.<br /> <br /> The three of them went there immediately. When they knocked on Rahma\u2019s door, they had a brief encounter with a guard. Bast\u2019s attempts to intimidate the man were unsuccessful, until a woman called him away to let her deal with the matter. The woman was beautiful, and introduced herself as Amia. She extracted Bast\u2019s name from her, but the Arisen steadfastly refused to discuss her business with anyone except Rahma. Finally, apparently from exasperation, Amia invited her inside and took her to see the Preman boss.<br /> <br /> They found Rahma passed out unconscious in a chair in a small living room. Track marks ran all the way up his arm. Bast saw the vessel, a vestige, gleaming on his chest, and realised that Amia was the real authority here. Amia said that the pendant had been very useful for her, making men extremely amenable to her preferred form of suggestions, and asked Bast what she could offer in return for what clearly interested her. Bast said that she had the power to make Amia the unquestioned leader here, without the need to rule through subjugated men. A master in her own right. Amia handed over the vestige with a smile.<br /> <br /> Bast\u2019s cult soon spread its influence into the area, rising to Grasp 3 in the process.<br /> <br /> Aquila had left Bast\u2019s presence feeling furious. She was approached on the edge of the slum by an old woman, sporting yellowing bruises on her face. The woman told her to stay close to her meret. Fate\u2019s time was ending, and the chance would come soon. There would be a day when the edges of reality would fray and the light\u2019s glory would spill into that world. On that day, they, the missionaries of the Radiance, would help Aquila claim the Prophet\u2019s head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:09:43-07:00","id":662426,"title":"","content":"Sesu Ra scored the following relics:<br /> <br /> The Shield of Ptah (2 dot Effigy)<br /> Size 1, Durability 3, Structure 4<br /> <br /> <i>The power of this necklace lies entirely within the small bronze representation of a shield. Its front is engraved with mystic wards invoking the protection of Ptah, the Nameless Bull, to turn aside harm. On its back is Iwseck\u2019s name, enclosed within a protective cartouche.</i><br /> <br /> Power: Once a scene, the bearer may invoke Ptah\u2019s protection as a reflexive action. The bearer rolls their Stamina + Composure. They are protected for a number of turns equal to their successes. This protection renders them completely immune to non-magical sources of damage for that many turns. Only attacks made with relics or Utterances may still harm the bearer.<br /> <br /> Curse: The Shield turns the damage aside, to the detriment of those around the bearer. For every attack that should have hurt the bearer, an ally or friend in the same area suffers the damage instead at the moment the damage is done.<br /> The Tef-Aabhi may pay a pillar point per attack to absorb these energies with the strength of their soul. By paying the pillar point they ensure that no harm comes to those around them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And:<br /> <br /> The Dark Truths \u2013 4 dot Text<br /> <br /> Powers: This quill has existed for centuries, passed down among occult sorcerers with an interest in Name Magic. Its creators have long since passed into myth. The bearer may learn many great secrets about the nature of the world with the use of this cursed quill, but the scales must always be balanced and they are doomed to lose as much knowledge as they gain. The bearer may ignore 3 different penalties when determining the target\u2019s true name. If the target is a Mummy, ignore the -5 penalty for that instead.<br /> If you know someone\u2019s true name, you can spend a point of Willpower to allow the quill to write on its own, held by your hand. It will describe what the target is doing.<br /> <br /> Curse: Whenever the text is used, the bearer loses their highest Mental Skill dot until the end of the next Chapter. Sesha-Hebsu are immune to this Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:08:38-07:00","id":663787,"title":"","content":"Poor Bast, you have to do something incredibly horrible to frighten a Su-Menent, who are universally fearless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:23:31-07:00","id":663797,"title":"","content":"&quot;Horrified&quot; in this context is probably closer to &quot;appalled&quot;. Not actually scared, but she did not appreciate what she was hearing in the slightest.<br /> <br /> That said, it had been a long day. Turned out everybody she thought she could trust were actually working against her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T23:04:18-07:00","id":665411,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I know odds are that anyone who reads Old Gods also reads its twin about the Deceived, but if you're wondering where Akenakhi got to...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/328717-jakarta-by-starlight-deceived-actual-play?p=663925#post663925\">He's right here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T21:30:45-07:00","id":672867,"title":"","content":"Session 49<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra now had everything he needed to complete his Geometric Network. The Vestige stolen from Yama-Het's tomb was the last piece he required, save for the head of the statue in Iwseck's possession. She called him shortly after their joint raid had been completed. She was so, so very pleased he had kept his side of the bargain, growing his Memory until he could recall the time they had spent together. Now, of course, she was going to follow through with her own side. She gave him an address, quite close to a local gem market, and asked him to meet her there.<br /> <br /> When Sesu Ra arrived, he found Iwseck waiting beside a large, unmarked truck. She beckoned him eagerly around to the back. It was dark in the car park, and she had to switch on the torch she was carrying to illuminate the interior. Sesu Ra could gaze upon his handiwork for the first time since his mortal life, Iwseck's stone-carved features looking back at him. He was about to set inside when something shifted in the dark.<br /> <br /> There was a rattle of chains, and a dark shape lunged at the pair of them. Iwseck stepped between the creature and Sesu Ra, snapping a single command at it in Iremite. It stopped just short, and Sesu Ra was able to examine it more closely. It had been a human male, but it was now badly decomposed. Its body was covered in lesions and tooth marks. Its eyes were blank and unfocussed, and it snapped its jaws in the air in a mindless test of the commands binding it. It took Sesu Ra a moment, but he finally recognised Rangarni beneath all the damage. Iwseck mentioned off-handily that she had needed some security for the statue when she wasn't around, and forcing Rangarni to commit acts that inevitably destroyed his mind and sanity had left her with a useful guard dog.<br /> <br /> This close to realising his project, Sesu Ra was all business. Iwseck put up a bit of a protest, wanting to be with him while he set the final elements of his dream into action, but Sesu Ra was reluctant to allow anyone to know the locations of the nodes in his network. He dropped Rangarni and her off at a place she nominated, and took the head to the heart of the city. There he carefully installed it beneath the National Monument, and felt his awareness of the city begin to expand. He carefully prepared the final hieroglyphs in the head's resting place. The original purpose of the network might have been to slow the descents of Arisen in the city, but it didn't take long for Sesu Ra to bend it to a different purpose. The entire network would funnel its energies into him, instead.<br /> <br /> He contacted Rekhenaten after that, ordering him to bring the Vestiges. It was time for the Tef-Aabhi to finally realise their decades long project. With much pomp and ceremony, Rekhenaten and his cultists conveyed the holy vessels to Sesu Ra. They travelled to each of the corners of the city, Sesu Ra carefully avoiding any revelations concerning the new purpose of the network. He made sure to proceed alone and on foot to each of the nodes once they were within a few city blocks. When he reached the Vault of the Stars, however, he made a startling discovery. The Vault's entrance was gone, and he could no longer enter it. It had not disturbed the geometric network he had created in the area, but the loss of the Vault was unnerving.<br /> <br /> Finally, the last Vestige was placed within the Tomb Tunnels in North Jakarta. Every Mummy in the city felt a wave of power flow out from the city's centre, along with an unaccountable sense of trespass. Sesu Ra had chosen to key the entire network to his tomb's Lifeweb, fuelling his own power. Jakarta itself had become his tomb.<br /> <br /> Elsewhere in the city, Bast was making preparations for a raid on Akenakhi's tomb. With the backing of Hetenatra, there was little chance any other Arisen in the city would disapprove of the action. Before she could set off, however, she witnessed the shooting stars filling the skies over Jakarta. The sight alarmed her, and she immediately decided to seek out mortal help with the situation. She had sent Kudama Jav to locate a useful astronomer a few days previously, a response to the sighting of a strange light in the skies above the city. Now seemed like a good time to call upon him.<br /> <br /> She sent Kudama Jav ahead of her and travelled to the University. The astronomer, a Professor Akihosomo was quite flustered at the strange spectacle playing out overhead, but he seemed to be unnerved by more than the shooting stars themselves. Bast, hardly renowned for her deft touch in social matters, effectively bullied him into revealing what was bothering him. He was feeling unaccountable pressure to go to a nearby lake, but he was baffled as to what connection this might have to the shooting stars. That this was connected, however, he had no doubt.<br /> <br /> Strange feelings and impulses could only be seen as a sign from Fate, Bast felt. She half-talked, half-dragged the astronomer to the edge of the nearby lake. His half-formed protests stopped the moment he arrived. He was staring at something in the middle distance, something Bast couldn't see. He muttered the word &quot;Beautiful&quot; beneath his breath and reached out to grasp at it. Bast, desperate for some way to perceive the occult phenomenon, manifested the Godsight affinity. She had a glimpse of glowing golden hieroglyphs streaming down Akihosomo's arm and into his chest before the light vanished. The professor's gaze then turned skyward and his expression grew both shocked and delighted.<br /> <br /> &quot;The sky is full of light,&quot; he said.<br /> <br /> It didn't take long before Bast had used the professor to work out what was happening. There was something happening, invisible to Arisen and most mortals, occurring in the sky alongside the shooting stars. It seemed to be concentrated in the city's north. She was still injured from her fights with LDI and Akenakhi, and reluctantly contacted Sesu Ra and Aquila for help.<br /> <br /> Kudama Jav drove them all, along with the increasingly confused Akihosomo, to the source of the lights. The three Arisen, together in one place for the first time since Sesu Ra's attack on Yama-Het and the debacle that had been Aquila's attempt to resurrect Mot-Tan, had a furious argument over the details of the matter. Sesu Ra admitted to having a part in the destruction of Yama-Het's cult, but claimed that he had salvaged her talisman from the ruins of her tomb after he witnessed a Shuankhsen entering it. When the others expressed their scepticism about the likelihood of such events, he pointed out that Gator had previously used the attack on Sem-Huf's tomb by Aquila's allies as a chance to feed. If he hadn't had Luca on guard, watching for any of Yama-Het's cultists who may have tried to summon her, then it's possible that the creature would have been able to carry out its blasphemous assault without any opposition at all.<br /> <br /> Neither Bast nor Aquila were particularly happy with this explanation, and Bast warned Sesu Ra that they would discuss this again once the current matter was dealt with. The rest of the trip passed in a furious silence. They met Quil and Luca once they reached the city's north, and Professor Akihosomo directed the group to a theme park on the edge of the city called the Dreamland. They reached it to find two Arisen, Mekshonat and Hetenatra, already there and contemplating the skies. Once Hetenatra was talked down from judging and sentencing Sesu Ra on the spot, she admitted that her use of Secrets Ripped From Skies had led her to this place. Sesu Ra called Rekhenaten, who wasn't far away, and told him to join them. And with that, every Arisen currently active in the city was in one place.<br /> <br /> The group wasn't sure how to proceed, however. A cursory overview of the Dreamlands told the Tef-Aabhi that the place had clearly been constructed by someone with a strange understanding of Iremite geometric principles. Rekhenaten spoke in haunted tones of the first Sothic Turn and the Priests of Iunu, and how they had built structures drawing power from the stars. As the others debated their best course of action, made more difficult by the fact that they couldn't even see the celestial event that was the cause of all this concern, Bast grew more and more impatient and more and more furious. Finally, she had enough. She called out to Fate with Secrets Ripped From Skies, and brought down an Epic Meteor Shower.<br /> <br /> When the earth stopped shaking and the smoke began to clear, the Arisen could see that Fate had made good use of the weapon handed to it by the impetuous Bast. The power of the Dreamlands had been completely disrupted. Every building with a trace of geometry about it was on fire or smashed by the waves of meteors. Bast, her faith as always in her Judge, did not even suffer any damage to her Memory for the innocents undoubtedly caught in the devastation. Professor Akihosomo, meanwhile, fled as the Sybaris overwhelmed him.<br /> <br /> It was fortunate that he did. The Arisen noticed something moving in one of the ruins, a shimmer in the air that suggested shapes reminiscent of coils and scales. It poured across the intervening space towards them, moving rapidly, and slammed into the midst of the Arisen with an explosion of fire. The Arisen were hurled backwards, and immediately moved to strike back. Bast charged first, trying to grapple the Coils of Apophis and hold them down for her allies to dispatch. Instead, she was lifted almost clear off the ground. Aquila armoured herself in stone and Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed Is The God-King, rushing to her aid. The other Arisen were more circumspect. Hetenatra couldn't unleash Secrets Ripped From Skies with the others so close to the creature, and Rekhenaten chose to simply quit the field. On low Sekhem and badly burned, he slipped beneath the surface of the ground rather than risk the end of his Descent. Only Mekshonat was able to contribute to the fight, unleashing the first tier of Revelations of Smoke and Flame and sending waves of burning ash to scour the Coils.<br /> <br /> Bast held on as long as she could, but everyone around the Coils could feel the strange gravities being exerted on her body. They grew stronger and stronger, shattering her bones and crushing her spine. It was as if she was being crushed and pulled at the same time. She struggled free of the Coils' grip and retreated, on the verge of death.<br /> <br /> The Coils then spoke directly to Aquila's mind, warning her that its quarrel was not with her. She demanded to know how she could be expected to work with a creature who sought the destruction of all life on Earth. The Coils tore into Sesu Ra, almost dropping him on the spot despite his augmented. With every blow the Coils suffered, the energies cascading from them appeared to grow stronger. It roared at Aquila, screaming words of denial tearing across the surface of her mind. All it wanted was to feed, and mortal life had no bearing one way or another on its whims or those of their master.<br /> <br /> The Arisen retreated then. It was clear that they were no match for the creature. Aquila and Sesu Ra each dropped into the ground with Dust Beneath Feet, and Sesu Ra sent Luca to pick Hetenatra up bodily and rush her away from the scene. Through his eyes he saw the Coils appear as if they were about to pursue, but instead they turned and rushed back towards the Dreamlands.<br /> <br /> The broken Bast sat slumped not far away, feeling her failure bite deep. And then the Prophet appeared beside her.<br /> <br /> &quot;Today is not the day I spoke of, the day of that beast's defeat,&quot; the Prophet said when Bast apologised for her failure. She would have her chance to kill it. But she needed to understand the creature. It fed upon Fate's wonders, the Prophet said, and gained much of its strength from them. If its meals could be poisoned, somehow, there was every chance it could be beaten. And something in the Prophet's words made Bast wonder. She knew enough of Egyptian Mythology to know that the Coils' namesake, Apep, was never depicted without another god to subjugate it. Perhaps a symbol of her Judge restraining the creature would grant her protection from its attacks. Despite the horrific damage done to her form, she felt better almost immediately. She now had a way to try and kill it, and she looked forward to the day she would get her chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T21:40:13-07:00","id":691984,"title":"","content":"Session 50<br /> <br /> Bast's injuries were severe, but she linked up with Luca and made sure to track down Professor Akihosomo in order to get him back to his home, safe and sound. The bloody and battered Mummy wasn't quite enough to snap the man out of his Sybaris-induced state, and Bast had neither the time nor the patience to be particularly gentle with him. Luckily, Aquila arrived on the scene not long afterwards and was able to coax the mortal into their car. Bast ordered her Sadikh to watch Akihosomo's apartment. The Radiance's children clearly desired whatever it was that he had touched, and she had no intention of letting her bait get away just yet.<br /> <br /> Once Akihosomo was secure, Aquila excused herself quietly. The attention of the city's Arisen was diverted, and she intended to use the opportunity to settle a score with Sem-Huf. The other Mesen-Nebu had remained in henet throughout all of this descent, so she figured it would be easy to get access to his tomb. She gathered her Amkhat, Tetasu Xex, and Quil, and they made their way through the city slums to locate the homes of Sem-Huf's lieutenants. None of them were in their homes. When she came to the apartment block containing Sem-Huf's tomb, she found that his cult was in an uproar. It seemed that they were aware of the multiple Epic unleashings that had occurred at the Ancol Dreamlands and were trying to decide if it was an event important enough to warrant the awakening of their master.<br /> <br /> Aquila didn't give them the time to decide. She sent Quil to create a diversion at the base of the building, luring away most of the guards, and then unleashed the third tier of Harvest the Divine Flesh. Sybaris overwhelmed the guards that remained, and she pushed past them into Sem-Huf's tomb. The first chamber was surprisingly subdued compared to what she was expecting, an antechamber with only a sparse scattering of decorations and a simple chair where the Arisen could sit in judgement. Behind it was a massive stone door sealed shut by an ornate lock. Examining it, Aquila figured she could easily create a key of her own, and transmuted one of the guards' weapons into the key. And with that, she entered Sem-Huf's inner sanctum.<br /> <br /> This was a tomb befitting one Born of Gold. From velvet drapes to golden statues, it was a place of opulence entirely out of place among the poverty of the surrounding slum. Aquila kept her anger in check as she approached the sarcophagus that lay in the centre of the room. Tetasu Xex manifested next to her, slithering along the floor, its bovine head almost on level with her shoulder. Aquila heaved off the lid and stared down at the dead khat within. And then the sleeping mummy's eyes opened.<br /> <br /> Magic lashed out at Aquila, trying to freeze her in place and turn her head to stone. She fended off the attack and watched as Sem-Huf's body turned to gold, matching her own body with an unleashing of Harvest the Divine Flesh. With a snarl she reached down and hauled him out of the sarcophagus, dimly noting that the spear entombed within him had been reforged into a relic. Tetasu joined the grapple, trying to feed off the newly woken Mummy's brimming Sekhem without success.<br /> <br /> Sem-Huf turned his attention to the Amkhat first. His spear blows rent the creature's flesh, while Aquila struggled to drain away Sem-Huf's will and render him unconscious. It had little effect on the Mummy. With her Lifeless servant almost dead, Aquila manifested a Bane Affinity in desperation and summoned a Chthonic Being.<br /> <br /> The creature appeared in Sem-Huf's tomb without warning, roaring and bellowing from its many mouths. It barrelled into Sem-Huf and ripped into his flesh, drawing his attention away from Tetasu. Clearly overwhelmed by the titanic creature, Sem-Huf unleashed the Power of Re. Aquila managed to avert her eyes just in time. When it was safe to look again, she could see a pile of ash on the ground where Tetasu had once been, and the Chthonic Being was retreating from the flames. Aquila had seen enough. Without the Amkhat to drain away Sem-Huf's Sekhem, there was little point to this venture. She fled as quickly as she could, vanishing into the walls of the building.<br /> <br /> Several days passed. Bast burned through a dot of Sekhem to speed up her healing, knowing that she would lose it to the descent shortly in any case. She dropped to Sekhem 6 (7). With Hetenatra's company she mounted a raid on Akenakhi's tomb, but found it empty save for some fake canopic jars. Frustrated, she returned to her cultists and her tomb to heal. Before she closed the doors to her tomb, she ordered her cultists to obtain for her a suit of armour and to cover it in depictions of her Judge, Her-Uru, subjugating snake-like creatures.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra received a request for a meeting from Mekshonat, the Maa-Kep Guildmaster. They met at an upmarket restaurant in the inner city, sitting in a private booth while they talked in Iremite. Mekshonat revealed that he had been approached by Hetenatra to aid in delivering her judgement on Sesu Ra. Hetenatra was very much aware that her position was precarious, with a weak cult and no Guildmates for support. She was trying to secure Bast and Yarikh to her cause as well, and the rest of the Su-Menent should they awake. According to Mekshonat, she simply wanted Yama-Het's relic returned. It was a mild judgement in deed, hardly more than lip service to the law, he pointed out as Sesu Ra grew indignant. Traditionally, Sesu Ra should have been forced to return all of the tomb's contents and forfeit something of his own on top of that, but Hetenatra was clearly aware that her authority was not all-encompassing. Through all this, Mekshonat did not make it entirely clear what his own position was on the matter, or whether he had actually agreed to help Hetenatra. The closest he came was simply stating that he wanted peace in the nome.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra tried to turn the discussion around. He claimed that he was willing to return Yama-Het's relic the moment its owner returned from henet. He was simply holding on to it for safe keeping, given that a Shuankhsen had been stalking its owner and that it clearly wasn't safe for it to stay in Yama-Het's tomb. Mekshonat agreed amiably, but said that it would make all the bystanders to this event feel easier if they could see Yama-Het's possessions given back to her guild. Or, at the very least, someone who hadn't been attacking her cultists moments before. It would alleviate worries that Sesu Ra may seek to &quot;save&quot; the relics of other Arisen in the city.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra walked out rather than respond.<br /> <br /> The days ticked past, and Bast's wounds began to heal. She had nearly returned to full strength when it happened. The sun set on the western horizon, and a light rose in the east that mimicked the dawn. The Arisen left their tombs and the people of Jakarta left their homes to see the evening sky grow brighter and brighter. And then it broke. Great fissures split the sky, the buildings, the people. The entire world seemed to fragment like a broken pane of glass. Mortals were frozen in place. The Arisen and their attendant supernatural creatures were still able to move, although they were certainly disorientated. Time seem to have come to a stop.<br /> <br /> Bast had emerged from her tomb in time to see the strange light. She was standing there, looking at the frozen people in the distance, when her cultists began to approach. They moved stiffly, like they were walking through treacle. They assembled in ordered ranks in front of her, and then Professor Akihosomo walked through the crowd and grasped her shoulders. &quot;The Coils are coming,&quot; he said in strangely accented Iremite, the timbre of his voice reminding her of something just on the edge of memory. &quot;You are our saviour. You must destroy it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bast called her meret to ask their help, pausing only a moment to wonder at the fact that phones were still working, and rushed to claim her armour. She had no time to question the strange appearance of the professor, or her cultists. By the time she returned, wearing armour adorned with hieroglyphs and artwork depicting Her-Uru crushing Apophis beneath his feet, her cultists had withdrawn to the edges of the graveyard around her tomb. Then, pooling from the nearby houses, came the Coils. Many of Bast's injuries from their past encounter still troubled her. For a moment she contemplated retreat, thinking she had little chance against the creature on her own. And yet, this day matched the Prophet's words exactly. The world had most certainly broken. She unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars and charged.<br /> <br /> The Coils came to meet her. There were no words from either of them. Bast's bone blade flicked into her hands and carved through the invisible, pulpy flesh of her nemesis. Its attacks in return were weak, paltry things. The violent energies that had nearly torn her apart in their last encounter seemed to melt against her armour, and where the creature's flesh made contact it steamed and hissed like it was being held to a brand. At the last, Bast tore the creature open and felt the unnatural energies settle about her like a mantle. It was dead.<br /> <br /> She turned back towards her cultists. Now that she could see into Neter-Khetet, she could see a creature standing among them. It was shrouded in corpus, its features impossible to discern, but it was unnaturally tall and thin and without any humanoid shape. Flagella spread from its body and rooted themselves in the heads of her cultists. As she stared, the cultists spoke in one voice in the same oddly flavoured Iremite she had heard Akihosomo use. &quot;We will keep your people safe. End this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Aquila arrived at the edges of Bast's slum, somewhat quicker than they should. The streets were impossible to navigate in vehicles, clogged as they were by frozen and broken cars. The strange geometry of the fractured world had allowed them to walk across the city very quickly, however, and they arrived to find Bast waiting for them. She said simply that she had killed the Coils, and asked them to follow her.<br /> <br /> The Arisen made for the light. It was clearly the source of whatever was happening. As they grew closer the fractures in the world's skein became more larger and more frequently, until they reached a point close to the shoreline where Earth ended and the void began. They stepped through and into the darkness beyond the light.<br /> <br /> They were inside a massive faraday cage made of criss-crossing beams of light. The exact scale was almost impossible to determine, changing from each angle and with every glance. At what was undisputedly its centre were two human beings, frozen in place. As the meret grew closer they recognised one of them as the Prophet of Java, but the other was unknown to them.<br /> <br /> A thundering, roaring sound suddenly filled the void. The meret looked up to see a helicopter had just entered the void. It circled around and landed on the darkness that formed the floor of the cage, and a group began to emerge. There were men and women dressed in combat gear befitting a special forces team, a small pack of mutant monstrosities that Sesu Ra recognised as products of Rekhenaten's experiments, and three beings who were clearly Deathless. Two of them were unknown to the Arisen. The third was Akenakhi.<br /> <br /> &quot;You!&quot; Bast's cry of rage echoed across the gap. Akenakhi didn't listen to her, however. He saw the Prophet and seemed to recognise that the man was in danger. He rushed towards the second man in the pair, unleashing Revelations of Smoke and Flame as he ran. His body vanished, consumed into a pillar of fire that arced across the intervening distance. The strange, unknown man's skin and flesh began to boil and blister, but he seemed unable to move or react to the assault.<br /> <br /> Aquila realised then what was happening. This was the day Lia had spoken of, when Fate would be vulnerable. Whoever the strange man was, he was the help promised to her by the cultists of the Radiance. And Akenakhi was trying to kill her help. She unleashed Harvest the Divine Flesh Tier 3 and closed the distance. Her flesh began to smoulder even through the layers of magic gold layered around her body, but she was able to reach into Twilight and deal a terrible blow to Akenakhi. Sesu Ra unleashed Blessed Is The God-King and Bast unleashed Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, preparing to go to the aid of their ally.<br /> <br /> At that point, one of the unknown Deathless moved. He was an odd-looking man, his features a bizarre composite as if he were composed of two different people. When he spoke though, his voice boomed with such authority that the warring Deathless checked their fighting. The fact that his words literally emerged from his mouth as fire certainly helped to catch their attention.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stop this!&quot;<br /> <br /> Akenakhi seemed to listen to the speaker. He backed away from Aquila, taking to the skies so that his fire would not harm anyone further. Aquila and Sesu Ra paused as well, but not Bast. She had come to the same realisation as Aquila, but had taken the opposite side. The Prophet had to be protected. She drew her knife and stepped behind the man Aquila had been trying to save. &quot;You have no authority here,&quot; she told the speaker, and cut the man's head from his shoulders.<br /> <br /> The cage shuddered. The Prophet could move again. To Aquila's despair he bowed his head, said, &quot;I am in your debt&quot; to Sekhet Bastet, and vanished.<br /> <br /> The strange Deathless was overcome with Fury. There was a moment when the chamber went absolutely still, and then the Deathless was gone. In his place was a titanic figure, a being robed in light and shadow. There was something about the figure that made every Arisen uneasy, but it was Sesu Ra, his memories closer to full restoration than any of his meret, who recognised the impossible nature of what they faced. A Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> &quot;Kneel before the Voice of Forever, Arisen!&quot; If the Deathless's voice had been impressive, this being's voice made the air tremble in its passing.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra thought of his wife, poisoned at the hands of the sorcerer-priests. He would not kneel. And the fight began.<br /> <br /> Luca and the armoured soldiers opened fire on one another, bullets criss-crossing the battlefield. Kudama Jav opened the Book of Dead Names and began to call up his spirits, while the second unknown Deathless opened his mouth and loosed half a dozen flaming spirits from his yawning maw. Akenakhi turned the Serpent Named upon Bast, using her true name to pull her soul from her body. Her khat crumpled to the ground, and her soul was assaulted by waves of spirits in Neter-Khetet. Just below him, Aquila summoned a second layer of armour with Dust Beneath Feet, the earth cascading through the rents in the void around them and attaching itself to her form. Mutants swarmed across the field and charged Kudama Jav, only to find Sesu Ra interposing himself between them and the pirate. He unleashed Blessed Is The God-King, and a blade of light and shadow carved the first of the creatures apart.<br /> <br /> The battle raged in the void and in Neter-Khetet. Aquila advanced on the Shan'iatu, a titan of stone and gold, and grappled it. She forfeited some of her oldest Affinities to be able to manifest Grip of Death, silencing the creature and preventing it from unleashing any Utterances. Then the second strange Deathless changed. Light exploded from his body, burning Bast's soul and forcing her back towards her body. A second Shan'iatu stood where he had been. Before Aquila could react, the new being named her. It pronounced the third tier of Rebuke the Vizier, and every enchantment was stripped from her. She tried to strike at it with her blows, but her fists passed straight through its body. She was bereft of her magic and alone in the face of its power. Quil, able to strike into Twilight thanks to his own unleashing of Harvest the Divine Flesh, charged the Shan'iatu she had been fighting. His blow did horrific damage to its form, shattering bone and tearing flesh apart with his fists of blessed gold, only to have the magic that allowed him to harm the creature torn from him a moment later with a second unleashing of Rebuke the Vizier.<br /> <br /> Luca and Sesu Ra had dispatched most of the attackers' forces that remained in the physical world, but the Pyrokinetic Ghosts had focussed on Sesu Ra and he was rapidly being consumed in fire. Sesu Ra unleashed Chthonic Dominion so that he could aid the battle in Twilight, and tried to turn an angel-winged ghost against its masters. The enchantment fell apart when he tried to lay it upon the creature, but he was able to wield it against some of the fire ghosts spawned from their silent attacker. The spirits turned on one another, and Aquila sacrificed another dot of Sekhem to throw a Chthonic Being into the fray. The Shan'iatu retaliated in turn, hurling meteors and blasts of fire from their mouths.<br /> <br /> The Arisen decided they were outmatched. They couldn't fight the Shan'iatu, the blessings allowing them to attack would be stripped from them as quickly as they could cast them and Sesu Ra was on the verge of death from the unrelenting waves of fire. They fled through the cracks in the void, returning to the material world. Bast's soul was forced back into her body as it sustained too much damage, and she woke in time to use Ancestry of Forgotten Stars to take herself, and Kudama Jav, straight back to her tomb. The Shan'iatu let them flee.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra and Aquila watched the cracks and rents in the world disappear, the light in the east fade, time resume its normal course. They were shaken, badly wounded, and spent.<br /> <br /> In her tomb, Bast found herself staring face to face with the Prophet of Java. He smiled at her, gripped either side of her head in his hands, and the two vanished from this time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T23:48:13-07:00","id":696821,"title":"","content":"Session 51<br /> <br /> Sekhet Bastet found herself on a road in the desert. She was alone, the Prophet of Java was nowhere in sight. The sun beat down overhead. Her path led East, winding through the red sand dunes. She had been walking for hours when she realised that she recognised this road. It had been used when Irem still stood. It was a path of the Empire.<br /> <br /> She heard the sounds of fighting coming from up ahead. When she crested the sand dune she saw a battle, two groups of men fighting. The men fought with wooden shields and spears, others with sickle-bladed khopesh. There were fifty or sixty men to each side, but this was not a battle fought by mortal men alone. The dead khat of mummies moved through the ranks, half a dozen of them at the head of the largest of the two armies. As Bast watched one broke the blade of a mortal fighter with its bare hands, then broke the terrified man's neck a moment later.<br /> <br /> Bast was content to watch the fighting at first, but then she spotted figures moving like sharks through the second army's ranks. Shuankhsen. Three of them fell upon one of the Arisen and tore it apart, and Bast could stand by no longer. She reached out with her magic and called down the Secrets Ripped From Skies. As flame consumed the group, she realised that she recognised one of them. The creature known as Gator. Before she could continue her bombardment, the Shuankhsen slipped beneath the desert sands and vanished. Their army broke and fled, pursued by the Arisen's forces.<br /> <br /> The Arisen themselves, however, converged on Bast. As she looked at their dry, desiccated bodies, she realised that there was something strange about them. Something she had never felt before. Something new.<br /> <br /> And that was it. These Arisen were new. Next to her, they were like babes still slick with afterbirth. They were newborn, and that told her everything she needed to know about when she was.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where are you from, stranger?&quot; one of the Arisen asked, its voice the sound of stones grinding together.<br /> <br /> Bast said that she was here on pilgrimage. The Arisen were awed by her display of power and asked her if she, too, had learned her arts at the feet of the Sha. At the mention of Sutek's Beast, Bast stiffened. She found out that the Shuankhsen had been trying to attack the Arisen here in order to get at the Sha. This meret had formed in order to defend the creature.<br /> <br /> The Arisen were happy enough to take Bast back to their camp. A small collection of huts and tents marked the site of the army's encampment, just a short march further up the road from the site of the battle. As Bast approached, she spotted a figure standing atop one of the taller sand dunes. It looked like a large canine, twin-scorpion tails rising above its head. A moment later, however, and the figure shimmered like a mirage and turned into a tall, North African man with reddish hair. She stiffened at the sight, and the words of her true purpose ran through her mind.<br /> <br /> <i>Fear the red-headed man. Exalt the Square-Eared Beast.</i><br /> <br /> The Arisen made a beeline straight for the red-headed man. As they grew nearer he looked out over the group and spoke in a soft, lilting voice, speaking Iremite with a strange accent. &quot;The battle is won. The Devourer's Hounds are at bay. Our lesson resumes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bast felt a sudden pressure from her Judge, and knew with a sudden certainty that her purpose was not to learn this lesson. She withdrew instead to a tent set aside for her among the soldiers, asking that the Sha join her there when the lesson was done.<br /> <br /> Later that night, the Sha entered the tent. It was in its canine form, watching her with eyes of lapis lazuli that left her feeling bare and naked. She asked its purpose, and it said that it had come out of the desert to teach the secret arts to Irem's diaspora. The Utterances, the words by which their cultists might raise them from henet, and other such secrets. Bast listened and felt regret, for she could remember the words of a strange version of one of Irem's oldest myths. It was not a version of the myth she could ever remember hearing before, but it seemed right for what she had to do. The myth spoke of Azar's exaltation by the mortal Aset, in which he was carved into 42 pieces and devoured over the course of 42 days and nights. She knew what she had to do.<br /> <br /> Bast lunged at the Sha before the creature could react, seizing it and silencing it before it could react. She plunged her knife into its chest and the blade lodged firm, the light died from the Sha's eyes. And then, slowly and carefully, Bast carved it into 42 pieces and devoured them.<br /> <br /> When she looked up, the Prophet was standing before her. His face was carefully neutral, no hint of his feelings apparent as he held out one hand to her. She reached up and grabbed it, and a moment later she was standing alone and in her tomb.<br /> <br /> Across the city, Sesu Ra had stumbled back into the world to find that time had resumed its normal course. He was badly injured, his flesh burned and torn and his skull showing through in places. That was almost as nothing next to the state of his mind. The presence of the Shan'iatu in Jakarta left him with only a single recourse.<br /> <br /> He'd returned to his tomb and retrieved his personal affects there when he received a call from Rom. The man sounded as if he was in pain. Asa Corp had been attacked. Rom wasn't sure who had done it or what had happened. One moment everything had been fine, and the next there was blood on the walls and dead bodies all around. He'd found himself lying against a wall, his ribs broken and blood matting his face. Sesu Ra ordered him to gather any surviving cultists and come to his tomb.<br /> <br /> There was another incoming call before he hung up. Rekhenaten. The Master of the Pit informed in a quiet, even voice that his cultists had been slaughtered. A creature like a strange, fleshy snake covered in blind eyes had rampaged through his home, slaughtering his people. Sesu Ra realised that this had been a city-wide attack on Arisen cults. He ordered Rekhenaten to contact as many of the others as he could, and then placed his head in his hands. A moment later, he called Iwseck.<br /> <br /> The phone call was short. They needed to meet. He had preparations to make. He gathered Yama-Het's talisman and his remaining vestige and brought them with him. When Iwseck joined him he ignored her shocked gasp at the state of him, cupped her head in his hands, and quickly told her everything she needed to know to raise him from henet. He handed her the vessels he was carrying to safeguard for him. Then he told her the location of his tomb, handed her Luca's key to work the lift, and left. He dropped to Sekhem 4, punished by his Judge for his continued failure to exact destruction upon the Lifeless.<br /> <br /> Finally, he went to Bast's tomb. Her cultists allowed him to pass through, Luca by his side. He told her what had happened and asked her to come with him to his tomb. Rom and the surviving members of Asa Corp would need to be assimilated with her cultists, one of the only functioning cults left in the city. Bast agreed, and didn't bat an eyelid when he said that Luca wouldn't be coming with them.<br /> <br /> The two Deathless went back to the city central. It was late at night when they pulled up near Sesu Ra's tomb. Besides Rom, there were fewer than a dozen cultists left alive. Ligo, Ami, and two of Pama Lehn's children were among the survivors. Bast began to make preparations for them, but Sesu Ra seemed distracted.<br /> <br /> Back at Bast's tomb, Luca was using Dust Beneath Feet and his prodigious skill at silent movement to evade notice as he crept towards her tomb. He gained entrance without anyone noticing, and quietly collected the World's Wound and the Heart of Sek-Bet from their respective alcoves, awaiting dispatch to Her-Uru. He fled the same way he had come.<br /> <br /> The business with their cultists resolved, Sesu Ra told Bast that he would be going into seclusion. Once she was gone, he went straight to the national monument, the heart of his geometric network. Luca met him there. They descended into the darkness beneath the monument, and Sesu Ra removed Thothekmet from his place in the heart of power. The other Mummy's corpse thudded to the ground and lay there, an inert khat. Sesu Ra then raised the World's Wound in its place. The bane relic's influence flooded the chamber, empowering Shuankhsen throughout Jakarta. The golden flow of Sekhem ended, replaced by viscous gore dripping from cracks and wounds in the ceiling. Sesu Ra left, his work complete.<br /> <br /> Once they had left the chamber, he turned to Luca and asked for the Heart of Sek-Bet. Once Sesu Ra had it in his hands, he released Luca from his service. The Sadikh dropped to the ground, his long-prevented death overwhelming him. As he died, however, Sesu Ra took the Heart and cracked open Luca's chest. The heart was then nestled inside. Luca gasped and his eyes opened. He was still undead, still immortal, but now he was free of Sesu Ra's service.<br /> <br /> &quot;Please sir, don't do this,&quot; Luca said. They both knew they weren't talking about Luca's position as Sadikh. He knew what Sesu Ra's plan was.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra ignored the request. Bast would be coming for her relics soon, and it would be in Luca's best interests if he was out of the country by then. Sesu Ra ordered Luca to leave him, to return to America or go wherever he wanted. Luca seemed on the verge of refusing, but Sesu Ra's final order seemed to have some remaining compulsion for him. And so the Unbending Spine watched the only man he had trusted in all his time in Jakarta walk away, into the dark and silent streets.<br /> <br /> That done, Sesu Ra returned to his tomb. He burned his remaining Sekhem, returning to the repose of henet for the last time.<br /> <br /> Across the city, Bast had noticed her missing relics. She made an immediate kepher roll and located Luca, heading towards the airport. She felt a wave of nausea. Had everyone betrayed her?<br /> <br /> Luca and Bast met in the streets near the airport. They saw one another at a distance and stopped, staring at one another. And then Luca continued on, walking towards her. He stopped when she ordered him to, and she asked him what his master had done.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just what he had to,&quot; was all Luca would say. &quot;He set me free.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bast stared at him. She knew the significance now of the Heart of Sek-Bet, which she could clearly sense inside his chest. The former Sadikh was evidently devastated by what had happened. She ordered him to leave, her voice cold. He would live on her time from now on. One day, she told him, she would come back for what he had stolen from her.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra felt his soul being called from his Judge's grip. He rose towards the living world, as he had so many times before. But something was wrong. There was a discordant note to the ritual. He felt his soul tremble, and then fall. He plunged into the darkest depths of Duat, into Ammut's own jaws. For a single moment he experienced darkness and pain, a moment that dragged on for an eternity. His five-fold soul was shattered and broken, torn apart by the Devourer's teeth. His mind buckled under the flood of pain, and he clung to the only thing he had left. Iwseck, and his need to keep her safe, to prevent the Shan'iatu from ever hurting her again.<br /> <br /> His eyes opened. He lifted his hands. Everything felt wrong, like a broken shadow of his previous descents. His body roared with power, the World's Wound's influence empowering him beyond what he had expected, but it was not enough to fill the gaping holes in the pillars of his soul. But there was a smell, a scent that he recognised. Iwseck.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra stepped from his sarcophagus as a newborn Shuankhsen, and into the arms of his lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T23:51:22-07:00","id":696822,"title":"","content":"And Bast's new relic:<br /> <br /> The Exalted Sha (5 dot Uter)<br /> <br /> This Uter consists of 42 fragments of mummified flesh and bone. Close examination will reveal that they appear to be from some kind of canine beast, but there are strange growths and bone structures that are unlike any animal, alive or dead. The bearer must consume these fragments to wield the power of the relic.<br /> <br /> Power: Only a mummy (Arisen, Shuankhsen, or Deceived) may benefit from this relic. Once consumed, they gain access to the following of the Sha\u2019s powers:<br /> -They can reflexively manifest the Sha\u2019s tail for the cost of a point of Willpower. This causes the twin-barbs of an enormous double-headed scorpion tail to sprout from their back. The tails are a 2L (2A against Mummies) brawl attack that injects the bearer with a mystic poison. From that point on the target suffers a damage roll of 8 minus the target\u2019s stamina at the start of each round. Successes do bashing damage. This effect continues until the target takes no damage from a roll.<br /> -They gain the ability to see through any magical disguise, enabling them to always see the true form of Sekhem-bearing beings.<br /> -The bearer may change their shape into a form that appears mortal to all extents and purposes. This mortal form is fixed and never changes, and appears like a red-haired man or woman of North African descent. Assuming this form is an instant action and costs a point of Willpower.<br /> -The bearer gains access to the Sha\u2019s Forgotten Lore, tapping into a primal channel to the Askhatic Record. The bearer may reflexively spend a point of Willpower to access knowledge of any Utterance of whose existence they are aware. This allows them to cast that Utterance as if it were one they knew. They lose access to the Utterance again at the end of the turn (although any enduring effects of the Utterance obviously remain).<br /> <br /> Curse: The bearer of the Exalted Sha is unable to conceal their nature, save by adopting the Sha\u2019s mortal form. So long as they bear this relic their Sahu cannot form properly, and they appear in their khat form to any onlookers. The Su-Menent have no special protection from this Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T16:51:35-07:00","id":730392,"title":"","content":"Session 52<br /> <br /> Iwseck had a present for her newly fallen lover. She led him from his old tomb to a rundown building in the city's south. There, locked away, was what remained of Yama-Het. She was still &quot;alive&quot;, but she was missing limbs and sported horrific wounds that would have killed any mortal. Sesu Ra paused at the threshold. He hadn't intended to personally assault an Arisen just yet. His newborn hunger was far too strong for any such principles, however, and the desire to regain his lost pillars overwhelmed any moral principles. He grew massive jaws and fell upon Yama-Het, devouring her in moments and restoring his Ka pillar to its former glory.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the city, Bast resolved to raise her Guildmaster and Aqhat to deal with the escalating war with the Radiance. It didn't take long to discover that the Batavian Maritime Banking and Insurance Firm, the face of Kotira's cult, had been one of the targets of the Radiance's attack on the Arisen cults. Bast turned to Yarikh for help, but the reclusive Su-Menent did not know the locations of the other's tombs nor the rituals by which they may be summoned. <br /> <br /> And so Bast turned to Mekshonat, asking him to raise his sister and use her connection to Kotira to bring back the Su-Menent Guildmaster. Mekshonat had no vessels with which to begin the process, however, so Bast sacrificed one of her Vestiges to raise Benerib.<br /> <br /> With Iwseck's guidance, Sesu Ra began to explore his new abilities. The ability to create Fasad was of particular interest to him, and he decided to seek out mortal fighters who could serve him as proxies. He decided to try for a backstreet martial arts school, locating one frequented by local gangs run by an Australian expat named Mark. He had leveraged Aquila's powers to obtain an enormous quantity of money for himself, and used it to persuade the men to demonstrate their abilities. Satisfied by their competence, he took each of the four best fighters, and Mark, aside and persuaded them to &quot;work&quot; for him. The moment their agreement was made he claimed their hearts and reduced them to Lifeless monsters, bound to his will, and ordered them out into the city to hunt. He sent them after Yarikh first, with orders to ambush the mummy if he ever appeared to be alone.<br /> <br /> Bast was busy organising a meeting of the city's Arisen. She deliberately snubbed the Tef-Aabhi, and Aquila couldn't be reached, but the rest of the city's Mummies were quick to gather. Mekshonat and Benerib arrived with the newly risen Kotira in tow. Sem-Huf and Hetenatra were not far behind, both of them brimming with power and scarred from battle. Even Yarikh made an appearance, although he did not speak much as Bast began her speech. The rambling monologue ranged from the betrayals she had suffered at the hands of each of her meret to the heresy perpetrated by the human followers of the Radiance, and the need of the Arisen to pool their remaining resources. Only Yarikh and Sem-Huf, and Bast of course, had been able to preserve their cults to any great degree. Mekshonat advocated fortifying a location so that the Arisen may support one another, and Kotira and Bast both demanded that said location be used as the foundation for a new temple. After some discussion, the isolated Thousand Islands were chosen from the site. The Arisen wanted a place where they could wield the most lethal of their powers without concern for the surrounding city.<br /> <br /> There was little time to prepare. The Arisen began to move their resources to the islands immediately. Yarikh and Sem-Huf were reluctant to completely abandon their cults' operations in the city, but they provided as much support as they felt they could spare. Mortal resources were useful, but Bast quickly realised that this would be a temple raised more through magic than hands alone.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra, on the other hand, was in the midst of a meeting of his own. Iwseck had confirmed that both Gator and Nenheta were active somewhere in the city, but she had yet to track them down. There were new Shuankhsen in the city as well, drawn by the corruption of the geometric network. She introduced Sesu Ra to a new arrival, Shaktib. The ancient creature had just arrived in Jakarta, its power ebbing, but drawn by the scent of power. It had taken lodgings in an airport hotel, and Sesu Ra and Iwseck met with it there. Shaktib was an unsettling creature, the features of an old man or woman merging with those of the child's corpse it wore to create a small, withered being with wrinkled hands and sagging skin. A dark, viscous liquid oozed from its chest and stained the clothes it wore, and it was attended by a silent Fasad swathed heavily in bandages.<br /> <br /> The newcomer and the new Shuankhsen eyed one another carefully throughout the conversation. Sesu Ra was newly fallen with a shattered soul, but Sekhem roared high in his veins. Shaktib was surely near the end of its descent, but possessed a soul built strong through feasting on Arisen prey. When Sesu Ra asked why the creature wished destruction upon the Arisen, it replied that the joy of being recognised, being feared, was the only feeling left to it.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra proposed a deal to divvy up the hunting rights in the city. Thothekmet's corpse was still at his disposal, and it had something they both wanted. If he provided it to Shaktib, the elder Shuankhsen could restore its Sekhem and leave the scraps for Sesu Ra so that he might feed on the Tef-Aabhi's pillars. Shaktib seemed to find this acceptable, and they parted ways to make the arrangements.<br /> <br /> A few days later, and Sesu Ra received a call from Shaktib. The ruined remains of an Arisen, almost unrecognisable. Sesu Ra didn't speak to his former subordinate, he simply devoured the last dregs of Sekhem and began to the process of building his Ren.<br /> <br /> The preparations being undertaken by the city's Arisen were almost complete. Before Bast herself left the city, she decided that she had to confront Sesu Ra about what he had done. He answered his phone, and she asked to meet somewhere on neutral ground. The two Mummies squared off, eyeing one another, and Bast demanded to know why her friend had betrayed her.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra claimed that there was power in the World's Wound that only he could use, power that she would never have let him use but that was necessary to defeat the Radiance. Bast declared that it was clearly too dangerous to wield the Bane Relic, that Sesu Ra himself must have known that if he hadn't even tried to ask her first. Their argued back at forth, almost on the edge of violence, before Bast told Sesu Ra that she would see judgement laid down upon him under the diasporic code. As she walked away, Sesu Ra called out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't stand in my way, Bast.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:50:41-08:00","id":748000,"title":"","content":"Session 53<br /> <br /> The new temple rose quickly on the secluded island, built with magic and the labour of undead slaves. Sem-Huf and Yarikh continued to make the trip to and from Jakarta, monitoring their cults and tombs, the rest of the city's Arisen had relocated to the island.<br /> <br /> On the mainland, Sesu Ra had used his understanding of the city's geometric webs to locate Hetenatra's and Yarikh's tombs. Since Yarikh had been active for more than a year, he believed the latter would be an easy target with little Sekhem to protect his pillars. He set his Fasad in place to ambush the Arisen. Days passed, but there was no sign of the Su-Menent.<br /> <br /> As the others made ready for the Radiance's onslaught and prepared their allies, Aquila sat despondent in self-imposed exile. Her every plan had failed. She could feel her mastery of her Guild's powers weaken as Sem-Huf made contact with Mesen-Nebu in other parts of the world and arranged for her to be removed as a Guildmaster. Everything she had touched had fallen into ruin.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra encountered another new Shuankhsen during his exploration of the area around Hetenatra's tomb. The creature was a nervous, twitchy young man named Kuuruuk, who proved to be extremely servile and offered himself up as Sesu Ra's slave at the earliest possible moment. Sesu Ra was well pleased with this, and ordered the newly arisen Shuankhsen to stand ready for the moment of the Radiance's attack. He intended to conscript all of the city's Shuankhsen to the defence of Jakarta.<br /> <br /> He then ordered his Fasad to return to him. He wielded Inscriptions Upon Flesh, gifting them with different Amkhata heads to better aid their efforts. Two were given falcon heads, to pierce magical disguises. Two were given jackal heads, so that they could track his enemies to their lairs. And Mark, the leader, was given the head of a lion to lead them into battle.<br /> <br /> This time, the hunt for Yarikh went a lot more smoothly. He had been shapeshifting whenever he entered or left his tomb, and the Fasad had been unable to recognise him as he walked through the streets around them. Now able to see his true form, they fell upon him the moment they saw that he was alone. As Sesu Ra feasted upon the Su-Menent's Sekhem, he was shocked to discover that Yarikh was not at the very end of his Descent. In fact, he still had plenty of Sekhem, more than enough to shield his pillars and deny Sesu Ra the prize he truly craved.<br /> <br /> Aquila's solitude was breached by Lia, the old woman they had encountered who served with the Radiance's cult. Lia said that, though their chance to destroy Fate itself had been lost, it was still possible to escape its grasp. The Radiance's influence could disrupt Fate's weaves and let them avoid the doom promised to each of them. She told Aquila that her eyes had been opened by the Radiance's new prophet. There was no need for it to destroy the world, it simply wanted to feed upon &quot;the light&quot;. Humanity could continue, oblivious, bathing in the Radiance's glow without ever realising that it had replaced the sun. If Aquila helped them, they could be free from fate. When Aquila appeared unmoved, Lia mentioned that Hakef, the creature she called Gator, was corralled and in a place where the Radiance's servants could easily manipulate him. If Aquila helped them, she could have control of her own enemy, bending his power towards her own objectives and whims. Aquila wavered, then snarled at Lia to leave her be.<br /> <br /> Bast had tried, repeatedly, to contact Aquila. The other Arisen refused to answer her phone, and there appeared to be no way to reach her or her Sadikh. In the end she gave up, and called upon Secrets Ripped From Skies to ask for a final piece of advice before the Radiance arrived. Fate warned her that the power that ran like veins beneath Jakarta's streets would be all the Radiance needed to reach through the void to the world.<br /> <br /> When the vision ended, leaving Bast feeling vaguely confused, she found that the Prophet was standing next to her. He took her by the hand, and a moment later they were standing next to Aquila. For a moment it looked as if Aquila were about to attack the Prophet, but then she seemed to shrug and turned back to her brooding. Bast seized her shoulders and tried to talk her out of the fugue, but to no avail. Aquila told Bast that they would be better off without her.<br /> <br /> At this, the Prophet spoke. He told Aquila that she was indeed doomed, as she had been told, but not by any higher cosmic order. Her fate was preordained because of who she was. She strove for good and worthy goals, time and again, but she would always fail because she lacked the strength of character to succeed. He told her that, time and again, she would always choose violence, becoming worse than the monsters she fought, never considering that her failures might be due to her own actions rather than that of a hostile universe. She was her own fate, he told her, and it was an ugly one.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're right,&quot; Aquila said, and she unleashed Dust Beneath Feet and fled deep into the earth. Down she plummeted, shedding her Sekhem as she did, until her body stopped frozen and inert in the darkness of the world.<br /> <br /> Bast stared down where her friend had once stood. She knew that Aquila would not be coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:23:45-08:00","id":748288,"title":"","content":"Session 54<br /> <br /> The temple was under attack. Kotira ordered the Su-Menent and Maa-Kep to join her in the central chamber. Bast joined her there, while the temple emptied of its defenders. The sounds of fighting carried to them, as Sem-Huf and Hetenatra lent their powers to aid the undead servants, ghosts, and mortal cultists who went forth to fight the Radiance's warriors.<br /> <br /> Standing in the chamber as the battle raged, Kotira began a low, dire chant. The name of the Herald of Forgotten Stars. Aqhat and Sekhet Bastet joined her as hierophants, Benerib and Mekshonat adding their strength as acolytes. The assembled Arisen spoke as the sounds of fighting grew closer and closer with every passing minute. And then it was done.<br /> <br /> The Herald's form left the Radiance's mortal followers dead and bleeding with nothing more than the sight of its fragmented, crawling form. They died in swathes and it fed upon their lives. Kudama Jav dragged an old woman, Lia, before the Herald and cut her throat, asking it what they needed to do to drive the Radiance back and keep it from the Earth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Seek the help of Irem's lost rulers. Aid the betrayed and betrayers in this fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> At that moment, the Radiance reached out and took Jakarta in its grasp. Sesu Ra was the first to realise that something had gone wrong. He felt something wrench and tear inside him as the geometric network was wrenched from his control and funnelled into the void. The power of Jakarta, the life and energy of tens of millions of souls and the city in which they lived, was bent towards its centre. Outside the city, the Herald turned its manifold gaze and could see the corruption leaking forth as light was twisted and changed, consumed by an unseen void in the midst of the city.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra stepped through fractured space to arrive at the heart of his geometric web, using the power of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars consumed from Yarikh's corpse. The Herald joined him moments later, its crawling chaos overwhelming the senses. They were standing at the foot of the national monument. Space was folded here with somewhere distant, somewhere impossibly cold. In the midst of this folded space was Nenheta.<br /> <br /> She looked at the horrors before her sadly. &quot;The Radiance will set me free,&quot; she told them. &quot;It will give me oblivion.&quot; And then she vanished into the cold and the dark.<br /> <br /> Sesu Ra charged after her without hesitation. The Herald though, seemed to pause on the threshold. Its eyes could pierce the frail dirt and concrete to see the chambers below, the chambers where the World's Wound pulsed in the midst of arcane geometry. But then the Herald wrenched itself away and followed the others through.<br /> <br /> They stood on the surface of a world of ice, its atmosphere frail and thin, cold beyond any comprehension. The pale light of the star they knew to be their sun gleamed in the sky, but so small that it was hardly bigger than any of the other stars in the cosmos. A part of Bast, buried deep within the Herald, knew this to be a planet on the outer edge of the solar system, the one called Pluto by modern men. <br /> <br /> The plain lay flat and bare around them, but Nenheta was nowhere in sight. In the distance they could see mountains of ice and nitrogen glaciers, while on their left rose a forest of dark spires. The spires were too regular to be natural, concentric rings rising to a peak at the very centre. It was the only way Nenheta could have gone. The Old Gods attacked.<br /> <br /> Light bloomed in the sky, throwing the shadowed plain into stark relief. A coruscating nimbus of colour marked the Radiance's arrival above their heads. It was too bright to look at, but even from the corners of their eyes they could see creatures moving amongst the light, descending towards them. The Radiance's children came to wipe these troubling undead from their parent's path. There were blind worms from the outer dark, creatures of light and shadow, horrors that defied all logic with their physiology and form.<br /> <br /> One such worm slammed into Sesu Ra. He fought back with tooth and fist. The two struggled back and forth, but fuelled by all the Sekhem he had consumed there was little hope for the alien being. He tore it apart and looked up, to find that the Herald had carved a terrible swathe through the attacking demons with little pause. The mixed forms of Bast and Aqhat, empowered by their union with so many other Arisen, could not be stopped. The children of the Radiance met their doom at the broken limbs of the Herald in amongst the spires.<br /> <br /> But the waves of creatures were never-ending, and the Herald would not be long for this world. The worms poured down in waves. Then they felt Sekhem flare around them, and other Arisen began to join the battle. Sesu Ra watched as Sem-Huf charged a creature moments before it could cut him off from a path to the central spire, pinning the creature to the ground with a flaming spear. Meteors began to run down, smiting horrors from the sky before they could reach the Arisen, as Hetenatra added her might to the attack. And Sesu Ra watched with pleasure as Kuuruuk and Shabtisk joined the fight, watched over by Iwseck, her identity disguised with a relic stolen from Aquila's tomb.<br /> <br /> The Herald reached the central spire, rending apart the creatures that assailed it. There was still no sign of Nenheta. As its eyes surveyed the battle, it saw a man it recognised approaching. One of the Deceived. The one who bore the Shan'iatu called Siranuthis made his way through the spires from the opposite direction to the way the Arisen had come, and began to ascend the spire. Demons attacked him, but the Herald recognised an ally and destroyed them. He reached the top and looked up towards the light, and began to sing. Despite the poorly lacking atmosphere, every being present could hear the song. The Radiance certainly did, and it struck.<br /> <br /> Nenheta flickered in and out among the spires, striking at the Arisen and Deceived in equal measure, gone before they could attack back. The Shan'iatu named Tutkepertanu appeared among the pillars and moved to defend the other Deceived. An enormous creature like a fleshy snake struck at Sesu Ra, splaying its body open like a cobra's hood to reveal dozens of milky white eyes, trying to compel him to turn on his allies. The Unbending Spine refused to give in to the creature's overwhelming power and struck back, his fists tearing gaping wounds in its form.<br /> <br /> Above the battlefield, a woman with a snake's head, composed entirely from stars, tore at a winged being with flaming wings. The Herald recognised Akenakhi writing in the woman's grip. As tempting as it was to let him die, the Herald struck and tore the woman apart before she could finish him off.<br /> <br /> A great tower of basalt began to grow from the snow, Chthonic Beings appearing en masse in its shadow. They raged across the battlefield, striking mostly at the far more numerous demons, the various mummies scrambling to stay out of their way.<br /> <br /> There was a surge of power in the centre of the battlefield, where the will of the Deceived was pitted against that of a star god. A creature of towering flame appeared, bow in hand, and began to smite any creatures that dared to try and approach those on the central spire. Flaming bolts rained down upon the battlefield, destroying a demon with every shot.<br /> <br /> Slowly, the Deathless and Lifeless fighters alike began to form a circle around the central spire. Back to back, they fought off waves of the Radiance's children. Tutkepertanu hurled a meteor and obliterated the blind-eyed snake. Nenheta threw herself at the Deceived, seeking to break their concentration and disrupt their ritual, but as she charged towards the singing Deathless she was seized by the throat by the being of fire that stood by their side. For a moment she struggled in its grip, and then she was gone in a flash of flame.<br /> <br /> There was a moment of pause as the light blazed brighter and brighter in the sky. The Sesu Ra felt his eyeballs began to boil in his skull. And then the moment passed, and the Radiance began to pour down out of the sky and into the chest of the Deceived. And then everything was dark and still.<br /> <br /> Everything, that is, save for the glorious creature of fire and magic. It turned its bow upon the Shuankhsen without a moment's pause. Kuuruuk was blasted to pieces before he even realised the fighting was not yet done. Shabtisk turned to flee, but the Herald was upon him before he could reach the portal. Sesu Ra went to run, only to watch the Herald tear across space towards the earth. He and Iwseck followed its path through Twilight, appearing back on Earth in Bast's tomb, staring at the Herald.<br /> <br /> The creature only had moments left before it separated into its component parts, but those moments would be more than enough to destroy him. Sesu Ra knew that if he fought, Iwseck would fight too, and they both would die. With the mask she was wearing though, there was a strong chance she would be mistaken for Aquila. He fell to his knees before the Herald.<br /> <br /> &quot;I accept your judgement.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Herald tore him apart, and the spell ended. Bast took Yama-Het's Talisman from his corpse. She spared a moment for Iwseck, thanking the woman she thought was Aquila for coming to her senses, and then rushed back to the national monument. She remembered the chamber she had seen as the Herald, and found its entrance. There, at its centre, was the World's Wound. This time, she would not make the mistake of trying to keep it safe. She summoned the bladed tail of the Exalted Sha, and destroyed the Bane Uter where it lay.<br /> <br /> By the time she returned to her tomb, Sesu Ra's corpse had vanished. She made her way back to the island temple, took a seat at its centre, and began to meditate. She was not left to her solitude for long. An explosion rocked the temple, and she dragged her weary self up to do battle once more.<br /> <br /> A helicopter hovered over the island, raining down fire. The Shan'iatu Siranuthis stood aboard, howling fire and blasphemy as he swore that he would drive the last Arisen from Jakarta. Bast summoned a meteor to strike him from the sky, but he dispelled the Utterance with a lazy gesture. Then Aqhat appeared beside her, vomiting forth a horde of scarabs. They flew into the helicopter and devoured its pilot's eyes, and the howling Shan'iatu descend in flames. It strode from the wreckage unharmed, hurling fire and spells. Sekhem flared as the two warriors of the Su-Menent charged into battle. They fought magic with axe and scorpion tail, and for the first time Siranuthis found himself wounded and bleeding and on the verge of defeat. He summoned flaming wings and ascended out of their reach, still hurling spells down upon their heads. Bast joined him in the air with wings of her own summoned through the Exalted Sha. As the two angels warred, immortal blood raining down on the beach below, the Shan'iatu realised he could not win this fight. His body scattered into sand, taking himself beyond Bast's reach.<br /> <br /> The temple still stood, damaged but not broken, not defiled by a heretic's presence. Only those Arisen who had been part of the Herald had returned from Pluto's surface. Mekshonat, Benerib, Kotira Nahan, Aqhat, and Sekhet Bastet. Where the other guilds had fallen or failed, the Su-Menent and their closest allies stood triumphant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:47:27-08:00","id":748314,"title":"","content":"Epilogue<br /> <br /> By the end of 2013, the nome of Jakarta lay in ruins. The city itself lay in the grip of the Deceived, the dark empire of their cult spreading through the halls of power and driving the Arisen away from any power or influence. The mummies of the city had seen their cults shattered, and those that remained existed only among the poor and deprived, the criminals and outcasts. They had fallen far.<br /> <br /> The Sesha-Hebsu and Mesen-Nebu have no presence in the city. Hetenatra and Sem-Huf were trapped on the frozen surface of a distant planet at the battle's end. When their descents ended, there was a chance that their cults could return them to Earth by raising them through their canopic jars. Nevertheless, they have not been seen since the Radiance was vanquished.<br /> <br /> Of the Tef-Aabhi, only Sesu Ra remains. He still plays the role of Guildmaster, although he has little influence among the other Arisen. Bast refuses to trust him and takes efforts to stymie his efforts to return himself to influence. For his part, he chooses to endure this exile, knowing that in time the others' memories will fail and that he will have his chance to move among them once more, a wolf in disguise. The Deceived remain his focus, and he does what he can to coordinate both Shuankhsen and Arisen against them. Thus far, this has had little impact.<br /> <br /> Benerib and Mekshonat have declared the Maa-Kep's support for the Su-Menent cause. Like the other Arisen of the Nome, they have made new tombs around the island temple, and have begun to build local cults to support them in future descents.<br /> <br /> Kotira, Aqhat, and Bast of the Su-Menent rule from their temple island. They have been forced from their city, but their fortress has stood against the might of the Deceived and their mystical might is singularly capable of defeating their opponents in open battle. While the Deceived rule their empire, the Su-Menent plot in their temple and lay the foundations for a great crusade, a bloody campaign to take back what they have lost.<br /> <br /> In the alleys and slums of the city, feral packs of Shuankhsen and Fasad hunt those Mummies they can find. Drawn to the city by the promised power of Sesu Ra's corrupted geometric network, they are now bereft of that strength and forced into the shadows by the Deceived. Reduced from a ravening horde to a pack of scavengers, they watch the warring deathless from the darkness and wait for their chance in the conflict that is bound to come.<br /> <br /> And somewhere in the dark of the world, a new Shuankhsen is being born. One without memory, with no knowledge of who she was, just a hunger in her soul and the barest memories of a name. &quot;Aquila&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:56:53-08:00","id":748322,"title":"","content":"And that's a wrap everyone! The Deceived perspective on the finale will go up sometime in the next few days, but those are the events as witnessed by the Arisen (well, Arisen and a Shuankhsen). A bit of a bitter ending for the Old Gods, with the meret completely fragmented, but it was a pretty impressive self-destruct at the very least.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any comments, queries, or criticisms about the finale or the whole of the campaign, I'm more than happy to answer them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:18:26-08:00","id":749113,"title":"","content":"(Standing ovation!)<br /> <br /> All things considered, that went waaaaay better that I certainly thought it would. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Feel really bad for Aquila though, in the end I feel she turned out alright...save for the whole Shuanhksen thing. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T11:49:09-08:00","id":749618,"title":"","content":"Well that was one heck of an ending. It's too bad Aquila was so deep in brooding she failed to notice the lifeline Fate had thrown her. Sesu Ra probably performed his noblest action since becoming Shuanhksen in sacrificing himself to protect Iwseck, even if self-sacrifice via death is less meaningful to the Deathless/Lifeless and is really just a slap on the wrist. Bast came across as almost <i>human</i> this time around, which after a long stretch as basically a relentless murder-machine of a zealot is pretty jarring. MPV of this whole thing probably goes to the Herald of the Forgotten Stars, though we have yet to see what the Deceived have done, and it appears as though they weren't exactly slouches either.<br /> <br /> Can't say I'm displeased with the Deceived ending up rulers of Jakarta, but on the other hand I'm strangely proud of the Su-Menent and Bast in particular for holding on. I find myself wondering what sort of powers are at the disposal of the Deceived, seeing as we haven't really seen character sheets, since when they are in full Shan'iatu mode they have access to many more Utterances, but it certainly seems like a significant amount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T15:00:12-08:00","id":750163,"title":"","content":"Actually getting to use the Herald in a fight for the first time in the chronicle (remember that Bast has been carrying the Utterance around all campaign) was incredible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's so logistically difficult to pull off, but it was great to get that payoff at last.<br /> <br /> Aquila was a bit frustrating given that she was presented with multiple opportunities to get involved in the finale, but ultimately opted to give in to despair. I'm not unconvinced that becoming a memory-less Shuankhsen (she destroyed her own Memory in her final moments, and as per the Roller that probably means she'll never, ever remember anything from before becoming a Shuankhsen) is entirely inappropriate as a fate. Horrible for her, of course, but it's a nice fresh start. Maybe she'll be happier this way? To be honest, I can very easily see her becoming the biggest monster of them all in her current circumstances...<br /> <br /> To me, Bast really stood out during the finale. She was everywhere, leading the charge, killing Shuankhsen, breaking the geometric network, reclaiming stolen relics, exacting retribution upon Sesu Ra. Watching Aquila abandon her did wring out a pretty human reaction, for sure.<br /> <br /> With regards to the Deceived, Arcanist, what sort of powers are you looking for? As you say, with Blessed Is The God-King up they have access to pretty much every Utterance. In terms of mystical might, however, I think the combined forces of the Su-Menent have them beat. It's an interesting situation that Jakarta is left in, with all the temporal power nested in the Deceived's cult while the Arisen are a rather more formidable body of supernatural beings, just deprived of mundane support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:22:14-08:00","id":757743,"title":"","content":"I had completely forgotten that the unleashed temakh could give itself any Utterance it desired, whoops. It was certainly not the brightest idea for Imhotep to go immediately charging after the Su-Menet without any backup, but I'm sure the Tomb Legion commander will have his day eventually, even if there are some terribly horrifying warrior-priests on the island capable of raising armies of the undead and other such terrible things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:45:45-08:00","id":757770,"title":"","content":"It's less the mystical power/armies of undead that the Su-Menent might have, and more that Aqhat and Sekhet Bastet are the only two Arisen capable of interacting with Twilight (and thus hurting the Temakh in Blessed Is The God-King mode) without relying on some kind of Utterance-based &quot;buff&quot;. The problem found with powers like Harvest the Divine Flesh and Words of Dead Hunger is that the Deceived promptly manifest the ability to Rebuke the Vizier, or in the case of Imhotep and Dalila actually knew the power from the get-go, and use Tier 3 to strip away their opponent's ability to hurt them. And since the Temakh regenerates 2 pillars a turn, their opponent will eventually exhaust themselves and be entirely at the creature's mercy.<br /> <br /> However, while Imhotep is a competent fighter, he doesn't quite hold up to the likes of Aqhat and Sekhet Bastet in a straight fight. Their ability to hurt him without the use of their powers definitely swung the battle the other way. But he actually hadn't had to experience that before (Bast spent their entire previous encounter having her soul yanked from her body by Akenakhi), so in his pride assumed he could crush the Su-Menent on his lonesome. Now we're back to the status quo, really, where the Arisen have the numbers and strength to win a straight fight and the Deceived must look to press their advantage in more subtle ways. And with the city itself under their control, the Deceived have a lot of different options at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:53:18-08:00","id":757775,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes sense. Don't the Deceived have the ability to use Rebuke the Vizier Tier 3 to prevent any <i>potential </i>enchantments or powers for the scene if they know the target's name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:18:07-08:00","id":757788,"title":"","content":"From memory, Tier 3 changes from the ability to cancel one enchantment currently on the target, to cancelling <i>every</i> enchantment they currently have.<br /> <br /> Both Bast and Sesu Ra had undergone changes that would have rendered the True Names known by the Deceived (obtained before their first encounter) ineffective mind you, so that probably wasn't an option for the Deceived this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:51:38-08:00","id":758261,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming in Bast's case that was the eating a Shah thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:07:42-08:00","id":759906,"title":"","content":"Not due to any inherent element of the act itself, but more in what it signified for the character personally and its interaction with one of the criteria of determining a true name. But yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}